+{"id": "P0796", "q": "If x - y = 5 and x³ - y³ = 520 , then the value of xy is :", "o": ["79", "3", "36", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "बीजगणित", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Formula used : - = (x - y) x³ y³ ( x − y )² + 3 xy [ ]⁵20 = 5¹04 = 25 + 3xy ⇒ 5² + 3 xy [ ] ⇒ 79 = 3xy xy = ⇒ ⇒ 79³"},
+{"id": "P0797", "q": "If P(x) = and ( x³ − 8 )( x + 1 ) Q(x) = the LCM of P(x) ( x³ + 1 )( x − 2 ) and Q(x) is:", "o": ["( x² + 2 x + 4 ) ( x² + 4 x + 1 )", "( x + 1 )( x − 2 )( x² + 2 x + 4 ) ( x² − x + 1 )", "( x + 1 )² ( x − 2 )² ( x² + 2 x + 4 ) ( x² + 4 x + 1 )", "( x − 2 ) ( x + 1 )"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "बीजगणित", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "P(x) = ( - 8 (x + 1) x³ ) = (x - 2) ( + 2x + 4) (x +1) x² Q(x) = ( +1) (x - 2) x³ = (x + 1) ( -x + 1) (x - 2) x² LCM of P(x) and Q(x) = (x + 1) (x - 2) ( + 2x + 4) ( -x + 1) x² x²"},
+{"id": "P0798", "q": "If = 3, x ≠ 0 , then the x + 1 x value of is: x⁷ + 1 x⁷", "o": ["749", "843", "746", "849"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "बीजगणित", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "…….(1) x + 1 x = 3 On squaring eqn (1), we get …….(2) x² + 1 x² = 7 On squaring eqn (2), we get …….(3) x⁴ + 1 x⁴ = 47 On cubing eqn (1), we get = = x³ + 1 x³ ( 3 )³ − ( 3 )( 3 )²7 − 9 = 18 So, 18 ……(4) x³ + 1 x³ = On multiplying (3) and (4), we get ( )( ) = (18) x⁴ + 1 x⁴ x³ + 1 x³ ( 47 ) ( ) + ( ) = 846 x⁷ + 1 x⁷ x + 1 x + = 846 So, = 843 x⁷ + 1 x⁷ 3 x⁷ + 1 "},
+{"id": "P0799", "q": "If a transversal intersects two parallel lines, and the difference between two interior angles on the same side of the transversal is 40°, then find the smallest angle among the interior angles.", "o": ["70°", "50°", "40°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the interior angles on the same side are and x ° y ° Where ( x > y ) We know that the sum of interior angles is 180°. ∴ ……(i) x + y = 180° And …….(ii) x − y = 40° From solving the equations (i) and (ii) we get, y = 70° Hence, small interior angle ( ) = 70° y"},
+{"id": "P0800", "q": "In , the straight line parallel to ∆ ABC the side BC meets AB and AC at the points P and Q, respectively. If AP = QC, the length of AB is 16 cm and the length of AQ is 4 cm, then the length (in cm) CQ is:", "o": ["( ） 2²1 + 2 ( )²¹8 − 2", "2¹7 − 2 ( )²¹9 + 2 ( )"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By using Thales theorem = = AP AB AQ AC ⇒ x¹6⁴ x + 4 = + 4⁶4 = 0 x² x − = x − 4 ± 4 ( )² − 4 × 1 × (− 64 )² × 1 = = x − 4 ± 272² × 1² 17 − 2 ( )"},
+{"id": "P0801", "q": "In the given figure, a circle is inscribed in PQR, such that it touches ∆ the sides PQ, QR and RP at points D, E, F, respectively. If the lengths of the sides PQ = 18 cm, QR = 13 cm and RP = 15 cm, then find the length of PD.", "o": ["10cm", "8 cm", "15 cm", "12cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "219 Let , PF = PD = , RF = RE = and x y QE = QD = Z According to the question, 2( ) = 13 + 15 + 18 = 46 x + y + z = 23 cm x + y + z Now, length of PD ( ) = ( ) x x + y + z − ( ) = 23¹3 = 10 cm y + z − Short trick :- PD = ( ) PQ + QR + RP 2 − RQ PD =( )¹8 + 13 + 15² − 13 PD = 23¹3 = 10 cm −"},
+{"id": "P0802", "q": "In the given figure, the length of arc AB is equal to 3 times radius r of the circle. Find the area of sector OAB in terms of radius r.", "o": ["1.5", "2.5", "3 r² r² 1² r² r²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= 180° = ( )° π c ⇒ 1 c¹80 ×7²2 (in radian) = = = 3 θ lengtℎ of arc radius 3 x x (in degree) = θ 3 × 180 × 7²2 Area of sector = θ 360° × 22⁷ × r² = = 1.5³ × 180 × 7²2 × 360 × 22⁷ × r² r²"},
+{"id": "P0803", "q": "In the given figure, if AD⊥ BC, AC = 26 units, CD = 10 units, BC = 42 units, ∠DAC = x and ∠B = y, then the value of - + 8 tan y is: (in unit)⁶ cos x⁵ cos y", "o": ["16", "9", "13", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "+ 8⁶ cos x − 5 cos y tan y = + 8 × 6²4²6 − 5³2⁴0²4³2 = + 8 × 26⁴ − 5 × 5⁴ 3⁴ = = units 26 − 25 + 24⁴ 25⁴"},
+{"id": "P0804", "q": "In a parallelogram, one of the parallel sides is 16 cm and the other side is 12 cm. If the perpendicular distance between the two parallel sides of dimension 16 cm is 24 cm, then the perpendicular distance between its other two parallel sides is: Matriculation Level 27/06/2023 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["16 cm", "12 cm", "32 cm", "24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ABCD is a parallelogram, DC॥AB and DA॥CB We know that, DC =AB =16 and DA=CB =12 According to the question, Area of ADC = Area of ABC ⇒ △ △ 16 × 24 = × 12 ×h ⇒ 1² × 1² h = = 32 cm ⇒ 16 × 24¹2"},
+{"id": "P0805", "q": "In the given figure, a circle is inscribed in PQR, such that it touches △ the sides PQ, QR and RP at points D, E, F, respectively. If the lengths of the sides PQ=15 cm, QR=11 cm and RP = 13 cm, then find the length of PD.", "o": ["9 cm", "8cm", "7.5cm", "8.5cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of tangents drawn from a common external point to the circle is always equal. Perimeter = PQ + QR + RP = 2x + 2y + 2z x + y + z = ……… eq . (1)³9² RF = RE ……..(tangent from external point) y + z = 11 …… eq .(2) On solving eq .(1) and eq ."},
+{"id": "P0806", "q": "In the given figure, MNP , SQP , NQR and MSR are straight lines. ∠NPQ = 54° and ∠QRS = 68°. What is the degree measure of ∠SMN?", "o": ["29°", "38°", "54°", "68°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In RMN ∆ + + 68° = 180° θ α + = 112° ……………….. eq 1 θ α Now, In PMS ∆ + 180 - + 54° = 180° θ α + 54° = θ α Putting the value of in equation 1 α + + 54° = 112° θ θ = 29° θ Short trick :- = 90° ∠ SMN − ∠ R + ∠ P² = 90° ∠ SMN − 68° + 54° 2 = 29° ∠ SMN"},
+{"id": "P0807", "q": "An arc on a circle that is 15 cm long subtends a²4° angle at the centre. What is the circumference of the circle?", "o": ["240 cm", "220 cm", "236 cm", "225 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of the circle = , l θ where l is arc of circle and is the angle θ in radian r = = cm 15²4 × π 180° 225² π Circumference of the circle = 2 × × = 225 cm π 225² π"},
+{"id": "P0808", "q": "In the following figure, P and Q are 190 centers of two circles. The circles are intersecting at points A and B. PA produced on both the sides meets the circles at C and D. If ∠CPB = , then 100° find the value of x.", "o": ["115", "120", "110", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Construction : we take a point E on the arc such that ABED is a cyclic quadrilateral. ∠PAB = ∠BPC (angle subtended at arc 1² is half the angle subtended at the centre.) ∠PAB = × 100° = 50° 1² ∠BED = ∠PAB = 50° (external angle property of cyclic quadrilateral) ∠BQD = 2∠BED (angle subtended at centre) ∠BQD = 2 × 50° = 100°"},
+{"id": "P0809", "q": "In triangle ABC, D and E are points on BC such that AD = AE and ∠BAD = ∠CAE. If AB = (2p + 3), BD = 2p, AC = (3q - 1) and CE =q, then find the value of (p + q).", "o": ["3", "4.5", "3.6", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As, AD = AE, ∠D = ∠E = x As ∠BAD = ∠CAE = y (let) By exterior angle property, ∠B = ∠C = (x – y) By symmetry, BD = CE, so, 2p = q, As, ∠B = ∠C, AB = AC ⇒ 2p + 3 = 3q – 1²p + 3 = 3²p – 1 ⇒ ⇒ × 4 = 4p p = 1. ⇒ ⇒ So, q = 2p = 2 (p + q) = 2 + 1 = 3."},
+{"id": "P0810", "q": "The side of an equilateral is ∆ ABC cm. P is a point on side BC such that 3⁷ BP : PC = 1 : 2. The length (in cm) of AP is:", "o": ["6", "7⁶ 3⁷ 3"], "ol": ["c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "PC = 2 = 2³ 7³ × 7 AD is the altitude and median of triangle DC = 3⁷ 2 PD = 2 - = 7³ 7² 7² AD = = = 3 a² 3 . 3 . 7² 3²1² AP = = 7 AD 2 + DP 2 Short Trick :- BP = × = 3⁷ 1³ 7 PC = × = 3⁷ 2³ 2⁷ = BP × PC AP ( )² Side ( )² − AP = = 7 cm 63 ( ) − 14"},
+{"id": "P0811", "q": "In , AD is a median. If points ∆ ABC E, F and G midpoints of AD, AE and DE, respectively, then what will be the area ∆ BFG ?", "o": ["1² ( Area ∆ ABC )¹⁸ ( Area ∆ ABC )", "1⁴ ( Area ∆ ABC )¹² ( Area ∆ BGC )"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As Median divides the triangle into two equal areas. And in ADB, ∆ Area of ADB = 2 Area of BGF(base(AD ∆ ∆ = 2GF) is half and height is same) So, Area of ABC = 4 × Area of BGF ∆ ∆ Area of BGF = Area of ABC ⇒ ∆ 1⁴ × ∆"},
+{"id": "P0812", "q": "In a ABC, ∠A = 90°, if BM and CN ∆ are two medians, is equal BM 2 + CN 2 BC 2", "o": ["3", "5", "4", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Short-Trick: We know, 4 ( BM 2 + CN 2 ) = 5 BC 2 = BM 2 + CN 2 BC 2⁵ 4"},
+{"id": "P0813", "q": "In the following figure (not to scale), ∠DAB + ∠CBA = 90°, BC = AD, AB = 20 cm, CD = 10 cm, then the area of the quadrilateral (in cm 2 ) ABCD is:", "o": ["120", "150", "100", "75"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In trapezium ABCD, CD = PQ = 10 cm AP = QB = 5 cm ∠DAB + ∠CBA = 90° let ∠DAB = ∠CBA = 45° In right angle triangle APD, ∠DAP + ∠APD + ∠PDA = 180° 45° + 90° + ∠PDA = 180° ∠PDA = 180° - 135° = 45° If ∠PDA = ∠DAP = 45° then AP = PD = 5cm Area of trapezium = × sum of parallel sides × height 1² = × 30 × 5 = 75 cm 2¹ 2"},
+{"id": "P0814", "q": "If in the given figure, ∠ACB + ∠BAC = 80°; ∠BDE = 35° ; ∠BCE = 45° , then the marked angle ∠CED is:", "o": ["150°", "120°", "160°", "135°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠CBD = 80° (exterior angle) In quadrilateral BCDE ∠CED = 360° - (80° + 45° + 35°) ∠CED = 200° (it ia a re flex angle) Obtuse angle (∠CED) = 360° - 200° = 160°"},
+{"id": "P0815", "q": "PA and PB are tangents to the circle and O is the centre of the circle. The radius is 5 cm and PO is 13 cm. If the area of the triangle PAB is M, then the value of is: M¹5", "o": ["24", "13", "24", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of PAB , M = PX ∆ 1² × AB × Let OX = a and PX = 13 - a Area of PAO = PA ∆ 1² × AO × = PO 1² × AX × 12 = 13 ⇒ 1² × 5 × 1² × AX × AX = ⇒ 60¹3 AB = 2 AX = × 120¹3 Use pythagoras theorem in AXO; ∆ OX 2 = OA 2 - AX 2 OX 2 = 5² - ( )² OX = ⇒ 60¹3 ⇒ 25¹3 PX = 13 - = = 25¹3¹69 − 25¹3¹44¹3 Area of PAB , ∆ M = 1² × 120¹3 × 144¹3 = M¹5¹ 15 × 1² × 120¹3 × 144¹3"},
+{"id": "P0816", "q": "In the given figure, MP is the tangent to a circle with centre A and NQ is a tangent to a circle with centre B. If MP = 15 cm, NQ = 8 cm, PA = 17 cm and BQ = 10 cm, then AB is:", "o": ["13.5 cm", "23 cm", "14 cm", "28 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "MP = 15 cm, NQ = 8 cm, PA = 17 cm and BQ = 10 cm AM = = 8 cm 17² − 15² NB = = 6 cm 10² − 8² AB = 8 + 6 = 14 cm"},
+{"id": "P0817", "q": "In the figure, two circles with centres P and Q touch externally at R. Tangents AT and BT meet the common tangent TR at T. If AP = 6cm and PT = 10 cm, then BT =?", "o": ["6 cm", "12 cm", "8 cm", "10 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AP , radius of first circle = 6 cm and PT = 10 cm Tangent is perpendicular to the radius. Apply pythagoras theorem in TAP , ∆ TP 2 = AP 2 + AT 2 AT = 8 cm ⇒ Tangents to a circle from a point outside the circle are equal in length."},
+{"id": "P0818", "q": "The lengths of the parallel sides of a trapezium are 51 cm, and 21 cm, and that of each of the other two sides is 39 cm. What is the area( in cm 2 ) of the trapezium?", "o": ["1206", "1296", "1152", "1260"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As given, the mentioned trapezium is isosceles In right triangle BNC BN = ( 39 )² − ( 15 )² = = 3 =36⁵4 × 24 × 2 × 6 Area of the trapezium = 1² × ( sum of parallel sides ) × ℎeigℎt = = 1296¹ 2 × 72 × 36 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P0819", "q": "PT is a tangent at the point R on a circle with centre O. SQ is a diameter. Which when produced meets the tangent PT at P . If 32 , then what will be ∠ SPT = ° the measure of ? ∠ QRP", "o": ["32", "58", "30", "29 ° ° ° °"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that OR is the radius of the circle that is perpendicular to the tangent PT. ∠ ORP = 90° In , OR = OQ = r ∆ ORQ ∠ORQ = ∠OQR ⇒ In ORP ∆ , ∠ ORP = 90° ∠ RPO = 32° ∠ ROP = 58° ⇒ Thus, In ∆ ORQ ∠ORQ = ∠OQR = 61° ∠QRP = 90 - 61 = 29 °"},
+{"id": "P0820", "q": "PQRS is a rectangle . T is a point on PQ such that RTQ is an isosceles triangle and PT= 5 QT. if the area of the triangle RTQ is 12√3 , then the area cm 2 of rectangle PQRS is :", "o": ["142√3 cm 2", "134√3 cm 2", "144√3 cm 2", "142 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since QRT is a right angled isosceles triangle due to ∠Q= 90 Area of △ QRT = 12√3( Given) = 12√3 x² = 24√3......(1) ⇒ 1 × x × x² ⇒ Now PQ = 6x, QR = x Area of rectangle = l b = 6x x = 6x² × × = 6 ……(using 1st) = 144 sq cm × 24√3 √3"},
+{"id": "P0821", "q": "If in , P = 120° , PS QR at S ∆ PQR ∠ ⊥ and PQ + QS = SR, then the measure of ∠ Q is :", "o": ["20°", "50°", "40°", "30°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, P = 120 ° , PS QR and ∠ ⊥ PQ + QS = SR. Draw PT= PQ . Let PQ = y and QT = 2x, and ∠ PQS = θ ∠ PRQ = ϕ In + + = 180 ∆ PQR ∠ PQR ∠ PRQ ∠ QPR = 180 - 120 = 60 …..(1) ⇒ θ + ϕ PQT is an isosceles triangle and PS ⇒ ⊥ QR QS = ST = x ⇒ ....(PQ = PT) ⇒ ∠ PTQ = θ And ∠ QPT = 180 − 2 θ Now, PQ + QS = SR …(given) y + x = x + TR TR = y ⇒ ⇒ PT = TR ……(Both are equal to y ) ⇒ ..(PT = T"},
+{"id": "P0822", "q": "The perimeter of is 24 cm ∆ ABC and its side, BC = 9 cm. AD is the bisector of BAC, while I is the incentre ∠ AI : ID is equal to :", "o": ["7 : 5", "5 : 2", "3 : 2", "5 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AB + AC + BC = 24 cm ⇒ AB + AC = 24 - 9 = 15 cm ⇒ = = = ⇒ AI ID AB + AC BC ⇒ AI ID 15⁹ 5³"},
+{"id": "P0823", "q": "In , D is a point on BC such ∆ ABC that ∠BAD = ∠ADC, ∠BAC = 87° and 1² ∠C = 42°. What is the measure of ∠ADB ?", "o": ["94°", "68°", "102°", "78°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, ∠BAD = ∠ADC 1² × , ∠BAC = 87° and ∠C = 42° ∠B = 180 ° - ∠BAC - ∠C = 180 ° - 87°- 42° = 51° ∠BAD + ∠B = ∠ADC (external opposite angle) ∠BAD + 51°= 102° ∠BAD = 51° ∠ADB = 180 ° - ∠BAD - ∠ABD = 180 ° - 51° - 51° = 78 °"},
+{"id": "P0824", "q": "ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral in which and . What is ∠ A = 67° ∠ B = 92° the difference between the measure of and ∠D ? ∠ C", "o": ["29°", "27°", "19°", "25°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "DAB = 67° and ABC = 92° ∠ ∠ DAB + BCD = 180° ∠ ∠ (opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral)⁶7° + BCD = 180° BCD = 113° ∠ ⇒ ∠ ABC + CDA = 180° (opposite ∠ ∠ angles of a cyclic quadrilateral)⁹2° + CDA = 180° CDA = 88° ∠ ⇒ ∠ Required difference = 113° - 88° = 25°"},
+{"id": "P0825", "q": "In AD BC and BE AC, ∆ ABC , ⊥ ⊥ AD and BE intersect each other at F. If BF = AC, then the measure of ∠ABC is:", "o": ["45°", "60°", "70°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ BDF and ∆ AEF , ∠ BDF = ∠ AEF ∠ BFD = ∠ AFE ⇒ ∆ BDF ∼ ∆ AEF ∠ DBF = ∠ FAE In ∆ BDF and ∆ ADC , BF = AC ∠ DBF = ∠ DAC 227 ∠ BFD = ∠ ACD By ASA congruence, ∆ BDF ≅ ∆ ADC Hence, BD = AD Therefore, ∠ ABD = ∠ BAD ABC = 45° ∠"},
+{"id": "P0826", "q": "Let ABC and PQR be two congruent triangles, such that ∠A = ∠P = 90°. If BC = 29 cm, PR = 21 cm, find the value (in cm) of AB.", "o": ["23", "19", "20", "22"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "These two triangles are congruent. So length of corresponding sides is equal AB = PQ, AC = PR, BC = QR AB = , BC 2 − AC 2 AB = = 20 cm 29² − 21²"},
+{"id": "P0827", "q": "In ΔΑΒC, ∠A = 85° and ∠C = 58°. If ΔPQR is similar to ΔABC, and in correspondence, then find ∠Q .", "o": ["37°", "85°", "58°", "73°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given that is similar to Δ ABC Δ PQR So, corresponding sides and angles are equal , and ∠ A = ∠ P ∠ B = ∠ Q ∠ C = ∠ R ∵ = 180° - (85° + 58°) = 37° ∠ B ∴ = 37° ∠ Q"},
+{"id": "P0828", "q": "The measures of two angles of a triangle are in the ratio 3 : 7. If the sum of these two measures is equal to the measure of the third angle, then find the smallest angle.", "o": ["27°", "3°", "9°", "36° SSC CGL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the measure of first two angels = 3 and 7 x x ∴ Measure of third angle = 10 x Sum of all three angles of a triangle = 180° 3 x + 7 x + 10 x = 180° ∴ x = 9° Hence smallest angle = 3 x = 27°"},
