+{"id": "P0859", "q": "Two chords of a circle, and AB CD , meet outside the circle at the point P . If m( ) = 200 mm, m( ) = 120 mm, and AP AB m( ) = 160 mm, what is the length (in CP mm) of ? CD", "o": ["100", "75", "60", "150"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Chord AB and Chord CD , when produced meet at point P outside the circle. PB = PA AB = 200¹20 = 80 mm − − By using secant theorem , we get PB × PA = PD × PC ⇒ 80 × 200 = PD × 160 PD = = 100 mm 80 × 200¹60 Now, CD = CP PD = 160¹00 = 60 mm − −"},
+{"id": "P0860", "q": "If ABC ~ PQR, AB = 4 cm, PQ = ∆ ∆ 6 cm, QR = 9 cm and RP = 12 cm, then find the perimeter of ABC. ∆", "o": ["18 cm", "16 cm", "20 cm", "22 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ABC ~ PQR ∆ ∆ Then , = = AB PQ BC QR CA RP = BC = 6⁴ 6 BC 9 ⇒ Again , = CA = 8⁴ 6 CA 12 ⇒ Now , perimeter of ABC = AB + BC + CA ∆ = 4 + 6 + 8 = 18 cm"},
