+{"id": "P0863", "q": "In the given figure, QPS ≅ SRQ ∆ ∆ . Find the measure of ∠PSR.", "o": ["64°", "74°", "52°", "82°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the given figure, QPS ≅ SRQ ∆ ∆ So, ∠P = ∠R¹06° ⇒ Now, in ∆ QRS ∠SQR + ∠R + ∠RSQ = 180° 52° + 106° + ∠RSQ = 180° ∠RSQ = 22° Now, ∠RQS = ∠PSQ = 52° {alternate angle} Hence, ∠PSR = ∠PSQ + ∠RSQ = 52° + 22° = 74 °"},
+{"id": "P0864", "q": "In the given figure, PQ is a chord passing through the centre 'O' of the circle. Calculate ∠PQS.", "o": ["40°", "60°", "20°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "234 According to the figure, ∠SRQ + ∠SPQ =180° {cyclic quadrilateral} So, 110° + ∠SPQ = 180° ∠SPQ = 70° ⇒ Now, ∠PSQ = 90° In PSQ ∆ ∠PQS = 180° (90 + 70)° = 20° −"},
+{"id": "P0865", "q": "DE is a chord and KDE is a secant of a circle. If KD = 9 cm, DE = 7 cm and KH is a tangent to the circle at point H, then find KH.", "o": ["12 cm", "25 cm", "16 cm", "144 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By using Tangent Secant theorem, ( KH )² = KD × KE = 12 cm ⇒ ( KH )² = 9×16 ⇒ KH = 144"},
+{"id": "P0866", "q": "The following formula is used to calculate which of the following? × π × diameter Angle of arc at centre 360°", "o": ["Length of a sector", "Area of an arc", "Radius of a circle", "Length of an arc"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of an arc = × × diameter angle of arc at centre 360° π"},
