+{"id": "P0872", "q": "In the figure, AB = AD = 9 cm and AC = AE = 13 cm and BC = 15 cm. Find ED?", "o": ["18 cm", "16 cm", "14 cm", "15 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In EAD and CAB △ △ AE = AC (given) , AD = AB (given) ∠EAD = ∠CAB (vertical opposite angles are equal) EAD CAB (By SAS rule) △ ≅ △ ED = BC = 15 cm"},
+{"id": "P0873", "q": "In ABC, D and F are the middle ∆ points of the sides AB and AC, respectively. E is a point on the segment DF such that DE : EF = 1 : 2. If DE = 4 cm, then BC is equal to: Graduate Level 27/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["20 cm", "26 cm", "22 cm", "24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As D and F are the mid- points of side AB and AC respectively . So using midpoint theorem , DF BC and BC = 2 × DF ∥ BC = 2 × (8 + 4) = 24 cm"},
