+{"id": "P0878", "q": "AD is a tangent of a circle, and ABC is the secant. If AB = 8 cm and BC = 10 cm, then find the length of AD.", "o": ["144 сm", "12.5 сm", "13.45 сm", "12 cm SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 1 Q.277 . Angle subtended by a chord xy on the centre of a circle is 180 degree. If the length of this chord is 36 cm, then what will be the radius of this circle? SSC CHSL 09/03/2023 (1st Shift)", "24 cm", "18 cm", "27 cm", "21 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Tangent - secant theorem :- = AB × AC AD ( )² AD = = 12 cm. 8×18"},
