+{"id": "P0880", "q": "In a triangle MNO, XA, XB and XC are perpendicular bisectors on sides MN, ON and OM respectively intersect each 201 other at X. If = 55 degree, then ∠ NMO what is the value of ∠NXO?", "o": ["130°", "110°", "95°", "125°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All perpendicular bisectors of a triangle concur at one point called circumcenter as a center of its circumscribing circle."},
+{"id": "P0881", "q": "If in triangle ABC, D is a point on the side BC such that the line joining AD bisects the angle A. If the length of BD and BC are 4cm and 10cm respectively, then find the ratio of the lengths of AB and AC.", "o": ["2 : 3", "5 : 3", "3 : 5", "3 : 2 Q.326 . Distance of a chord RS from the centre is 20 cm, If the length of this chord is 30 cm, then what will be the diameter of this circle ? (in cm) SSC CHSL 21/03/2023 (3rd Shift)", "45", "55", "60", "50"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By angle bisector theorem :- = = = AB AC DB CD 4⁶ 2³"},
+{"id": "P0882", "q": "If one of the interior angles of a regular polygon is times of one of the 15¹6 interior angles of a regular decagon, then find the number of diagonals of the polygon.", "o": ["20", "14", "2", "35"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Each interior angle of a polygon = ( n − 2 ) × 180 n According to question, = ( n − 2 ) × 180 n¹5¹6 × 8 × 180¹0 n = 8 Number of Diagonals = n ( n − 3 )² Number of Diagonals of the polygon which is octagon = 20"},
+{"id": "P0883", "q": "In the given figure, AB=DB and AC = DC. If ∠ABD = 58° and ∠DBC = (2x - 4)°, ∠ACB = (y + 15)° and ∠DCB = 63°, then the value of 2x + 5y is:", "o": ["325", "273", "259", "268"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the given figure , ≅ ∆ ABC ∆ DBC As AB = BD , AC = CD and BC is common in both triangles . Then , = y +15° = 63° ∠ ACB ∠ BCD ⇒ y = 48° ⇒ And = = (2x-4)° ∠ ABC ∠ CBD + = 58° ……(given) ∠ ABC ∠ CBD (2x- 4)°+ (2x - 4)° = 58° x = 16.5° ⇒ Now, 2x + 5y = 2 × 16.5° + 5 × 48° = 33° + 240° = 273°"},
+{"id": "P0884", "q": "XYZ ~ GST and XY : GS = 2 : 3, ∆ ∆ XV is the median to the side YZ, and GD is the median to the side ST. The value of ( )² is ______. YV SD", "o": ["4", "9", "3", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If two triangles are similar then the ratio of their corresponding sides are equal. If , ∆ XYZ ~ ∆ GST Then = …….eq .(1) XY GS YZ ST YV = and SD = …..eq .(2) YZ 2 ST 2 Putting the value of eq .(2) in eq .(1) , we get = = ( )² = XY GS 2 YV 2 SD 2³ ⇒ YV SD 4⁹"},
