+{"id": "P0897", "q": "The hour hand moves through 4 hours and has a length of 6 cm. Find the area (in cm 2 , rounded off to two decimal places) of the sector covered by the hour hand.", "o": ["32.69", "30.67", "37.71", "35.75"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, the hour hand moves by 30° every 1 hour. So, angle formed , in 4 hours = 30 × 4 = 120° So, area of sector formed = × × 6 × 6 = = 37.71¹20³60²2⁷ 264⁷ c m²"},
+{"id": "P0898", "q": "A triangle and a parallelogram have the same base 28 cm and the same area. If the height of the parallelogram is 12 cm, then find the length of the altitude of the triangle.", "o": ["28 cm", "23 cm", "24 cm", "21 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the height of triangle be ‘h’ cm According to question Area of parallelogram = Area of triangle 12 × 28 = × 28 × h h = 24 cm 1² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0899", "q": "In the given figure, if KI = IT and EK = ET, then ∠TEI = .", "o": ["75°", "125°", "105°", "150°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "KI = IT, KE = ET and side IE is common So, ∆ KIE ≅ ∆ TIE Therefore, ∠ KEI = ∠ TEI ∠KET = 150° (Given) ∠KET + ∠KEI + ∠TEI = 360° So, ∠TEI = = 105° 360 − 150²"},
+{"id": "P0900", "q": "Find the area of the shaded portion of an equilateral triangle with 6 units shown in the following figure.A circle of radius 1 unit is centered at the midpoint of a side of the triangle.", "o": ["(9√3 - ) unit 2¹ 2¹1⁷", "(9√3 - ) unit 2¹ 4¹1⁷", "(6√3 - ) unit 2¹ 2¹1⁷", "(9√3 - ) unit 2¹ 2²2⁷ SSC CPO 2022 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of equilateral triangle = × = 9 square unit 3⁴ 6² 3 Area of quadrant = × × 1⁴ 22⁷ 1² = square unit 11¹4 Area of shaded portion = 9 - ( + )³⁹ 3² 11¹4 = - 9³ 2¹1¹4 = ( 9 - ) square unit 1² 3¹1⁷"},
+{"id": "P0901", "q": "In the given figure, AB = 8 cm; AC = 17 cm. What is the length of AD ?", "o": ["4.68 cm", "5.36 cm", "3.76 cm", "8.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= AD × AC A B² = AD × 17 AD = = 3.76 cm 8² ⇒ 64¹7"},
+{"id": "P0902", "q": "In the given figure, the circle with centre O has radius 10 cm. The radius of the circle with centre P is x. STR is a common tangent to the two circles at points R and S as shown in the figure. RT = 16 cm and TS = 24 cm. What is the value of x (in cm)?", "o": ["15", "16", "12", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ORT PST (By AAA rule) △ ∼ △ So, = = OR PS RT ST ⇒ 10 x¹6²4 x = = 15 cm ⇒ 10 × 24¹6"},
+{"id": "P0903", "q": "In the given circle with diameter AB, find the value of X.", "o": ["40°", "20°", "30°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "243 = = x°………..(angle drawn by ∠ DAB ∠ DCB the same arc DB) and AB is a diameter so = 90° ∠ ACB = 50° + x° = 90° x° = 40° ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0904", "q": "Two circles touch each other externally. The radius of the first circle with centre A is 18 cm. The radius of the second circle with centre B is 8 cm. Find the length of their common tangent CD.", "o": ["23cm", "26cm", "24cm", "25cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the common tangent = 2 r¹ . r² = 2¹8 × 8 = 24 cm"},
+{"id": "P0905", "q": "In the given figure, DE|| BC. If AD = 5 cm, DB = 10cm, and AE = 8cm, then AC is:", "o": ["24 cm", "32 cm", "8 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If AD = 5 cm, DB= 10cm, and AE = 8cm When DE|| BC, AD AB = AE AC AC = 8 × 15⁵ = 24 cm"},
+{"id": "P0906", "q": "AB is the common tangent to both circles as shown in the given figure. What is the distance between the centres of the circles ?", "o": ["20 cm", "15 cm", "10 cm", "30 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠CAE = ∠DBE (90°) ∠CEA = ∠BED (vertically opposite angle) From AAA - similarity , ∆ ACE ∼ ∆ BED So, AC AE = BD BE ⇒ BD = 15 × 4³ = 20 cm Now, from pythagoras theorem, DE = 25 cm and CE=5cm The distance between the centers of the circles = 25 + 5 = 30 cm"},
+{"id": "P0907", "q": "ABC is a right angle triangle and angle ABC = 90 degrees. BD is a perpendicular on the side AC. what is the value of ? BD 2", "o": ["AD DC", "BC AB × ×", "BC CD", "AD AC × ×"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, When in a right angled ABC, BD ⟂ AC, ∆ then = AD DC BD 2 ×"},
+{"id": "P0908", "q": "x, y and z are the sides of a triangle. If z is the largest side and , then the triangle is a : x² + y² > z²", "o": ["Isosceles right angled triangle", "Acute angled triangle", "Obtuse angled triangle", "Right angled triangle"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": ", where z is the x² + y² > z² longest side and x, y are the two smaller sides. The triangle formed here is an acute angled triangle as the square of the longest side is less than the sum of the squares of the other two smaller sides."},
+{"id": "P0909", "q": "TAP , TAP = 60°, TA = 6cm, AP ∆ ∠ = 8 cm. K is the midpoint of AP . A line form k is produced to meet TP at O such that ∠AKO = 120°. Find the length of OK. Graduate Level 01/08/2022 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["3 cm", "4 cm", "5 cm", "6 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since, TAP + OKA = 60° + 120° = 180° ∠ ∠ (pair of interior angles on the same side of transversal is supplementary) So, OK AT and also K is the midpoint of AP ."},
+{"id": "P0910", "q": "If AB is a chord of a circle with radius 5 units and C is a point on the circle such that ACB = , then the ∠ π 2 length of chord AB is: Graduate Level 02/08/2022 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["10 units", "2.5 units", "7.5 units", "5 units"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, radius of the circle = 5 units Theorem used :- When angles subtended at the circumference of a circle from the two end points of a chord is 90° , then that chord is act as the diameter of the circle."},
+{"id": "P0911", "q": "Given that MAN and CPT are ∆ ∆ congruent to each other such that = ∠ M⁷5, = 65, = 40, = , = 6y + ∠ N ∠ A ∠ C x² ∠ P¹6. Find the value of (x- 5y). Graduate Level 04/08/2022 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["130", "125", "135", "120"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "MAN ≅ CPT (given) ∠A = ∠P △ △ ⇒ 40 = 6y + 16 , 24 = 6y , y = = 4²4⁶ Also, ∠M = ∠C , 75 = , x = 75 × 2 = 150 x² So, x - 5y = 150 - 5 × 4 = 150 - 20 = 130"},
+{"id": "P0912", "q": "Observe the given figure and find the value of s. Graduate Level 04/08/2022 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["5", "3", "2", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the given triangle , = = 2⁴ 2¹0⁵ and one angle of each triangle is equal to 35°. so, 1² (by SAS rule) △ ∼ △ 2 = ; s = = 3 ⇒ 6 s⁶ 2"},
+{"id": "P0913", "q": "Given that triangle ABC is congruent to triangle DEF. If AC = 11m, ED = 6m, EF = 15m, ∠ FDE = 85° and ∠ABC = 55°,then the perimeter of triangle ABC and ∠EFD are, respectively: Higher Secondary 01/08/2022 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["32 m, 45°", "32 m, 40°", "30 m, 50°", "35 m, 45°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "244 ABC is congruent to DEF. So, ∆ ∆ , AB = DE = 6m ∠ B = ∠ E = 55° BC = EF = 15m , Perimeter of ABC ∆ = 11 + 6 + 15 = 32m , In DEF, + + = 180° (Sum of ∆ ∠ D ∠ E ∠ F angles of a triangle is always 180°)⁸5° + 55° + = 180° ⇒ ∠ F = 40° ⇒ ∠ F"},
+{"id": "P0914", "q": "The longest chord of a circle is equal to : Higher Secondary 02/08/2022 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["three times the radius", "two times the diameter", "two times the radius", "the radius"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The longest chord of a circle is the diameter itself. And diameter = 2 × radius So, the longest chord of a circle is equal to two times of radius."},
+{"id": "P0915", "q": "In a ABC, a line DE is drawn from ∆ D point on AB to E point on AC such that DE is parallel to BC. Also AD : DB is 2: 5. If AC is 4.2 cm, then what is the length of AE ? Higher Secondary 04/08/2022 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1.2 cm", "3.5 cm", "0.9 cm", "2.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using thales theorem, we have : = = AD AB AE AC ⇒ 2² + 5 AE 4 . 2 = AE = = 1.2 cm ⇒ 2⁷ AE 4 . 2 ⇒ 4 . 2 × 2⁷"},
+{"id": "P0916", "q": "In a ΔPQR, a line segment ST is drawn joining the midpoint S of PQ and T of PR. Also, ST is parallel to QR. Which of the following options is correct? Higher Secondary 05/08/2022 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["2 ST = PQ + PR", "ST = PS + PT", "ST = 2 (QR)", "2 ST = QR SSC CHSL 2021 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using thales theorem, we get 2ST = QR"},
+{"id": "P0917", "q": "In the following figure, is an ∆ ABC inscribed triangle as shown and DE is a tangent to the circle at C. which of the angles from the given options is necessarily equal to ∠ACD?", "o": ["∠BAC", "∠BCE", "∠ABC", "∠BCA"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using the alternate segment theorem, the angle between tangent and chord through the point of contact of the tangent is equal to the alternate segment angle."},
+{"id": "P0918", "q": "Triangle ABC and PQR are similar to each other. If m( ) = 5 cm, m( ) = BC QR 12.5 cm, and m( ) = 6.25 cm. Find m( PQ ) in (cm). AB", "o": ["6", "2.5", "6.25", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since, ABC PQR, △ ∼ △ = = AB PQ BC QR ⇒ AB 6 . 25⁵ 12 . 5 AB = = 2.5 cm 5 × 6 . 25¹2 . 5"},
+{"id": "P0919", "q": "In the given figure, if ∠RPS = 25°, the value of ∠ROS is _______ .", "o": ["155°", "145°", "135°", "165°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠ORS =∠OSR = 25° 2 In ORS, △ ∠ROS = 180 - ( + ) ° 25° 2²5° 2 = 180 - 25 = 155 ° ° °"},
+{"id": "P0920", "q": "Find the area (in cm 2 ) of the given quadrilateral ABCD.", "o": ["50", "35", "45", "40"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of quadrilateral ABCD = × AC ( DE + BF ) ⇒ 1² = × 10 × (3 + 5) = 5 × 8 = 40¹ 2 c m²"},
+{"id": "P0921", "q": "The lengths of a pair of parallel sides of a trapezium are 20 cm and 25 cm, respectively, and the perpendicular distance between these two sides is 14 cm. What is the area (in ) of the cm 2 trapezium?", "o": ["512", "250", "300", "315"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of trapezium = × (sum of parallel side) × perpendicular 1² distance between them × (20 + 25) × 14 = × 45 × 14 ⇒ 1² 1² = 315 c m²"},
+{"id": "P0922", "q": "If the corresponding angles of two triangles are equal and satisfy = = , then PX ER ZX RF PZ EF", "o": ["ΔPXZ is similar to ΔEFR", "ΔPXZ is similar to ΔERF", "ΔXPZ is similar to ΔERF", "ΔPXZ is similar to ΔREF"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since, = = PX ER ZX RF PZ EF so, PXZ ERF △ ∼ △"},
+{"id": "P0923", "q": "Given below are some of the measures of the sides and angles of five triangles. Which of the triangles given in the options is not congruent to ? ∆ ABC In = 5cm ∆ ABC , m ( AB ) = 3 . 6 cm , m ( BC ) = 4cm, = 52. , m ( CA ) m ( ∠ B )⁴° m ( ∠ C ) = 45 . 5° In ∆ DEF , m ( DE ) = 4 cm , m ( EF ) = 5 cm , m ( FD ) = 3 . 6 cm In = 5cm ∆ GHL , m ( HI ) m ( ∠ H ) = 52 . 4° , m ( ∠ I ) = 45 . 5° In , = 3.6 cm, ∆ JKL m ( JK ) m ( L J ) = 4 cm , m ( ∠ J ) = 52 . 4° In = 3.6cm, = 5 cm ∆ MNO , m ( MN ) m ( NO ) , m ( ∠ N ) = 52 . 4 °", "o": ["ΔMNO", "ΔGHI", "ΔJKL", "ΔDEF"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "On Checking the options , we get ABC JKL △ ≠ △ For, ABC to be congruent to JKL we △ △ should have, AB = JK = 3.6 cm , BC = LJ = 4 cm , A = J = 52.4° but here B = ∠ ∠ ∠ J = 52.4°, which is not possible."},
+{"id": "P0924", "q": "The area of a right-angled triangle is 42 . If the length of one of its two cm 2 sides containing the right angle is 10 cm, find the length (in cm) of the other side that contain the right angle.", "o": ["4.0", "8.0", "8.4", "4.8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let base of right angles triangle = 10 cm Area of triangle = × base × height 1² 42 = × 10 × Height 1² Height = = 8.4 cm 42 × 2¹0 So, the length of other side that contain right angle = 8.4 cm"},
+{"id": "P0925", "q": "ABCD is a square of 21 cm. A circle is inscribed in the square, which touches the sides of the square at P , Q , R , and S as shown below in the figure . What is the area (in ) of the cm 2 non-shaded region? [figure is not drawn to scale and take ] π = 22⁷", "o": ["88.4", "84.6", "90.7", "94.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = 21 × 21 = 441 c m² Length of the side of square = diameter of the circle 245 Area of circle = × × 22⁷ 21² 21² = = 346.5⁶93² c m² So, the area of non- shaded region = 441 - 346.5 = 94.5 c m²"},
+{"id": "P0926", "q": "Calculate the area (in cm 2 ) of the following diagram.", "o": ["45", "42", "48", "50"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In this figure we can clearly see five squares of side 3 cm is formed when a line is produced So, area of shaded region = 5 × = 45³ 2 c m²"},
+{"id": "P0927", "q": "Each edge of the following square is 20 cm long, and a circle is inscribed in the square as shown. What is the area of the shaded region (in cm 2 ) ? [Use = π ]³ . 14", "o": ["88", "85", "86", "84"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the square = a² = 20² = 400 Radius of circle = half of the side of square = 10 cm Area of the circle = r² π = 3.14 × 10 × 10 = 314 Area of shaded region = 400 - 314 = 86 cm 2."},
+{"id": "P0928", "q": "In the following figure, △ABC is an inscribed triangle as shown and DE is a tangent to the circle at C. If m∠ACD = 65° and m∠ACB = 35°, find the measure of m∠BAC.", "o": ["80°", "75°", "60°", "65°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, ∠BCE = 180° - ∠ACD - ∠ACB = 180° - 65° - 35° = 180° - 100° = 80° Angle between tangent and chord is equal to the angle in the alternate segment."},
+{"id": "P0929", "q": "AB is a diameter of a circle with centre O. A tangent is drawn at point A. C is a point on the circle such that BC produced meets the tangent at P . If ∠APC = 62°, then find the measure of angle subtended by the minor arc AC.", "o": ["56°", "62°", "28°", "31°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The tangent is perpendicular to the diameter. ∠A = 90 , ° Now ∠ABP + ∠APB = 90 ° ∠ABP + 62 = 90 ∠ABP = 28 ° ° ⇒ °"},
+{"id": "P0930", "q": "Two common tangents AC and BD touch two equal circles each of radius 7 cm, at points A, C, B and D, respectively, as shown in the figure. If the length of BD is 48 cm, what is the length of AC (in cm)?", "o": ["40", "30", "50", "48"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here radius r = 7 cm (both circles) = B D A C² − ( r + r )² = ⇒ B D² A C² − ( 2 r )² = ⇒ 4⁸ 2 A C² − ( 14 )² = 2304 + 196 = 2500 AC= 50 cm ⇒ A C² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0931", "q": "A cyclic quadrilateral ABCD is drawn in a circle with centre O. A and C are joined to O. If ∠ABC = 2p and ∠ADC = 3p, what is the measure (in degrees) of the ∠AOC re flex?", "o": ["200", "245", "210", "216"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral, = 180° ∠ B + ∠ D²p + 3p = 180° 5p = 180° p = 36° ⇒ ⇒ ABC = 2p = 72° ∠ AOC = 2⁷2 = 144° ∠ × Reflex AOC = 360° – 144° = 216° ∠"},
+{"id": "P0932", "q": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle. ∠POQ = 54°. What is the measure (in degree) of ∠PRQ?", "o": ["235", "137", "207", "153"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let S be any point on the circumference. ∠PSQ = × ∠POQ = 27° 1² ∠PSQ + ∠PRQ = 180° (cyclic quadrilateral) ∠PRQ = 180° – 27° = 153°"},
+{"id": "P0933", "q": "Let ABC ~ PQR and ∆ ∆ ar (∆ ABC ) ar (∆ QPR ) = . If AB = 10cm, BC = 7cm and AC 64¹69 = 16cm, then PR(in cm) is equal to :", "o": ["21", "13", "26", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, = ( )² = ar (∆ ABC ) ar (∆ QPR )⁶4¹69 ⇒ AC PR 64¹69 = = = 26 cm AC PR 8¹3 ⇒ 16 PR 8¹3 ⇒ PR"},
+{"id": "P0934", "q": "In the following figure, P and Q are centers of two circles. The circles are intersecting at points A and B. PA produced on both the sides meets the circles at C and D. If ∠CPB = , then 100 ○ find the value of x.", "o": ["115", "120", "110", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Construction : we take a point E on the arc such that ABED is a cyclic quadrilateral. ∠PAB = ∠BPC (angle subtended at arc 1² is half the angle subtended at the centre.) ∠PAB = × 100° = 50° 1² ∠BED = ∠PAB = 50° (external angle property of cyclic quadrilateral) ∠BQD = 2∠BED (angle subtended at centre) ∠BQD = 2 × 50° = 100°"},
+{"id": "P0935", "q": "AB is chord of a circle with centre O,while PAQ is the tangent at A.R is a point on the minor arc AB.If ∠BAQ = 70°, then find the measure of ∠ARB.", "o": ["110°", "125°", "70°", "145°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By alternate segment theorem, ∠RAQ = ∠BSA = 70° Now, cyclic quadrilateral SARB ∠S + ∠R = 180° ∠R = 180° – 70° = 110°"},
+{"id": "P0936", "q": "A circle with center O has radius 15cm, D is a point on the circle such that a²4cm long chord AB is bisected by OD at point C. find the length of CD (in cm).", "o": ["9", "6", "4", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here, BC = = = 12 cm AB 2²4² So, OC = = O B² − C B² 1⁵ 2 − 1² 2 = = 9 cm 9² Length of CD = OD – OC = 15 – 9 = 6 cm"},
+{"id": "P0937", "q": "In a triangle ABC, the bisector of angle BAC meets BC at point D such that DC = 2BD . If AC - AB = 5 cm then find the length of AB (in cm).", "o": ["10", "12", "7", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : DC = 2BD = ⇒ BD DC 1² AC – AB = 5cm AD is angle bisector of A Let AB = x cm Then , AC – x = 5cm AC = (5 + x) ⇒ = = ……."},
+{"id": "P0938", "q": "In a circle with centre O and radius 13 cm, and two parallel chords are 208 drawn on different sides of the centre.If the length of one chord 10cm and the distance between two chords is 17cm, then find the difference in length of the two chords (in cm)", "o": ["10", "14", "24", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here we have to use pythagoras triplet of (5, 12, 13) in both the right angle triangle In OQD it is right angle at Q ∆ ……(perpendicular from center divides chord in two equal parts ) QD = × CD QD = × 24 = 12 cm 1² ⇒ 1² So by pythagoras triplet of (5, 12, 13) OQ = 5 cm Now OP = PQ – OQ = 17 – 5 = 12cm Now in OBP by pythagoras triplet of (5, ∆ 12, 13) Two sides are 12 and 13 so"},
+{"id": "P0939", "q": "In a circle with center O, PA and PB are tangents to the circle at point A and point B , respectively , C is a point on the major arc AB, If ∠ACB = 50°, then find the measure of ∠APB.", "o": ["100°", "90°", "80°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠ACB = 50°…..(given) ∠AOB = 2 × 50° = 100° …..(angle at center is double of angle at circumference ) ∠A = ∠B = 90° ……(point of contact of tangents makes 90° ) Now in quadrilateral AOBP ∠A + ∠B + ∠AOB + ∠P = 360° ∠P = 360° - 90° - 90° - 100° = 80°"},
+{"id": "P0940", "q": "In a right triangle ABC , right angle at B , altitude BD is drawn to the hypotenuse AC of the triangle . If AD = 6 cm, CD = 5cm, then find the value of AB 2 + BD 2 (In cm 2 )", "o": ["30", "96", "36", "66"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : If AD = 6 cm, CD = 5cm And BD AC ⊥ BD² = AD × CD BD² = 6 × 5 BD = ⇒ 30 in BDA applying pythagoras theorem ∆ AB² = = 6² + ( )² = 66 AD ² + BD ² 30 So, AB 2 + BD = 66 + 30 = 96 cm² ²"},
+{"id": "P0941", "q": "AC is the diameter of a circle dividing the circle into two semicircles. ED is a chord in one semicircle, such that ED is parallel to AC, B is a point on the circumference of the circle in the other circumference . ∠CBE = 75°, what is the measure (in degree) of ? ∠ CED", "o": ["68°", "37°", "75°", "15°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: AC is a diameter AC ED and ∠CBE = 75° ॥ Now ,∠ABC = 90°…. (AC is diameter) ∠ABE = 90° - 75° = 15° ∠ACE = ∠ABE = 15° ………(angle on circumference by same arc AE) ∠CED = ∠ACE = 15° ………(alternate opposite angle of parallel lines are equal)"},
+{"id": "P0942", "q": "A circle is circumscribed on a quadrilateral ABCD, If DAB = 100°, ∠ ∠ ADB = 35° and CDB = 40°, then find the ∠ measure of DBC. ∠", "o": ["35°", "60°", "45°", "40°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given that , DAB = 100° ∠ CDB = 40° ∠ So CDB = 40°…..(angle on ∠ CAB = ∠ circumference by same arc BC) DAC = DAB - CAB = 100° - 40° ∠ ∠ ∠ = 60° DBC = = 60° …….(angle on ∠ ∠ DAC circumference by same arc DC )"},
+{"id": "P0943", "q": "In the following figure , AD bisects angle BAC. Find the length (in cm ) of BD ?", "o": ["4", "5", "9", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "248 As shown in given figure in question AD bisects ∠BAC So, = AB AC BD DC = ⇒ 6² x − 3 x − 2 x⁶x = 2x² - 4x - 3x + 6 ⇒ 0 = 2x² - 4x - 3x - 6x + 6 ⇒ 0 = 2x² - 13x + 6⁰ = 2x² - 12x - x + 6 ⇒ ⇒ 0 = 2x(x - 6) -1(x - 6)⁰ = (2x - 1)(x - 6) ⇒ ⇒ x = , 6 ⇒ x = is not possible ⇒ 1² 1² because BD = x - 2 will become negative So x = 6 and BD = x - 2 = 6 - 2 = 4"},
+{"id": "P0944", "q": "and are two regular polygons. A¹ A² The sum of all the interior angles of is A¹ 1080°. Each interior angle of exceeds A² its exterior angle by 132°. The sum of the number of sides and is : A¹ A²", "o": ["21", "22", "23", "24"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let number of sides of polygon = n A¹ So, (n – 2)¹80 = 1080 n = 8 × ⇒ In polygon , A² Each interior angle + Each exterior angle = 180° (Each exterior angle + 132°) + Each exterior angle = 180° 2 (Each exterior angle) = 48° Each exterior angle = 24° 249 So, number of sides of polygon A² = = = 15³60 Eacℎ exterior angle 360²4 So, total sides = 8 + 15 = 23"},
+{"id": "P0945", "q": "In ∠ °, AD is ∆ ABC , BAC = 90 drawn perpendicular from A on BC. Which among the following is the mean proportional between BD and BC ?", "o": ["AD", "AB", "CD", "AC SSC CGL 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In right angle BAC, where ∠A = 90° and ∆ line AD perpendicular to line BC then = AB 2 BD × BC = AB BD × BC So mean proportional between BD and BC = = BD × BC AB"},
+{"id": "P0946", "q": "In ABC, ∠C = 90° and Q is the ∆ midpoint of BC. If AB = 10 cm and AC = 2 , then the length of AQ is : 10 cm", "o": ["√55 cm", "5√3 cm", "5√2 cm", "3√5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Applying pythagoras theorem in ABC, ∆ AB 2 - AC 2 = CB 2 CB = = 100 − 40² 15 CQ = CB = 1² 15 Applying pythagoras theorem in ACQ ∆ AQ 2 = AC 2 + CQ 2 AQ 2 = 40 + 15 AQ = cm ⇒ 55"},
+{"id": "P0947", "q": "In a triangle ABC, point D lies on AB, and points E and F lie on BC such that DF is parallel to AC and DE is parallel to AF. if BE = 4cm, CF = 3 cm, then find the length (in cm) of EF .", "o": ["3", "1.5", "5", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the figure ABC is similar to DBF ∆ ∆ = BC BF AB BD ABF is similar to BDE ∆ ∆ = BF BE AB BD Comparing both the equations = (Let EF = x) BC BF BF BE = ⇒ 7 + x⁴ + x⁴ + x⁴ 28 + 4x = 16 + 8x + x² x² + 4x -12 = 0 ⇒ ⇒ x = 2 or -6 (x is a distance and it can’t ⇒ be negative) x = 2 ⇒ Short trick :- BF 2 = BE × BC (Remember this) (x +4)² = 4 × (7 + x) x² + 16 + 8x = 28 + 4x x "},
+{"id": "P0948", "q": "From an external point A, two tangents AB and AC have been drawn to a circle touching the circle at B and C respectively. P and Q are points on AB and AC respectively such that PQ touches the circle at R. If AB = 11 cm, AP = 7 cm and AQ = 9 cm, then find the length of PQ (in cm).", "o": ["8", "7", "5", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept used : from a point outside the circle only two tangents can be drawn and both are equal From point A, AB = AC = 11cm AB = AP + PB , BP = 4cm From point P , BP = PR = 4cm AC = AQ + QC QC = 2cm ⇒ From point Q, QC = QR = 2cm So, PQ = 4 + 2 = 6 cm"},
+{"id": "P0949", "q": "In a triangle ABC, a point D lies on AB and points E and F lie on BC such that DF is parallel to AC and DE is parallel to AF. If BE = 4 cm, EF = 6 cm, then find the length (in cm) of BC.", "o": ["25", "30", "15", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AFB DEB ∆ ∼∆ So, = …..(i) DB AB BE BF Now, DBF ABC ∆ ∼∆ So, = …….(ii) DB AB BF BC From eq . (i) and eq . (ii) = BC = = 25 cm BE BF BF BC ⇒ 10 × 10⁴ Short trick :- BF 2 = BE × BC (Remember this)¹0 × 10 = 4 × (BC) BC = 25cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0950", "q": "Points A and B are on a circle with center O. PAM and PBN are tangents to the circle at A and B respectively from a point P outside the circle. Point Q is on the major arc AB such that ∠QAM = 58° and ∠QBN = 50°, then find the measure of ∠APB.", "o": ["30°", "32°", "36°", "40°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "251 ∠QAM = ∠QBA = 58° (alternate segment) ∠QBN = ∠QAB = 50°(alternate segment) ∠AQB = 180° - 58° - 50° = 72° ∠AOB = 2 × 72° = 144° ∠APB = 180° - 144° = 36°"},
+{"id": "P0951", "q": "In triangle ABC, D is a point on BC 210 such that BD: DC = 3: 4. E is a point on AD such that AE:ED = 2 : 3. Find the ratio of area (∆ ECD ): area (∆ AEB ).", "o": ["9 : 8", "1 : 2", "2 : 1", "8 : 9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= (triangles with same Area of ADC Area of ABD 4 x³ x height)³x = 5 unit x = unit ⇒ ⇒ 5³ = 4x = 4 = unit Area of ADC × 5³ 20³ = (Triangles with the Area of ACE Area of ECD 2 y³ y same base) ⇒ 5 y = unit 20³ = 3y = 4 unit Area of ECD = = 2 : 1 Area of ECD Area of ABE 4²"},
+{"id": "P0952", "q": "If the areas of ∆ ABC ∼ ∆ DEF and are 100 cm 2 and 81 cm 2 , ∆ ABC ∆ DEF respectively and the altitude of is ∆ DEF 6.3 cm, then the corresponding altitude (in cm) of is : ∆ ABC", "o": ["5.6", "9", "7", "8.4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "( )² Area of ∆ ABC Area of ∆ DEF = ℎeigℎt of ∆ ABC ℎeigℎt of ∆ DEF ⇒ ⇒ x = 7 cm 100⁸1 = x⁶ . 3¹0⁹ = x⁶ . 3"},
+{"id": "P0953", "q": "A chord AB of circle C¹ of radius 17 cm touches circle C² which is concentric to C¹ . The radius of C² is 8 cm. What is the length (in cm) of AB ?", "o": ["30", "25", "20", "24"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In triangle DOB ( is of 90°) ∠ D DB 2 = = 15² 17² − 8² DB = 15 cm So, AB = 30cm"},
+{"id": "P0954", "q": "In D is a point on side AB ∆ ABC , such that BD = 3 cm and DA = 4 cm. E is a point on BC such that DE॥ AC. Then Area of : Area of trapezium ACED = ? ∆ BDE", "o": ["16 : 33", "40 : 9", "33 : 16", "9 : 40"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "DE॥ AC △BAC ∆ BDE ∼ = = ar ( △ BDE ) ar ( △ BAC ) BD 2 AB 2⁹ 49 Area of : Area of trapezium ACED ∆ BDE = 9 : (49 - 9) = 9 : 40"},
+{"id": "P0955", "q": "Triangle ABC is an equilateral triangle. D and E are points on AB and AC respectively such that DE is parallel to BC and is equal to half the length of BC. If AD + CE + BC = 30 cm, then find the perimeter (in cm) of the quadrilateral BCED.", "o": ["45", "25", "37.5", "35"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "DE ॥ BC △ADE △ABC ∼ = = = AD AB AE AC DE BC 1² AD = AE = DE = 1 unit AB = AC = BC = 2 unit CE = AC - AE = 1 unit AD + CE + BC = 30 cm 4 unit = 30 cm 1 unit = 7.5 cm Perimeter of BCED = DB + DE + EC + BC = 5 unit = 37.5 cm"},
+{"id": "P0956", "q": "The angles of a triangle are in AP (arithmetic progression). If measure of the smallest angle is 50° less than that of the largest angle, then find the largest angle (in degrees)", "o": ["80", "85", "90", "75"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Three angles are (60° - d), 60°, (60° + d) Difference between largest and smallest angle = 2d²d = 50° d = 25° ⇒ ⇒ Largest angle = 60° + 25° = 85°"},
+{"id": "P0957", "q": "Points P and Q are on the sides AB and BC respectively of a triangle ABC, right angled at B. If AQ = 11 cm, PC = 8 cm and AC = 13 cm, then find the length (in cm) of PQ:", "o": ["4√7", "√15", "4.5", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "+ = ---- (1) AB 2 BQ 2 AQ 2 + = ---- (2) BC 2 BP 2 PC 2 On adding (1) and (2) + + + = + AB 2 BQ 2 BC 2 BP 2 AQ 2 PC 2 + = + 169 + ⇒ AC 2 PQ 2 AQ 2 PC 2 ⇒ PQ 2 = 121 + 64 = 16 PQ = 4 ⇒ PQ 2 ⇒ Short trick :- + = + (remember this) AC 2 PQ 2 AQ 2 PC 2¹69 + = 121 + 64 ⇒ PQ 2 = 16 PQ = 4 ⇒ PQ 2 ⇒ 252 ∠ OAB = ∠ OBA = (180° - 116°) = 32° 1² ×"},
+{"id": "P0958", "q": "In the triangle ABC, D and E are mid-points of AB and BC respectively. If area ( CED) = 8 cm 2 , then what is the ∆ area (ADEC) in cm 2 ?", "o": ["21", "32", "24", "16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "BE = EC (E is midpoint of CB) In CBD, E is the midpoint of BC so it ∆ divides the triangle into two equal areas So, Area of BDE = Area of DEC = 8 ∆ ∆ Hence, Area of BCD = 8 + 8=16 ∆ Now, In ABC , D is the mid point of AB ∆ so it divides ABC in two equal areas."},
+{"id": "P0959", "q": "In a triangle ABC, length of the side AC is 4 cm more than 2 times the length of the side AB. Length of the side BC is 4 cm less than the three times the length of the side AB. if perimeter of ∆ ABC is 60 cm, then its area (in cm 2 ) is:", "o": ["120", "150", "144", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB = x, then AC = 2x + 4 and BC = 3x - 4 According to the question, x + 2x + 4 + 3x - 4 = 60 x = 10 ⇒ AB = 10, AC = 24, BC = 26 It is a right angle triangle, Area = = 120 cm 2¹ 2 × 24 × 10"},
+{"id": "P0960", "q": "The area of table top in the shape of an equilateral triangle is 9 cm 2 . 3 What is the length (in cm) of each side of the table?", "o": ["6", "2", "4", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of equilateral triangle = = 9 ⇒ = 36 ⇒ a = 6³ 4 × a² 3 a²"},
+{"id": "P0961", "q": "Points M and N are on the sides 211 PQ and QR respectively of a triangle PQR, right angled at Q . If PN = 9 cm, MR = 7 cm, and MN = 3 cm, then find the length of PR (in cm).", "o": ["13", "11", "12", "41"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the diagram MN 2 + PR 2 = PN 2 + RM 2 PR 2 = 81 + 49 - 9 = 121 PR = 11 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0962", "q": "Points A, B and C are on a circle with centre O such that ∠BOC = 84°. If AC is produced to a point D such that ∠BDC = 40°, then find the measure of ∠ABD (in degrees).", "o": ["92", "102", "56", "98"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the diagram ∠BAC = ∠BOC (Angle on the same 1² arc) ⇒ ∠BAC = 42° In ABD, ∠B = 180° - (42° + 40°) = 98° ∆"},
+{"id": "P0963", "q": "In a circle with centre O, AB is a chord of length 10 cm. Tangents at points A and B intersect outside the circle at P . If OP = 2 OA, then find the length (in cm) of AP .", "o": ["10", "12", "12.5", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In OAP , ∠A is of 90° ∆ So, PA = a³ Area of the OAP ∆ ⇒ × a × a = × 2a × 5 a = 5¹ 2³ 1² ⇒ 3² a = , So a = 10cm. ⇒ 10³ 3"},
+{"id": "P0964", "q": "In ABC and DEF, we have = ∆ ∆ AB DF = , then which of the following BC DE AC EF is true ?", "o": ["DEF ~ ABC", "BCA ~ DEF ∆ ∆ ∆ ∆", "CAB ~ DEF", "DEF ~ BAC ∆ ∆ ∆ ∆"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = AB DF BC DE AC EF Write it as = = BA DF BC DE CA EF On comparing the corresponding terms BCA ~ DEF ∆ ∆"},
+{"id": "P0965", "q": "Triangle ABC is right angled at B. BD is an altitude intersecting AC at D. If AC = 9 cm and CD = 3cm, then find the measure of AB (in cm).", "o": ["3", "6", "6", "3³ 6 SSC CHSL 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As ∆ ABC ∼ ∆ ADB So, = AC AB AB AD AB 2 = AC × AD = 9 × 6 = 54 AB = ⇒ 3⁶ Short trick :- AB 2 = AC × AD AB 2⁹ × 6 = 54 AB = = ⇒ 3⁶ 253"},
+{"id": "P0966", "q": "In an isosceles triangle ABC, AB = AC and AD is perpendicular to BC. If AD = 12 cm and the perimeter of of is 36 ∆ ABC cm, then the length of BC (in cm) is:", "o": ["5", "12", "10", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB = AC = x We know, In an isosceles triangle, perpendicular, median and angle bisector are the same line. and AD is median also."},
+{"id": "P0967", "q": "The in-radius and circumradius of a right-angled triangle is 3 cm and 12.5 cm, respectively. The area of the triangle (in cm 2 ) is:", "o": ["64", "48", "88", "84"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumradius(R) = 12.5 It means, Hypotenuse = 25 cm Inradius(r) = 3 cm We know, 7, 24 and 25 are triplets. So , Area of triangle = = 84¹ 2 × 7 × 24 Short trick :- Area = r² + 2Rr = 9 + 2 × 12.5 × 3 = 9 + 75 = 84 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P0968", "q": "If the perimeter of an isosceles right triangle is then the 15 ( 2 + 1 ) cm , area of the triangle (in cm 2 ) will be:", "o": ["46 .", "5", "45", "56 ."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that a right angle isosceles triangle has ratio of its side as 1 : 1 : 2 Let, sides of right angle isosceles triangle = a, a, a² So perimeter = a(2 + ) = 15( + 1)²² a ( + 1) = 15( + 1) a = ⇒ 2² 2 ⇒ 15² So, Area = a a¹ 2 × × = = 56.25 ⇒ 1² × 15² × 15² 225⁴"},
+{"id": "P0969", "q": "If the length of a chord of a circle, that makes an angle of 60° with the tangent drawn at one end point of the chord is . then the radius of the 8³ cm circle (in cm) will be:", "o": ["8", "5", "6", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "PB = 8³ cm ∠ APB = 60°, ∠ APO = 90°, ∠ OPB = 30° ∠ OBP = ∠ OPB = 30° (OP = OB) ∠POB = 180° - (30° + 30°) = 120° = OP sin 30° PB sin 120° = OP = 8 cm OP × 2¹ 8³ × 2³ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0970", "q": "If O is the centroid and RP is the median with the length 24 cm of ∆ RST , where P is a point on ST, then the value of RO (in cm) is:", "o": ["18", "14", "20", "16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Centroid divides the median in 2:1 ratio RO = 24 = 16 cm 2³ ×"},
+{"id": "P0971", "q": "The area (in cm 2 ) of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle of radius 6 cm is:", "o": ["36", "34", "35", "38"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "254 Area of the largest triangle = cm 2¹ 2 × 12 × 6 = 36"},
+{"id": "P0972", "q": "Line AC is a tangent to a circle at point B on it, and PQ is a chord of the circle such that BP = BQ . If ∠ABP = 64°, then find the measure of ∠PBQ .", "o": ["58°", "64°", "52°", "32°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠ABP = 64° ∠BQP = 64° (Alternate segment theorem) BQ = BP so that ∠BQP = ∠BPQ = 64° ∠PBQ = 180° - 64° - 64° = 52°"},
+{"id": "P0973", "q": "In , ∆ ABC ∠ A = 135° , CA = E and F are 5² cm and AB = 7 cm . the midpoints of sides AC and AB respectively. The length of EF is:", "o": ["6.5", "5.5", "6", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using Cosine rule: COS A = b² + c² − a² 2 bc Where - ( AB = b , AC = c and BC = a ) Cos135° = 7² + ( 5² )² − B C² 2 × 7 × 5² = ⇒ − 1² 49 + 50 − BC ² 70² BC² = 99 + 70 = 169 BC = 13 so, EF = = 6.5¹3² Short trick :- Draw CD DB (when BA is extended to ⊥ D) ⇒ ∠CAD= 180° - 135° = 45° ∠CAD= ∠ACD= 45° (∠CDA = 90°) AC = 5 , AB = 7 (given) ⇒ 2 CD = DA = 5 DB = 5 + 7 = 12 ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0974", "q": "The altitude AD of a triangle ABC is 9 cm. If AB = 6 cm and CD = cm, 3³ 3 then what will be the measure of ? ∠ A", "o": ["90°", "30°", "45°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In , tanA = = ∆ ADC 3³ 9¹ 3 ㄥDAC = 30° In , ⇒ ∆ ABD cosA = = 9⁶ 3³ 2 ㄥBAD = 30° ∠BAC = 30° + 30° = 60° ⇒ Alternate method :- BD 2 = (6 )² - 9² BD = 3 = DC 3 ⇒ 3 BC = 3 + 3 = 6³ 3³ In triangle BAC, AD works as a median because it divides BC into two equal parts, that means AB = AC. But here the length of all sides are equal."},
+{"id": "P0975", "q": "is an isosceles triangle with ∆ PQR PQ = PR = 25 cm. If PS is the median on QR from P such that PS = 7 cm, then the length of QR is:", "o": ["45cm", "42cm", "38cm", "48cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The median of the isosceles triangle is also a altitude So, Applying pythagoras PS 2 + QS 2 = PQ 2 QS 2 = 25² - 7² = 24² , So, QS = 24 As, QS = SR therefore QR = 48 cm"},
+{"id": "P0976", "q": "is drawn in a circle such ∆ ABC that AC = BC and ∠BAC = 65°.From points B and C two tangents are drawn which intersect at point P . What is the measure of ∠BPC?", "o": ["52.5°", "50°", "55°", "32.5°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠COB = 2 × 65° = 130°(Angle at centre is double the angle on major arc) In the quadrilateral OCPB(∠C and ∠B are of 90°) ⇒ ∠BPC = 180° - 130° = 50°"},
+{"id": "P0977", "q": "In AC = BC, and the length ∆ ABC , 212 of the base AB is 10 cm. If CG = 8 cm, where G is the centroid, then what is the length of AC (in cm) ?", "o": ["13", "15", "12⁹1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AC = BC G is the centroid so GD = 4cm Therefore CD = 8 + 4 = 12cm By apollonius theorem, (AC² + BC²) = 2(CD² + AD²)²AC² = 2(5² + 12²) AC² = 13² AC = 13 ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0978", "q": "The perimeter of an isosceles triangle is 3.6 m and its base is 30 cm shorter than each of the equal side. What is the area (in m² ) of the triangle ?", "o": ["0.6", "0.72", "0.54", "0.8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "perimeter of an isosceles triangle = 360 cm Let the equal side be ‘a’ cm and its base is (a - 30) cm. Now, a + a + a - 30 = 360 , a = 130 cm s = = 180³60² Area of the triangle = 180 × 50 × 50 × 80 = 6000 cm 2 = 6000¹0000 = 0 ."},
+{"id": "P0979", "q": "The sum of the radius of two circles is 286 cm and the area between the concentric circles is 50336 cm 2 .What are the radius (in cm) of the two circles? Take ( = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["115 and 91", "115 and 171", "91 and 84", "171 and 84"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ‘R’ is the radius of a big circle and ‘r’ is the radius of a small circle. R + r = 286 …………..(i) (given) R² - r² = 50336 ………….(given) π π (R² - r² ) = 50336 (R - r) (R + r) ⇒ 22⁷ ⇒ = 2288 × 7 (R - r) = ⇒ 2288²86 × 7 = 56 …………….(ii) By solving equ n (i) and (ii) (R + r) + (R - r) = 286 + 56 = 342 R = 171, r = 115"},
+{"id": "P0980", "q": "The three medians RQ, SP and TN of intersect at point O. If the area of ∆ RST is 48 , then the area of ∆ RST cm 2 quadrilateral SQON is: (in ) cm 2", "o": ["20", "12", "16", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "255 Median divides a triangle into 6 equal triangles. 6 unit = 48² unit = 16 ⇒ area of quadrilateral SQON = 16 cm²"},
+{"id": "P0981", "q": "If the area of a right-angled isosceles triangle is 676 , then the cm 2 length of its hypotenuse is:", "o": ["52", "51", "53", "50"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let sides of isosceles right angled triangle be a, a and . 2 a ATQ, a = 26¹ 2 × a × a = 676 ⇒ 2 cm . Hypotenuse ( )² a = 2 × 26² = 52 cm"},
+{"id": "P0982", "q": "In , medians BE and CF are ∆ ABC perpendicular to each other and intersect at M. If BE = 9 cm and CF = 13 cm, then the area of will be: (in ) ∆ ABC cm 2", "o": ["75", "78", "76", "68"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know, Centroid divides median in 2 : 1 BM = 6 cm, ME = 3 cm CM = , MF = 26³ 13³ Area of = 3 × Area of ∆ ABC ∆ MBC = 3 × = 78 cm² 1² × 6 × 26³"},
+{"id": "P0983", "q": "The side BC of is produced ∆ ABC to D. The bisectors of and ∠ ABC ∠ ACD meet at E. If AB = AC and , ∠ BEC = 35° then the measure of will be: ∠ ABC", "o": ["75°", "55°", "35°", "45°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Short-Trick: ∠BAC = 2³5° = 70° × In triangle ABC ∠ABC = ∠ACB ⇒ = (180° - 70°) = 55° 1²"},
+{"id": "P0984", "q": "A and B are two points on a circle with centre O. C is a point on the minor arc of the circle between points A and B. The tangents to the circle at A and B meet each other at a point D. If , then ( in degrees) is ∠ ADB = 25° ∠ ACB equal to:", "o": ["105", "100.5", "102.5", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠AOB = 360° - (90° + 90° + 25°) = 155° ∠AEB = = 77.5° (Angle at the 155° 2 circumference of the circle from the chord is half of the angle at the center) ∠ACB = 180° - 77.5° = 102.5 (Sum of the opposite angles of the cyclic quadrilateral is 180°)"},
+{"id": "P0985", "q": "is inscribed in a circle. The ∆ PQR bisector of ∠P cuts QR at S and the circle at T. If PR = 5 cm, PS = 6 cm and ST = 4 cm, then the length (in cm) of PQ ?", "o": ["13", "12", "10", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In △PQS and △PTR ∠PQS = ∠PTR ∠QPS = TPR △PQS △PTR ∼ = = PQ = 12 cm PQ PT PS PR ⇒ PQ 10⁶ 5 ⇒ Short trick :- PQ × PR + PT × S T = PT 2 PQ × 5 + 10 × 4 = 10 × 10 ⇒ 5PQ = 60 PQ = 12 ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0986", "q": "In , D and E are points on ∆ ABC sides AB and BC, respectively, such that BD : DA = 1 : 2 and CE : EB = 1 : 4 . If DC and AE intersect at F, then FD : FC is equal to:", "o": ["3 : 2", "5 : 2", "8 : 3", "4 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Short-Trick: By mass point geometry DF = 8 unit, FC = 3 unit FD : FC = 8 : 3"},
+{"id": "P0987", "q": "In ∆ ABC , ∠ A − ∠ B = 33° , What is the sum of ∠ B − ∠ C = 18° , the smallest and the largest angles of the triangle?", "o": ["143°", "125°", "92°", "108°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know ………….(1) ∠ A + ∠ B + ∠ C = 180° ………….(2) ∠ A − ∠ B = 33° On subtracting eq (2) from (1) ………..…(3)²∠ B + ∠ C = 147° …………(4) ∠ B − ∠ C = 18° On adding eq (3) and (4)³∠ B = 165° ⇒ ∠ B = 55° ∠ A = 55° + 33° = 88° ∠ C = 55° − 18° = 37° Sum of smallest and largest angle = 88° + 37° = 125°"},
+{"id": "P0988", "q": "In ABC, C=90°, Points P and Q ∆ ∠ are on the sides AC and BC, respectively, such that AP : PC = BQ : QC = 1 : 2 Then is equal: AQ 2 + BP 2 AB 2", "o": ["4", "7", "4", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "BA = ⇒ 3² AQ = ⇒ AC 2 + QC 2 = 13 BP = ⇒ 13 = = ⇒ AQ 2 + BP 2 AB 2¹3 + 13¹8¹3⁹"},
+{"id": "P0989", "q": "The perimeter of ABC and DEF ∆ ∆ are 43.2 cm and 28.8 cm, respectively, and . If DE =12 cm, then ∆ ABC ∼ ∆ DEF the length of AB is:", "o": ["20", "18.4", "18", "20.4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ABC ～ DEF ∆ ∆ Ratio of sides = ratio of perimeters Ratio of perimeters = = 3 : 2⁴3 . 2²8 . 8 AB : DE = 3 : 2 AB = 12 = 18cm ⇒ × 3²"},
+{"id": "P0990", "q": "In PQR, ∠P = 90°, S and T are the ∆ mid points of the sides PR and PQ, respectively. What is the value of ? RQ 2 / ( Q S² + R T² )", "o": ["3", "4", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= + = + ( ⇒ QS 2 PQ 2 PS 2 ⇒ QS 2 PQ 2 PR 2 )²⁴ = 4 + ------ eq.(1) QS 2 PQ 2 PR 2 = + = ( + ⇒ RT 2 PT 2 PR 2 ⇒ RT 2 PQ 2 )² PR 2⁴ = + 4 ------ eq.(2) RT 2 PQ 2 PR 2 Add eq (1) and (2)⁴( + ) = 5( + ) ⇒ QS 2 RT 2 PQ 2 PR 2⁴ ( + ) = 5 ⇒ QS 2 RT 2 QR 2 = ⇒ RQ 2 Q S² + R T² 4⁵ Short trick :- 4(QS 2 + RT 2 ) = 5RQ 2 = ⇒ RQ 2 Q S² + R T² 4⁵"},
+{"id": "P0991", "q": "In the given figure, ABCD is a rectangle and P is a point on DC such that BC = 24 cm, DP = 10 cm, and CD =15 cm. If AP produced intersects BC produced at Q . Find the length of AQ .", "o": ["35 cm", "24 cm", "39 cm", "26 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AP 2 = A D² + P D² AP = 576 + 100 = 26 ⇒ ∆ ADP ≃ ∆ QCP ⇒ AD CQ = DP PC CQ = 12 , ⇒ ⇒ PQ 2 = P C² + CQ 2 PQ = 13 AQ = 26 + 13 = 39 ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P0992", "q": "In the given figure, the measure of ∠A is:", "o": ["40°", "20°", "60°", "50° SSC CHSL 2019 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As both triangles are congruent , 2x = x + 20 , x = 20 , 2x = 40°"},
+{"id": "P0993", "q": "In the given figure, BC is a chord and CD is a tangent through the point C. If ∠AOC = 118°, then find the ∠ACD.", "o": ["63°", "56°", "65°", "59°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠AOC = 118° ∠ABC = = 59° 118² ∠ACD = ∠ABC = 59° (Alternate segment theorem)"},
+{"id": "P0994", "q": "In the given figure, AD is bisector of angle ∠CAB and BD is bisector of angle ∠CBF. If the angle at C is 34°, the angle ∠ADB is:", "o": ["34°", "32°", "17°", "16°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠ADB = ∠ACB 1² ∠ADB = 34° = 17° 1² ×"},
+{"id": "P0995", "q": "In the following figure , if angles ∠ABC = 95° , ∠FED = 115° (not to scale). Then the ∠APC is equal to:", "o": ["120°", "150°", "135°", "155°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Construct FA ∠AFC = 180° - 95° = 85° (ABCF is a cyclic quadrilateral) ∠FAD = 180° - 115° = 65°(ADEF is a cyclic quadrilateral) ∠APC = ∠AFC + ∠FAD (exterior angle property) ∠APC = 85° + 65° = 150°"},
+{"id": "P0996", "q": "If in the following figure (not to the scale), ∠ACB = 135° and the radius of the circle is 2 cm, then the length of 2 the chord AB is:", "o": ["3 cm", "4 cm", "4 cm", "6 cm 2²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ACB = 135°, ∠ ADB = 180° - 135° = 45° , ∠ Let ‘O’ be the centre AOB = 2⁴5° = 90° ∠ × = + , AB = 4 cm AB 2 ( 2² )² ( 2² )²"},
+{"id": "P0997", "q": "In the following figure (not to scale), at the centre O, if the chord AB subtends double the angle that is subtended by chord CD and the angle ∠AEB = 2∠AOB, then ∠COD is equal to:", "o": ["30°", "45°", "60°", "75°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ∠AOB = , ∠AEB = 2 θ θ + 2 = 180° = 60° ⇒ θ θ ⇒ θ ∠COD = = 30° 60²"},
+{"id": "P0998", "q": "In the given figure, chords AD and BC in the circle are extended to E and F, respectively. If ∠CDE = 85°; ∠DCF = 94°, then the value of ∠ABF + ∠EAB is:", "o": ["182°", "194°", "179°", "168°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠ADC = 180°- 85° = 95° ∠BCD = 180° - 94° = 86° Sum of all angles of a quadrilateral is 360° ∠ABF + ∠EAB = 360° - (95° + 86°) =179°"},
+{"id": "P0999", "q": "ABCDE is a regular pentagon. Its sides are extended as shown in the figure. The value of is: ∠ ABC + 2∠ EGD + 3∠ BAJ 6", "o": ["45°", "30°", "75°", "66°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ABCDE is a pentagon, and each pentagon has 108° angle DEG = 180° - 108° = 72° ∠ EDG = 180° - 108° = 72° ∠ DGE = 180° - 72° - 72° = 36° ∠ BAJ = 180° - 108° = 72° ∠ ABC = 108° ∠ ∠ ABC + 2∠ EGD + 3∠ BAJ 6 = = 66° 108° + 72° + 216° 6"},
+{"id": "P1000", "q": "In the given figure, if AD = 3, DE = 4, AB = 12, BF = 2, FG = 6, BC = 10. then the value of is: M N (Assume : M is the area of the quadrilateral FGDE and N is the area of the triangle ABC.)", "o": ["31", "60", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "257 Short trick: By sin formula, area of triangle ABC area of quadrilateral DEFG 1² × ( 5 + 4 + 3 ) × ( 2 + 6 + 2 ) sinB 1² × ( 5 + 4 ) × ( 2 + 6 ) sinB − 1² × 5 ×2 sinB = = = 12 × 10 ( 9 × 8 ) − ( 2 × 5 )¹20⁶2 N M = = ⇒ M N⁶2¹20³1⁶0"},
+{"id": "P1001", "q": "In the given figure, PQR is a triangle in which ∠P : ∠Q : ∠R = 3 : 2 : 1, and PR is perpendicular to RS. What will be the measure of angle TRS ?", "o": ["60°", "45", "50°", "30°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "3x + 2x + x = 180° x = 30° , ∠R = 30° , ∠PRS = 90° ⇒ ∠SRT = 180°-90°-30° = 60°"},
+{"id": "P1002", "q": "In the given figure, if OQ = QR, then the value of m is:", "o": ["3n°", "n°", "2n°", "4n°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "OQ = QR , ∠QOR = n° ∠PQO = 2n° (by exterior angle) ∠QPO = 2n° , ∠POQ = 180°- 4n° m° + 180° - 4n° + n° = 180° m = 3n° ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1003", "q": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle. If ∠BAO = 30° and ∠BCO = 50°, then ∠AOC is equal to:", "o": ["160°", "60°", "40°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠BAO = ∠OBA = 30° (radius) ∠BCO = ∠OBC = 50° (radius) ∠ABC = 50° + 30° = 80° ∠AOC = 2⁸0° = 160° ×"},
+{"id": "P1004", "q": "In the given figure, AB, AC and EF are tangents to a circle. If AC = 15 cm and DE = 3 cm, then the length of AE is:", "o": ["24 cm", "9 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AC = AB = 15 cm (By tangent rule) DE = BE = 3 cm AE = 15 - 3 = 12 cm"},
+{"id": "P1005", "q": "In the given figure, TB is a chord which passes through the centre of the circle. PT is a tangent to the circle at the point. T on the circle. If PT = 10 cm, PA = 5 cm and AB = x cm, then the radius of the circle is:", "o": ["5", "3", "6", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB = cm , x PT 2 = PA × PB 100 = 5( + 5) = 15 cm x ⇒ x Here PT = 10 cm, PB = 20 therefore TB = ( by pythagoras theorem)¹0³ Radius of the circle = TB/2 = cm 5³"},
+{"id": "P1006", "q": "In , AB = AC. If ∠A is twice ∆ ABC the sum of other two angles of the triangle, then the measure of is: 1² ∠ A", "o": ["70°", "60°", "30°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As AB = AC , so ∠B = ∠C Let ∠B = 1 unit then ∠A = 4 units Sum of all angles = 180° (1 + 1 + 4) = 6 units = 180° 1 unit = 30° ∠A = 4³0° = 120° × = = 60° ⇒ 1² ∠ A¹20° 2"},
+{"id": "P1007", "q": "ABCD is a quadrilateral such that = 90°. A circle with centre O touches ∠ D the sides AB, BC and CD and DA at P , Q, R and S respectively. If BC = 40 cm, BP = 28 cm and CD = 25 cm, then what is the radius of the circle is:", "o": ["12", "13", "5", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "BP = BQ = 28 cm (by tangent rules) QC = 40 - 28 = 12 cm QC = RC = 12 cm (by tangent rules) DR = 25 - 12 = 13 cm DR = DS = 13 cm , = 90° ∠ D If we draw perpendicular to R and S then it also makes 90° DR = DS = OR = OS = 13"},
+{"id": "P1008", "q": "A circle is inscribed in the triangle ABC whose sides are given as AB = 10, BC = 8, CA = 12 units as shown in the figure. The value of AD BF is: ×", "o": ["18 units", "21 units", "16 units", "15 units"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "258 Let, BF = x so, FC = 8 - x Then , FC = CD = 8 - x ∵ AD = 12 - (8 - x) = 4 + x Then , AD = AE = 4 + x And, BE = 10 - (4 + x) = 6 - x As we know , BE = BF So, 6 - x = x²x = 6 ⇒ BF(x) = 3 AD = 4 + x = 7, ⇒ ⇒ AD BF = 7³ = 21 ⇒ × ×"},
+{"id": "P1009", "q": "In ABC, AB = AC and AL is ∆ perpendicular to BC at L. In DEF, DE = ∆ DF and DM is perpendicular to EF at M. If (area of ABC):(area of DEF) = 9:25, ∆ ∆ then is equal to: DM + AL DM − AL", "o": ["6", "4", "3", "5²15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = ( )² area (∆ ABC ) area (∆ DEF )⁹²5 AL DM = Then, = = 4 : 1 AL DM 3⁵ DM + AL DM − AL 8²"},
+{"id": "P1010", "q": "In ∠A = 90°, M is the ∆ ABC , midpoint of BC and D is a point on BC such that AD BC. If AB = 7 cm and AC = ⊥ 24 cm, then AD:AM is equal to:", "o": ["168 : 275", "24 : 25", "32 : 43", "336 : 625"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "M is the mid point of BC and AD BC. ⊥ Using pythagoras theorem: BC = 25 cm M is the midpoint, BM = MC = AM = 12.5 cm In ; BA AC = AD BC ∆ BAC × × 7²4 = AD 25 AD = × × ⇒ 168²5 Hence, = = AD AM 168 × 2²5 × 25³36⁶25"},
+{"id": "P1011", "q": "In AC = 8.4 cm, BC= 14 cm. ∆ ABC , P is a point on AB such that CP = 11.2 cm and ∠ACP = ∠B. What is the length (in cm) of BP ?", "o": ["4.12", "2.8", "3.78", "3.6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∠ACP = ∠B ∆ ABC , In and : ∆ ABC ∆ ACP ∠ACP = ∠B, ∠A and side AC is common Hence, = = AB AC BC PC AC AP = = AP = 6.72 ⇒ BC PC AC AP ⇒ 14¹1 . 2⁸ ."},
+{"id": "P1012", "q": "D is the midpoint of BC of . ∆ ABC Point E lies on AC such that CE = AC. 1³ BE and AD intersect at G. What is ? AG GD", "o": ["8 : 3", "4 : 1", "5 : 2", "3 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Apply mass point theorem in the following diagram: AG : GD = 4 : 1"},
+{"id": "P1013", "q": "In , PQ = 24 cm and ∠Q = ∆ PQR 58°. S and T are points on side PQ and PR, respectively such that ∠STR = 122°. If PS = 14 cm and PT = 12cm, then the length of RT is:", "o": ["16.4cm", "15cm", "16cm", "14.8cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In PQ = 24 cm and ∠Q ∆ PQR , = 58°, ∠STR = 122°, PS = 14 cm and PT = 12cm ∠PTS = (180° - 122°) = 58° {∠PTS = ∠PQR = 58° and ∠P ∆ PQR ∼∆ PTS is common} Thus, = = PT PQ PS PR ⇒ 12²4¹4 PR PR = 28 cm , RT = 28 - 12 = 16 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1014", "q": "In ∠B = 90°. If points D and ∆ ABC , E are on side BC such that BD = DE = EC, then which of the following is true ?", "o": ["8AE 2 = 3AC 2 + 5AD 2", "8AE 2 = 5AC 2 + 3AD 2", "5AE 2 = 2AC 2 + 3AD 2", "5AE 2 = 3AC 2 + 2AD 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∠B= 90°. Let AB = 8 ∆ ABC , cm and BC = 6 cm. BD = BE = EC = 2 cm. AC 2 = b² + 9a² = 100 cm AD 2 = b² + a² = 68 cm AE 2 = b² + 4a² = 80 cm Put values in options: 8AE 2, = 3AC 2 + 5AD 2⁸(80) = 3(100) + 5(68)⁶40 = 300 + 340 Thus, option (a) is the answer."},
+{"id": "P1015", "q": "In the given figure, if ∠KLN = 58°, then ∠KMN ?", "o": ["58°", "42°", "26°", "32°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠KLN = 58° In a cyclic quadrilateral, angles formed on the same arc are equal in measurement. Thus, ∠KMN = ∠KLN = 58°"},
+{"id": "P1016", "q": "In the given figure, if ∠ APO = 35°, then which of the following options is correct?", "o": ["∠ APB = 60°", "∠ BPO = 35°", "∠ BPO = 55°", "∠ APB = 80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠APO = 35° , ∠OAP = ∠OBP = 90° In quadrilateral. OAPB; OA = OB = radius AP = BP (two tangents from a same point to a circle are equal in length) OP common."},
+{"id": "P1017", "q": "In the given figure, if AB = 8 cm, AC = 10 cm, ∠ABD = 90° and AD = 17 cm, then the measure of CD is:", "o": ["9 cm", "8 cm", "10 cm", "11 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AB = 8 cm, AC = 10 cm, ∠ABD = 90° and AD = 17 cm Using pythagoras theorem, BC = 6 cm and BD = 15 cm Then CD = 9 cm"},
+{"id": "P1018", "q": "In D, E and F are the ∆ ABC , midpoints of sides AB, BC and CA, respectively. If AB = 12 cm, BC = 20 cm and CA = 15 cm, then the value of 1² is: ( DE + EF + DF )", "o": ["23.5", "11.75", "15.67", "5.88"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Line formed by joining the midpoint of a triangle is half the length of its opposite side. DE = AC, DF = BC & FE = AB 1² 1² 1² (DE + EF + DF) = ( [AB + BC + AC])¹² 1² 1² = (12 + 20 + 15) = 11.75 cm 1⁴"},
+{"id": "P1019", "q": "In the figure, PA is a tangent from an external point P to the circle with centre O. If ∠POB = 110°, then the measure of ∠APO is:", "o": ["30°", "40°", "25°", "20°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠POB = 110° Then, ∠POA = 70° In ∠PAO = 90° (radius tangent) ∆ APO , ⊥ Thus, ∠APO = 20°"},
+{"id": "P1020", "q": "A chord of the larger among the two concentric circles is of the length 10 cm and it is tangent to the smaller circle. What is the area( in ) of the annular cm 2 portion between the two circles ?", "o": ["25π", "5π", "10π 5π 2"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AB = 10cm O’B = R , OO’ = r ⇒ - = 25 (Pythagoras theorem applied R² r² in triangle OO’B) The annular or shaded portion between the two concentric circles is = 𝜋 - 𝜋 = 𝜋( - ) = 25𝜋 R² r² R² r²"},
+{"id": "P1021", "q": "In ABC, C = 90° and CD is ∆ ∠ perpendicular to AB at D. If AD/BD = k then AC/BC = ?", "o": ["k", "k¹ k⁴ k"], "ol": ["a", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that, = AD . DB = CD 2 ⇒ CD 2 k Now consider ADC ∆ AC = AD 2 + CD 2 AC = ……...eq (1) k + k Now, consider BDC ∆ BC = ……...eq (2)¹ + k Now , = AC BC k + k¹ + k = = 4 k ."},
+{"id": "P1022", "q": "In , A = 52° and O is the ∆ ABC ∠ orthocentre of the triangle (BO and CO meet AC and AB at E and F respectively when produced). If the bisectors of ∠ OBC and OCB meet at P , then the ∠ measure of BPC is: ∠", "o": ["124°", "132°", "138°", "154°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, A = 52 ∠ ° BOC = 180 - 52 = 128 ⇒ ∠ ° ° ° In ∆ BOC OBC + OCB = 180 ∠ ∠ ° − ∠ BOC = 180¹28 = 52 ° − ° ° PBC + PCB = ( OBC + OCB) ⇒ ∠ ∠ 1² ∠ ∠ = 52 = 26¹ 2 × ° ° In , ∆ BPC P = 180 - ( PBC + PCB) ∠ ° ∠ ∠ = 180 - 26 = 154 ° ° ° Alternate :- Given, A = 52 ∠ ° BOC = 180⁵2 = 128 ⇒ ∠ ° − ° ° BPC = 90° + = 90° + ∠ ∠ BOC 2¹28° 2 = 90° + 64° = 154°"},
+{"id": "P1023", "q": "In , AB = 6cm, AC = 8cm, ∆ ABC and BC = 9 cm. The length of median AD:", "o": ["cm (b ) cm 317² 119²", "cm", "cm 313² 115²"], "ol": ["a", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= AD 2 AB 2 + 2 AC 2 − BC 2² …...(Apollonius's theorem) AD = = ⇒ 2 ( 6 )² + 2 ( 8 )² − ( 9 )²² 119²"},
+{"id": "P1024", "q": "A circle is inscribed in , ∆ ABC touching AB, BC and AC at points P , Q and R respectively. If AB - BC = 4cm, AB - AC = 2cm and the perimeter of = ∆ ABC 32 cm, then PB + AR is equal to (in cm) :", "o": ["12", "13", "33⁵ 38³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, perimeter of = 32 cm ∆ ABC AB - BC = 4cm ………(1) AB - AC = 2cm ……….(2) Add (1) and (2)²AB - BC - AC = 4 + 2 = 6 cm ……..(3) AB + BC + CA = 32 cm……..(4) ……(perimeter) Add (3) and (4) (2AB - BC - AC) + (AB + BC + CA) = 32 + 6³AB = 38 cm ⇒ PB + AR = AB = cm ⇒ 38³"},
+{"id": "P1025", "q": "In , D is a point on side BC ∆ ABC such that ADC = BAC . If CA = 12 cm, ∠ ∠ and CB = 8cm, then CD is equal to :", "o": ["12 cm", "15 cm", "18 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ ABC and ∆ ADC ∠ADC = ∠BAC ….(Given) ∠ACD = ∠ACB …..(Same angle) ⇒ ∆ BAC ∼ ∆ ADC = CD = = 18 cm ⇒ BC AC AC CD ⇒ 12 × 12⁸"},
+{"id": "P1026", "q": "In , the perpendiculars ∆ ABC drawn from A, B and C meet the opposite sides at D, E and F, respectively. AD, BE and CF intersect at point P . If EPD = ∠ 116° and the bisectors of A and B ∠ ∠ meet at Q, then the measure of AQB is : ∠", "o": ["96°", "122°", "124°", "64°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, EPD = 116 ∠ ° PEC = PDC = 90 ...(perpendiculars) ∠ ∠ ° ECD = 360 ∠ ° − ∠ EPD − ∠ PEC − ∠ PDC = 360¹16⁹0⁹0 = 64 ° − ° − ° − ° ° BAC + ABC = 180 ⇒ ∠ ∠ ° − ∠ ECD = 180⁶4 = 116 ° − ° ° Now, ABQ + BAQ = ( BAC + ABC) ∠ ∠ 1² × ∠ ∠ = 116 = 58¹ 2 × ° ° AQB = 180 - ( ABQ + B&Q) ⇒ ∠ ° ∠ ∠ = 180 - 58 = 122 ° ° ° Short trick :- Given, EPD = 116 ∠ ° PEC = PDC = 90 ...(perpendicu"},
+{"id": "P1027", "q": "In , D and E are the points on ∆ ABC AB and AC respectively such that AD AC × = AB AE. If ADE = ACB + 30° and × ∠ ∠ ABC = 78°, then A = ? ∠ ∠", "o": ["56°", "54°", "68°", "48°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, AD AC = AB AE and ADE × × ∠ = ACB + 30° and ABC = 78° ∠ ∠ = BC DE ⇒ AD AB AE AC ⇒ ∥ = = 78° and = ∠ ADE ∠ ABC ∠ AED ∠ ACB ….(corresponding angle) ADE = ACB + 30° ∠ ∠ 78° = ACB + 30° ACB = 48° ∠ ⇒ ∠ A = 180° ( + ) ⇒ ∠ − ∠ ABC ∠ ACB = 180° 78° - 48° = 54° −"},
+{"id": "P1028", "q": "WXYZ is a quadrilateral in which XQ and ZP are perpendicular to WY such that XQ = ZP . Diagonals ZX and WY intersect each other at point O. If OX = 12 cm, then find the value of ZX (in cm).", "o": ["12", "24", "36", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ZOP and XOQ ∆ ∆ XQ = ZP …..(Given ) ∠ P = ∠Q … (each 90°) ∠ POZ = ∠XOQ …(vertically opposite angle ) ∴ ZOP ≅ XOQ ( AAS Congruence ) ∆ ∆ So , OX = ZO = 12 cm (CPCT ) Hence , ZX =XO + ZO = 12 + 12 = 24cm"},
+{"id": "P1029", "q": "In ABD and FEC, ∠BAD = 60°, ∆ ∆ l(BD) = l(EC), ∠ABD = ∠FEC = 90°, and l(AB) = l(FE). Find the ratio of . ∠ BAD ∠ FCE", "o": ["2 : 3", "1 : 2", "2 : 5", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given , In ABD and FEC, ∠BAD ∆ ∆ = 60°, l(BD) = l(EC), ∠ABD = ∠FEC = 90°, and l(AB) = l(FE) Now in ABD , ∆ + B + D = 180° ∠ A ∠ ∠ 60° + 90° + D = 180° D = 30° ∠ ⇒ ∠ Now, According to question , In ABD and FEC ∆ ∆ AB = FE (Given) B = E (Each 90°) ∠ ∠ BD = CE (Given) By SAS , ABD ≅ FEC ∆ ∆ ∵ D = C = 30° ∠ ∠ Now, ratio of = 60° : 30° = 2 : 1 ∠ BAD ∠ FCE"},
+{"id": "P1030", "q": "In an obtuse-angled triangle ABC, the length of its longest side AB is 50 cm and one of the other two sides are 42 cm. If the area of the triangle is 294 cm 2 , what is the length (in cm) of its third side?", "o": ["12", "8", "15", "2⁴3³5²1⁵8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the height of is AD ∆ ABC Area of = BC AD ∆ ABC 1² × × 294 = 42 AD 1² × × 14 = AD ….. (i) Now in ∆ ADB = + A B² A D² B D² = + … [from (i)]⁵⁰ 2¹ 4² B D² = 2500 - 196 = 2304 B D² = 48 cm BD DC = BD - BC = 48 - 42 = 6 cm In ∆ ADC = + A C² A D² DC 2 = + = 196 + 36 = 232 cm 1⁴ 2⁶ 2 = cm AC 2⁵8"},
+{"id": "P1031", "q": "In the diagram, if || , AG = GD AB CE = DH = HB, then which of the following is correct? I) ACG ΔΒΕΗ ∆ ≅ II) CDE ≅ DEB ≅ DCA ∆ ∆ ∆ III) HFB ≅ AFG ∆ ∆", "o": ["I, II and III", "I and III", "Only I", "I and II"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "I) For, ACG ΔΒΕΗ ∆ ≅ In the AGC and EHB ∆ ∆ AGC = EHB = 90° ∠ ∠ Side (AG) = side(HB) [given] And, CG = EH [lengths between two parallel lines] So, by SAS theorem, ACG ΔΒΕΗ (true) ∆ ≅ II) Now, for CDE ≅ DEB ≅ DCA ∆ ∆ ∆ In the CDE and DEB , CE ॥ AB (given) ∆ ∆ DE = DE [common] CED = BDE [alternate interior angle] ∠ ∠ CE = DB So, CDE ≅ DEB by SAS theorem, ∆ ∆ Similarly, In CDE and"},
+{"id": "P1032", "q": "ABC is a right-angled triangle, right angled at A in such a way that AB = AC and the bisector of angle B intersects the side AC at D. DM is perpendicular to BC, intersecting BC at M. If AB = 12 cm and BC = 12 cm, then find the length of 2 side AD. Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["12( + 2) cm", "12( - 1) cm 2²", "12( - 2) cm", "12( + 1) cm 2²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In DAB and DMB, ∆ ∆ ∠ABD = ∠MBD ∠BAD = ∠BMD = 90° BD = BD (common) So, DAB ≅ DMB by ASA ∆ ∆ AB = BM = 12 cm ⇒ Then, MC = BC - BM = (12 - 12) cm 2 Now, ∠MDC = 180° - (90° + 45°) = 45° So, MC = DM = (12 - 12) cm 2 As, DM = AD (by congruence) Hence, AD = (12 - 12) = 12( - 1) cm 2² Alternate method:- In this type of question we use direct property, The property is AB + AD = BC AD "},
+{"id": "P1033", "q": "In a circle, ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral in which AE is drawn parallel to CD, and BA is produced to F. If ∠ABC = 85° and ∠FAE = 24°, find the value of ∠BCD.", "o": ["119°", "124°", "115°", "125°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In cyclic quadrilateral ABCD + = ∠ B ∠ D¹8⁰ ° = - = ∠ D¹8⁰ ° 8⁵ ° 95 ° Now EA DC ∥ So, = … (co-interior angle) ∠ DAH + ∠ D¹8⁰ ° = ∠ DAB + ∠ BAH + ∠ D¹8⁰ ° = - - = ∠ DAB 18⁰ ° 95 ° 24 ° 61 ° Now + = ∠ C ∠ DAB 18⁰ ° = - = ∠ C¹8⁰ ° 61 ° 119 °"},
+{"id": "P1034", "q": "The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3, then find the ratio of the corresponding sides.", "o": ["1 : 2 :", "1 : 2 : 3³", "1 : : 3", "1 : : 2² 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the angles are , 2 , 3 x x x Sum of angles of triangle = 180° + 2 + 3 = ⇒ = x x x¹80° x³0° Hence angles are ; 30° 60° 90° On Using sine rule = = a sin A b sin B c sin C = = a sin 30° b sin 60° c sin 90° = = = k a¹ 2 b³ 2 c¹ = = = k² a² 3 b c¹ = , = , = 1 a¹ 2 b³ 2 c = 1 : : 2 a : b : c³"},
+{"id": "P1035", "q": "The lengths of the three sides of a triangle are given as 3 cm, 4 cm and 5 cm. The ratio of their corresponding altitudes to the opposite vertices will be: Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["3 ∶ 4 ∶ 5", "9 ∶ 8 ∶ 7", "20 ∶ 15 ∶ 12", "5 ∶ 4 ∶ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept used : Altitudes of the triangle are inversely proportional to the side of that triangle. Sides → 3 : 4 : 5 Altitude → : : = 20 : 15 : 12¹ 3¹ 4¹ 5"},
+{"id": "P1036", "q": "The median AD of a triangle ABC is produced and a perpendicular CF is dropped on it. BE is perpendicular to AD. If BC = 34 cm and DF = 8 cm, what is the length (in cm) of BE ? Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["17", "9", "15", "19"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, CF = = 15 cm 1⁷ 2 − 8² In BED and CFD, △ △ ∠DEB = ∠CFD = 90° ∠EDB = ∠FDC (vertical angle ) BD = DC (given) So, BED CFD (By AAS rule) △ ≅ △ Then, BE = CF = 15 cm"},
+{"id": "P1037", "q": "How many times does the hour hand and minute hand of a clock coincide in half a day ? Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["55", "22", "11", "44"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The minute hand and hour hand coincide after every 65 minutes. Let us take the time when they meet after 12¹2 : 00, 01 : 05, 02 : 10, 03 : 15, 04 : 20, 05 : 25, 06 : 30, 07 : 35, 08 : 40, 09 : 45, 10 : 50, 11 : 55 Hence, in hlaf a day hour hand and minute hand coincide 11 times."},
+{"id": "P1038", "q": "The three sides of a triangle are 9, Search on TG: @apna_pdf 24 and S units. Which of the following is correct ?", "o": ["15 < S < 33", "15 S < 33 ≤", "15 < S³3", "15 S³3 ≤ ≤ ≤"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Value of third side will lies between :- S²4 − 9 ( ) ＜ ＜ 24 + 9 ( ) S¹5 ( ) ＜ ＜ 33 ( )"},
+{"id": "P1039", "q": "In the following figure, P and Q are centers of two circles. The circles are intersecting at points A and B. PA Search on TG: @apna_pdf produced on both the sides meets the circles at C and D. If ∠CPB = , then 100° find the value of x.", "o": ["115", "120", "110", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Construction : we take a point E on the arc such that ABED is a cyclic quadrilateral. ∠PAB = ∠BPC (angle subtended at arc 1² is half the angle subtended at the centre.) ∠PAB = × 100° = 50° 1² ∠BED = ∠PAB = 50° (external angle property of cyclic quadrilateral) ∠BQD = 2∠BED (angle subtended at centre) ∠BQD = 2 × 50° = 100°"},
+{"id": "P1040", "q": "A circle is inscribed in a quadrilateral ABCD , touching sides AB, BC, CD and DA at P , Q, R, and S respectively. If AS = 8 cm , BC = 11 cm and CR = 5 cm, then the length AB (in cm) is equal to: Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["12", "13", "16", "14"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, AS = 8 cm, BC = 11 cm and CR = 5 cm AS = AP = 8 cm (Tangent of same circle) CQ = RC = 5 cm (Tangent of same circle) BQ = BC - QC = 11 - 5 = 6 cm BP = BQ = 6 cm (Tangent of same circle) AB = AP + BP = 8 + 6 = 14 cm"},
+{"id": "P1041", "q": "Side AB of a triangle ABC is 80 Search on TG: @apna_pdf cm long, whose perimeter is 170 cm. If angle ABC = 60°, the shortest side of triangle ABC measures_____cm.", "o": ["17", "15", "25", "21"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "a + b + 80 = 170 a + b = 90 a = 90 - b ⇒ From cosine rule Cos60 ° = a² + 80² − b² 2 × 80 × a⁸0(90 - b) = ( 90 − b )² + 80² − b² 7200 - 80b = 8100 - 180b + 6400¹00b = 7300 b = 73 ⇒ a = 90 - 73 = 17"},
+{"id": "P1042", "q": "The numbers of Commerce, Science and Arts postgraduates working in a company are 40, 80 and 60, respectively. If these figures are represented by a pie chart, then what is the angle corresponding to Commerce postgraduates?", "o": ["60°", "50°", "70°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Angle corresponding to commerce postgraduates = × 360° = 80° 40¹80"},
+{"id": "P1043", "q": "ABCD is a trapezium in which AB is parallel to CD, and E and F are the mid - points of non - parallel sides AD and BC. If EF is parallel to AB, AB = 28 cm and CD = 18 cm, then find EF (in cm).", "o": ["46", "10", "5", "23 SSC MTS 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "EF = = = = 23 cm AB + DC 2²8 + 18² 46²"},
+{"id": "P1044", "q": "The centroid of a ΔXYZ is G. The area of ΔXYZ is 45 cm 2 . The area of ΔGYZ is:", "o": ["22.5 cm 2", "7.5 cm 2", "15 cm 2", "30 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The centroid divides the triangle into 3 smaller( GYZ, GXY and GXZ) triangles ∆ ∆ ∆ of equal area Area of GYZ = ∆ area of ∆ XYZ 3 = = 15 cm 2⁴5³"},
+{"id": "P1045", "q": "If the sum of two sides of an equilateral triangle is 16 cm, then find the third side.", "o": ["1. 4 cm", "16 cm", "Cannot be found", "8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the side of an equilateral triangle be x According to the question, 2 = 16 = 8 cm x ⇒ x We know that an equilateral triangle all side equal to each other so the third side will be 8 cm."},
+{"id": "P1046", "q": "The distance between the centres of two circles of radii 22 cm and 10 cm is 37 cm. If the points of contact of a direct common tangent to these circles are M and Q, then find the length of the line segment MQ .", "o": ["35 cm", "39 cm", "29 cm", "25 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the common tangent(MQ) = ( distance between centre of two circle )² − ( c¹ − c² )² MQ = ( 37 )² − ( 22 − 10 )² = ( 37 )² − ( 12 )² MQ = = = 35 cm 1369 − 144¹225"},
+{"id": "P1047", "q": "Let C be a circle with centre O and P be an external point to C. Let PA and PB be two tangents to C with A and B being the points of tangency, respectively. If PA and PB are inclined to each other at an angle of 60°, then find∠POA.", "o": ["40°", "60°", "80°", "30°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the POA ∆ OPA = 30° [when two tangents are ∠ drawn to a circle from an external point, the line drawn from that external point to the center of the circle bisects the angle formed between the two tangents.] OAP = 90° [radius tangent] ∠ ⊥ Hence, POA = 180° - (30 + 90) = 60° ∠"},
+{"id": "P1048", "q": "Two triangles EFG and HIJ are congruent. If the area of ΔEFG is 124 cm 2 , then the area of ΔHIJ will be:", "o": ["124 cm 2", "248 cm 2", "62 cm 2", "31 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept :- congruent triangles always have the same area. Hence, arΔHIJ = arΔEFG = 124 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1049", "q": "The side of an equilateral triangle is 28 cm. Taking each vertex as the centre, a circle is described with a radius equal to half the length of the side of the triangle. Find the area of that part of the triangle which is not included in the circles (use = and = 1.73 ). π 22⁷ 3", "o": ["30.89 cm 2", "38.08 cm 2", "31.08 cm 2", "39.08 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of 3 sectors = 3 × ( × × ) = 308⁶0° 360° 22⁷ 1⁴ 2 c m² Area of ABC = × = 339.08 △ 3⁴ 2⁸ 2 c m² Then, area of shaded region = 339.08 - 308 = 31.08 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1050", "q": "If 45° and 65° are the angles of a triangle, then find the exterior angle of Search on TG: @apna_pdf the third angle (remaining angle).", "o": ["110°", "120", "70°", "100°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using Exterior angle property ∠RQS = ( P + R) = 65° + 45° = 110° ∠ ∠"},
+{"id": "P1051", "q": "If ΔPQR ≅ ΔMON such that ∠PQR = 82°, ∠QRP = 47°, ∠RPQ = 51°, ∠MON = (5 - 8)°, QR = 24 and ON = 3 + , then y x y find ( + ). x y", "o": ["14", "18", "16", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ΔPQR ≅ Δ MON ∠P = ∠M, ∠Q = ∠O , ∠R = ∠N and ⇒ QR = ON 5y - 8 = 82 y = 18 ⇒ ⇒ And 3 + y = 24 = 2 x ⇒ x Hence, + y = 18 + 2 = 20 x"},
+{"id": "P1052", "q": "In a rhombus ABCD, O is any interior point such that OA = OC. What is five-ninths of the degree measure of ∠DOB?", "o": ["120°", "150°", "100°", "90°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As per figure, Since, DOB is straight line So, of ∠DOB = × 180° = 100° 5⁹ 5⁹"},
+{"id": "P1053", "q": "In ΔPQR, M, N, and S are the mid-points of sides PQ, PR and QR, respectively. If the area of the ΔPQR is 46 cm 2 , what is the area (in cm 2 ) of the quadrilateral MNRQ?", "o": ["39", "27.6", "23", "34.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of each triangle = = 11.5⁴6⁴ c m² Area of quadrilateral MNRQ = 11.5 × 3 = 34.5 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1054", "q": "In a triangle ΔABC, AB = AC and ∠A = 80°, then fi nd ∠B.", "o": ["50°", "80°", "40°", "45°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, we have given triangle ; 80° + 2x = 180° 2x = 180° - 80° = 100° x = 50° ⇒"},
