+{"id": "P1056", "q": "A pair of straight lines from an external point F intersects a circle at A and B (FA < FB), and touches the circle at C. O is the centre of the circle. Given that ∠ACF = 50° and ∠AFC = 30°, fi nd ∠AOB.", "o": ["80°", "90°", "100°", "40°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ ACF ∠CAF = - - = 180 ° 50 ° 30 ° 100 ° = ∠ACF + ∠CFA …. z (exterior angle property) = + = 50 ° 30 ° 80 ° = = … z x⁸0 ° (alternate segment theorem) = - - ∠ACF …."},
+{"id": "P1057", "q": "ABC is an equilateral triangle. P , Q and R are the mid-points of sides AB, BC and CA, respectively. If the length of the side of the triangle ABC is 11 cm, then the area (in cm 2 ) of PQR is: ∆", "o": ["21³ 16¹1³ 16", "121³ 16¹11³ 16"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "is an equilateral triangle. ∆ ABC Area of = area of ∆ PQR 1⁴ × ∆ ABC Area of = × × 11 × 11 ∆ PQR 1⁴ 3⁴ = 121³ 16 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1058", "q": "P and Q are two fixed points 10 cm apart, and R is a point on PQ such that PR = 6 cm. By what percentage is the length of QR decreased when the length of PR is increased by 5% ?", "o": ["8.5%", "7.5%", "7%", "8%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length PR : QR → Initial 6 : 4 → +5% ↓ Final 6.30 then QR = 3.7 → Decreased % = × 100⁴ − 3 . 7⁴ = 0.30 × 25 = 7.5 %"},
+{"id": "P1059", "q": "Two circles, centred at P and Q intersect at two points C and D. AB is tangent to the two circles at A and B. If ∠ADB = 68°, then ∠ACB = ______. Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["132°", "112°", "124°", "102°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ ACD = … (i)… (alternate segment ∠ BAC ∠ ADC theorem) In ∆ BCD = … (ii)… (alternate segment ∠ ABC ∠ BDC theorem) + = - … (iii) ∠ BAC ∠ ABC 180 ° ∠ ACB On adding (i) and (ii) we get, + = + ∠ BAC ∠ ABC ∠ ADC ∠ BDC - = … [from(iii)]¹80 ° ∠ ACB 68 ° = - = ∠ ACB 180 ° 68 ° 112 °"},
+{"id": "P1060", "q": "If arcs PAQ and RBS of a circle are congruent, then find the ratio of PQ and RS.", "o": ["2 : 3", "1 : 3", "1 : 1", "1 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Arcs PAQ and RBS are congruent, then PQ = RS So, Ratio of PQ and RS = 1 : 1"},
+{"id": "P1061", "q": "If we extend a chord infinitely on both sides, then the chord becomes a _________.", "o": ["diameter", "tangent", "secant", "normal"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If we extend a chord infinitely on both sides, then the chord becomes a secant."},
+{"id": "P1062", "q": "Triangle XYZ is an isosceles Search on TG: @apna_pdf triangle with sides XY = XZ. If the measure of angle Y is 80°, what is the measure of angle X ?", "o": ["30°", "40°", "20°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In XYZ is an isosceles ∆ triangle with side XY = XZ. ∴ ∠Y and ∠Z = 80° In XYZ, ∆ ∠X + ∠Y + ∠Z = 180° ⇒ ∠X = 180° - 80° - 80° ∠X = 20° ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1063", "q": "PQ is the diameter of a circle with centre A. M is a point on the circumference of the circle. If m∠MAP = 110°, then find the value of m∠MQA.", "o": ["55°", "35°", "65°", "70°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here , ∠ MAQ = 180° - 110° = 70° Now in , ∠M = ∠ Q = x (AM = AQ ∆ MAQ = Radius ) ∠ A + ∠M + ∠Q = 180° ⇒ 70° + 2x = 180° x = 55° ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1064", "q": "Let C be a circle with centre O and PQ be a minor arc on C. Let R and S be two points on the major arc of PQ on C. If PQ subtends an angle 80° at O, find ∠PRQ and ∠PSQ, respectively.", "o": ["40° and 60°", "50° and 80°", "40° and 40°", "40° and 50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that the angle made by the chord on the circumference is half to the angle made by the on the center of the circle ."},
+{"id": "P1065", "q": "In ΔABC, AB = 6 cm, BC = 9 cm and AC = 12 cm. If AD is the angle bisector of ∠BAC, where D is a point on BC, then find DC.", "o": ["9", "6", "3", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= … (angle bisector theorem) AB BD AC DC = = 6 BD 12 DC ⇒ DC BD 4² BC (6 unit) = 9 cm DC (4 unit) = × 4 = 6 cm 9⁶"},
+{"id": "P1066", "q": "If the lengths of two sides of an isosceles triangle are 6 cm and 12 cm, then find the length of the third side.", "o": ["8 cm", "6 cm", "12 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In triangle, Third side < 18 (12 + 6) Third side > 6 (12 - 6) For isosceles triangle side must be equal to 12 or 6 cm but third side should be greater than 6 cm."},
+{"id": "P1067", "q": "The side BC of ΔABC is produced to a point D. If AC = BC and ∠BAC = 70°, then find the value of ∠ACD − ∠ABC.", "o": ["70°", "60°", "75°", "45°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠BAC = ∠ABC = … (angle opposite to 70 ° equal side) ∠ACD = ∠ABC + ∠BAC … (exterior angle property) ∠ACD - ∠ABC = ∠BAC ∠ACD - ∠ABC = 70 °"},
+{"id": "P1068", "q": "In the figure shown above, quadrilateral PQRS has its vertices on the circumference of the circle with centre O. If m∠QOS = 20x° and m∠QRS = 26x°, then what is the value of ‘x’ ?", "o": ["6", "5", "4", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠QPS = ∠QOS = 10¹ 2 × x ° Now, ∠QPS + ∠QRS = … (opposite angles 180 ° of cyclic quadrilateral)¹0 + 26 = = = 5 x ° x ° 180 ° ⇒ x¹80 ° 36 °"},
+{"id": "P1069", "q": "ABC is a right-angled triangle △ with ∠ABC = 90°. If m( ) = 28 cm, and AB m( ) = 96 cm, find the area (in cm²) of BC the circumcircle of ABC. (Use π = 3.14.) △", "o": ["7,850", "8,164", "7,693", "7,536"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AC = = A B² + B C² 2⁸ 2 + 9⁶ 2 = = 100⁷84 + 9216 Circumradius = = Hypotenuse 2¹00² = 50 cm Area of circumcircle = 50⁵0 π × × = 3.14²500 = 7850 × c m²"},
+{"id": "P1070", "q": "The side BC of ΔABC is produced to a point D. If AC = BC and ∠BAC = 70°, then find the value of 2.5∠ACD − 1.5∠ABC.", "o": ["245°", "235°", "225°", "230°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ ABC ∠A + ∠B + ∠C = 180 ° ∠ACD = ∠A + ∠B … (exterior angle property) ∠ACD = 140 ° now, 2.5 ∠ACD - 1.5 ∠ABC × 2.5 × 140° - 1.5° × 70° = 350° - 105°= 245°"},
+{"id": "P1071", "q": "Two circles touch each other at a point O. AB is a simple common tangent to both the circles touching at point A and point B. If radii of the circles are 9 cm and 4 cm, then find AB.", "o": ["72 cm", "12 cm", "24 cm", "144 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of tangent AB = 2 = 2 r¹ r² 4 × 9 = 12 cm"},
+{"id": "P1072", "q": "In a triangle ABC, AB = 6 units, BC = 8 units and AC = 10 units. Let M be a point on AC such that BM = 5 units. With a point D, a triangle BMD is formed and the triangle BMD is similar to the triangle ABC with = What is the length BM AB BD AC of BD in units ?", "o": ["40", "3", "10", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, = = BD = units BM AB BD AC ⇒ 5⁶ BD 10 ⇒ 25³"},
+{"id": "P1073", "q": "Diagonals of a trapezium ABCD with AB∥DC, intersect each other at the point ‘O’. If AB = 2.5 CD, find the ratio of the area of triangle AOB to the area of triangle COD.", "o": ["16 : 1", "25 : 4", "9 : 2", "5 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the trapezium ABCD = ar ∆ AOB ar ∆ DOC A B² D C² = = = ar ∆ AOB ar ∆ DOC ( 2 . 5 )² ( 1 )² ( 5² )² ( 1 )²²5⁴ Hence, required ratio = 25 : 4"},
+{"id": "P1074", "q": "The areas of two similar triangles ΔPQR and ΔXYZ are 12.96 cm 2 and 635.04 cm 2 , respectively. If QR = 2.9 cm, then the length (in cm) of YZ equals:", "o": ["23.2", "25.2", "30.4", "20.3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ΔPQR ~ ΔXYZ The ratio of the area of two similar triangles is equal to the square of the ratio of any pair of the corresponding sides of the similar triangles. Then, = ( )² ar Δ PQR ar Δ XYZ QR YZ = ( )² ⇒ = ( )²¹2 . 96⁶35 . 04² . 9 YZ 1 . 44⁷0 . 56² . 9 YZ = ⇒ = 1 . 44⁷0 . 56² . 9 YZ 1 . 2⁸ . 4² . 9 YZ = ⇒ = 20.3¹ 7² ."},
+{"id": "P1075", "q": "If Δ ABC ~ Δ QRP; area of Δ ABC : area of Δ PQR = 9 : 4; AB = 18 cm and BC = 15 cm, then find the length of PR.", "o": ["15 cm", "12 cm", "10 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= ( )² area of ∆ ABC area of ∆ QRP BC RP = ⇒ = ⇒ PR = 10 cm 9⁴ BC RP 15 RP 3²"},
+{"id": "P1076", "q": "In ΔEFG, XY ∥ FG, area of the quadrilateral XFGY = 44 m² . If EX : XF = 2 : 3, then find the area of ΔEXY (in m² ).", "o": ["7.28", "8.10", "8.38", "9.46"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= ( )² = area of ∆ EXY area of ∆ EFG 2 ( 2 + 3 )⁴²5 Area of quadrilateral XFGY= 25- 4 = 21 units 21 units = 44 m² (area of EXY)² units = × 4 = 8.38 m² ∆ 44²1"},
+{"id": "P1077", "q": "In a right-angled triangle ABC such that ∠BAC = 90° and AD is perpendicular to BC. If the area of ΔABC is 63 cm 2 , area of ΔACD = 7 cm 2 , and AC = 5 cm, then the length of BC is equal to:", "o": ["10 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm", "15 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= ( )² [∵ ACB DCA] area of ∆ ACB area of ∆ DCA BC AC ∆ ∼∆ = ⇒ = ⇒ BC = 15 cm 63⁷ BC 5⁹ BC 5"},
+{"id": "P1078", "q": "PQ is parallel to SR in a trapezium PQRS. It is given that PQ > SR and the diagonals PR and QS intersect at O. If PO = 3 x − 15, OQ = x + 9, OR = x − 5 and OS = 5 and x has two values x¹ and x² , then the value of ( 1² - 2² ) is: x x", "o": ["15", "11", "13", "19"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Concept used : - = PO OR QO OS = 3 x − 15 x − 5 x + 9⁵ 15 - 75 = 2 + 9 - 5 - 45 x x x x² - 11 + 30 = 0 x x² - 6 - 5 + 30 = 0 x x x ( - 6) - 5( - 6) = 0 x x x ( - 5)( - 6) x x = 5, = 6 x x Now, the value of ( 1² - 2² ) = ( 2 - 2 ) x x⁶ 5 = 36 - 25 = 11"},
+{"id": "P1079", "q": "If the perimeters of two similar triangles are in the ratio of 4 : 7, and the sum of the areas is 195 cm 2 , then what is of the difference between the areas 1³ (in cm 2 ) of the two triangles?", "o": ["99", "33", "63", "54"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "concept :- in similar triangles the ratio of their area is equal to square of their corresponding sides or perimeters Perimeter ratio of similar triangles = 4 : 7 So their area ratio = 16 : 49 Sum of areas = (16 + 49) sq . unit = 65 sq . unit According to the question, 65 sq . unit = 195 sq . cm 1 sq . unit = 3 sq ."},
+{"id": "P1080", "q": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle, AE is the diameter and ∠AOC = 100°. The value of ∠CDE + ∠CEA is:", "o": ["90°", "60°", "80°", "100°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept used : - The angle made by an arc at the center is twice the angle made by the same arc at the circumference. So, ∠CEA = ∠ADC = = 50° 100² ∠ADE = 90° (In a semicircle, any angle formed by a diameter is always 90°) ∠CDE = ∠ADE - ∠ADC = 90° - 50° = 40° ∠CDE + ∠CEA = 40° + 50° = 90°"},
+{"id": "P1081", "q": "There is a circle with a centre T and a radius of 8 cm. Two tangents KE and KI are drawn from point K, which is 17 cm from the centre. The area of the quadrilateral TEKI is: Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["127.5 sq .cm", "130 sq .cm", "136 sq .cm", "120 sq .cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "the angle between the radius and the tangent will always be exactly 90° = ⇒ = 289 - 64 ( KE )² ( 17 )² − ( 8 )² ( KE )² = 225 ⇒ KE = 15 cm ( KE )² Area of KET = × 15 × 8 = 60 sq .cm ∆ 1² Area of KIT = area of KET (both ∆ ∆ triangle are congruent) So the Area of quadrilateral TEKI = 60 × 2 = 120 sq .cm"},
+{"id": "P1082", "q": "ABC is a right-angled triangle ∆ where m∠ABC = 90°. If m( ) = 15 cm, AB m( ) = 20 cm, and , BC BD ⊥ AC intersecting at the point D, find m( ) AC BD (in cm).", "o": ["9", "12", "12.5", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By pythagorean : - AC = ( 15 )² + ( 20 )² AC = ⇒ AC = 25 cm 225 + 400 Property of right angle :- ∆ AB × BC = BD × AC 15 × 20 = BD × 25 ⇒ BD = 12 cm"},
+{"id": "P1083", "q": "In right triangle ABC with right angle at C, M is the mid - point of hypotenuse AB. C is joined to M and produced to a point D, such that DM = CM. Point D is joined to B. If CD = 10 cm, and BD = 6 cm, find the value of CM.", "o": ["11.4 cm", "5 cm", "9.5 cm", "8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CM = = 5 cm 10²"},
+{"id": "P1084", "q": "In a circle, O is the centre and AOB is the diameter. AT is a tangent to the circle. Line TB intersects the circle at Q . Given that ∠AOQ = 94°, fi nd ∠ATQ .", "o": ["133°", "43°", "86°", "47°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠AQB = 90° (angle subtended by a diameter on any point of a circle is always 90°) So, ∠TQA = 90° ∠OAQ = = 43° 180° − 94° 2 ∠QAT = 90° - 43° = 47° In TQA, ∆ ∠QTA = 180° - (90° + 47°) ∠QTA = 180° - 137° = 43° Required angle(∠ATQ) = 43°"},
+{"id": "P1085", "q": "AB is parallel to DC in a trapezium ABCD. It is given that AB > DC and the diagonals AC and BD intersect at O. If AO = 3 - 15, OB = + 9, OC = - 5 and OD = x x x⁵, and has two values and , then x x¹ x² the value of ( ² + 2 ) is: x¹ x²", "o": ["45", "56", "61", "73"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In trapezium ABCD, The diagonals of a trapezium divide each other proportionally, = = ⇒ AO OC OB OD ⇒ 3 x − 15 x − 5 x + 9⁵ 15 - 75 = + 9 - 5 - 45 ⇒ x x² x x + 4 - 15 + 75 - 45 = 0 ⇒ x² x x -11 + 30 = 0 ……(i) ⇒ x² x On solving the eqn."},
