+{"id": "P1087", "q": "The hypotenuse of a right triangle is 6m more than twice the shortest side. If the third side is 2 m less than the hypotenuse, find the area(in m² ) of the triangle.", "o": ["110", "100", "120", "130"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Smallest side = x Then, hypotenuse = 2 + 6 x And, third side = 2 + 4 x Take = 10 m x Then, sides of right angle triangle = 10 , 24 and 26 m ( pythagorean triplet) So, area of triangle = × 10 × 24 = 120 m¹ 2"},
+{"id": "P1088", "q": "Let C be a circle with center O and PQ be the diameter of C. Let AB be a chord on C. If ∠QOB = 40°, ∠AOP = 80°, then find ∠AOB.", "o": ["70°", "90°", "100°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "+ + = ∠ POA ∠ AOB ∠ QOB 18⁰ ° + + = ⇒ = 8⁰ ° ∠ AOB 4⁰ ° 18⁰ ° ∠ AOB 6⁰ °"},
+{"id": "P1089", "q": "From an external point A, tangents AP and AQ are drawn to a circle with centre O. If ∠ APQ = 40°, then find ∠ POQ .", "o": ["110°", "100°", "60°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Theorem : Tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal. As we know, PAQ + POQ = 180° ∠ ∠ POQ = 180° - 100° = 80° ∠"},
+{"id": "P1090", "q": "The secant CD intersects the circle at E and CF is tangent to the circle at F. If the length of the secant CD is equal to 20 cm and the length of tangent CF is 15 cm, find the length of the chord DE.", "o": ["3.75 cm", "11.25 cm", "9.25 cm", "8.75 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CF 2 = CD CE × 15² = 20 CE × CE = = 11.25²25²0 Hence, DE = 20 - 11.25 = 8.75 cm"},
+{"id": "P1091", "q": "If the vertical angle of an isosceles triangle is 42°, then the measure of the other two angles will be: Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["59° and 59°", "79° and 79°", "89°and 89°", "69° and 69°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that: An isosceles triangle has two equal angles. And sum of three angles of a triangle = 180° Let each of the other two angles = x°."},
+{"id": "P1092", "q": "ΔABC is inscribed in a circle with centre O. If AB = 35 cm, BC = 12 cm and AC = 37 cm, then what is the circumradius of a triangle ? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["13.5 cm", "16.5 cm", "18.5 cm", "14.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumradius of the triangle = = = 18.5 cm ℎypotenuse 2³7²"},
+{"id": "P1093", "q": "In a parallelogram ABCD, if vertices are in respective order and diagonals AC and BD intersect at O, then which of the following is NOT always correct ? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["ΑΟΒ ≅ COD", "AOD ≅ COD ∆ ∆ ∆ ∆", "ΔABC ≅ ADC", "ВОС ≅ AOD ∆ ∆ ∆"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Option (a) ΑΟΒ ≅ COD ∆ ∆ In ΑΟΒ and COD, AB ॥ CD ∆ ∆ ∠BAO = ∠DCO (alternate interior angle) ∠ABO = ∠CDO (alternate interior angle) ∠AOB = ∠COD (vertically opposite angle) So, ΑΟΒ ≅ COD (true) ∆ ∆ Similarly, Option (c) ΔABC ≅ ADC (true) ∆ Option (d) ВОС ≅ AOD (true) ∆ ∆ But, Option (b) AOD ≅ COD (false) ∆ ∆ Both triangles angles are not equal to each other because AD does not pa"},
+{"id": "P1094", "q": "In ΔABC, D is the mid-point of BC and G is the centroid. If GD = 10 cm, then the length of AD is _______ . Higher Secondary 24/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["20 cm", "10 cm", "15 cm", "30 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know Centroid divides the median in 2 : 1. GD = 1 → 10 AG = 10² = 20 × AD = AG + GD = 20 + 10 = 30 cm"},
+{"id": "P1095", "q": "In a triangle ABC, P is the midpoint of BC. If AB = (2 + 4) cm, AC = x⁶ cm and AP ⟂ BC, then the value of is: x Higher Secondary 24/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["3", "4", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given P is the mid point of BC BP = PC ⇒ We know In an equilateral triangle, AP ⟂ BC if and only if P is the mid point of BC. Hence, ABC is an equilateral triangle."},
+{"id": "P1096", "q": "ΔABC and ΔABD are on a common base AB and AC = BD and BC = AD as shown in the given figure. Which of the following options is true ? Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["There are no congruent triangles in the given figure", "ΔABC ≅ ΔABD", "ΔABC ≅ ΔBAD", "ΔABC ≅ ΔADB"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, AC = BD BC = AD ⇒ AB is common. Hence, by SSS rule Both triangles ΔABC and ΔBAD are congruent. ΔABC ≅ ΔBAD ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1097", "q": "In an isosceles ΔLMN, LM = LN, and ∠MLN = 37°. Find ∠MNL. Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["70.0°", "65.0°", "71.5°", "60.5°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since LM = LN ∠LMN = ∠LNM = x (say) ⇒ And ∠L + ∠M + ∠N = 180 ° 37 + x + x = 180 ⇒ ° 2x = 180 - 37 = 143 ⇒ ° ° ° x = = 71.5° ⇒ 143° 2"},
+{"id": "P1098", "q": "If x² -1, 2x and x² + 1 are the three sides of a right angled triangle, then which of the following can be its hypotenuse ? Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["x² + 1", "x²", "2x", "x² - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, + = P² B² H² -1 + 2x = ( x² )² ( )² ( x² + 1 )² + 1 - 2 + = x⁴ x² 4 x² ( x² + 1 )² + 2 + 1 = x⁴ x² ( x² + 1 )² = ( x² + 1 )² ( x² + 1 )² LHS = RHS So, hypotenuse = 2 + 1 x"},
+{"id": "P1099", "q": "PQ is a diameter of a circle and PS is a chord. If PQ is 82 cm and PS is 80 cm, the distance (in cm) of PS from the center of the circle is: Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["18", "9", "39", "24"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept used : The perpendicular distance from centre of circle to the chord bisects the chord. In OPM, we have ; △ OM = = 4¹ 2 − 4⁰ 2¹681 − 1600 = = 9 cm 81"},
+{"id": "P1100", "q": "If the angles of a triangle are in the ratio of 9 ∶ 11 ∶ 16, then the difference between the greatest angle and the smallest angle is : Graduate Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["30°", "25°", "40°", "35°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, sum of the angle of triangle is 180° 9+11+16 = 36 unit → 180° Then, (16 - 9) = 7 unit → × 7 = 35° 180° 36"},
+{"id": "P1101", "q": "In ΔABC and ΔPQR, AB = 7 m, BC = 8 m, AC = 9 m, PQ = 7 m, QR = 8 m and PR = 9 m. Which of the following is true for these triangles ? Graduate Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["ΔCBA ≅ Δ PQR", "ΔABC ≅ Δ PQR", "ΔABC ≅ Δ RQP", "ΔABC ≅ ΔQRP"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ABC and ΔPQR, △ AB = PQ = 7 cm BC = QR = 8 cm AC = PR = 9 cm Then, ΔABC ≅ Δ PQR (by SSS rule)"},
+{"id": "P1102", "q": "Select the correct statement about the properties of a triangle. Graduate Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["The sum of two sides is always greater than the third side.", "The sum of two sides may be equal to the third side.", "The sum of two sides is always equal to the third side.", "The sum of two sides is always less than the third side."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the triangle the sum of two sides is always greater than the third side."},
+{"id": "P1103", "q": "ΔPQR and ΔABC are two congruent triangles. If the area of ΔPQR is 225 cm 2 , then the area of ΔABC is: Graduate Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["15 cm 2", "112.5 cm 2", "25 cm 2", "225 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of two congruent triangles are always equal. Hence, Area of ΔPQR = Area of ΔABC = 225 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1104", "q": "If three angles of a triangle are (18 + 6°), (10 + 30°) and (15 + 15°), x x x then the triangle is: Graduate Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["scalene", "equilateral", "isosceles", "right angled"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, Sum of the angle of triangle = 180° (18 + 6°) + (10 + 30°) + (15 + 15°) x x x = 180° 43 + 51° = 180° x⁴3 = 129 = 3 x ⇒ x So, 18 + 6° = 18 × 3 + 6 = 60°, 10 + 30° x x = 10 × 3 + 30 = 60°, 15 + 15° = 15 × 3 + x¹5 = 60° Therefore, the triangle is equilateral ."},
+{"id": "P1105", "q": "ΔXYZ is an isosceles triangle such that XY = XZ. It is given that YS ⊥ XZ and ZT ⊥ XY. What is the relation between YS and ZT ? Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["YS > ZT", "YS = 2 ZT", "YS < ZT", "YS = ZT"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, we have given triangle Search on TG: @apna_pdf XYZ = XZY = (angles opposite to ∠ ∠ θ equal side) In TYZ, TZY = 90° - △ ∠ θ In SYZ, SYZ = 90° - △ ∠ θ TZA = SYZ ⇒ ∠ ∠ Now, In TYZ and SZY, we have ; △ △ TYZ = SZY ∠ ∠ YZ = YZ (common) TZA = SYZ ∠ ∠ So, TYZ ≅ SZY (By ASA rule) △ △ Then, ZT = YS"},
+{"id": "P1106", "q": "In ΔABC, AB = 9 cm and AC = 13 cm, then the length of BC could be: Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["4 cm", "2 cm", "22 cm", "20 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the ABC, ∆ As we know, AC + AB > BC > AC - AB 13 + 9 > BC > 13 - 9²2 > BC > 4 From the above option, we get BC = 20 cm"},
+{"id": "P1107", "q": "In the following figure, ∠A = ∠P and AC = PR. Which of the following options needs to be satisfied for Δ PQR and Δ ABC to be congruent ? Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["BC = QR by ASS criteria", "AB = PQ by SAS criteria", "BC = QR by SSA criteria", "AB = PQ by SSA criteria SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the given option, option (b) is the correct one. As in ΔPQR and ΔABC, ∠A = ∠P (given) AC = PR (given) AB = PQ Then, ΔPQR ≅ ΔABC (by SAS rule)"},
+{"id": "P1108", "q": "In ABC, the internal bisectors of ∆ ∠ABC and ∠ACB meet at X and ∠BAC = Search on TG: @apna_pdf 30°. The measure of ∠BXC is:", "o": ["120°", "115°", "105°", "150°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that :- ∠BXC = 90° + = 90° + 15° = 105° ∠ BAC 2"},
+{"id": "P1109", "q": "Chords and of a circle AB CD intersect inside the circle at point F. If m( ) = 2.4 cm, m( ) = 1.8 cm, and m( ) AF BF CD = 5.7 cm, what is the length (in cm) of the longer of the two line segments, and CF ? DF", "o": ["4.5", "4.8", "5.4", "3.6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AF × BF = CF × DF 2.4 × 1.8 = × x⁵ . 7 − x ( )⁴.8 × 0.9 = × x⁵ . 7 − x ( )⁰.9 × = × 5 . 7 − 0 . 9 ( ) x⁵ . 7 − x ( ) Longest of two line segments = 4.8 cm"},
+{"id": "P1110", "q": "The lengths of two parallel chords of a circle are 10 cm and 24 cm lie on the opposite sides of the centre. If the smaller chord is 12 cm from the centre, what is the distance (in cm) between the Search on TG: @apna_pdf two chords ?", "o": ["13", "5", "17", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pythagorean triplets :- (5, 12, 13) Distance between the chords = 12 + 5 = 17 cm"},
+{"id": "P1111", "q": "Let A, B, C be the mid-points of sides PQ, QR and PR, respectively, of ∆ PQR. If the area of PQR is 32cm², then ∆ find the area ( in cm² ) of ABC . ∆", "o": ["24", "16", "32", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Theorem : Area of the Triangle formed by Joining the Middle Points of the Sides of a Triangle is Equal to One-fourth Area of the given Triangle."},
+{"id": "P1112", "q": "In a triangle MNO, XA, XB and XC are perpendicular bisectors on sides MN, ON and OM respectively intersect each other at X. If = 55 degree, then ∠ NMO what is the value of ∠NXO?", "o": ["130°", "110°", "95°", "125°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All perpendicular bisectors of a triangle concur at one point called circumcenter as a center of its circumscribing circle."},
+{"id": "P1113", "q": "If △ABC is right angled at B, AB = 12 cm and ∠CAB = 60°, determine the Search on TG: @apna_pdf length of BC.", "o": ["24 cm", "12 cm 3", "12 cm", "12 cm 2³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Angle 30° : 60° : 90° → Side 1 : : 2 → 3 According to the questions , 1 unit = 12 cm units = 12 cm 3³"},
+{"id": "P1114", "q": "ABCD is a square and △MAB is an equilateral triangle. MC and MD are joined. What is the degree measure of ∠MDC ? Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["78°", "60°", "65\"", "75°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ABCD is a square and △MAB is an equilateral triangle. Then, AB = MB = AM = AD = CD = BC So, ∠ADM +∠AMD + ∠MAD = 180° 2x + (90 + 60)° = 180° ⇒ 2x = 180° - 150° 2x = 30° x = 15° ⇒ ⇒ ⇒ So, ∠MDC = 90 - 15 = 75°"},
+{"id": "P1115", "q": "If two tangents to a circle of Search on TG: @apna_pdf radius 3 cm are inclined to each other at angle of 60°, then the length of each tangent is:", "o": ["cm", "3 cm 3³ 4³", "3 cm", "6 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AOC ≅ BOC (by RHS) △ △ In AOC , we have: △ Tan30° = = AO AC 3 AC ⇒ = ⇒ AC = 3 cm 1³ 3 AC 3 So,the length of each tangent = 3 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1116", "q": "In a Δ ABC D , E and F are the mid-points of side BC, CA and AB respectively. If BC = 14.4 cm. CA = 15.2 Search on TG: @apna_pdf cm and AB = 12.4 cm, what is the perimeter of the Δ DEF ?", "o": ["42", "28", "21", "35"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ΔABC BC = 14.4 cm , CA = 15.2 cm and AB = 12.4 cm As we know D,E,F are mid points of sides of triangle So perimeter of DEF is half of ∆ perimeter of ABC ∆ And Also FE॥ BC , FD॥ AC , DE AB ॥ = = 21 cm 14 . 4 + 15 . 2 + 12 ."},
+{"id": "P1117", "q": "In a circle with centre O and radius 13 cm, and two parallel chords are drawn on different sides of the centre.If the length of one chord 10cm and the distance between two chords is 17cm, then find the difference in length of the two chords (in cm)", "o": ["10", "14", "24", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here we have to use pythagoras triplet of (5, 12, 13) in both the right angle triangle In OQD it is right angle at Q ∆ ……(perpendicular from center divides chord in two equal parts ) QD = × CD QD = × 24 = 12 cm 1² ⇒ 1² So by pythagoras triplet of (5, 12, 13) OQ = 5 cm Now OP = PQ – OQ = 17 – 5 = 12cm Now in OBP by pythagoras triplet of (5, ∆ 12, 13) Two sides are 12 and 13 so"},
+{"id": "P1118", "q": "In triangle ABC, D is a point on BC such that BD: DC = 3: 4. E is a point on AD such that AE:ED = 2 : 3. Find the ratio of area (∆ ECD ): area (∆ AEB ).", "o": ["9 : 8", "1 : 2", "2 : 1", "8 : 9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= (triangles with same Area of ADC Area of ABD 4 x³ x height)³x = 5 unit x = unit ⇒ ⇒ 5³ = 4x = 4 = unit Area of ADC × 5³ 20³ = (Triangles with the Area of ACE Area of ECD 2 y³ y same base) ⇒ 5 y = unit 20³ = 3y = 4 unit Area of ECD = = 2 : 1 Area of ECD Area of ABE 4²"},
+{"id": "P1119", "q": "In ABC, D is a point on BC such ∆ that ∠BAD = ∠ADC and ∠BAC = 77° 1² and ∠C = 45°, What is the measure of ∠ADB? Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["64°", "77°", "45°", "58°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ∠BAD = , ∠ADC = 2 θ θ ∠C = 45°, ∠BAC = 77° ∠ABC = 180° - 77° - 45° = 58° 58° + = 2 (By external angle theorem) θ θ = 58°, ∠ADB = 180° - 116° = 64° θ"},
+{"id": "P1120", "q": "The three medians RQ, SP and TN of intersect at point O. If the area of ∆ RST is 48 , then the area of ∆ RST cm 2 Search on TG: @apna_pdf quadrilateral SQON is: (in ) cm 2", "o": ["20", "12", "16", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Median divides a triangle into 6 equal triangles. 6 unit = 48² unit = 16 ⇒ area of quadrilateral SQON = 16 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1121", "q": "In △KLM, NO || LM and intersects KL and KM at N and O If KN = 2, NL= 4, and KO = 3, find OM.", "o": ["6", "4.5", "3", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since NO || LM, KLM KNO ∆ ∼ ∆ (both triangles are proportional)"},
+{"id": "P1122", "q": "If two complementary angles are in the ratio 2 : 7, find the angles", "o": ["10°, 80°", "20°, 70°", "40°, 50°", "35°, 55°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of two complementary angles = 90° Ratio 2 : 7 ⇒ Total parts = 9¹ st angle = × 2 = 20 o⁹0⁹ 2 nd angle = × 7 =70 o⁹0⁹"},
+{"id": "P1123", "q": "From an external point X, two tangents XY and XZ touch a circle at points Y and Z respectively. What is the relationship between the lengths XY and XZ? Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["XY > XZ", "XY < XZ", "XY = XZ", "They form curved paths"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From an external point, the two tangents drawn to a circle are always equal in length because the tangents from a common external point to a circle are congruent."},
+{"id": "P1124", "q": "A quadrilateral PQRS is inscribed around a circle. If PQ=12 cm, QR=14 cm, and the perimeter of the quadrilateral is 42 cm, what is the length of side RS? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["8 cm", "9 cm", "10 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of length of opposite sides are equal PQ + RS = QR + SP…..(i) Given, PQ = 12 cm , QR = 14 cm A/Q, PQ + QR + RS + SP = 42²6 + RS + SP = 42 RS + SP = 16…..(ii) From eq . (i) QR - PQ = RS - SP 2 = RS - SP….(iii) Add eq ."},
+{"id": "P1125", "q": "Tangents AB and AC are drawn to a circle from a point A, such that, ∠BAC = 40°. A chord CP is drawn parallel to BA. The measure of ∠CBP is: Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["55°", "45°", "35°", "40°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AB = AC …..(tangent to the circle) ∠ABC = ∠ACB ∠ABC + ∠ACB + ∠BAC = 180° 2∠ABC + 40° = 180° ∠ABC = 70° ⇒ It is given that CP∥BA and BC is a transversal. Alternate interior angles are equal, therefore: ∠BCP = ∠ABC = 70° The angle formed between a tangent and a chord is equal to the angle formed in the alternate segment of the circle."},
+{"id": "P1126", "q": "There are two circles with radii of 7 cm and 4 cm are positioned so that they touch each other internally. What is the distance between their centers? Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1 cm", "3 cm", "6 cm", "7 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "So, Required difference = 7 - 4 = 3 cm"},
+{"id": "P1127", "q": "In a given circle, if AB is the diameter, the value of 3x is: Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["194°", "191°", "186°", "148°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Straight angle AOB, ∠ROB = 180° - 56° = 124° ⇒ In ROB, ∆ ∠R + ∠B + 124° = 180° ⇒ 2∠B = 56° [∵ ∠R = ∠B] ⇒ ∠B = 28° ⇒ In TAB, ∆ + 28° + 90° = 180° = 62° ⇒ x ⇒ x So, the angle 3 = 186° x"},
+{"id": "P1128", "q": "Two chords PQ and RS of a circle with centre O intersect each other at X. ∠PXR = 85° and ∠POS = 120°. ∠QOR is : Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["70°", "95°", "110°", "125°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that, ∠SRP = = = 60° = ∠R ⇒ ∠ SOP 2¹20° 2 In PXR, ∆ ∠P + ∠X + ∠R = 180° ⇒ ∠P + 85° + 60° = 180° ⇒ ∠P = 35° = ∠QPR ⇒ Now, ∠QOR = 2 ×∠QPR = 2 × 35° = 70°"},
+{"id": "P1129", "q": "A circle has two chords, PQ and RS, which are of equal length, subtend angles of x° and y° respectively at the center. Which of the following is true? Higher Secondary 26/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["x > y", "x < y", "x = y", "x + y = 180°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "I n POQ , and ROS ∆ ∆ PQ = RS ..(Given ) OR = OQ ….(Radius ) OS = OP …(Radius) ∴ POQ ≃ ROS ∆ ∆ Hence = ∠y ∠ x"},
+{"id": "P1130", "q": "Two circles intersect at points M and . A line through meets the first N M circle again at and the second circle A again at . Another line through meets B N the first circle again at and the second C circle again at D. if = 55 o and ∠ CAM = 75 o , find the value of ∠ MBD . ∠ MNC + ∠ MND Higher Secondary 24/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["50°", "65°", "130°", "20°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CAMN is a cyclic quadrilateral ∠CAM = ∠MND -----(i) MNBD is a cyclic quadrilateral ∠DBM = ∠MNC -----(ii) Adding the eq (i) & (ii) ∠CAM + ∠DBM = ∠MND + ∠MNC 55 o + 75 o = ∠MND + ∠MNC ∠MND + ∠MNC = 130 o"},
+{"id": "P1131", "q": "A chord of length 24 cm is 7 cm away from the center. Find the radius. Matriculation Level 30/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["14 cm", "cm 193", "19 cm", "17 cm 17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TG: @ikunal_x By using pythagoras theorem r² = 12² + 7² r = r = cm 144 + 49 ⇒ 193"},
+{"id": "P1132", "q": "What is the longest chord of a circle called? Matriculation Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Radius", "Center", "Tangent", "Diameter"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The chord that passes through the center of the circle is the longest chord, and it is called the Diameter."},
+{"id": "P1133", "q": "From a point T, a tangent TP at TG: @ikunal_x point P, is drawn to a circle with centre O. A secant TQR (point Q is near to point T) is drawn from the point T. ΔPQR is inscribed into the circle by joining the points P, Q and R. Draw lines OQ and OR. If ∠PTQ is 27° and ∠ TPQ = 55°, what is the degree measure of ∠ROQ?", "o": ["86", "82", "98", "94"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ PTQ ∠PQR = + = … (exterior angle 55 ° 27 ° 82 ° property) ∠RPS = ∠PQR ∠RPS = 82 ° Now, ∠RPS + ∠RPQ + ∠QPT = … 180 ° (linear pair) + ∠RPQ + = 82 ° 55 ° 180 ° ∠RPQ = - = 180 ° 137 ° 43 ° Now, ∠ROQ = 2∠RPQ = 2 = × 43 ° 86 °"},
+{"id": "P1134", "q": "ABC is a right-angled triangle, right angled at A in such a way that AB = AC and the bisector of angle B intersects the side AC at D. DM is perpendicular to BC, intersecting BC at M. If AB = 12 cm and BC = 12 cm, then find the length of 2 side AD.", "o": ["12( + 2) cm", "12( - 1) cm 2²", "12( - 2) cm", "12( + 1) cm 2²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In DAB and DMB, ∆ ∆ ∠ABD = ∠MBD ∠BAD = ∠BMD = 90° BD = BD (common) So, DAB ≅ DMB by ASA ∆ ∆ AB = BM = 12 cm ⇒ Then, MC = BC - BM = (12 - 12) cm 2 Now, ∠MDC = 180° - (90° + 45°) = 45° So, MC = DM = (12 - 12) cm 2 As, DM = AD (by congruence) Hence, AD = (12 - 12) = 12( - 1) cm 2² Alternate method:- In this type of question we use direct property, The property is AB + AD = BC AD "},
+{"id": "P1135", "q": "‘O’ is a point in the interior of an equilateral triangle. The perpendicular distance from 'O' to the sides are √3 cm, TG: @ikunal_x²√3cm, 5√3 cm. The perimeter of the triangle is:", "o": ["48 cm", "32 cm", "24 cm", "64 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side (a) = 2³ ( ℎ 1 + ℎ 2 + ℎ 3 ) = = 16 cm 2³ ( 3 + 2³ + 5³ ) Perimeter of equilateral triangle = 3 × a = 48 cm"},
+{"id": "P1136", "q": "PA and PB are tangents to the circle and O is the centre of the circle. The radius is 5 cm and PO is 13 cm. If the area of the triangle PAB is M, then the value of is : M¹5 TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["24", "13", "24", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of PAB , M = PX ∆ 1² × AB × Let OX = a and PX = 13 - a Area of PAO = PA ∆ 1² × AO × = PO 1² × AX × 12 = 13 ⇒ 1² × 5 × 1² × AX × AX = ⇒ 60¹3 AB = 2 AX = × 120¹3 Use pythagoras theorem in AXO; ∆ OX 2 = OA 2 - AX 2 OX 2 = 5² - ( )² OX = ⇒ 60¹3 ⇒ 25¹3 PX = 13 - = = 25¹3¹69 − 25¹3¹44¹3 Area of PAB , ∆ TG: @ikunal_x M = 1² × 120¹3 × 144¹3 = M¹5¹ 15 × 1² × 1"},
+{"id": "P1137", "q": "In a circle with centre O, A diameter AB and a chord CD intersect each other at E, AC and AD are joined. If ∠BOC = 48° and ∠AOD = 100°, then what is the measure of ∠CEB ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["72°", "74°", "78°", "82°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∠BOC = 48 ° and ∠AOD = 100 ° ∠BAC = × ∠BOC 1² ∠BAC = × 48 = 24 ° 1² ∠ACE = × ∠AOD 1² ∠ACE = × 100 = 50 ° 1² ∠CEB = ∠BAC + ∠ACE (external opposite angle) = 24 ° + 50 ° = 74 °"},
+{"id": "P1138", "q": "A chord of a circle has a length of 10cm. The angle subtended by the chord at a point on the circumference is 30°. What is the distance from the center of the circle to the chord? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["5 cm", "3 cm", "5 cm", "3 cm 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TG: @ikunal_x In OPB, ∠ P = 90°, ∠O = 30° , ∆ ∴ ∠ B = 180° - (90° + 30°) = 60° Now, tan 60° = OP PB = OP = 5 cm ⇒ 3 OP 5 ⇒ 3"},
+{"id": "P1139", "q": "Two circles with radii r¹ = 14 cm and r² = 6 cm have their centers 40 cm apart. Find the length of the transverse common tangent between them.", "o": ["cm", "1200 cm 1200", "cm", "13 cm 1275"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: = 14 cm, = 6 cm, d = 40 cm r¹ r² For the transverse common tangent, the formula is: L = d² − ( r¹ + r² )² = 40² − ( 14 + 6 )² = cm ⇒ 1600 − 400¹200"},
+{"id": "P1140", "q": "A circle with radius touches 2 x another circle with radius externally. 4 x What is the length of a direct common tangent ?", "o": ["2", "3", "4", "3 x x x² x²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Direct common tangent = d² − ( r¹ − r² )² TG: @ikunal_x Direct common tangent = = = 4³6 x² − ( 2 x )²³2 x² x"},
+{"id": "P1141", "q": "Each side of a regular octagon is of the side of a regular hexagon. If 3⁴ the perimeter of the hexagon is 24 cm, what will be the perimeter of the octagon? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["18 cm", "20 cm", "24 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Side of the hexagon = = 4 cm 24⁶ Side of the octagon = × 4 = 3 cm 3⁴ Perimeter of the octagon = 8 × 3 = 24 cm"},
+{"id": "P1142", "q": "A right-angled triangle has a hypotenuse of 17 cm and one leg of 8 cm. A second right-angled triangle is similar to the first, and its hypotenuse is 51 cm. What is the area of the second triangle?", "o": ["390 cm²", "460 cm²", "260 cm²", "540 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As 8² + 15² = 17², the set (8, 15, 17) is a Pythagorean triplet Area 1 = × 8 × 15 = 60¹ 2 cm 2 Since the second triangle is similar and its hypotenuse is 51 cm, then the scale factor k = = 3⁵1¹7 Area 2 = Area 1 × = 60 × 9 = 540³ 2 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1143", "q": "A circle that has a radius of 17 TG: @ikunal_x centimeters, and there is a chord measuring 30 centimeters in length. What is the distance from the center of the circle to the chord ?", "o": ["6 centimeters", "8 centimeters", "10 centimeters", "12 centimeters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From Pythagoras’ theorem in triangle ∆ OAG. = + OA 2 OG 2 AG 2 = + 17² OG 2¹5² = = 8 cm OG 289 − 225"},
+{"id": "P1144", "q": "The sum of all interior angles of a¹8-sided polygon is:", "o": ["2880°", "3600°", "3060°", "3420°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of the interior angles = (n - 2) × 180° = (18 - 2) × 180° = 16 × 180° = 2880°"},
+{"id": "P1145", "q": "In triangle LMN, a line segment OP is drawn parallel to the side MN, with O on LM and P on LN. If LO = 4 cm, LM = 12 cm, and LP = 5 cm, find the length of PN.", "o": ["11 cm", "12 cm", "15 cm", "10 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, LM = LO + OM 12 = 4 + OM OM = 8 cm In LMN ∆ OP is parallel to MN By Thale’s Theorem = = LO OM LP PN ⇒ 4⁸ 5 PN = 10 cm PN"},
+{"id": "P1146", "q": "The sum of the measures of 8 interior angles of a⁹-sided polygon is 1,120°. What is the measure of the 9th exterior angle?", "o": ["60°", "20°", "40°", "80°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Sum of 9 interior angle = 180° × (9 - 2) ⇒ = 1260° Now, 9th interior angle = 1260° - 1120° ⇒ = 140° We know that, Exterior angle + interior angle = 180° ⇒ Exterior angle = 180° - 140° = 40° ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1147", "q": "In a triangle PQR, the sides are p, q, and r, and the area of the triangle is T. What is the radius of the inscribed circle (inradius)? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["T p + q + r² T p + q + r", "p + q + r² T T² ( p + q + r )"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know Area of a triangle in terms of in radius T = r × s Where s = is the semi-perimeter. p + q + r² T = r × s r = ⇒ T S r = = ⇒ T p + q + r² 2 T p + q + r"},
+{"id": "P1148", "q": "If the difference between the interior and exterior angles of a regular polygon is 60°, find the number of sides of the polygon.", "o": ["6", "9", "13", "11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let each interior angle = x° exterior angle = 180° − x°. According to the question, x − (180° − x) = 60° ⇒ 2x − 180° = 60° ⇒ 2x = 240° ⇒ x = 120° For a regular polygon, Exterior angle = 180° − 120° = 60° No."},
+{"id": "P1149", "q": "The measures of the interior angles of a pentagon are , + 5, + 10, y y y + 15, and + 20. What is the measure y y of the smallest angle?", "o": ["88°", "98°", "108°", "118°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of interior angles of a pentagon = (5 – 2) × 180 = 540° According to question, + ( + 5) + ( + y y y¹0) + ( + 15) + ( + 20) = 540 y y⁵ + 50 = 540 = 98 ⇒ y ⇒ y ∴ Smallest angle = = 98° y"},
+{"id": "P1150", "q": "A circle with a radius of 12 cm, and a chord makes a⁶0° angle at the center. What is the length of that chord ?", "o": ["6 cm", "12 cm", "12 cm", "12 cm 3²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": ""},
+{"id": "P1151", "q": "A sector of radius 7 cm has an area of 38.5 cm 2 . Find the angle of the sector.", "o": ["90°", "60°", "30°", "75°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector = × r² θ 360 π 38.5 = × × (7)² θ 360²2⁷ = = 90° θ 38 . 5 × 360¹54"},
+{"id": "P1152", "q": "In triangle PQR, ST is drawn parallel to QR, intersecting PQ and PR at S and T respectively. If PS = 5 cm, SQ = 15 cm, and PT = 4cm, find TR.", "o": ["14 cm", "16 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since ST ∥ QR, PST PQR ∆ ∼ ∆"},
+{"id": "P1153", "q": "If the angle subtended by arc AB at the center is 105°, what is the reflex angle made by this arc at the center?", "o": ["255°", "210°", "105°", "245°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Reflex Angle = 360 o −Angle at center = 360 o − 105° = 255°"},
+{"id": "P1154", "q": "The sum of the interior angles of a regular polygon is five times the sum of its exterior angles. Determine the number of diagonals in the polygon.", "o": ["63", "72", "54", "97"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question , (n - 2) × 180° = 5 × 360° ⇒ n - 2 = 5 × 2 n = 12 ⇒ ⇒ Number of diagonal in the polygon = = = 54 n ( n − 3 )²¹2 × 9²"},
+{"id": "P1155", "q": "A tangent is drawn to a circle with a radius of 8 cm. At the point of TG: @ikunal_x tangency, what is the angle between the tangent and the radius ?", "o": ["45°", "60°", "90°", "180°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required angle would be 90°"},
+{"id": "P1156", "q": "If in triangle PQR, DE || QR and = , and PE = 6 cm, then ER is: PD DQ 1²", "o": ["2.5 cm", "12 cm", "10 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using the Basic Proportionality Theorem (Thales theorem), ⇒ = ⇒ = ER = 12 cm PD DQ PE ER 1² 6 ER ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1157", "q": "A triangle has sides 5 cm, 12 cm, and 13 cm. What type of triangle is this? Matriculation Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Right-angled", "Obtuse", "Acute", "Equilateral"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(5, 12, 13) is a Pythagorean triple(5² + 12² = 13² ), therefore the triangle will be a right-angled triangle ."},
+{"id": "P1158", "q": "From a point P, a tangent is drawn to a circle with center O. The radius is 5 cm, and the distance from O to P is 13 cm. What is the length of the tangent? Matriculation Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["46 cm", "12 cm", "40 cm", "44 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pythagorean theorem in OPM ∆ = + ( OP )² ( OM )² ( PM )² = + ( 13 )² ( 5 )² ( PM )² = = 12 cm ( PM )¹69 − 25 TG: @ikunal_x"},
+{"id": "P1159", "q": "A triangle has angles 40°, 60°, and 80°. It is a/an ______. Matriculation Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Equilateral", "Right-angled", "Isosceles", "Scalene"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All three angles are different, so all three sides are different. Therefore, the triangle is a scalene triangle."},
+{"id": "P1160", "q": "How many tangents can be drawn at a specific point on a circle? Matriculation Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["infinitely many", "2", "1", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "There is exactly one tangent to a circle at a specific point on it."},
+{"id": "P1161", "q": "A tangent BC at point B of a circle with radius 8 cm meets a line through the center A at point C such that AC = 17 cm. What is the length of the tangent BC ? Matriculation Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["12", "15", "13", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ABC, ∆ = - = - ⇒ BC 2 AC 2 AB 2 ⇒ BC 2¹7² 8² BC = = ⇒ 289 − 64²25 BC = 15 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1162", "q": "In a triangle, two angles are 35° and 65°. What is the measure of the third angle? Matriculation Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["90°", "80°", "100°", "70°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The sum of all interior angles of a triangle is 180° Given angles = 35° and 65° Third angle = 180° − (35° + 65°) = 80°"},
