+{"id": "P1164", "q": "What is the number of sides of a regular polygon if the sum of its interior angles is 1440 degrees? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["9", "10", "11", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of interior angles (n - 2) × = → 180 ° 1440 ° (n - 2) = 8 n = 10 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1165", "q": "In a triangle, if one exterior angle is 140°, and the opposite interior angle is 60°, what is the other interior angle adjacent to it? Matriculation Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["100°", "130°", "80°", "180°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Exterior angle is equal to sum to its interior opposite angle:- 140 o = 60 o + = 80 o x o ⇒ x o"},
+{"id": "P1166", "q": "In a circle with center X, a chord PQ is such that ∠PXQ = 140°. What is the measure of ∠PRQ, where R lies on the arc PQ ? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["30°", "70°", "65°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In a circle, the angle formed on the circumference by an arc is half of the angle formed at the center by the same arc. ∠PRQ = ∠PXQ = × 140° = 70° 1² 1²"},
+{"id": "P1167", "q": "A triangle has angles in the ratio 3 : 1 : 2. What are the angles? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["40°, 60°, 80°", "30°, 45°, 105°", "36°, 54°, 90°", "90° , 30° , 60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the angle = 3x , 1x , 2x sum of three angles of a triangle = 180° 3x + 1x + 2x = 180° 6x = 180° x = 30° ⇒ Angle = 3 × 30° , 1 × 30°, 2 × 30° = 90°, 30°, 60°"},
+{"id": "P1168", "q": "A triangle has two angles measuring 55° and 75°. What is the measure of the third angle? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["65°", "70°", "60°", "50° Q.328 . In a triangle PQR, if angle P = 60° and angle Q = 50°, then what is the measure of angle R? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "80°", "50°", "70°", "90°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of all three angles of a triangle = 180° Third angle = 180° - (55° + 75°) = 50°"},
+{"id": "P1169", "q": "Two circles have the same centre. Their radii are 200 m and 220 m respectively. A small wheel of radius 60 cm rolls once around the inner circle. Another wheel rolls once around the outer circle. After completing one full round each, both wheels are found to have completed the same number of rotations about their own axes. What is the radius of the second wheel? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["23", "66", "50", "121"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number of rotations of a wheel: Rotations = Distance travelled Circumference of wℎeel = = 2 π R² π r R r = = 200⁰ . 6²20 r² ⇒ r² 22 × 0 . 3¹0⁰ ."},
+{"id": "P1170", "q": "How many diagonals are there in a regular decagon (a polygon with 10 sides)? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["35", "40", "45", "50"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "D iagonals = n ( n − 3 )² = = 35¹0 ( 10 − 3 )² = 70²"},
+{"id": "P1171", "q": "A right prism is cut vertically into two equal halves. How does its volume change? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3) TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["Becomes double", "Becomes half", "Stays the same", "Increases by 25%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Becomes half"},
+{"id": "P1172", "q": "Consider the following two statements, labeled Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Assertion (A): Two circles touching internally have only one common tangent. Reason (R): One circle lies entirely inside the other, touching at a single point, which prevents the existence of direct common tangents. Higher Secondary 24/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A", "Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A", "A is true, but R is false", "A is false, but R is true"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true, and the Reason correctly explains the Assertion."},
+{"id": "P1173", "q": "A quadrilateral PQRS is cyclic, ∠P=60° ∠R=120° and diagonals intersect at point T. What is the value of ∠Q+∠S? Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["360°", "180°", "90°", "120°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The sum of opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral = 180° ∠P +∠R = 180° 60° + 120° = 180° Since ∠Q and ∠S are also opposite angles, ∴ ∠Q + ∠S = 180°"},
+{"id": "P1174", "q": "Which of the following properties regarding circles is CORRECT? Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["The angle in a semicircle is a right angle (90 o )", "The angle in a semicircle is 180 o", "Angles in the same segment of a circle are always unequal.", "The angle subtended at the circumference is twice the angle at the center."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The angle formed in a semicircle (i.e., angle subtended by the diameter at the circumference) is always 90°."},
+{"id": "P1175", "q": "In right-angled triangle with ABC B = 90 o , let D be the midpoint of . ∠ AB From drop a perpendicular to the D DE hypotenuse AC, meeting AC at E. if AB = 40 cm and BC = 30 cm, find the area of △AED (in cm 2 ). Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["84 cm²", "96 cm²", "72 cm²", "108 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since D is the midpoint of AB: AD = = = 20 cm AB 2⁴0² In △AED and △ACB: ∠A is common ∠AED = 90° = ∠ABC ∴ △AED ∼ △ABC (AA similarity) = ( )² = ( )² = Area ( △ AED ) Area ( △ ABC ) AD AC 20⁵0⁴ 25 Area(△ABC) = × 40 × 30 = 600 cm 2¹ 2 Area (△AED) = 600 × = 96 cm 2⁴ 25"},
+{"id": "P1176", "q": "Consider a triangle ABC where the angle at vertex B measures 90 degrees and P is the midpoint of hypotenuse AC. What can be said about point P? Higher Secondary 26/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["P is the centroid of the triangle", "P is the incenter of the triangle", "P is the circumcenter of the triangle", "P lies on side BC"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In a right-angled triangle, the midpoint of the hypotenuse is the circumcenter of the triangle."},
+{"id": "P1177", "q": "and are similar if ∆ ABC ∆ PQR their corresponding sides are proportional. This is known as the: Higher Secondary 26/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["AA (Angle-Angle) Similarity", "SAS (Side-Angle-Side) Similarity", "SSS (Side-Side-Side) Similarity", "ASA (Angle-Side-Angle) Similarity"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If the corresponding sides of two triangles are proportional, it is called the (Side-Side-Side) similarity."},
+{"id": "P1178", "q": "Two tangents are drawn from an external point P to a circle, touching at points A and B. If the distance from P to the center O is 10 cm, and radius is 8 cm, what is the length of tangent PA? Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["5 cm", "6 cm", "4 cm", "7 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, OAP = 90 o [tangent] ∠ OP 2 = AO 2 + AP 2 (10)² = (8)² + AP 2 AP 2 = (10)² - (8)² = 100 - 64 =36 AP = = 6 cm 36"},
+{"id": "P1179", "q": "If triangle PQR is congruent to triangle XYZ , which of the following is true? Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["PQ = ZY", "QR = YX", "RP = XZ", "∠P = ∠Y"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When ΔPQR ≅ ΔXYZ, the order shows the correspondence: So the matching sides are: PQ = XY QR = YZ RP = XZ"},
+{"id": "P1180", "q": "If a chord of a circle is equal in length to the radius, what is the angle subtended by the chord at the center of the circle? Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["30°", "90°", "45°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If chord = radius, the triangle formed at the center is equilateral (all sides = radius). So each angle = 60°, hence the chord subtends 60° at the center."},
+{"id": "P1181", "q": "The radii of two concentric circles with centre 'O' are 6 cm and 10 cm. AB is a chord of the larger circle which is tangent to the smaller circle at point 'C'. If AD is a diameter of the larger circle, then find the length of CD. Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["cm", "cm 136²08", "cm", "cm 244¹64"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, AO = OD = 10 cm If a line divides any two sides in the same ratio ( = ) then the line is AO OD AC CB parallel to the third line. DB II OC ∴ OC = 6 cm ,BD = 12 In AOC, ∆ AC = = 8 cm 10 ( )² − 6 ( )² AC = BC = 8 cm ⇒ In BCD, ∆ CD = = cm 12 ( )² + 8 ( )²²08 ∴ The length of the CD is cm."},
+{"id": "P1182", "q": "The distance between the centres of the two circles is 58 cm, and the radii of the circles are 28 cm and 14 cm. Find the length of the transverse common tangent drawn to the two circles. Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["36 cm", "40 cm", "42 cm", "48 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of Transverse common tangent = d² − r¹ + r² ( )² = ( 58 )² − 28 + 14 ( )² = = 40 cm 3364 − 1764"},
+{"id": "P1183", "q": "Which of the following sets of conditions is NOT suﬃcient to prove that two triangles are similar? Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["AAA", "SAS", "SSS", "SSA"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "SSA does NOT guarantee similarity because two sides and a non-included angle can form more than one possible triangle (ambiguous case)."},
