+{"id": "P1186", "q": "Comparing the measure of an internal angle to the measure of an external angle of a regular polygon is 4 : 1. Find the number of sides of the polygon. Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["15", "18", "10", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Internal angle + External angle = 180° ⇒ 4 + = 180° ⇒ x x = = 36° ⇒ x¹80° 5 So, Side of the polygon = 360° exterior angle = = 10³60° 36°"},
+{"id": "P1187", "q": "PQR is an equilateral triangle inscribed in a circle. 'S' is any point on the minor arc QR and ∠RQS = 40 o . Find the measure of ∠QRS. Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["30°", "20°", "45°", "60°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "△PQR is equilateral, so ∠PQR = ∠PRQ = ∠QPR = 60 o . We know that, ∠QPR + ∠QSR = 180 o⁶0 o + ∠QSR = 180 o ⇒ ∠QSR = 180 o - 60 o = 120 o ⇒ In RQS, ∆ ∠RQS + ∠QSR + ∠QRS = 180 o ⇒ 40 o + 120 o + ∠QRS = 180 o ⇒ ∠QRS = 180 o - 40 o - 120 o = 20 o ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1188", "q": "In ΔPQR, EF is parallel to QR. If PE = 16 cm, PQ = 30 cm and PR = 90 cm, then find the length of PF. Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["48 cm", "52 cm", "36 cm", "44 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By Basic Proportionality Theorem, Since, EF ∥ QR, triangle PEF is similar to triangle PQR = = PF = 48 cm ⇒ PE PQ PF PR ⇒ 16³0 PF 90 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1189", "q": "A circle is completely enclosed within a parallelogram in such a way that all four sides of the parallelogram are tangents to the circle. The specific type of parallelogram formed in this manner will have its angles as ? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["All equal", "All unequal", "Two equal", "Three equal"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When all sides of a parallelogram touch a circle, it becomes a tangential parallelogram. Such a parallelogram can only be a rhombus."},
+{"id": "P1190", "q": "Match the concepts in Column I with their corresponding properties in Column II: Column I (Concept) Column II (Property) A. Distance from the center to the circumference 1. 90° angle with the tangent B. Equal chords 2. Subtend equal angles at center C. Distance from center to chord 3. Helps compare chord lengths D. Perpendicular from the center to the tangent 4. Equal to the radius Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1", "A-4, B-2, C-3, D-1", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2", "A-2, B-1, C-4, D-3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A-4 , B-2 , C-3 , D-1"},
+{"id": "P1191", "q": "Two circles touch each other externally. How many common tangents can be drawn? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["3", "2", "1", "0"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Three common tangents can be drawn."},
+{"id": "P1192", "q": "In a triangle, which of the following centers is always located inside the triangle? Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Circumcenter", "Orthocenter", "Incenter", "None of these"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Incenter The incenter always lies inside the triangle, regardless of its type."},
+{"id": "P1193", "q": "Within a circle, two parallel chords are positioned such that the center lies between them if the distance TG: @ikunal_x between these chords is 28 cm, and the length of one chord is 24 cm having radius of 20 cm, what is the length of the other chord? Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["36 cm", "35 cm", "32 cm", "40 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "32 Length of CD = 16 + 16 = 32 cm"},
+{"id": "P1194", "q": "Two complementary angles differ by 24°. What are the angles? Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["33°, 57°", "30°, 60°", "43°, 47°", "23°, 67°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the two complementary angle be and 90 - x x A/Q, 90° - - = 24° x x⁹0° - 24° = 2⁶6° = 2 = 33° x ⇒ x ⇒ x And other angle = 90° - 33° = 57°"},
+{"id": "P1195", "q": "Two tangents PA and PB are drawn from an external point P to a circle with center O. If the angle between the tangents is 50°, what is the angle subtended by the chord of contact AB at a point on the major arc? Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["50 o", "65 o", "80 o", "130 o"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the quadrilateral , the sum of OAPB angles = 360 o ∠AOB + ∠OBP + ∠APB + ∠OAP = 360 o ⇒ ∠AOB + 90 o + 50 o + 90 o = 360 o ⇒ ∠AOB = 130 o ⇒ Now, ∠AMB = = = 65° ∠ AOB 2¹30° 2"},
+{"id": "P1196", "q": "The length of a tangent drawn from an external point to a circle is 16 cm. If the shortest distance from the external point to the circle is 8 cm, what is the radius of the circle? Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["10 cm", "12 cm", "20 cm", "24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In OTA ∆ OA 2 = OT 2 + TA 2 (r + 8)² = r² + (16)² r² + 64 + 16 r = r² + 256¹6 r = 192 r = 12 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1197", "q": "Complement of an angle is 9°, more than twice the angle. Find the angle. Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["28°", "32°", "34°", "27°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the angle be x Complement angle = 2 + 9° x We know that, + 2 + 9° = 90° 3 = 81° = 27° ⇒ x x ⇒ x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1198", "q": "Find the angle if 2 times its complement equals the angle itself. Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["22.5°", "60°", "30°", "65.5°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let angle = x° A/Q, 2(90° - x ) = x° 180° - 2x = x° 3x° = 180° x = 60° ⇒ ⇒ ⇒ Reqd. angle = 60°"},
+{"id": "P1199", "q": "The angle between two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle is 80°. What is the angle subtended by the chord connecting their points of contact at the center ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["100°", "110°", "115°", "120°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If two tangent segments are drawn to a circle from the same external point, then those segments are equal in length. ∠MON + ∠MPN = 180° ∠MON + 80° = 180° ∠MON = 100° ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1200", "q": "Two circles have radii of 10 cm and 5 cm. The distance between their centers is 25 cm. What is the length of a direct common tangent ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["10cm", "20 cm", "10 cm", "12 cm 6⁶"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of direct common tangent = d² − r¹ − r² ( )² ⇒ 25² − 10 − 5 ( )² = = 10 cm. ⇒ 625 − 25⁶00⁶"},
+{"id": "P1201", "q": "There are two circles with radii of 7 cm and 5 cm are positioned so that they touch each other internally. What is the distance between their centers? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2 cm", "3 cm", "4 cm", "8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TG: @ikunal_x So, Required difference = 7 - 5 = 2 cm"},
+{"id": "P1202", "q": "If the difference between an angle and its complement is 24°, what is the angle? Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["38°", "57°", "62°", "70°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the angle be and other x angle be 90° - x A/Q, - (90° - ) = 24° x x² = 114° = 57° x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1203", "q": "In the given figure, AB = AD = 10 cm and AC = AE = 15 cm and BC = 18 cm. Find ED Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["18 cm", "16 cm", "14 cm", "15 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In EAD and CAB △ △ AE = AC (Given) AD = AB (Given) ∠EAD = ∠CAB (Vertically opposite angles are equal.) EAD CAB ( From SAS ) △ ≅ △ ED = BC = 18 cm"},
+{"id": "P1204", "q": "Two circles with radii 8 cm and 7 cm have their centers 25 cm apart. What is the length of their transversal common tangent? Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["12 cm", "18 cm", "20 cm", "22 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length = 25² − ( 8 + 7 )² Length = = = 20 cm 625 − 225⁴00"},
+{"id": "P1205", "q": "Complement of angle is equal y to ( + 20). Find the angle. y Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["35°", "40°", "45°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q, 90 - = + 20⁷0 = 2 = 35° y y ⇒ y ⇒ y"},
+{"id": "P1206", "q": "In a triangle, the distances from the incenter to the vertices are 4 cm, 5 cm, and 6 cm. Find the inradius. Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2 cm", "3 cm", "4 cm", "Cannot be determined"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For incentre we have to find the either area or side length. It cannot be determined."},
+{"id": "P1207", "q": "If ABC is an equilateral triangle inscribed in a circle and D is any point on arc BC.What is the measure of ∠ADB. 1² Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["20°", "30°", "60°", "15°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that angles made by the same chord at circumference are the same. So, ∠ACB and ∠ADB are same ∠ADB = 60° ∠ADB = 30° 1²"},
+{"id": "P1208", "q": "A quadrilateral PQRS has a circle inscribed within it. Given that the lengths of sides PQ, QR, and RS are 5 cm, 6 cm, and 7 cm respectively, what is the length of side PS? Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["4 cm", "6 cm", "5 cm", "8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of the opposite sides of parallelogram are equal PQ + RS = QR + PS 5 + 7 = 6 + PS PS = 6cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1209", "q": "A circular disc of radius 15 cm is divided into 4 equal sectors. What is the angle of each sector? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["15°", "60°", "30°", "90°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of each sector = = 90° 360° 4"},
+{"id": "P1210", "q": "The complement of an angle is one-fifth the angle. Find the angle Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["75°", "7°", "42°", "85°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the angle be ° and its x complementary angle be 90° - x Given, 90° - = 90° = = 75° x x⁵ ⇒ 6⁵ x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1211", "q": "The inradius of a triangle with sides 9 cm, 40 cm, 41 cm is: Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2 cm", "4 cm", "6 cm", "7 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Inradius = , when a + b − c² given right angle triangle r = r = = 4 cm 9 + 40 − 41² ⇒ 8²"},
+{"id": "P1212", "q": "Chords AB and CD intersect inside a circle at point O. If AO = 16 cm, OB = 7 cm, and CO = 8 cm, find OD. (O is the origin) Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["14 cm", "15 cm", "17 cm", "12 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that, AO × OB = CO × OD 16 × 7 = 8 × OD OD = 14 cm ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1213", "q": "An arc of a circle with radius 12 cm subtends an angle of 3 radians at the center. Find the length of the arc. Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["36 cm", "14 cm", "27 cm", "25 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the arc = radius × angle Length of arc = 12 × 3 = 36 cm"},
+{"id": "P1214", "q": "If the circumradius of triangle ABC is 21 cm, and its area is 84cm², find the product of its sides. Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["7048 cm³", "7192 cm³", "7204 cm³", "7056 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that , Area of triangle = Product of sides 4 × circumradius According to question , Product of three sides = 84 × 4 × 21 = 7056 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1215", "q": "A circular garden is divided into 4 equal parts. If the total area is 300 m² , what is the central angle of one part and its area? Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["60°, 75 m²", "90°, 75 m²", "120°, 90 m²", "90°, 60 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Central angle of one part = 90° Area = × 300 = 75¹ 4 m²"},
+{"id": "P1216", "q": "A sector having a radius of 8 cm and has a central angle of 90°. What is the area of the sector? Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["cm 2", "13 cm 2¹6 π π", "8 cm 2", "cm 2 π 8 π 6 eduquity-based pattern (ebp) Questions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector = × θ 360° π r² Area of sector = × 90° 360° π( 8² ) Area of sector = × × 64 = 16 cm 2¹ 4 π π"},
+{"id": "P1217", "q": "The centroid of a ΔXYZ is G. The TG: @ikunal_x area of ΔXYZ is 45 cm 2 . The area of ΔGYZ is:", "o": ["22.5 cm 2", "7.5 cm 2", "15 cm 2", "30 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The centroid divides the triangle into 3 smaller( GYZ, GXY and GXZ) triangles ∆ ∆ ∆ of equal area Area of GYZ = ∆ area of ∆ XYZ 3 = = 15 cm 2⁴5³"},
+{"id": "P1218", "q": "If 45° and 65° are the angles of a triangle, then find the exterior angle of the third angle (remaining angle).", "o": ["110°", "120", "70°", "100°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using Exterior angle property ∠RQS = ( P + R) = 65° + 45° = 110° ∠ ∠"},
+{"id": "P1219", "q": "In a triangle ΔABC, the ∠ABC = 90°. If sin(A) = , then cos(C) is equal to: 1²", "o": ["1", "1² 3² 1²"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "sinA = 1² sinA = sin30° A = 30° ⇒ Then, C = 90° - 30° = 60° ∠ cosC = cos60° = 1²"},
+{"id": "P1220", "q": "In ΔABC, two medians AD and BE intersect at G at right angles. If AD = 12 cm and BE = 9 cm, then the length of AB TG: @ikunal_x is equal to:", "o": ["14 cm", "16 cm", "12 cm", "10 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, centroid (G) divides the median in the ratio 2 : 1. So, we have ; AG = AD = × 12 = 8 cm 2³ 2³ BG = BE = × 9 = 6 cm 2³ 2³ Now, In BGA, AB = = △ 8² + 6² 100 = 10 cm"},
+{"id": "P1221", "q": "A quadrilateral PQRS is inscribed in a circle of centre O, such that PQ is a diameter and ∠PSR = 120°. Find the value of ∠QPR. TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["30°", "60°", "40°", "50°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that , ∠PRQ = 90° Since , PQRS is cyclic quadrilateral , so ∠PSR + ∠ RQP = 180° ∠ RQP = 180° - 120° = 60° ⇒ In PRQ ∆ ∠P + ∠Q + ∠R = 180° ∠P = 180° - 90° -60° ∠P = 30° ⇒ So, ∠QPR = 30°"},
+{"id": "P1222", "q": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle, AE is the diameter and ∠AOC = 100°. TG: @ikunal_x The value of ∠CDE + ∠CEA is:", "o": ["90°", "60°", "80°", "100°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept used : - The angle made by an arc at the center is twice the angle made by the same arc at the circumference. So, ∠CEA = ∠ADC = = 50° 100² ∠ADE = 90° (In a semicircle, any angle formed by a diameter is always 90°) ∠CDE = ∠ADE - ∠ADC = 90° - 50° = 40° ∠CDE + ∠CEA = 40° + 50° = 90°"},
+{"id": "P1223", "q": "In ΔABC, D is the mid-point of BC and G is the centroid. If GD = 10 cm, then TG: @ikunal_x the length of AD is _______ .", "o": ["20 cm", "10 cm", "15 cm", "30 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know Centroid divides the median in 2 : 1. GD = 1 → 10 AG = 10² = 20 × AD = AG + GD = 20 + 10 = 30 cm"},
+{"id": "P1224", "q": "In a triangle ABC, P is the midpoint of BC. If AB = (2 + 4) cm, AC = x⁶ cm and AP ⟂ BC, then the value of is: x", "o": ["3", "4", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given P is the mid point of BC BP = PC ⇒ We know In an equilateral triangle, AP ⟂ BC if and only if P is the mid point of BC. Hence, ABC is an equilateral triangle."},
+{"id": "P1225", "q": "ΔABC and ΔABD are on a common base AB and AC = BD and BC = AD as shown in the given figure. Which of the following options is true ?", "o": ["There are no congruent triangles in the given figure", "ΔABC ≅ ΔABD", "ΔABC ≅ ΔBAD", "ΔABC ≅ ΔADB"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, AC = BD BC = AD ⇒ AB is common. Hence, by SSS rule Both triangles ΔABC and ΔBAD are congruent. ΔABC ≅ ΔBAD ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1226", "q": "If x² -1, 2x and x² + 1 are the three sides of a right angled triangle, then which of the following can be its hypotenuse ?", "o": ["x² + 1", "x²", "2x", "x² - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, + = P² B² H² -1 + 2x = ( x² )² ( )² ( x² + 1 )² + 1 - 2 + = x⁴ x² 4 x² ( x² + 1 )² + 2 + 1 = x⁴ x² ( x² + 1 )² = ( x² + 1 )² ( x² + 1 )² LHS = RHS So, hypotenuse = 2 + 1 x"},
+{"id": "P1227", "q": "ΔPQR and ΔABC are two congruent triangles. If the area of ΔPQR is 225 cm 2 , then the area of ΔABC is:", "o": ["15 cm 2", "112.5 cm 2", "25 cm 2", "225 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of two congruent triangles are always equal. Hence, Area of ΔPQR = Area of ΔABC = 225 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1228", "q": "If three angles of a triangle are (18 + 6°), (10 + 30°) and (15 + 15°), x x x then the triangle is:", "o": ["scalene", "equilateral", "isosceles", "right angled"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, Sum of the angle of triangle = 180° (18 + 6°) + (10 + 30°) + (15 + 15°) x x x = 180° 43 + 51° = 180° x⁴3 = 129 = 3 x ⇒ x So, 18 + 6° = 18 × 3 + 6 = 60°, 10 + 30° x x = 10 × 3 + 30 = 60°, 15 + 15° = 15 × 3 + x¹5 = 60° Therefore, the triangle is equilateral ."},
+{"id": "P1229", "q": "In the following figure, ∠A = ∠P and AC = PR. Which of the following options needs to be satisfied for Δ PQR and Δ ABC to be congruent ?", "o": ["BC = QR by ASS criteria", "AB = PQ by SAS criteria", "BC = QR by SSA criteria", "AB = PQ by SSA criteria"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the given option, option (b) is the correct one. As in ΔPQR and ΔABC, ∠A = ∠P (given) AC = PR (given) AB = PQ Then, ΔPQR ≅ ΔABC (by SAS rule) TG: @ikunal_x"},
+{"id": "P1230", "q": "Let ABC, PQR be two congruent triangles such that ∠A = ∠P = 90°. If BC = 17 cm, PR = 8 cm, find AB (in cm). TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["9", "14", "12", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pythagorean triples (8, 15, 17) And ABC and PQR are the congruent ∆ ∆ triangles so the length of AB will be 15"},
+{"id": "P1231", "q": "The diameter PQ of a circle with centre O is perpendicular to the chord RS. PQ intersects RS at T. If RS = 16 cm TG: @ikunal_x and QT = 4 cm, what is the length (in cm) of the diameter of the circle?", "o": ["20", "48", "24", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ज्यामिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "RT × TS = PT × TQ 8 × 8 = PT × 4 ⇒ PT = 16 Diameter = PT + TQ = 16 + 4 = 20 cm"},
+{"id": "P1232", "q": "What is the HCF of ( + 1) and ( - 1) x⁶ x⁴", "o": ["(1 + )", "(1 + x)", "1", "(1 ) x² − x²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "( x⁶ + 1 ) = ( x² + 1 )( x⁴ + 1 − x² ) ( x⁴ − 1 ) = ( x² + 1 )( x² − 1 ) H.C.F = ( )¹ + x²"},
+{"id": "P1233", "q": "What is the HCF of the polynomials ( ³ - 8), ( ³ - 6 ² + 12 - 8) and ( ³ - 4 ² + 4 x x x x x x ) ? x", "o": ["( - 1)", "( - 2)", "( - 8)", "( - 4) x x x x"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "( ³ - 8) = ( 2) ( 2 + 2 + 4) x x − x x ( ³ - 6 ² + 12 - 8) = ( 2)³ x x x x − and ( ³ - 4 ² + 4 ) = ( 2)² x x x x x − HCF of ( ³ - 8), ( ³ - 6 ² + 12 - 8) and x x x x ( ³ - 4 ² + 4 ) = ( 2) x x x x −"},
+{"id": "P1234", "q": "There is a circular path around a sports field. Rahul takes 15 minutes to drive one round of the field, while Anil takes 18 minutes for the same. Suppose they both start from the same point and at the same time, and go in the same direction. After how many minutes will they meet again at the starting point?", "o": ["120", "100", "80", "90"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Required time when they meet = LCM (15, 18) = 90 min"},
+{"id": "P1235", "q": "13, a, b, c are four distinct numbers and the HCF of each pair of numbers (13, a) : (13, b) : (13, c) is 13, where a, b, c are each less than 60 and a < b < c. What is the value of ? a + c b", "o": ["3.5", "2", "5", "4.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As, HCF of (13, a), (13, b) and (13, c) is 13 where a, b and c must be multiples of 13. Only possible value for a, b and c such that a < b < c < 60 is 26, 39 and 52. So, a = 26, b = 39 and c = 52. = = 2."},
+{"id": "P1236", "q": "In finding the HCF of two numbers by division method, the quotients are 1, 8 and 2 respectively, and the last divisor is 105, what is the sum of the numbers?", "o": ["3570", "3885", "3780", "3675"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In such cases the last remainder is always zero. The required two numbers are 1995 and 1785 Sum of these two numbers = 1995 + 1785 = 3780"},
+{"id": "P1237", "q": "The Highest Common Factor and Lowest Common Multiple of two numbers p and q are A and B respectively. IF A + B = p + q, then the value of is : A³ + B³", "o": ["p³", "q³", "p³ + q³", "p³ - q³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2019", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Formula used : = A³ + B³ ( A + B ){( A + B )² − 3 AB } A + B = p + q (given) We know that , HCF LCM = product of the two no’s × A B = ⇒ × p × q Now, = A³ + B³ ( p + q ){( p + q )² − 3 pq } + ⇒ p³ q³"},
+{"id": "P1238", "q": "An oil merchant has 3 varieties of oil of volumes 432, 594 and 702 respectively. The number of cans of equal size that would be required to fill the oil separately is:", "o": ["13, 15, 17", "8, 11, 13", "8, 13, 15", "6, 9, 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "432 = , 2⁴ × 3³ 33⁵94 = 2¹1 , 702 = 2 × 3³ × × 3³ × 13 HCF = 2 = 54 × 3³ Cans for first variety of oil = = 8⁴32⁵4 Cans for 2nd variety of oil = = 11⁵94⁵4 Cans for 3rd variety of oil = = 13⁷02⁵4"},
+{"id": "P1239", "q": "The LCM and HCF of two numbers are 1105 and 5. If the LCM is 17 times the first number, then find the two numbers.", "o": ["55 and 85", "65 and 75", "60 and 80", "65 and 85"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, 1105 = 17 × 1st number ⇒ 1st number = 65 Formula:- 1st no. × 2nd no. = LCM × HCF 65 × 2nd no. = 1105 × 5²nd no. = 85 So the no."},
+{"id": "P1240", "q": "The LCM of two numbers is five times their HCF. If the product of the two numbers is 20480, then find their HCF and LCM, respectively.", "o": ["64 and 320", "56 and 280", "48 and 240", "46 and 230"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given , LCM = 5 HCF × Let numbers be “a” and “b” a b = 20480 × HCF LCM = a b × × HCF 5 HCF = 20480 × × = = 4096 ⇒ HCF = 64 HCF 2²0480⁵ LCM = 5 HCF = 5⁶4 = 320 × ×"},
+{"id": "P1241", "q": "The least number of five digits which is exactly divisible by 9, 12, 15, 25 and 27 is:", "o": ["10250", "10800", "10600", "10700 SSC MTS 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, LCM of 9, 12, 15, 25 and 27 will be 2700 So the smallest 5 digit number which exactly divisible by these numbers = 2700 × 4 = 10800"},
