+{"id": "P1253", "q": "The sides of a triangular field are 62 m, 186 m and 279 m. Find the greatest length of tape that would be able to exactly measure each of them without any fractions.", "o": ["62 m", "93 m", "31 m", "30 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The greatest length of tape = HCF of 62, 186 and 279 Prime factorization of the given no’s : 62 = 31 × 2, 186 = 31 × 6, 279 = 31 × 9 So, the HCF of the given no’s is 31"},
+{"id": "P1254", "q": "What is the LCM of a³ b - ab 3 , a³ b² - a² b³ , ab(a - b) ?", "o": ["a² b² (a² + b² )", "a² b² (a² - b² )", "a² b³ (a² + b² )", "a³ b² (a² - b² )"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM of a³ b - ab 3 ,a³ b² - a² b³ , ab (a - b) a³ b - ab 3 = ab ( a² − b² ) a³ b² - a² b³ = a² b² ( a − b ) ab (a - b) = ab ( a − b ) Hence, L.C.M = a² b² ( a² − b² )"},
