+{"id": "P1260", "q": "A and B are two prime numbers such that A > B and their LCM is 209. The value of A² - B is ?", "o": ["350", "372", "361", "339"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "HCF-LCM", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "since, the given no’s are prime no’s. So, the HCF of (A, B) = 1 and LCM of (A, B) = A × B = AB According to the question, A × B = 209 = 19 × 11 So, A = 19 and B = 11 (∵ A > B) Hence, = - 11= 361 - 11 = 350 A² − B¹9²"},
