+{"id": "P1274", "q": "Subhas, a³.15 m tall tree, and an 11.25 m tall building are positioned such that their feet on the ground are collinear and the tree is located between Subhas and the building. The tree is located at a distance of 7.5 m from Subhas and at a distance of 45 m from the building. Further, the eyes of Subhas, the top of the tree, and the top of the building fall in one line. Find the height (in m) from the ground at which Subhas' eyes are situated.", "o": ["1.75", "1.8", "1.6", "1.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "EC = SP = 7.5 + 45 = 52.5 metre BP = 11.25 metre − x ∽ ∆ SOT ∆ SPB = = = SO SP TO BP ⇒ 7 . 5⁵2 . 5 TO BP ⇒ TO BP 1⁷ 6 units = = 8.1 metre 11 . 25 − 3 . 15 ( ) TO (1 unit) = = 1.35 metre 8 . 1⁶ SE = OD = = 1.8 meter 3 . 15 − 1 ."},
+{"id": "P1275", "q": "A clock tower stands at the crossing Of two roads which point in the north-south and the east-west directions. P ,Q,R and S are points on the roads due north, east, south and west respectively, where the angles of elevation of the top of the tower are respectively, . Then ( )² is equal to : α, β, γ and δ PQ RS", "o": ["tan 2 α + tan 2 δ tan 2 γ + t an 2 β tan 2 α + tan 2 β tan 2 γ + t an 2 δ", "cot 2 α + cot 2 β cot 2 γ + cot 2 δ cot 2 α + cot 2 δ cot 2 γ + cot 2 β"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let OA be a straight tower. P , Q, R and S are points on the roads due north, east, south and west respectively. In Δ POQ and ΔORS PQ 2 = PO 2 + OQ 2 RS 2 = OR 2 + OS 2 = ---------- (1) ( PQ )² ( RS )² P O² + O Q² O R² + O S² Here, ∠AOQ = ∠AOP = ∠AOR = ∠AOS = 90°(as AO is a straight tower) Now, the angle of elevation are α, β, and δ."},
+{"id": "P1276", "q": "The angle of elevation of a flying drone from a point on the ground is 60°. After flying for 5 seconds the angle of elevation drops to 30°. If the drone is flying horizontally at a constant height of 1000 m, the distance (in m) travelled 3 by the drone is:", "o": ["2000", "1000", "3000", "4000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ACB, we have : △ tan 60° = = 1000³ BC ⇒ 3¹000³ BC BC = 1000 m In EDB, we have : △ tan30° = = 1000³ BD ⇒ 1³ 1000³ BD BD = 3000 m Distance covered by drone = BD – BC = 3000 – 1000 = 2000 m"},
+{"id": "P1277", "q": "The top of a broken tree touches the ground at a⁶0° angle, 45 meters away from the root of the tree. What will be the total height (in m) of the tree? (Use = 1.73 and = 1.41)³²", "o": ["153.45", "141.3", "167.85", "137.24"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let BD be the total height of the tree. AD = AC (given) Here, 1 unit = 45 m Then, unit = m³ 45³ and 2 unit →= 45 × 2 = 90 m So, the total height of tree = + 90⁴5³ = 77.85 + 90 = 167.85 m¹10"},
+{"id": "P1278", "q": "From the top of a¹2 m high building, the angle of elevation of the top of the tower is 60° and the angle of depression of the foot of the tower is , θ such that tan = . What is the height θ 3⁴ of the tower ? ( = 1.73)³", "o": ["41.41", "36.22", "39.68", "37.95"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As per the directions given, we have following figure : In AQP , tan 60° = = AP 16 ⇒ 3 AP 16 AP = 16 = 16 × 1.73 = 27.68³ So, height of tower = 27.68 + 12 = 39.68 m"},
+{"id": "P1279", "q": "A pole stands vertically on the ground with the help of a¹2-metre steel wire tied to its top and aﬃxed on the ground. If the steel wire makes an angle of 30° with the horizontal ground, then the height of the pole is equal to:", "o": ["meters 6³", "meters", "6 meters 8³"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sin30° = ℎ 12 , m¹ 2 = ℎ 12 ℎ = 6"},
+{"id": "P1280", "q": "A man observed the top of an electric pole at angles of elevation of 60° and 30°, respectively, from two different observation points P and Q . If the distance between P and Q is 10 m, find the height of the pole (in m).", "o": ["5", "15", "15³ 3 SSC CGL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "tan 60° = ℎ x ……..(i) ℎ = 3 x tan 30° = ℎ x + 10³ ℎ = x + 10 ……..(ii) ℎ = x + 10³ From equations (i) and (ii) we get , 3 x = x + 10³ ∴ ⇒ m x = 5 ℎ = 5³"},
+{"id": "P1281", "q": "From the top of a tower, the angle of depression of the top of a¹0 m high building is 60°. If the distance between the tower and the building is m, find 50³ the height of the tower.", "o": ["150 m", "100 m", "160 m", "140 m SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB and CD be the height of tower and building respectively. Height of tower = ( x + 10)m³ ATQ, x = 50³ Then, height of tower = × 50 + 10) ( 3³ = 150 + 10 = 160m"},
+{"id": "P1282", "q": "A vertical pillar 42 cm long casts a³5 cm long shadow. At the same time, a tower casts a shadow 25 m long. Find 107 the height of the tower.", "o": ["28 m", "35 m", "32 m", "30 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= ⇒ = = 30 m⁴2³5 x²5 x⁴2 × 25³5"},
+{"id": "P1283", "q": "Suhas, a³.15 m tall tree, and a building are positioned such that their feet on the ground are collinear and the tree is located between Suhas and the building. The tree is located at a distance of 7.5 m from Suhas and at a distance of 45 m from the building. Further, the eyes of Suhas, the top of the tree, and the top of the building fall in one line, and the eyes of Suhas are at a height of 1.8 m from the ground. Find the height (in m) of the building.", "o": ["11.25", "11.50", "10.25", "10.75"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TO = TD OD = 3.15¹.8 = 1.35 m − − ∆ SOT ⩭ ∆ SPB = = SO SP TO BP ⇒ 7 . 5⁴5 + 7 . 5¹ . 35 BP BP = = 9.45 m¹ . 35 × 52 . 5⁷ ."},
+{"id": "P1284", "q": "A vertical pole of 28m height casts a¹9.2m long shadow. At the same time, find the length of the shadow cast by another pole of 52.5m height.", "o": ["36 m", "35 m", "40 m", "30 m SSC CGL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Shadow of pole ∝ height of pole A pole of 28 m height casts a shadow of 19.2 m long . 52.5 m long pole casts a shadow of = = 36 metre 19 . 2²8 × 52 ."},
+{"id": "P1285", "q": "Two ships are on the opposite side of a lighthouse such that all three of them are collinear. The angles of depression of the two ships from the top of the lighthouse are 30° and 60°. If the ships are 230 m apart, then find the 3 height of the light house (in m).", "o": ["175.4", "165.2", "172.5", "180.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let B and C be two ships and AD be the lighthouse In triangle ADC Angle 30° : 60° : 90° → Side 1 : : 2 → 3⁴ units = 230³ m Height of the light house ( )³ units = = = 172.5 meters."},
+{"id": "P1286", "q": "The angle of elevation of the top of an unfinished tower at a point distant 78 m from its base is 30°. How much higher must the tower be raised (in m) so that the angle of elevation of the top of the finished tower at the same point will be 60°?", "o": ["78", "80", "52", "26³ 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB be the height of tower and the AD be the height of the tower to be raised In ABC, tan30° = ∆ ℎ 78 = = 26¹ 3 ℎ 78 ⇒ ℎ 3 In DBC, ∆ Tan 60° = ⇒ = 26³ + x⁷8³ 26³ + x⁷8⁷8 = 26 + x = x = 52 m³ 3³ So, the required height of tower = 52 m³"},
+{"id": "P1287", "q": "A vertical pole and a vertical tower are on the same level ground in such a way that, from the top of pole, the angle of elevation of the top of the tower is 60° and the angle of depression of the bottom of the tower is 30°. If the height of the pole is 24 m, then find the height of the tower (in m).", "o": ["24√3(√3 + 1)", "72", "96", "24(√3 + 1)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ED and AC be the height of pole and tower respectively ATQ, we have following figure; Here, 1 unit ------- 24m Then, (3 + 1) = 4 unit ------ 24 × 4 = 96m So, the height of tower = 96m"},
+{"id": "P1288", "q": "A kite is flying at a height of 123 m. The thread attached to it is assumed to be stretched straight and makes an angle of 60° with the level ground. The length of the string is(nearest to a whole number)", "o": ["140 m", "139 m", "142 m", "138 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB is the height of the kite and AC be the length of string respectively Here, unit ------------- 123 m³ Then, 2 unit ------------- × 2 = 82¹23³ 3 = 82 × 1.73¹42 m ≈"},
+{"id": "P1289", "q": "A pole of length 7 m is fixed vertically on the top of a tower. The angle of elevation of the top of the pole observed from a point on the ground is 60° and the angle of depression of the same point on the ground from the top of the tower is 45°. The height (in m) of the tower is:", "o": ["7(2", "3 − 1 )⁷² ( 3 + 2 )", "7", "3⁷ 2 ( 3 + 1 )"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let CB and AB be the height of pole and tower respectively Here ( - 1) unit -------------- 7 m³ Then, 1 unit -------------- 7³ − 1 = = ( + 1) m⁷ ( 3 + 1 ) ( 3 − 1 )( 3 + 1 )⁷² 3"},
+{"id": "P1290", "q": "A boy is standing near a pole which is 2.7 m high and the angle of elevation is 30° The distance (in m) of the boy from the pole is ( = 1.73)³", "o": ["4.42", "4.53", "4.68", "4.63"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here, 1 unit = 2.7 m Then, unit = 2.7³ 3 = 2.7 × 1.73 = 4.68 m¹13"},
+{"id": "P1291", "q": "A man looks at the reflection of the top of the lamp-post on the mirror that is 6.6 m away from the foot of the lamppost. The man’s height is 1.25 m and he is standing 2 m away from the mirror. Assuming that the mirror is placed on the ground, facing the sky and the man, and that the mirror and the lamp-post are in a same line, find the height of the lamp-post (in metres).", "o": ["3.97", "4.28", "4.45", "4.13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From similarity concept :- = EC ED BC AB = 2¹ . 25⁶ . 6 AB (height of the lamp post) AB = 3.3 × 1.25 = 4.125 m (4.13 approx)"},
+{"id": "P1292", "q": "The shadow of a tower standing on level ground is found to be 40 m longer when the Sun's altitude is 30° than when it was 45°. Find the height (in meters) of the tower. Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["20 ( 3 − 1 ) ( 3 − 1 )", "20", "10 ( 3 + 1 ) ( 3 + 1 )"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "tan 30° = ℎ ℎ + 40¹ 3 = ℎ ℎ + 40 ℎ + 40 = 3 ℎ ∴ height of tower ( ℎ ) = 40³ − 1 = meter 20 ( 3 + 1 )"},
+{"id": "P1293", "q": "A vertical pole of length 6 m casts a⁴ m long shadow on the ground. At the same time, a tower casts a²8 m long shadow. Find the height of the tower.", "o": ["48 m", "32 m", "36 m", "42 m SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB be the length of the pole and BC be the shadow on the ground. So, the height of tower = 42 m"},
+{"id": "P1294", "q": "The angle of elevation of the top of Search on TG: @apna_pdf a tall building from the points M and N at the distances of 72m and 128m , respectively, from the base of the building and in the same straight line with it , are complementary . The height of the building ( in m ) is ?", "o": ["84", "96", "80", "90"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the height of building be h when angles are complementary = Product of the distance of two ℎ 2 points from the building = = = 96 m ℎ 72 × 128⁹216"},
+{"id": "P1295", "q": "A person was standing on a road near a mall. He was 1220 m away from the mall and able to see the top of the mall from the road in such a way that the top of a tree, which is in between him and the mall, was exactly in line of sight with the top of the mall. The tree height TG: @ikunal_x is 40m and it is 80m away from him. How tall (in m) is the mall? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["605", "610", "600", "675"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "we have to find out the length of AB ABC MDC(by AAA rule) △ ∼ △ = x = = 610 m X⁴0¹220⁸0 ⇒ 1220 × 40⁸0"},
+{"id": "P1296", "q": "From a point on a bridge built over a river, the angles of depression to the two opposite banks are 30° and 45° respectively. If the width of the river is 80( + 1) metres, find the height of the 3 bridge above the river banks. Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["80m", "60m", "40 m", "65 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Width of river = BD + DA = BA + 1 = 80( + 1)¹ unit = 80 m³ 3 ⇒ So, the height of bridge = 1 unit = 80 m"},
+{"id": "P1297", "q": "An observer on a tower 45 meters high spots a car. The angle of depression to the car is 45°. What is the distance of the car from the base of the tower? Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["45 m", "m³ 45²", "45 m", "90 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ PQR , tan 45° = 45 x¹ = ⇒ x = 45 m⁴5 x"},
+{"id": "P1298", "q": "Two pillars of equal height stand on either side of a roadway which is 150 m wide. At a point in the road between pillars, the elevations of the pillars are ° x and ° so that = = , y tanx ° 2⁵ , tany ° 3⁵ then the height of each pillar is :", "o": ["39 m", "36 m", "42 m", "33 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB and CD be the two pillars of equal height = = or tanx ° AB BE 2⁵ 6¹5 = = or tany ° CD DE 3⁵ 6¹0 ATQ, 15 + 10 = 25 unit ---------------- 150 m Then, 6 unit ---------------- × 6 = 36 m¹50²5"},
+{"id": "P1299", "q": "A flagpole has a shadow measuring 20 meters. Given that the height of the flagpole is 20 meters, 3 What is the angle at which the sun is elevated ?", "o": ["45°", "30°", "60°", "90°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ABC, ∆ tan = = ⇒ X AB BC 20³ 20 tanX = = 60° ⇒ 3 ⇒ X"},
+{"id": "P1300", "q": "A steel cable is tied from the top of a vertical flagpole to a point on the ground 20 meters away from its base. If the cable makes an angle of 60° with the ground, find the length of the cable?", "o": ["10 m", "10 m", "40 m", "20 m³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Angle 30° : 60° : 90° → Side 1 : : 2 → 3 According to the question , 1 unit = 20 meters ⇒ 2 units = 40 meters Length of the cable = 40 meters"},
+{"id": "P1301", "q": "A man standing on the top of a¹50 m high tower observes the angles of depression of two cars on the same sides of the tower to be 45° and 60°. What is the distance between the two cars?", "o": ["150( - 1) m", "150 m³ 3", "150(1 - ) m", "150 ( 1 + ) m¹ 3¹ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let , AO = tower length = 150 m In AOC , ∆ tan45° = ⇒ 150 OC OC = 150 m ⇒ Now , in AOB , ∆ tan60° = ⇒ 150 OB = OB = m ⇒ 3¹50 OB ⇒ 150³ Hence, the distance between the two cars = 150 - = 150 ( 1 - ) m¹50³ 1³"},
+{"id": "P1302", "q": "A vertical tree PQ has its base on the ground Q . From a point A²0 m away from Q, the angle of elevation of P is x°. From another point B⁶0 m away from Q (and in the same line as A), the angle of elevation of P is y°. If the height of the tree is 20√3 m, what is the value of x° + y° ?", "o": ["60°", "75°", "90 °", "120°"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, tan x° = = = ℎeigℎt AQ 20³ 20³ x°= 60° ⇒ Now tan y° = = = ℎeigℎt BQ 20³ 60³ 3 y° = 30° ⇒ Hence , x° + y° = 60° + 30° = 90°"},
+{"id": "P1303", "q": "An airplane flying at a height of 400 m notices the angles of depression to two boats located on opposite sides as 45° and 30°. Find the distance between the two boats.", "o": ["400( - 1) m", "400 m³ 3", "400(1 + ) m", "400( + 1) m¹ 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the right triangles: tan45 o = BD = 400 m AD BD ⇒ tan30 o = CD= 400 m AD CD ⇒ 3 Distance between boats: BD + CD = 400 + 400 = 400(1 + ) m³ 3"},
