+{"id": "P1326", "q": "From the top of a tower, the angle of depression of the top of a¹0 m high building is 60°. If the distance between the tower and the building is m, 50³ find the height of the tower.", "o": ["150 m", "100 m", "160 m", "140 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "ऊँचाई-दूरी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let AB and CD be the height of tower and building respectively. Height of tower = ( x + 10)m³ ATQ, x = 50³ Then, height of tower = × 50 + 10) ( 3³ = 150 + 10 = 160m"},
+{"id": "P1327", "q": "The base of a right prism is an equilateral triangle with each side measuring 4 cm. If the lateral surface area is 120 cm 2 , find the volume (in cm 3 ) of the prism.", "o": ["30", "40", "10", "20³ 3³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area = 120 cm 2 Lateral surface area of prism = perimeter of base × height 120 = 3 × 4 × height Height = 10 cm Now, volume of prism = area of base × height = = 40³ 4 ×4×4×10³ cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1328", "q": "The length and the breadth of the floor of a rectangular hall are 126 feet and 90 feet, respectively. What will be the area (in square feet) of each of the largest identical square tiles that can be used to tile this floor in a way that no part of the floor remains uncovered?", "o": ["196", "256", "324", "484"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "H.C.F of 90 and 126 = 18 Largest possible side of the tiles = 18 feet Area of tiles = 18 × 18 = 324 feet 2"},
+{"id": "P1329", "q": "The radii of the ends of a frustum of a solid right-circular cone 45 cm high are 28 cm and 7 cm. If this frustum is melted and reconstructed into a solid right circular cylinder whose radius of base and height are in the ratio 3 : 5, find the curved surface area (in cm 2 ) of this cylinder. [Use .] π = 22⁷", "o": ["4610", "4620", "4580", "4640"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of frustum = π H³ ( R² + r² + Rr ) = 22×45⁷×3 ( 28² + 7² + 28 × 7 ) = 22×45⁷×3 × 1029 = 48510 Now, Volume of cylinder = Volume of frustum 22⁷ × 3 x × 3 x × 5 x = 48510 x³ = 343 ⇒ x = 7 So, curved surface area of cylinder = 2 rh π = 2 × 22⁷ × 21 × 35 = 4620 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1330", "q": "The weight of a cube varies directly as the product of its volume and its density. The ratio of densities of the materials of the first cube and second cube is 27:16. If the weight of the first cube is 4 times the weight of the second cube, then what is the ratio of the edges of the first cube and second cube?", "o": ["2 : 3", "3 : 2", "3 : 4", "4 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Weight (density × volume) ∝ Volume = × k weigℎt density Ratio - 1st cube : 2nd cube 149 Density - 27 : 16 Weight - 4 : 1 ------------------------------------------- Volume - : 64 : 27⁴ 27¹ 16 → Side = : 4 : 3³ 64³ 27 →"},
+{"id": "P1331", "q": "The weight of a circular disc varies directly as the product of the square of the radius and its thickness. Two identical/similar discs have their thickness in the ratio of 16 : 9. What is the ratio of their radii if the weight of the first is four times that of the second ?", "o": ["3 : 2", "2 : 3", "1 : 2", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, weight = radii 2 thickness × Ratio of weight = 4 : 1 Ratio of thickness = 16 : 9 Ratio of their radii = : 4¹6¹ 9 = : = 3 : 2² 4¹ 3"},
+{"id": "P1332", "q": "A path of uniform width 2.5 m runs around the outside of a rectangular field of dimensions 45 m³5 m. What is the × area of the path (in m² ) ?", "o": ["500", "425", "475", "525"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length and the breadth of the rectangular field along with the path = 45 + 5 = 50, 35 + 5 = 40 Area of the path = (50 × 40) - (45 × 35) = 425 m²"},
+{"id": "P1333", "q": "A hemispherical dome of a building needs to be painted. If the circumference of the base of the dome is 154 cm, then find the cost of painting it if the cost of painting is ₹4 per 100 cm² (use ). π = 22⁷", "o": ["₹150.92", "₹ 150.66", "₹ 105.29", "₹ 105.66"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumference of dome (2 ) = 154 cm π r = 154 × = 24.5 cm r⁷ 44 Curved surface area of hemispherical dome = 2 × × 24.5 × 24.5²2⁷ Required cost = 2 × 22 × 24 . 5 × 24 . 5⁷ × 100 × 4 = = 150.92 ₹ 2 × 22 × 3 . 5 × 24 ."},
+{"id": "P1334", "q": "The sum of the radius of the base and the height of a cylinder is 42 m. If the total surface area of the cylinder is 6336 , find the curved surface area of the m² 117 cylinder correct to two places of decimals (use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["2157.43", "2571.43 m² m²", "2715.43", "2517.43 m² m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of cylinder = (h + r)² π r⁶336 = 2 × 22⁷ × r × 42 = = 24 m r⁶336²2 × 12 Curved surface area of cylinder = h² π r = = 2715.43² × 22⁷ × 24 × 18 m²"},
+{"id": "P1335", "q": "The perimeter of equilateral triangle is 3 × units. Determine ( 4¹6³ ) the area of the triangle. Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["4 unit 2", "1 unit 2", "3 unit 2", "2 unit 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of equilateral angle triangle= 3a Area of equilateral angle triangle = 3⁴ a² According to question , a = 4¹6³ Therefore, required area = ( )²³ 4 × 4¹6³ = × = 1³ 4⁴ 3 unit 2"},
+{"id": "P1336", "q": "A spherical ball of diameter 8 cm is cut into two equal parts. The curved area of one such part has to be painted with green colour, while the other part has to be painted with red colour. The bases of both the hemispheres are to be painted with blue colour. The cost of painting with blue is ₹2/cm², while the cost of painting the curved area is ₹3/cm². What will be the cost (in₹) of painting the hemispheres? Take л = 3.14 Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["₹451.92", "₹492.92", "₹803.84", "₹401.92"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of hemisphere= 2 π r² Cost for green colour = 3 × (2 × 3.14 × 4 × 4) = 301.44 Rs. Cost for red colour = = 301.44 Rs. 3 × 2 × 3 . 14 × 4 × 4 ( ) Area of two bases = + = π r² π r² 2 π r² = = 100.48² × 3 . 14 × 4 × 4 ( ) The cost of painting with blue = = 200.96 Rs. 2 ×100 ."},
+{"id": "P1337", "q": "The external diameter of an iron pipe is 20 cm and its length is 12 cm. If the thickness of the pipe is 1 cm, find the surface area of the pipe (take = ) π 22⁷ correct to two places of decimal.", "o": ["1,662.67 cm 2", "1,552.57 cm 2", "1,442.48 cm 2", "1,772.76 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "External radius (R) = 10 cm Internal radius (r) = 9 cm and length (h) = 12 cm Total surface area of hollow cylinder pipe = 2 π( R + r ) ℎ + R − r { } = 13² × 22⁷ × 19 × = = 1552.57⁴4 × 247⁷ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1338", "q": "The area of a trapezium shaped field is 1785 square feet. The distance between the two parallel sides is 35 feet and one of the parallel sides is 42 feet long. What is the length of the other parallel side ?", "o": ["60 ft", "35 ft", "40 ft", "65 ft"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, area of the trapezium = 1785 sq .feet. Height of the trapezium = 35 feet, length of one parallel side = 42 feet. Let the length of the other parallel side be x feet."},
+{"id": "P1339", "q": "If the sum of the diagonals of a rhombus is L and the perimeter is 4P , find the area of the rhombus?", "o": ["(L² - P²)", "(L² - 4P²)¹⁴ 1⁴", "(L² - 4P²)", "(L² + 3P²)¹² 1⁴"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of the rhombus be ‘a’ Perimeter of rhombus = 4a = 4P a = P ⇒ As we know that, + = 4 , D¹ + D² = L D¹ 2 D² 2 a² Then, D¹ D² = L² − 4 a² 2 Area of Rhombus = × D¹ × D² 1² = × = × ( - 4 )¹² L² − 4 a² 2¹ 4 L² P²"},
+{"id": "P1340", "q": "Water is flowing through a cylindrical canal with an internal diameter of 7 m at the speed of 18 km/h.Find the volume of water flowing through the canal in 30 minutes. (take π = )²2⁷", "o": ["3,76,500 m³", "3,56,500 m³", "3,66,500 m³", "3,46,500 m³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of water flowing through the canal in 30 min = × × × (18 × ) × (30 × 60)²2⁷ 7² 7² 5¹8 = 3,46,500 m³"},
+{"id": "P1341", "q": "Three sides of a triangle are , and a² + b² ( 2 a )² + b² a² + ( 2 b )² units. What is the area (in unit squares) of a triangle?", "o": ["3", "4", "5² ab ab ab 3² ab"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let a = b = 2 units BC = = 2 units a² + b² 2 AB = = 2 units ( 2 a )² + b² 5 AC = = 2 units a² + ( 2 b )²⁵ It becomes an isosceles triangle as below."},
+{"id": "P1342", "q": "The circumference of a circle is ‘aπ’ units and the area of the circle is ' b π ' square units. If a:b is equal to 4:5, then the radius of the circle is:", "o": ["3 cm", "2.5 cm", "5 cm", "2 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumference of a circle = aπ 2πr = aπ 2r = a ⇒ Area = bπ πr² = bπ b = r² ⇒ ⇒ a : b = 2r : r² or 2 : r⁴ : 5 = 2 : r ⇒ r = 2.5 cm"},
+{"id": "P1343", "q": "The area of a triangular field whose sides are 65m, 72m and 97m is equal to the area of a rectangular park whose sides are in the ratio of 5 : 13. What is the perimeter (in m) of the rectangular park?", "o": ["108", "180", "216", "144"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "65 m, 72 m and 97 m are triplets of a right - angled triangle. So area of triangular park = × = 1² 65 × 72²340 Let sides of the rectangle be 5x and 13x ."},
+{"id": "P1344", "q": "A wire is bent to form a square of area 169 If the same wire is bent to cm 2 . form a circle, then what is its area in cm 2 (to the nearest whole number) ?", "o": ["215", "227", "532", "531"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the square = a² = 169. So, a = 13 , Perimeter = 4a = 4 × 13 = 52 Circumference of the circle = 2 r = 52 π r = × 52 = 7⁴4⁹1¹1 Area = r² π = 22⁷ × 91¹1 × 91¹1 = = 215.09²15²366¹1 ≈ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1345", "q": "A sector of radius 10.5 cm with the central angle is folded to form a¹20 ◦ cone by joining the two bounding radii of the sector. What is the volume (in ) of cm 3¹18 the cone so formed ?", "o": ["343² 6 π 343³ 6 π", "343³ 12 π 343² 12 π"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height of the cone = radius of the sector And θ 360 × perimeter of the circle = perimeter of the base of the cone Let the radius of cone = r = 120³60 × 2 × π × 10 . 5² × π × r r = 3.5 ⇒ Height of the cone = l² − r² = = 7 ( 10 . 5 )² − ( 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1346", "q": "The base of a right prism is a triangle with sides 20 cm, 21 cm and 29 cm. If its volume is 7560 , then its cm 3 lateral surface area (in ) is : cm 2", "o": ["2484", "2556", "2520", "2448"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "20, 21 and 29 are triplet pairs, clearly a given triangle is a right angle triangle. Area of the triangle = 1² × 20 × 21 = 210 cm 2 Volume of the prism = Base Area Height × 7560 = 210 Height Height = 36 ⇒ × ⇒ Lateral surface area of the prism = Base perimeter Height × = (20 + 21 + 29)³6 = 2520 × cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1347", "q": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 4 cm, its surface area is increased by 464 What is the π cm 2 . volume (in ) of the original sphere ? cm 3", "o": ["15625⁶ π 35937⁸ π", "11979² π 15625⁸ π"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the original radius be r. According to the question 4 ( = 4 + 464 π r + 4 )² π r² π = r = 12.5 ⇒ r² + 16 + 8 r r² + 116 ⇒ Volume of the sphere = 4³ π r³ = × 12.5 × 12.5 × 12.5 × 4³ π = 15625⁶ π cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1348", "q": "The base of right prism is a trapezium whose parallel sides are 11 cm and 15cm and the distance between them is 9 cm. If the volume of the prism is 1731.6 , then the height (in cm) of cm 3 the prism will be :", "o": ["15.6", "15.2", "14.8", "14.2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of prism = base area height × 1731.6 = (15 + 11)⁹ height 1² × × × height = 14.8 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1349", "q": "A ribbon of equal width and length is wrapped around the curved surface l of a right circular cylinder to cover it completely. If the base circumference of this cylinder is c, then how many times the ribbon was wrapped around the cylinder ?", "o": ["l", "4", "c", "l"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let n be the number of turns. Total length of the ribbon = number of turns × circumference of the base of cylinder = n × c n = l ⇒ l c"},
+{"id": "P1350", "q": "ABCD is a rhombus with each side being equal to 8 cm. If BD = 10 cm, AC = 2 cm, what is the value of ? x x + 10", "o": ["2", "3", "7", "5³ 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "151 BO = = = 5 BD 2¹0² AO = = = AC 2² x² x Now, = AB 2 AO 2 + BO 2 = x = 39⁸ 2 ( x )² + 5² ⇒ = 7 cm x + 10 ⇒ 39 + 10"},
+{"id": "P1351", "q": "Equilateral triangles are drawn on the hypotenuse and one of the perpendicular sides of a right-angled isosceles triangle. Their areas are H and A respectively. is equal to : A H", "o": ["1", "4", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the length of the perpendicular and base of the right angle triangle is a cm. Hypotenuse of the triangle = a ⇒ 2 Area of formed on hypotenuse(H) ∆ = = 3⁴ × ( a² )²³ a² 2 Area of formed on perpendicular(A) ∆ = = = 3 a² 4 ⇒ A H³ a² 4³ a² 2¹ 2"},
+{"id": "P1352", "q": "The parallel sides of a trapezium are 20 cm and 10 cm and its non-parallel sides are equal to each other. If its area is 180 , then what is the length (in cm) cm 2 of each non parallel side?", "o": ["11", "13", "12", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ABCD be the given trapezium. And AE be its height. Area of trapezium = (CD + AB) AE 1² × 180 = (20 + 10) AE 1² × AE = 12 cm Draw AF || BC AB = FC = 10 cm and AF = BC ⇒ DF = DC - FC = 20 - 10 = 10 cm ⇒ In ADF ⇒ AF = AD ….(AD = BC, given) ∆ DE = EF = = 5 cm DF 2 …..(Perpendicular drawn on the base of an isosceles triangle ) = , AF = AF 2 AE 2 + EF 2 AE 2 + EF 2 = = 13¹2² "},
+{"id": "P1353", "q": "The area of a field in the shape of a hexagon is 2400√3 square meters. What will be the cost(Rs.) of fencing it at Rs. 18.50 per meter?", "o": ["4440", "5920", "5550", "5180"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of Hexagon = 6 × 3⁴ a² Here, 6 = 2400 , × 3⁴ a² 3 = 1600, a = 40 a² Perimeter of the hexagonal field = 6a⁶ × 40 = 240 metre Required cost of fencing = 240¹8.5 × = Rs."},
+{"id": "P1354", "q": "The area of a field in the shape of a triangle with each side x meter is equal to the area of another triangular field having sides 50m, 70m and 80m. The value of x is closest to :", "o": ["65.5", "63.2", "62.4", "61.8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of triangular field with side x m = 3⁴ x² Area of other triangular field = s ( s − a )( s − b )( s − c ) Where s = a + b + c² = 100 m ⇒ 50 + 70 + 80² Area of field = 100 ( 100 − 50 )( 100 − 70 )( 100 − 80 ) = = 1000¹00 × 50 × 30 × 20³ m² According to question, = 1000³ 4 x² 3 = 4000 x = 63.25 x² ⇒ m²"},
+{"id": "P1355", "q": "The volume of a metallic cylindrical pipe is 7480 . If its length is 1.4 m cm 3 and its external radius is 9 cm, then its thickness (given π = ) is: 22⁷", "o": ["1 cm", "0.8 cm", "0.9 cm", "1.2cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cylinder = π( R² − r² ) ℎ Where R = external radius r = internal radius h = height or length of the cylinder 7480 = 22⁷ × ( 9² − r² ) × 140¹7 = 81 - = 64 r = 8 cm r² ⇒ r² ⇒ Thickness = 9 - 8 = 1 cm"},
+{"id": "P1356", "q": "The areas of the three adjacent faces of a cuboid are 32 , 24 cm 2 cm 2 and 48 . What is the volume (in cm 2 cm 3 )of the cuboid ?", "o": ["192", "256", "288", "128"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cuboid = a × b × c Here a, b and c are the area of three faces = = 192³2 × 24 × 48 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1357", "q": "How much iron sheet (in ) will m² be needed to construct a rectangular tank measuring , if a¹0 m × 8 m × 6 m circular opening of radius one meter is to be left at the top of the tank? (correct to one decimal place)", "o": ["371.6", "370.4", "372.9", "370.8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required area of sheet = Total surface area of rectangular tank - Area of circular opening = 2 × ( 80 + 48 + 60 ) − π × 1² = 376 − 3 . 1 = 372 ."},
+{"id": "P1358", "q": "A solid cube of volume 13824 cm 3 is cut into 8 cubes of equal volumes. The ratio of the surface area of the original cube to the sum of the surface areas of three of the smaller cubes is :", "o": ["2 : 3", "4 : 3", "8 : 3", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of bigger cube = R = 13824 R = = 24 R³ ⇒ 3¹3824 Let side of smaller cubes = r¹3824 = 8¹728 = 12 = r × r³ ⇒ r³ ⇒ Required ratio = (6 ) : (3⁶ ) × 24² × × 12² = 4 : 3"},
+{"id": "P1359", "q": "What will be total cost of polishing curved surface of a wooden cylinder at rate of Rs 20 per , if its diameter is 40 m² cm and height is 7m ?", "o": ["176 rs", "184 rs", "175 rs", "186 rs"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of the cylinder = 2 = × 22⁷ × 7 × 20¹00⁴4⁵ m² Total cost = 20 = 176 rs 44⁵ ×"},
+{"id": "P1360", "q": "Original breadth of a rectangular box is 20cm. The box was then remade in such a way that its length increased by 30% but the breadth decreased by 20% and the area increased by 100 . What cm 2 is the new area(in ) of the box ? cm 2", "o": ["2500", "2200", "2600", "2400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Old : New Length 10 : 13 → Breadth 5 : 4 → _________ Area 50 : 52 → 52 - 50 = 2 unit = 100¹ unit = 50 ⇒ New area = 52⁵0 = 2600 × cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1361", "q": "12 buckets of water fill a tank when the capacity of each bucket is 13.5 liters. How many buckets will be needed to fill the same tank, if the capacity of each bucket in 9 liters ?", "o": ["15", "16", "18", "17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required number of buckets = 12 × 13 . 5⁹ = 18"},
