+{"id": "P1381", "q": "A cylinder has some water in it at a height of 16 cm. If a sphere of radius 9 cm is put into it, then find the rise in the height of the water if the radius of the cylinder is 12 cm.", "o": ["1.6 cm", "8.75 cm", "8 cm", "6.75 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Volume of cylinder = Volume of sphere = 12 × 12 × h π r² ℎ 4³ π r³ ⇒ = × 9 × 9 ×9 h = 4³ ⇒ 4 × 9 ×9 ×9³ × 12 × 12 h = 6.75 cm"},
+{"id": "P1382", "q": "If the slant height of a cone is 29 cm and its height is 20 cm, find the ratio between the magnitudes of total surface area and the volume.", "o": ["3 : 7", "3 : 14", "5 : 14", "7 : 15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given,Slant height ( ) = 29 cm l Height ( ) = 20 cm ℎ Radius ( ) = r ( 29 )² − ( 20 )² = = = 21 cm 841 − 400⁴41 According to question, = = T . S . A . of cone Volume of cone π r ( l + r )¹³ π r² ℎ ( l + r )¹³ rℎ = T . S . A ."},
