+{"id": "P1419", "q": "The curved surface area of a hemisphere is 693 cm². Its radius will be __________ .(Take = ) π 22⁷ Matriculation Level 27/06/2023 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["10.5 cm", "9 cm", "10 cm", "9.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of hemisphere = 2 π r² 693 = 2 × × cm 2²2⁷ r² = = r⁶93 × 7⁴4⁶3 × 7⁴ = = 10.5 cm 21²"},
+{"id": "P1420", "q": "The perimeter of an isosceles right - angled triangle having an area of 200 cm² is: Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["68.3 cm", "78.2 cm", "70.6 cm", "58.6 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of triangle = 1² × base × Heigℎt As we know, the base and height of an isosceles right angle triangle are equal. According to question, 200 = × a × a ⇒ a = 20 cm 1² By using pythagoras theorem, Hypotenuse = 20 cm 2 Perimeter of isosceles right-angle triangle = 20 + 40 = 68.3 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1421", "q": "A solid sphere has a surface area of 616 cm². This sphere is now cut into two hemispheres. What is the total surface area of one of the hemispheres? Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["440 cm²", "462 cm²", "452 cm²", "390 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of sphere = 4 π r² According to question, 616 = 4 × × ⇒ = 49 ⇒ = 7 cm 22⁷ r² r² r Now, total surface area of hemisphere = 3 = 3 × × 7 × 7 = 462 π r² 22⁷ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1422", "q": "A solid iron sphere of radius 21 cm is melted down into a cone of height 84 cm. What will be the radius of the cone ? Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["24 cm", "28 cm", "32 cm", "21 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of sphere = volume of cone = 4³ π r³ 1³ π R² ℎ = ⇒ = 21 cm 4 × 21 × 21 × 21 R² × 84 R"},
+{"id": "P1423", "q": "The curved surface area of a cylindrical pillar is 528 m² and its volume is 1848 m³ . The ratio between its radius and height is ________. Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["9 : 10", "7 : 12", "7 : 3", "9 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = = 7 m π r² ℎ 2 π rℎ 1848⁵28 ⇒ r² × 7² Now, = 528² π rℎ m² = = 12 m ℎ 528 × 7² × 22 × 7 Required ratio = 7 : 12"},
+{"id": "P1424", "q": "The radius of the base of a solid right circular cone is 20 cm and its height is 21 cm. What is its total surface area (in cm 2 ) ? Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["760", "980", "890", "680 π π π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pythagoras Triplets :- (20, 21, 29) So , here slant height ( ) = 29 cm l Total surface area of cone = π r ( l + r ) = = 980 π × 20 ( 29 + 20 ) π cm 2"},
