+{"id": "P1436", "q": "The ratio of the volume of the first and second cylinder is 32 : 9 and the ratio of their heights is 8 : 9. If the area of the base of the second cylinder is 616 cm², then what will be the radius of the first cylinder ?", "o": ["24 cm", "20 cm", "28 cm", "36 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let, the radius of the 1st cylinder be ‘R’ and radius of the smaller cylinder be ‘r’ . Ratio 1st cylinder : 2nd cylinder → Volume 32 : 9 → Height 8 : 9 → According to the question, Area of base of 2 nd Cylinder ( ) π r² = 616 ⇒ = = 14 cm."},
+{"id": "P1437", "q": "The breadth of a rectangular floor is of its length. If the area of the floor 3⁵ is 60 , then what is the difference metre 2 between the length and breadth of the floor ?", "o": ["6 m", "7.5 m", "5 m", "4 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the length of the rectangle = 5 x Breadth = 3 x Area of rectangle = length × breadth 60 = 5 × 3² x x ⇒ x → Now, Length = 5¹0m , Breadth = 3⁶m x → x → Difference between length and breadth 10⁶ 4 m ⇒ − →"},
+{"id": "P1438", "q": "The area of a square Is 1156 cm 2 . What is the respective ratio between the length and the breadth of a rectangle whose length is twice the side of the square and whose breadth is 14 cm less than the side of the square?", "o": ["16 : 7", "19 : 5", "17 : 5", "21 : 19"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = side 2¹156 = , side = 34 cm side 2 So the length of rectangle = 34 × 2 = 68 cm Breadth of rectangle = 34¹4²0 cm − = Ratio of length and breadth of rectangle = 68 : 20¹7 : 5 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1439", "q": "A rectangular park is 120 m long and 104 m wide. A¹ - m wide path runs along the boundary of the park, remaining completely inside the park area. Thus, the outside edges of the path run along the boundary wall of the park. The inside edges of the path are marked with a white line of negligible thickness. If it costs ₹2.50 to mark each metre with the white line, then how much would it cost (in ₹ ) to fully mark the inside edges of the path ?", "o": ["1090", "1080", "1120", "1100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required perimeter for marking = = = 440 metre 2 l + b ( )² ( 102 + 118 ) Total price = 440 × 2.5 = 1100 Rs."},
+{"id": "P1440", "q": "A hemispherical bowl of internal radius 18 cm is full of liquid. This liquid is to be filled in cylindrical bottles each of radius 3 cm and height 6 cm. How many bottles are required to empty the bowl?", "o": ["72", "70", "68", "66"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number of bottles be n. Volume of hemispherical bowl = 2³ π r³ Volume of cylinder = h π r² Number of Bottles ( ) n = Volume of Hemispℎerical bowl Volume of Cylinder ( ) = = 72."},
+{"id": "P1441", "q": "A pyramid has an equilateral triangle as its base, of which each side is 133⁸ cm. Its slant edge is 24 cm. The whole surface area of the pyramid (in ) is: cm 2", "o": ["(16 + 24 )", "(12 + 24 )³³5³ 35", "(24 + 36 )", "(16 + 48 )³³5³ 35"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LSA = × Perimeter of Base 1² × Slant height TSA of pyramid = LSA + Area of Base ( )² ( Edge )² = ( Slant ℎeigℎt )² + Side 2 ( )² ( 24 )² = ( Slant ℎeigℎt )² + 8² Slant height = cm ⇒ 4³5 LSA = cm 48³5 TSA = 16 + 3⁴8³5 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1442", "q": "If the curved surface area of a cylinder is 126 and its height is 14 π cm 2 cm, what is the volume of the cylinder.", "o": ["283", "137¹ 2 π cm 3¹ 2 π cm 3", "128", "125¹ 2 π cm 3¹ 2 π cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "C.S.A of Cylinder = 126² π rℎ ( ) π 2 = 126 ⇒ = cm × π × r × 14 π r⁹ 2 Volume of cylinder π r² ℎ ( ) = 14 = π × 9² × 9² × 567² π cm 3 = 283¹ 2 π cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1443", "q": "The difference between the length of two parallel sides of a trapezium is 12 cm. The perpendicular distance between these two parallel sides is 60 cm. If the area of the trapezium is 1380 , then cm 2 find the length of each of the parallel sides (in cm).", "o": ["27, 15", "31, 19", "29, 17", "24, 12 SSC CGL 2022 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the parallel sides of trapezium be a and b cm . Area of Trapezium = × Sum of two 1² parallel sides × height 1380 = × (a + b) × 60¹ 2 a + b = 46 and a b = 12 − On Solving these equations , we get a = 29 cm and b = 17 cm."},
+{"id": "P1444", "q": "The radius of a right circular cylinder is five times of its height. If the height of the cylinder is 3.5 cm, then what is the volume of the cylinder?", "o": ["3368.75 cm³", "3872.75 cm³", "3146.75 cm³", "3524.25 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Height of the cylinder = 3.5 cm Then radius of the cylinder = 17.5 cm Volume of cylinder = π r² ℎ = = 3368.75²2⁷ × ( 17 . 5 )² × 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1445", "q": "In the given figure, a square ABCD is inscribed in a quadrant APCQ . If AB = 16 cm, find the area of the shaded region (take = 3.14) correct to two places of π decimal.", "o": ["155.98cm 2", "179.68cm 2", "163.85cm 2", "145.92cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = = = 256 Side ( )²¹6² cm 2 Diagonal of square = =16 cm 2 × Side 2 Here , diagonal of square is the radius for the quadrant , So, area of the quadrant = 1⁴ × π r² = = 401.92¹ 4 × 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1446", "q": "If the volume of a sphere is 24,416.64 , find its surface area (take cm 3 π=3.14) correct to two places of decimal.", "o": ["3069.55 cm 2", "4069.44 cm 2", "5069.66 cm 2", "6069.67 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of sphere = 4³ × π r³ Now, = 24416 . 64⁴ 3 × 3 . 14 × r³ = = 5832 ⇒ r = 18 cm r³ 7776 × 3⁴ Now, surface area of sphere = 4 π r² = 4 × 3.14 × 18 × 18 = 4069.44 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1447", "q": "The length of the side of a cube is 5.6 . What is the volume of the cm largest sphere that can be taken out of the cube ?", "o": ["91.98", "99.96 cm 3 cm 3", "96.98", "90.69 cm 3 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side of given cube = 5.6 cm. For largest sphere to be inscribed in the cube, diameter of sphere should be equal to edge length of cube, 2 × radius = 5.6cm radius (r) = 2.8 ⇒ ⇒ Volume of the sphere = 4³ π r³ = = 91.98⁴ 3 π( 2 ."},
+{"id": "P1448", "q": "Three cubes of equal volume are joined end to end. Find the surface area of the resulting cuboid if the diagonal of the cube is . 6³ cm", "o": ["509 cm 2", "504 cm 2", "516 cm 2", "512 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of cube = side 3 Side of cube = 6 cm. Three cube of equal volume are joined end to end , then a cuboid in formed , having length=18 cm , breadth = 6 cm and height = 6 cm Now, Surface area of cuboid = 2 lb + bℎ + ℎl ( ) Surface area of cuboid = = 504² 108 + 36 + 108 ( ) cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1449", "q": "The diagonal of the square is 8² cm. Find the diagonal of another square whose area is triple that of the first square.", "o": ["8 cm", "8 cm 5³", "8 cm", "8 cm 2⁶"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of the first square = 8² Side of the first square = 8² 2 = 8 cm Area of the square = 8 × 8 = 64 cm 2 Area of the new square = 64 × 3= 192cm 2 Side of the new square = 8 cm 192 = 3 Diagonal of the new square = 8 × = 8³ 2⁶ cm"},
+{"id": "P1450", "q": "Area of the floor of a cubical room is 64 m². The length of the longest rod that can be kept in the room is:", "o": ["16 m", "4 m³ 3", "12 m", "8 m³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let a be the edge of the cubical room. ATQ, Area of the floor = = 64 a = 8 m a² ⇒ So, length of the longest rod = × 8 = 8 m³ 3"},
+{"id": "P1451", "q": "A field is in the shape of a rectangle of length 90 m and breadth 75 m. In one corner of the field, a pit, which is 18 m long ,15 m broad and 6 m deep, has been dug out. The Earth taken out of it is evenly spread over the remaining part of the field. Find the rise in the level of the field ?", "o": ["27 cm", "25 cm", "28 cm", "24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the rise in the level of the field be h The area of field = 90 × 75 = 6750 m² Area of pit = 18 × 15 = 270 m² Area of the remaining part of the field = 6750 - 270 = 6480 m² ATQ, Volume of earth taken out = Volume of earth spread over remaining part of field 270 × 6 = 6480 × h¹620 = 6480 h ⇒ h = = m = 25cm 1620⁶480¹ 4"},
+{"id": "P1452", "q": "In the given figure, the length of arc AB is equal to twice the length of radius r of the circle. Find the area of sector OAB in terms of the radius r.", "o": ["3r", "2r", "πr²", "r²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector OAB = = = lengtℎ of arc × radius 2² r × r² r²"},
+{"id": "P1453", "q": "The total surface area of a solid metallic hemisphere is 462 cm 2 . This is melted and moulded into a right circular cone. If the radius of the base of the cone is the same as that of the hemisphere, then its height is: (use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["14 cm", "7 cm", "21 cm", "28 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of hemisphere = 3 , π r² 462 = 3 × × 22⁷ r² = = 49 r = 7 cm r² 462 × 7⁶6 ⇒ Volume of hemisphere = Volume of cone × = × × h² 3 π 7³ 1³ π 7² 686 = 49h h = = 14 cm ⇒ 686⁴9"},
+{"id": "P1454", "q": "As shown in the given figure, inside the large semicircle, three semicircles (with equal radii) are drawn so that their diameters all sit on the large semicircle's diameter. What is the ratio between the unshaded and shaded areas?", "o": ["4 : 3", "1 : 2", "2 : 1", "3 : 4¹35"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the radius of each of the smaller semicircle be r Then, the diameter of larger semicircle = 6r The area of larger semicircle = × = 4.5 π 2 ( 6 r² )² π r² The area of unshaded region = 3 × × = 1.5¹ 2 π r² π r² The required ratio = 1.5 : (4.5 -1.5) π r² π r² = 1.5 : 3 = 1 : 2 π r² π r²"},
+{"id": "P1455", "q": "What is the length of the longest pole that can fit itself in a hall 60 feet long, 30 feet broad and 20 feet high?", "o": ["50 ft.", "70 ft.", "30 ft.", "20 ft."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the longest pole = 6⁰ 2 + 3⁰ 2 + 2⁰ 2 = = 70 feet 3600 + 900 + 400⁴900 ="},
+{"id": "P1456", "q": "The length of a cold storage is 5 times its breadth, and its height is 8 m. The area of its four walls (including the doors) is 720 m² . Find the total surface area of cold storage.", "o": ["1290.6 m²", "1275.3 m²", "1265.25 m²", "1282.5 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the breadth of a cold storage be x Then, length of the cold storage = 5x The area of four walls = 2(l+b)×h⁷20 = 2(5x + x) × 8⁴5 = 6x x = = 7.5m ⇒ 45⁶ Now, 2lb = 2 × 5x × x = 10 = 10 × = 562.5 x² 7 ."},
+{"id": "P1457", "q": "The area of the sector of a circle is 128 . If the length of the arc of that cm 2 sector is 64 cm, then find the radius of the circle.", "o": ["4 cm", "8 cm", "2 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The area of sector = 128 × 2 = 64r lengtℎ of arc × radius 2 ⇒ 256 = 64r r = = 4 cm ⇒ 256⁶4"},
+{"id": "P1458", "q": "A hall of 10 m length, 5 m width and 6 m height is to be painted (one side only). Determine the total surface area to be painted. (neglect the area of windows and doors) & (floor area is NOT to be painted)", "o": ["300 m²", "280 m²", "330 m²", "230 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of hall to be painted = 2 l + b ( ) × ℎ + l × b = 2(10 + 5) × 6 + 10 × 5 = 2 × 15 × 6 + 50 = 180 + 50 = 230 m²"},
+{"id": "P1459", "q": "A hemispherical bowl of internal radius 6 cm contains a liquid. This liquid is to be filled into cylindrical shaped small bottles of diameter 2 cm and height 4 cm. How many bottles will be needed to empty the bowl?", "o": ["32", "37", "38", "36"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of hemispherical bowl = volume of cylindrical bottles 2³ π R³ = n × π r² ℎ Required number of bottles = 2 × 6 × 6 × 6³ × 1 × 1 × 4 = 36 bottles"},
+{"id": "P1460", "q": "The total surface area of a hemisphere is 462 cm 2 .The diameter of this hemisphere is:", "o": ["28 cm", "21 cm", "7 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, total surface area of hemisphere = 462 cm 2³ π R² = 462 ⇒ R = 462 × 7³ × 22 = 7 So, the diameter of the hemisphere is 14 cm"},
+{"id": "P1461", "q": "The sum of the curved surface area and the total surface area of a solid cylinder is 2068 . If the radius of its cm 2 base is 7 cm, then what is the volume of this cylinder ? (use ) π = 22⁷", "o": ["2060", "2480 cm 3 cm 3", "3080", "2760 cm 3 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CSA + TSA of cylinder = 2068 c m² 2 rh + (2 rh + 2 ) = 2068 π π π r² 2 r(2h + r) = 2068 π 2 × × 7(2h + 7) = 2068²2⁷ 2h + 7 = = 47²068⁴4²h = 40 h = 20 cm ⇒ So, the volume of cylinder = × × 20 = 3080²2⁷ 7² c m³"},
+{"id": "P1462", "q": "The slant height of a cone is 20 cm. If area of its base is 616 , then cm 2 what is the curved surface area of this cone ?", "o": ["960", "440 cm 2 cm 2", "1760", "880 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height = 20 cm l According to the question, Area of base of cone = 616 cm 2 = 616 = 616 π r² ⇒ 22⁷ × r² = 196 = 14 cm r² ⇒ r So, CSA of cone = π rl = = 880²2⁷ × 14 × 20 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1463", "q": "The base of a prism is a right angle triangle whose sides are 9 cm, 12 cm and 15 cm. Volume of this prism is 648 cm 3 . What will be the height of prism ?", "o": ["14 cm", "12 cm", "9 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of prism = Area of base × height ( × 9 × 12) × h = 648¹ 2⁵4 h = 648 h = = 12 cm ⇒ 648⁵4 So, the height of the prism = 12 cm."},
+{"id": "P1464", "q": "The difference between the areas of two concentric circles is 264 . cm 2 What is the difference between the square of their radius ? (use ) π = 22⁷", "o": ["70", "140 cm 2 cm 2", "84", "64 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the radius of the inner and outer circle be r and R respectively. According to the question, Difference between the areas of two concentric circles = 264 cm 2 - = 264 = 264 π R² π r² ⇒ π( R² − r² ) = 264²2⁷ × ( R² − r² ) = 84 R² − r² cm 2 So, option (c) is the correct answer."},
+{"id": "P1465", "q": "Volume of a cone whose radius of a base and height are r and h respectively, is 400 . What will be the cm 3 volume of a cone whose radius of base and height are 2r cm and h cm respectively ?", "o": ["100", "1600 cm 3 cm 3", "1200", "800 cm 3 cm 3 SSC Selection Post (Phase - X)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Volume of cone = 400 cm 3 Volume of cone with radius r and height h = = 400¹ 3 π r² ℎ = 400 = 1³ × 22⁷ × r² ℎ ⇒ r² ℎ 4200¹1 Volume of cone with radius 2r and height h = = 1³ π( 2 r )² ℎ 4³ π r² ℎ = × × = 1600⁴ 3²2⁷ 4200¹1 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1466", "q": "A conical vessel has radius 4 cm and its curved surface area is 20 cm 2 . π The volume of conical vessel is: Graduate Level 02/08/2022 ( Shift - 3 )", "o": ["18 cm 3", "12 cm 3 π π", "26 cm 3", "16 cm 3 π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, radius of the cone = 4 cm, C.S.A of cone = π rl π r l = 20π ⇒ l = 20⁴ = 5 cm Now, height of the cone = l ( )² − r ( )² = 25 − 16 = 3 cm Volume of the conical vessel = 1³ π r² ℎ = = 1³ × π × 4 × 4 × 3¹6π cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1467", "q": "A student wants to know the area of a rhombus, one of whose diagonals is 6 cm. He measures another diagonal as 8 cm. What is the area of the rhombus? Graduate Level 05/08/2022 ( Shift - 3)", "o": ["25", "20 cm 2 cm 2", "24", "48 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rhombus = × × 1² d¹ d² = × 6 × 8 = 24¹ 2 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1468", "q": "The volumes of two cubes are in the ratio of 8 : 27. If the volume of the larger cube is 513 more than that of cm 3¹36 the smaller cube, find the length of each side of the smaller cube. Higher Secondary 01/08/2022 ( Shift - 3 )", "o": ["27 cm", "7 cm", "6 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cube = a³ Where a = side of a cube = Side of smaller cube Side of larger cube 3 Volume of smaller cube volume of larger cube = = Side of smaller cube Side of larger cube 3⁸ 27² 3 Then , side of smaller cube = 2x and side of larger cube = 3x According to question, 27x³ - 8x³ = 513cm 3¹9x³ = 513 ⇒ x³ = 27 x = 3 ⇒ So, Side of smaller cube = 2 × 3 = 6cm"},
+{"id": "P1469", "q": "A chord of a circle of radius 21 cm makes a right angle at the center. Find the area of major segment. (take π = ) closest to nearest integer. 22⁷ Higher Secondary 03/08/2022 ( Shift - 4 )", "o": ["1360", "1436 cm 2 cm 2", "1260", "1160 cm 2 cm 2 SSC MTS 2021 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of minor sector(OBC) = × × 21 × 21 = 346.5⁹0³60²2⁷ c m² Area of BOC △ = × 21 × 21 × sin = 220.5¹ 2⁹0⁰ c m² Area of minor segment = 346.5 - 220.5 = 126 c m² Now , area of major segment = area of circle - area of minor segment = × - 126 = 1386 - 126 = 1260²2⁷ 2¹ 2 c m² Short Trick:- Area of major segment :- area of major sector + area of triangle Required area "},
+{"id": "P1470", "q": "A goat is tied with a¹0.5 m-long rope to one corner of a plot which is in the shape of an equilateral triangle each side of which is 16 m long. Find the area that the goat can graze on.", "o": ["62.25 m²", "53.5 m²", "57.75 m²", "51.75 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As it is given that plot is in the shape of an equilateral triangle then, the grazed area is part of circle of radius 10.5m. so, angle is 60° 170 Hence, required area = × × 10.5 × 10.5⁶0° 360° 22⁷ = = 57.75²425 ."},
+{"id": "P1471", "q": "A smaller circle touches a bigger circle internally and also passes through the centre ‘O’ of the bigger circle. If the area of the smaller circle is 192 , the cm 2 area of the bigger circle (in ) is : cm 2", "o": ["768", "384", "1024", "720"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the smaller circle = 192 = 192 × ( )² = 192 π r² ⇒ π R² = 192 × 4 = 768 π R² So, area of the bigger circle = 768 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1472", "q": "The perimeter of a square is equal to the perimeter of a rectangle, and the latter has a width of 12 cm. The area of the square is 400 . Find the area of cm 2 the rectangle.", "o": ["412", "394 cm 2 cm 2", "324", "336 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the length of the rectangle be L cm and the side of the square be a cm. Area of square = 400 c m² = 400 a = 20 cm a² ⇒ ATQ,Perimeter of square = perimeter of rectangle 4a = 2(L + 12)⁴ × 20 = 2(L + 12) ⇒ 40 = L + 12 L = 40 - 12 = 28 ⇒ So, the area of rectangle = 28 × 12 = 336 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1473", "q": "The volume of a wall whose height is six times its breadth and length is half its height, is 23958 . What is cm 3 the breadth of the wall ?", "o": ["21 cm", "15 cm", "11 cm", "18 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The ratio of length, breadth and height of the wall = 3 : 1 : 6, Let the length, breadth and height of the wall be 3x, x and 6x respectively ATQ, The volume of wall = 23958⁶x × 3x × x = 23958¹8 = 23958 = = 1331 x³ ⇒ x³ 23958¹8 x = = 11 cm 3¹331"},
+{"id": "P1474", "q": "A goldsmith uses 110 of cm 3 gold to make a wire 1 mm in diameter. He will use this wire to make gold chains of equal lengths. If each chain requires 56 cm length of wire, then how many gold chains can he make? [use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["320", "250", "160", "210"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diameter of a wire = 1 mm = 0.1 cm Radius of a wire = = 0.05 cm 0 . 1² Let the no of gold chain required be n ATQ, Volume of wire × n = Volume of gold × 0.05 × 0.05 × 56 × n = 110²2⁷ n = = 250¹10 × 7²2 × 0 . 05 × 0 ."},
+{"id": "P1475", "q": "The volume of a cuboid is 3300 . The sum of the length and the cm 3 breadth of the cuboid is 37 cm. If the difference between the length and the breadth of the cuboid is 13 cm, then what is the height of the cuboid?", "o": ["18 cm", "11 cm", "14 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "It is given that, L + B = 37 — (1), L - B = 13 — (2) Adding eqn. (1) and (2), we have : L = = = 25 cm, B = 12 cm 37 + 13² 50² ATQ, Volume of cuboid = 25 × 12 × H³300 = 300H H = = 11 cm ⇒ 3300³00"},
+{"id": "P1476", "q": "the total surface area of a closed cube is 128 more than the area of a cm 2 square. If the length of each side of the cube is 8 cm, then what is the length of each side of the square?", "o": ["16 cm", "12 cm", "18 cm", "9 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, The total surface area of cube having 8 cm side = area of a square +128 cm² Let side of square is, X⁶ × 8 × 8 = + 128 X² + 128 = 384 X² = 256 X = 16 cm X² ⇒ 256 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1477", "q": "A rectangular LCD has an area of 480 and a perimeter of 92 cm. If the cm 2 size of the LCD is defined in term of length of the diagonal, then what is the size of the LCD?", "o": ["34 cm", "39 cm", "31 cm", "35 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a rectangle = l × b = 480 Perimeter of rectangle =2(l + b) = 92 l + b = 46 = 30 + 16 l × b = 480 = 30 × 16 So clearly length is 30 cm and breadth is- 16 cm Now diagonal of a rectangle = = l² + b² 30 × 30 + 16 × 16 = = 34 cm 1156"},
+{"id": "P1478", "q": "A person uses a rectangular 137 metallic sheet of 45 m³0 m for × making an open box. From each corner of the sheet he cut offs a square. If the length of one side of each of the squares is 10 m, then what will be the volume of the box (in m³ ) ?", "o": ["5000", "4500", "7000", "2500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When the 4 square shaped cuts are made in rectangular sheet then Length = 25m, Breadth = 10m, Height = 10m Volume - = l × b × h = 25m × 10m × 10m = 2500 m³"},
+{"id": "P1479", "q": "The total surface area of a closed hemisphere is 16632 cm 2 . What is the sum of the radius and the diameter of this hemisphere? [use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["172 cm", "168 cm", "126 cm", "154 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of hemisphere = 3 π R² R = = , D = 2R = 84 cm 16632³π 42 cm Radius + Diameter = 42 + 84 = 126 cm"},
+{"id": "P1480", "q": "The larger diagonal of a rhombus is 150% of its smaller diagonal, and its area is 432 cm 2 . Find the length ( in cm ) of the side of the rhombus ?", "o": ["8", "4", "6", "2¹3¹3¹3¹3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the smaller diagonal be x and larger diagonal be = ⇒ 150¹00 x³ 2 x⁴32 = 1² × 3² x² = 24 cm x = 432 × 4³ So, d₁ = 24 cm and d₂ = 36 cm Side of the rhombus = 12² + 18² = 6¹3"},
+{"id": "P1481", "q": "The surface area of a sphere is 2464 cm 2 . Find the radius of the sphere. [use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["14 cm", "28 cm", "42 cm", "40 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "4π R² = 2464 R = = 14 cm 2464 × 7⁴ × 22"},
+{"id": "P1482", "q": "Two cubes, each having a total surface area of 150 ,are joined cm 2 together to form a cuboid. Find the total surface area of the resulting cuboid.", "o": ["225", "250", "275", "300"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "T.S.A of cube (6 ) = 150 side 2 side = 5 cm Now, T.S.A of cuboid = 2(10 × 5 + 5 ×5 +10 × 5) = 2(50 + 50 + 25) = 250 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1483", "q": "What is the radius of a circular field whose area is equal to the sum of the area of three smaller circular fields of radii 8 m, 9m and 12m respectively?", "o": ["20 m", "21 m", "29 m", "17 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of large field = area of three smaller field R² = 8² + 9² + 12² ⇒ π π π π R² = (8² + 9² + 12²) ⇒ π π R² = 64 + 81 + 144 ⇒ R) = 17m ⇒ Radius ( 289 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1484", "q": "A toy is formed by placing a solid circular cone on a solid hemisphere and the radius of the common base of the cone and the hemisphere is 15 cm, If the volume of the toy is 2850 , then find π cm 3 the total surface area of that toy.", "o": ["815", "755 π cm 2 π cm 2", "705", "685 π cm 2 π cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of common base r = 15 cm Volume of toy = r³ + r²h² 3 π 1³ π 2850 = r² (2r + h) ⇒ π 1³ π × 15 × 15 × (30 + h) = 2850 ⇒ 1³ (30 + h) = 38 h = 8 ⇒ ⇒ Hence , by Pythagoras L(Slant Height) = = 17cm 15² + 8² Therefore, Surface area of toy = 2 r² + rl π π r( 2r + l) × 15 ×(30 + 17) = 705 cm² ⇒ π ⇒ π π"},
+{"id": "P1485", "q": "A large solid cube is melted and cast into ‘N’ small solid spheres, each of radius 3 cm , and ‘N+2’ small solid cuboids, Each of dimensions 4 cm × 4cm 6.5cm. If the length of each side × of the large solid cube is 12 cm, then find the value of ‘N’ [use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["8", "5", "7", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Side of the large cube = 12cm Radius of small spheres= 3cm So 12 × 12 × 12 ⇒ = N × r³ + (N + 2)⁴ × 4 × 6.5⁴ 3 π = N × r³ + (N + 2)⁴ × 4 × 6.5 = 1728⁴ 3 π = N × × × 3 × 3 × 3 + 104N + 208⁴ 3²2⁷ = 1728 [ ] = 1728 - 208 N⁷92⁷ + 104 N [ ] = 1520⁷92 + 728⁷ N [ ] = 1520 N = 7¹520⁷ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1486", "q": "The height of a trapezium is 68 cm and the sum of its parallel sides is 75 cm. If the area of the trapezium is 6¹7 times of the area of a square, then the length of the diagonal of the square is: (take = 1.41)²", "o": ["127.39 cm", "183.49 cm", "119.85 cm", "102.39 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of trapezium = 1² ( 68 × 75 ) = 2550 cm 2 Area of square = 2550 × 17⁶ = 7225 cm 2 Side of square = cm 7225 = 85 Diagonal of square = = 119.85 cm 2 × 85"},
+{"id": "P1487", "q": "The ratio of the length to the width of a rectangle is 3:2. If the length of this rectangle is increased by 25% and its width is kept constant, then the area of the rectangle increases by 24 . m² What is the width of this rectangle?", "o": ["12 m", "10 m", "8 m", "15 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the length and width of the rectangle be 3 , 2 x x Area of rectangle = 6 x² According to question, Now, = 24 ( 125¹00 × 3 x ) × 2 x − 6 x² = = = 15² x² − 6 x² 24 ⇒ x²4 × 2³ 4 Width of the rectangle = 8 m"},
+{"id": "P1488", "q": "The area of a square is 1296 cm 2 and the radius of a circle is of the 7⁶ length of a side of the square. What is the ratio of the perimeter of the square and the circumference of the circle ? (use = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["13:11", "8:11", "6:11", "3:7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a square = 1296 a² = 1296 a = 36 ⇒ Perimeter of square = 4a = 4 × 36 = 144 Radius = 36 × = 42⁷ 6 Circumference of circle - = 2 × × 42 = 264²2⁷ Required ratio = 144 : 264 = 6 : 11"},
+{"id": "P1489", "q": "The diameter of a circle is 7⁴ times of the base of a triangle, and the height of the triangle is 14 cm. If the area of the triangle is 56 , then what is the cm 2 circumference (in m) of the circle - (use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["0.44 m", "2.46 m", "0.48 m", "1.74 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the diameter of circle = 7x Base of triangle = 4x Area of the triangle = × b × h¹ 2 = 56 = × 4x × 14 x = 2¹ 2 ⇒ Diameter = 7x = 14 cm Radius = 7 cm ⇒ Circumference of circle - = 2 × × 7 = 44 cm or 0.44 m²2⁷"},
+{"id": "P1490", "q": "A square of side is taken. A p rectangle is cut out from this square such that the length of one side of the rectangle is equal to half of the length of one side of the square and the length of another side of the rectangle is equal to of the length of the first side of the 1³ rectangle. What is the area of the portion of the square that remained after the rectangle is cut out?", "o": ["7", "8", "p", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given length of side of square = p¹72 So, length of rectangle = p² Breadth of rectangle = p⁶ Now, required area = area of square - area of rectangle = - = p² p² 12¹1 p² 12"},
+{"id": "P1491", "q": "A pillar 11 m in radius is 21 m high. How much material(in ) was m³ used to construct it? (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["7996", "7886", "7989", "7986"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since, Pillar is cylindrical in shape. So, to reach the required answer we have to find the volume of the cylinder. Volume of cylinder (pillar) = π r² ℎ = × 11 × 11 × 21 = 7986²2⁷ m³"},
+{"id": "P1492", "q": "A sphere passes through the eight corners of a cube of side 14 cm. Find the volume (in ) of the sphere. cm 3 ( π = )²2⁷", "o": ["4312", "4012³ 3", "4312", "4012² 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of cube = diameter of sphere = 14 cm 3 Radius of sphere = = 7 cm 14³ 2³ Volume of Sphere = × × 7 × 4³ 22⁷ 3⁷ × 7 = 4312³ 3³ c m³"},
+{"id": "P1493", "q": "Find the total surface area (cm 2 ) of a container in cylindrical shape whose diameter is 14 cm and height is 25 cm. [Use π = ]²2⁷", "o": ["1452", "1392", "1408", "1424"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius = = 7 cm 14² TSA of cylinder = 2 π r ( ℎ + r ) = 2 × 22⁷ × 7 ( 25 + 7 ) = 44³2 = 1408 × c m²"},
+{"id": "P1494", "q": "What is the volume (cm 3 )of a right circular cylinder whose curved surface area is 12π cm 2 and the circumference of its base is 4π cm ?", "o": ["48π", "36π", "12π", "24π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumference of the base of cylinder = 2 r π 4 = 2 r r = 2 cm ⇒ π π ⇒ CSA of cylinder = 2 rh , π 12 = 2× × 2 × h h = = 3 cm π π ⇒ 12⁴ Volume of cylinder = × 2 × 2 × 3 =12 π π c m³"},
+{"id": "P1495", "q": "The sum of the length, breadth and depth of a cuboid is 23 cm, and its diagonal is cm. Its total surface area 5⁷ (cm 2 ) is:", "o": ["144", "354", "188", "111"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "+ + = 23 cm (Given) L B H Length of the diagonal of cuboid = L² + B² + H² 5 = ⇒ 7 L² + B² + H² 175 = + + ⇒ L² B² H² + + = + + + 2 ( + ⇒ ( L B H )² L² B² H² LB B + ) H H L = 175 + 2 ( + + ) ⇒ 2³ 2 LB B H H L⁵29 = 175 + 2 ( + + ) ⇒ LB B H H L³54 = 2 ( + + ) ⇒ LB B H H L So, TSA of cuboid = 354 c m²"},
