+{"id": "P1502", "q": "The length of each side of a regular hexagon is 10 cm. What is the area .of the hexagon ? ( cm 2 )", "o": ["156", "144", "148", "150³ 3³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of each side of hexagon = 10 cm Area of Hexagon = 6 × area of equilateral triangle Area of Hexagon = 6 × × 10 × 10³ 4 = = 150⁶00³ 4³ c m²"},
+{"id": "P1503", "q": "The area of a square is 9 + m² 12m + 4. Find the measure of the side of the square.", "o": ["3m + 2", "3m + 4", "3 + 2", "3 + 2m m² m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = + 12m + 4⁹ m² = + 2 × 3m × 2 + ( 3 m )²² 2 ⇒ ( 3 m + 2 )² Side of square = = 3m + 2 ( 3 m + 2 )²"},
+{"id": "P1504", "q": "The area of a square is , which of the following 4 x² − 12 x + 9 will be the side of the square?", "o": ["(2x + 3)", "(2x - 3)", "(3x - 2)", "(3x + 2)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = 4 - 12 + 9 x² x = 2 - 2 × 2 × 3 + = 2 - 3 ( x )² x³ 2 ( x )² Side of the square = = 2 - 3 ( 2 x − 3 )² x"},
+{"id": "P1505", "q": "If the areas of three adjacent faces of a cuboidal box are 729 , 529 cm 2 and 289 , respectively, then find cm 2 cm 2 the volume of the box.", "o": ["10557", "10560 cm 3 cm 3", "10555", "10551 cm 3 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "L × B = 729 , B × H = 529 c m² , H × L = 289 c m² c m² × × = 729 × 529 × 289 L² B² H² L × B × H = 729 × 529 × 289 = 27 × 23 × 17 = 10557 c m³"},
+{"id": "P1506", "q": "The diameter of the base and the slant height of a right circular cone are 10 cm and 16cm, respectively. Find its total surface area .[Use π = ] ( cm 2 )²2⁷", "o": ["330", "5720⁷ 720⁷ 1760⁷"], "ol": ["c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cone = r (r + l) π = × ( + 16)²2⁷ 10² 10² = × 5 × 21 = 330²2⁷ c m²"},
+{"id": "P1507", "q": "The diagonal of a rhombus is 8 cm and its area is 48 , then the length cm 2 of each side of the rhombus is:", "o": ["2", "6", "5¹3¹3¹3¹3"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of rhombus(D¹ ) = 8cm Area of rhombus = × 8 × D² 1² 48 = 4 × D² D² = = 12 cm ⇒ 48⁴ Now, side of rhombus 173 = = ( 8² )² + ( 12² )²¹6 + 36 = = 2 cm 52¹3"},
+{"id": "P1508", "q": "The total surface area of a solid cylinder whose radius is r cm and height is cm (in ) is : r² cm 2", "o": ["3π", "r", "2", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cylinder = 2 r (r + h) π = 2 r (r + ) = 2 r × = 3 π r² π 3 r² π r²"},
+{"id": "P1509", "q": "The surface area of a spherical volleyball is 100π . Find the volume cm 2 of air enclosed in the ball.", "o": ["400³ π 350³ π", "500³ π 200³ π"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of spherical volleyball = 100 π 4 r² = 100 r² = 25 r = 5 π π ⇒ ⇒ Volume of air = = 4³ × π × 5 × 5 × 5⁵00³ π"},
+{"id": "P1510", "q": "The total surface area of a hemisphere is 64.57 . Find its curved cm 2 surface area . ( cm 2 )", "o": ["64.57", "53.44", "43.04", "33.04"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The total surface area of a hemisphere = 64.57 cm 2³ r² = 64.57 ⇒ π 3 × × r² = 64.57 r² = 6.848 ⇒ 22⁷ ⇒ Curved surface area = 2 × × 6.848²2⁷ = 43.04 cm 2 Short trick :- CSA of hemisphere = = 43.04⁶4 ."},
+{"id": "P1511", "q": "If the curved surface area of a closed cylinder is 225 cm 2 and the area of its base is 169 cm 2 , then find the total surface area (cm 2 ) of the cylinder.", "o": ["394", "343", "563", "195"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cylinder = CSA of cylinder + 2 Area of base × = 225 + 2¹69 = 225 + 338 = 563 × c m²"},
+{"id": "P1512", "q": "The length of the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle is 37cm and the length of one of its other two sides is 12cm. What is the area of the triangle in ? cm 2", "o": ["222", "204", "216", "210"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, = = A B² A C² − B C² 3⁷ 2 − 1² 2 = = = 35 cm 1369 − 144¹225 Area of triangle = AB BC 1² × × = 35¹2 = 210¹ 2 × × c m²"},
+{"id": "P1513", "q": "The area of quadrilateral is 336 and the perpendiculars drawn to one m² diagonal from the opposite vertices are 16 m and 12 m long. Find the length of this diagonal.", "o": ["28 cm", "26 cm", "21 cm", "24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of ABCD = area of ADC + area of ABC 336 = 1² × AC × DE + 1² × AC × BF 336 = (DE + BF )¹² × AC 672 = AC(16 + 12)⁶72 = AC × 28 AC = 24 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1514", "q": "What is the height of a solid right circular cylinder whose radius is 3 cm and total surface area is 60 π ? cm 2", "o": ["3 cm", "5 cm", "7 cm", "9 cm SSC CGL 2021 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area= 2πr(h + r)⁶0π = 2 × π × 3(h + 3)¹0 = h + 3 h = 10 - 3 = 7 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1515", "q": "A solid cube of side 8 cm is dropped into a rectangular container of length 16cm, breadth 8 cm and height 15cm which is partly filled with water. If the cube is completely submerged, then the rise of water level (in cm) is :", "o": ["2", "6", "5", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let, the rise of water level = a cm According to the question, Volume of cube = Length of rectangle × Breadth of rectangle a × = 8⁸ 8 = 16⁸ a a = 4 cm × × × × ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1516", "q": "What is the difference in the volume (in ) of a sphere of radius 7 cm 3 cm and that of a cone of a radius 7 cm and height of 10 cm?[Use π = ]²2⁷", "o": ["205", "704", "924", "1078"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required difference = Volume of sphere - Volume of cone = – = (4 – )⁴³ π r³ 1³ π r² ℎ 1³ π r² r ℎ = (4⁷ – )¹³ × 22⁷ × 7² × × 10 = (18) = 924¹ 3 × 154 × c m³"},
+{"id": "P1517", "q": "Let be the surface area and x cm 2 be the volume of a sphere such y cm 3 that y = 14 . What is the radius (in cm) of x the sphere ?", "o": ["102", "42", "51", "68"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, y = 14 x Volume of sphere = 14 surface area of × sphere = 14⁴ 3 π r³ × 4 π r² = 14 = 42 cm 1³ × r ⇒ r"},
+{"id": "P1518", "q": "A hemispherical depression of diameter 4 cm is cut out from each face of a cubical block of sides 10 cm. Find 140 the surface area of the remaining solid (in ) (Use π = ) cm 2²2⁷", "o": ["900", "112⁴ 7⁴ 7", "675", "713³ 7¹ 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of the hemisphere = 2 π r² Base area of the hemisphere = π r² Effective area increase on each face of the cube = 2 – = π r² π r² π r² Area of each face of the cube = = 100 + = 112 ( 10 )² + π r² 22⁷ × 2² 4⁷ c m² Total surface area of the cube = 6 × 112 = 675⁴ 7³ 7 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1519", "q": "From the body of a solid cube of edge 7 cm, a solid sphere is removed. The volume of the remaining solid was found to be 163 . What is the 1³ cm 3 diameter (in cm) of the sphere? (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["10", "7", "5", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cube = volume of sphere + remaining part volume a³ = r³ + 163⁴ 3 π 1³ 7³ = × r³ + 4³ × 22⁷ 490³ 343 – = × r³ 490³ 4³ × 22⁷ = × r³ 539³ 4³ × 22⁷ r³ = r = d = 2r = 7cm 7 × 7 × 7² × 2 × 2 ⇒ 7² ⇒ 174"},
+{"id": "P1520", "q": "The inner circumference of a circular path enclosed between two concentric circles is 264m. The uniform width of the circular path is 3m. What is the area (in m² ,to the nearest whole number ) of the path ?.(Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["696", "756", "820", "948"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Take inner radius = r Outer radius = R = (r + 3) According to the question 2πr = 264 m ⇒ r = = 42 m²64 × 7²2 × 2 R = (r + 3) = 42 +3 =45 m Area of path = π (R² - r²)²2⁷ ( R + r )( R − r ) = = 820.28⁸20 m² 22⁷ ( 87 m × 3 m ) ≈"},
+{"id": "P1521", "q": "The total surface area of a right pyramid , with base as a square of side 8 cm , is 208 . What is the slant height cm 2 (in cm) of the pyramid?", "o": ["7", "10", "9", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of square based pyramid = Surface area of base + 4 × surface area of wall 8² + 4 × × 8 × AB = 208 cm² 1² AB = Slant height = = 9 cm 208 − 64¹6"},
+{"id": "P1522", "q": "A²2.5 m high tent is the shape of a frustum of a cone surmounted by a hemisphere. If the diameter of the upper and the lower circular end of the frustum are 21 m and 39 m respectively, then find the areas of the cloth (in ) used to m² make the tent (ignoring the wastage). (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["787", "2107² 7² 7", "1635", "2800⁶ 7² 7 SSC CGL 2020 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Upper radius = 21/2 = 10.5 Lower radius = = 19.5³9² Height of frustum = 22.5 - radius of hemisphere Height of frustum = 22.5 - 10.5 = 12 Now by pythagoras theorem Slant height (l)= = 15¹2² + 9² Total surface area = surface area of hemisphere + surface area of frustum Total surface area = + (R + r)l² π r ² π = 2 × + × 22⁷ × 10 . 5 × 10 ."},
+{"id": "P1523", "q": "A solid metallic cuboid of dimensions 12 cm × 54 cm × 72 cm is melted and converted into 8 cubes of the same size. What is the sum of the lateral surface areas (in ) of 2 such cubes ? c m²", "o": ["2592", "2268", "3888", "1944"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let, side of each cube so formed be a. Volume of cuboid = number of cubes formed × a³ Volume of cuboid = 8 × a³ 12 × 54 × 72 = 8 × a³ = 5832 a = 18 cm a³ ⇒ Lateral surface area of 2 such cube = 2 × (4 × ) = 8 × 324 = 2592¹ 8² c m²"},
+{"id": "P1524", "q": "The radius of a spherical balloon is inflated from 3.5 cm to 4.9 cm by pushing air into it. What is the percentage increase in the volume of the original balloon ?", "o": ["74.4%", "174.4%", "73.6%", "173.6%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of old radius to new radius = 3.5 : 4.9 = 5 : 7. Old : New Radius 5 : 7 Volume : 5³ 7³ 125 : 343 Required percentage increase = × 100 = 174.4% 343 − 125¹25"},
+{"id": "P1525", "q": "The slant height and radius of a right circular cone are in the ratio 29 : 20. If its volume is 4838.4 , then its π c m³ radius is:", "o": ["20 cm", "28 cm", "24 cm", "25 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As height, radius and slant height of a cone form a triplet, we have height 21x and radius = 20x = 4838.4¹ 3 π. ( 20 x )² × 21 x π ⇒ x = 1.2 x³ = 1 ."},
+{"id": "P1526", "q": "The base of a right prism is a triangle with sides 16 cm, 30 cm and 34 cm. Its height is 32 cm. The lateral surface area (in ) and the volume (in c m² ) are, respectively: c m³", "o": ["2560 and 7680", "2688 and 7680", "2624 and 7040", "2560 and 6400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "16, 30 and 34 forms a triplet so it is right angled triangle. So, base area = = 240¹ 2 × 16 × 30 c m² Volume of prism = base area × height 240 × 32 = 7680 ⇒ c m³ Lateral surface area of prism = perimeter of base × height (16 + 30 + 34 ) × 32 = 80 × 32 = 2560 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1527", "q": "The areas of three adjacent faces of a cuboidal solid block of wax are 216 cm², 96 cm² and 144 cm². It is melted and 8 cubes of the same size are formed from it. What is the lateral surface area (in ) of 3 such cubes? c m²", "o": ["648", "432", "576", "288"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, ( ) ( ) ( ) l × b × b × ℎ × ℎ × l = 216⁹6¹44 × × = 216⁹6¹44 ( lbℎ )² × × = = 1728 lbℎ 216 × 96 × 144 c m³ Let the edge of each cube = x So, volume of cuboid = 8 (volume of cube) = 8 lbℎ ( x )³¹728 = 8 ⇒ = 216 ⇒ = 6 cm ( x )³ ( x )³ x Lateral surface area of three cubes = 3 = 3 = 432 × 4 ( x )² × 4 ( 6 )² c m²"},
+{"id": "P1528", "q": "A cylindrical tube, open at both ends, is made of a metal sheet which is 0.5 cm thick. Its outer radius is 4 cm and length is 2 m. How much metal (in ) c m³ has been used in making the tube ?", "o": ["800π", "450π", "750π", "550π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the sheet = volume of cylinder with outer radius - volume of cylinder with inner radius. Inner radius = 4 cm - 0.5 cm = 3.5 cm h = 2 m = 200 cm. Required volume = π × 200 ( 4² − 3 . 5² ) = π × 200 ( 16 − 12 . 25 ) = = 750 π × 200 × 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1529", "q": "The base of a right prism is a triangle whose sides are 8 cm, 15 cm and 17 cm, and its lateral surface area is 480 . What is the volume (in ) of c m² c m³ the prism?", "o": ["540", "600", "720", "640"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area of prism = Perimeter of base Height × 480 = 40 Height Height = 12 cm × ⇒ Volume of prism = Area of base height × = 12 = 720 ( 1² × 8 × 15 ) × c m³"},
+{"id": "P1530", "q": "The curved surface area of a right circular cone is 2310 and its radius c m² is 21 cm. If its radius is increased by 100% and height is reduced by 50%, then its capacity (in litres) will be correct to one decimal place) .(Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["27.8", "28.2", "26.7", "25.9 SSC MTS 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, CSA of cone = 2310 c m² = 2310 ⇒ = 35 cm 22⁷ × 21 × l l So, = = ℎ l² − r² 35² − 21² = = = 28 cm 1225 − 441⁷84 Let new height = H and new radius = R So, H = 28 = 14 cm and R × 50¹00 = 21 = 42 cm × 200¹00 Capacity of cone = 1³ π R² H = = 25872¹ 3 × 22⁷ × ( 42 )² × 14 c m³ So, capacity (in litres)¹75 = = 25.872²5.9 litres 25872¹000 ≈"},
+{"id": "P1531", "q": "The area of a square is S and that of the square formed by joining the mid points of the given square is A. Then the value of is equal to: A S", "o": ["0.25", "0.5", "0.125", "1.25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the side of square = 4 So area of square S = = 16⁴ 2 For square formed by joining mid point, diagonal (PQ) = 4 So, area of square which formed = (diagonal = (4 = 8¹ 2 × )²¹ 2 × )² So, = = = 0.5 A S⁸ 16¹ 2"},
+{"id": "P1532", "q": "A container in the shape of a right circular cone, whose radius and depth are equal, gets completely filled by 128000 spherical droplets, each of diameter 2mm. What is the radius (in cm) of the container?", "o": ["6", "4", "8", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of spherical droplet (in cm) = R = = cm 2¹0 × 2¹ 10 Radius of cone = Height of cone = r Volume of 128000 droplets = Volume of cone 128000 = × 4³ π R³ 1³ π r² ℎ 128000 = × 4 ( 1¹0 )³ r² × r = 512 ⇒ = 8 cm r³ r"},
+{"id": "P1533", "q": "The total surface area of a solid right circular cylinder of height 13cm, is 880 . Its volume (in ) is 11k.The cm 2 cm 3 value of k is:(Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["208", "182", "104", "91"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cylinder = 880 c m² = 880² π r ( ℎ + r ) = 880² × 22⁷ × r ( 13 + r )¹3 + = 140 + 13 – 140 = 0 r r² ⇒ r² r + 20 – 7 – 140 = 0 r² r r ( + 20) – 7 ( + 20) = 0 = 7 cm r r r ⇒ r According to question, Volume of cylinder = 11k = 11k π r² ℎ = = 11k k = 182²2⁷ × ( 7 )² × 13 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1534", "q": "The area of a parallelogram ABCD is 300 . The distance between AB cm 2 and CD is 20cm and the distance between BC and AD is 30cm. What is the perimeter (in cm) of the parallelogram?", "o": ["60", "50", "40", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Area of parallelogram = Base Altitude × For base AD, 300 = AD CP ⇒ 300 = AD 30 × × ⇒ AD = 10 cm, BC = AD = 10 cm Similarly, for base CD, 300 = CD AQ ⇒ 300 = CD 20 × × ⇒ CD = 15 cm, AB = CD = 15 cm So, perimeter = AB + BC + CD + AD = 10 + 15 + 10 + 15 = 50 cm"},
+{"id": "P1535", "q": "If the width of the path around a square field is 4.5 m and the area of the path is 252 , then the length of the m² side of the field is:", "o": ["9.5 m", "9 m", "8 m", "8.5 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let each side of the square be “a” Side including the road = a + 2 × 4.5 = a + 9 According to the question, - = 252 ( a + 9 )² a² + 18a + 81 - = 252 a² a² 18a = 171 ⇒ a = = 9.5 m¹71¹8"},
+{"id": "P1536", "q": "A path 6m wide runs around and outside of a rectangular plot of length 10m and breadth 8m. Find the area (in of path ? m² )", "o": ["440", "600", "80", "360"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the path = (22²0) – (10⁸) × × = 440 – 80 = 360 m²"},
+{"id": "P1537", "q": "The internal dimensions of a rectangular closed wooden box are 30 cm , 18cm and 23cm,. What space (in ) will it occupy, if the wood used is cm 3¹cm thick?", "o": ["12420", "16000", "14136", "9408"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here the thickness = 1 cm, so for outer surface : Length = 30 + 2(1) = 32 cm, Breadth = 18 + 2(1) = 20 cm, Height = 23 + 2(1) = 25 cm Space occupied by rectangular box = Lengtℎ × Breadtℎ × Heigℎt = 32²0²5 = 16000 × × c m³"},
+{"id": "P1538", "q": "A solid metallic cylinder with a base radius of 3 cm and a height of 120 cm is melted and recast into a sphere of radius r cm. What is the value of r if there is a¹0% metal loss in the conversion?", "o": ["9", "8", "13.5", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, [ Volume of cylinder ] = Volume 90¹00 × of sphere = [ ] = 90¹00 × π R² ℎ 4³ π r³ = [ ] = 9¹0 × 3² × 120⁴ 3 r³ = [ 1080 ] = 9¹0 × 4³ r³ = = 729 = 9 cm r³ ⇒ r"},
+{"id": "P1539", "q": "The difference between the areas of two concentric circles is 88 . If cm 2 the radius of the inner circle is 6 cm then the area ( in ) of the larger circle is cm 2 closest to: (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["196", "201", "197", "198"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Difference between areas of two concentric circles = 88 cm 2 = 88 = 88 π R² − π r² ⇒ π( R² − r² ) = 88²2⁷ ( R² − 6² ) = 28 = 64 R² − 36 ⇒ R² Area of largest circle = π R² = 64 = 201.14²01²2⁷ × ≈ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1540", "q": "A rectangular plot is 420 m long and 84 m wide. It is surrounded by semi-circular flower beds along all its sides. The area of the entire plot (in hectares) is x. The value of x (correct to one decimal place) is: (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["19.1", "18.7", "17.9", "19.4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total area(x) = Area of rectangular plot + Area of two semi-circular of diameter 84 m + Area of two semi-circular of diameter 420 m = 420⁸4 + 2( ) + 2( ) × π r² 2 π R² 2 = 35280 + ( ) π r² + R² = 35280 + [ ( )² ( )² ]²2⁷ 84² + 420² = 35280 + [ ]²2⁷ ( 42 )² + ( 210 )² = 35280 + [ ]²2⁷ 1764 + 44100 = 35280 + [ ]²2⁷ 45864 = 35280 + 144144 = 179424 m² 1 hectare "},
+{"id": "P1541", "q": "A hall is 18 m long and 12 m broad. If the sum of the areas of the floor and the ceiling is equal to the sum of the areas of the four walls, the volume (in m³ ) of the hall is:", "o": ["1175.5", "1876.2", "1555.2", "1376.4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of four walls = Area of floor and ceiling 2h(l + b) = 2(l b) × 2h(18 + 12) = 2(18¹2) × 60h = 432 h = 7.2 m ⇒ Volume of hall = l b h × × = 18¹2⁷.2 = 1555.2 × × m³"},
+{"id": "P1542", "q": "A wooden piece in the shape of a cuboid is divided into five equal parts by cutting it with four cuts perpendicular to its length, and it turns out that each piece is a cube of volume 27 . What is the cm 3 total surface area (in ) of the cuboid? cm 2", "o": ["150", "174", "216", "198"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the edge of each cube be . x Volume of each cube so formed = 27 ⇒ = 27 ⇒ = 3 c m³ x³ x So length of cuboid = 3⁵ = 15 cm, × breadth = 3 cm, and height = 3 cm So, TSA of cuboid = 2 (lb + bh + hl) = 2(15³ + 3³ + 3¹5) × × × = 2(45 + 9 + 45) = 2(99) = 198 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1543", "q": "A boy walked along two adjacent sides of a rectangular field. If he had walked along the diagonal, then he would have saved a distance equal to one-fourth of the larger side.The ratio of the larger to the smaller side is:", "o": ["7 : 24", "11 : 18", "24 : 7", "18 : 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the larger side of the rectangle be “4a”, and other side be “b” According to the question, length of diagonal = 4a + b - a = 3a + b Applying pythagoras theorem we get, = b² + ( 4 a )² ( 3 a + b )² + 16 = 9 + + 6ab b² a² a² b² 7 = 6ab ⇒ = , a² a b⁶ 7 ratio of larger side : smaller side = 4a : b ⇒ 4 × 6 : 7 = 24 : 7"},
+{"id": "P1544", "q": "The length of a rectangle is three- fifth of the radius of a circle. The radius of the circle is equal to the side of a square whose area is 6400 . Find the m² area (in ) of the rectangle, if the m² breadth is 20 m is:", "o": ["1200", "480", "960", "1000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the square = 6400 m² Side of the square = = 80 m⁶400 So, radius of circle = 80 m Length of rectangle = × 80 = 48 m³ 5 Area of rectangle = length × breadth = 48 × 20 = 960 m²"},
+{"id": "P1545", "q": "Kamala has three cylindrical containers, each with radius 20 cm that she wants to fill with grain. If her bag of grain contains 100 kg of grain, and she fills all three containers to a height of 70 cm, how much grain will be left in the bag. If 1 kg grain occupies 3000 cm 3 space ? (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["88 kg", "50 kg", "58 kg", "12 kg"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of 3 cylinder to be filled with grain = 3 volume of each cylinder × = 3 ( h) = 3 ( × π r² × 22⁷ × ( 20 )² × 70 ) = 3 (88000) = 264000 × c m³ 3000 corresponds to 1 kg of grain, c m³ so 264000 = = 88 kg c m³ 264000³000 Grain left in the bag = 100 – 88 = 12 kg"},
+{"id": "P1546", "q": "The radius of a spherical balloon increases from 6 cm to 10 cm when more air is pumped into it. The ratio of the surface area of the original balloon and the inflated balloon is:", "o": ["4 : 5", "27 : 125", "3 : 5", "9 : 25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of original balloon : Surface area of in flated balloon = : = : = : 4 π r² 4 π R² r² R² ( 6 )² ( 10 )² = 36 : 100 = 9 : 25"},
+{"id": "P1547", "q": "Four solid cubes, each of volume 1728 ,are kept in two rows having c m³ two cubes in each row. They form a rectangular solid with a square base. The total surface area (in of the c m² ) resulting solid is:", "o": ["1440", "2304", "576", "1152"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Clearly, the following cuboidal figure with dimensions 24 × 24 × 12 will be formed. Total surface area of a cuboid = 2 (lb + bh + lh) = 2(24 × 24 + 24 × 12 + 24 × 12) = 2(576 + 288 + 288 ) = 2 × 1152 = 2304 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1548", "q": "Three circles, each having radius equal to 4 cm, are drawn with the vertices of an equilateral triangle as the centres. If the length of each side of the triangle is equal to 8 cm, then what is the area (in ) of the portion of the triangle c m² that is NOT covered by the sectors of the circles ?", "o": ["16 (2 )", "8 (2 )³ − π 3 − π", "8 (2 )", "16 (2 )³ − π 2³ − π 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required area = Area of equilateral triangle - Area of 3 sectors with angle 60° Area of equilateral triangle = = = 16³ 4 a² 3⁴ × 8 × 8³ c m² Area of three sectors with central angle 60° and radius 4 cm = 3 × × × 4 × 4 = 8 ."},
+{"id": "P1549", "q": "Three cubes each having volume 1728 c are placed one above the m³ other. What is the total surface area of the resulting solid?", "o": ["2304", "2592", "2160", "2016"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side of each cube = = 12 cm 1728 By putting three cubes one above the other, the resulting figure will be cuboid with dimension of 36 cm × 12 cm × 12 cm 177 Total surface area of the cuboid = 2 (LB + BH + HL) = 2(12 × 12 + 12 × 36 + 12 × 36) = 2 × 1008 = 2016 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1550", "q": "In the given figure, the area of the unshaded region is 35% of the area of the shaded region. What is the value of x", "o": ["20", "15", "10", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of shaded region = 80⁵0 = 4000 × m² So , area of unshaded region = 4000 = 1400³5¹00 × m² Total area = (80 + x) (50 + x) × 4000 + 1400 = 4000 + 130x + x² + 130x – 1400 = 0 x² + 140x – 10x – 1400 = 0 x² x (x + 140) – 10 (x + 140) = 0 x – 140, so x = 10 ≠"},
+{"id": "P1551", "q": "The sum of the height and radius of the base of a solid right circular cylinder is 46 cm. If the total surface area of the solid cylinder is 6072 what is c m² , the volume ( in ) of the cylinder ? c m³", "o": ["11025", "3030 π π", "11020", "3036 π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Here, (r + h) = 46 cm, Total surface area of cylinder = ⇒ = 6072² π r ( r + ℎ )² π r ( r + ℎ )² × × r × 46 = 6072²2⁷ r = , r = 21 cm 6072 × 7² × 22 × 46 h = 46 - 21 = 25 cm."},
+{"id": "P1552", "q": "A hall is 18 m long and 12 m broad. If the area of the floor is equal to the sum of the areas of the four walls, the volume (in m³ ) of the hall is:", "o": ["876.2", "777.6", "576.4", "675.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the floor = l × b = 18 × 12 = 216 Area of four walls = 2 × (l + b) × h ⇒ 2 × (18 + 12) × h Given, 2 × (30) × h = 216 So, h = 3.6 Now volume of a cuboidal shape = l × b × h = 12 × 18 × 3.6 = 777.6 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1553", "q": "The area of a triangular field with sides 60 m, 175 m and 185 m is equal to that of a rectangular park whose sides are in the ratio of 21 : 10. The perimeter (in m) of the park is:", "o": ["341", "403", "372", "310"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sides of the triangular field are triplets. Area of = Area of rectangular park ∆ 60¹75 = 21x¹0x¹ 2 × × × = 25 x = 5 x² ⇒ Perimeter of rectangular park = 2 [ 21x + 10x ] = 62x = 62 (5) = 310 m"},
+{"id": "P1554", "q": "A solid metallic toy has a hemispherical base with radius 3.5 cm surmounted by a cone. If the height of the cone is the same as the radius of its base, then the volume of metal used in cm 3", "o": ["89", "144", "134", "179² 3³ 4³ 4² 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Height of cone = radius of base , so h = r Volume of metal used = Volume of cone + volume of hemisphere = h + 1³ π r² 2³ π r³ = + 1³ π r³ 2³ π r³ = (1 + 2) = (3)¹³ π r³ 1³ π r³ = = = 134 c²2⁷ × ( 7² )³⁵39⁴ 3⁴ m³"},
+{"id": "P1555", "q": "A bucket in the shape of the frustum of a cone has its top and bottom radii as 20 cm and 10 cm, respectively. The depth of the bucket is 24 cm. The capacity of the bucket (in ) is : c m³ (π = )²2⁷", "o": ["8800", "13200 c m³ c m³", "17000", "17600 c m³ c m³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of frustum = h [ + + ( × ]¹³ π r¹ 2 r² 2 r¹ r² ) = × × 24( + + × 1³ 22⁷ 20² 10² 20¹0 ) = × × 24 × 700 = 17600¹ 3²2⁷ c m³"},
+{"id": "P1556", "q": "A rectangle of dimension 10 cm and 5 cm is placed adjacent to another rectangle of the same size to draw an L shape figure. Find the perimeter of the shape so formed.", "o": ["100", "40", "50", "60"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The given figure is Total perimeter = ( 5 + 10 + 5 + 10 + 5 + 10 + 5 ) = 50 cm."},
+{"id": "P1557", "q": "The area (in ) of a sector of a c m² circle of radius 2 cm is . What is the 4 π 5 central angle (in degrees) of the sector?", "o": ["60", "75", "36", "72 SSC CGL 2020 Tier - 1 Q.630 . A heap of wheat is in the form of a cone whose base diameter is 8.4 m and height is 1.75 m. The heap is to be covered by canvas. What is the area (in m² ) of the canvas required ? (π = )²2⁷ SSC CGL 16/08/2021 (Afternoon)", "60.06", "115.05", "63.6", "115.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector making angle at the centre = θ θ 360° × π r ² = × ⇒ θ 360° π ( 2 ) ² = 4 π 5 θ = 360° 5 = 72°"},
+{"id": "P1558", "q": "The area of the square shaped field is 1764 m². The breadth of a rectangular park is 1/3rd the side of the square field and its length is two times its breadth. What is the cost (in Rs.) of leveling the park at Rs.15 per m² ?", "o": ["4200", "4290", "5880", "4320"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side of the square = = 42 m¹764¹78 Breadth = of 42 = 14 m¹ 3 Length = 28 m , Area = 28 × 14 Cost of levelling = 28 × 14 × 15 = ₹ 5880"},
+{"id": "P1559", "q": "The area of the circular path enclosed by two concentric circles is 3080 m² . If the difference between the radius of the outer edge and that of the inner edge of the circular path is 10m, what is the sum (in m) of the two radii?", "o": ["70", "112", "98", "84 SSC CHSL 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the ring = (R² - r² ) = 3080 π (R² - r² ) = 3080 × =980⁷ 22 (R + r)(R - r) = 980 (R + r) × 10 = 980 R + r = 98 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1560", "q": "One diagonal of a rhombus is If the other diagonal is equal to 8³ cm . its side, then the area of rhombus is:", "o": ["12", "3", "24", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of the rhombus = 2a Other diagonal = 2a ; OB = OD = a cm In ΔOAB ; AB = 2a, OB = a, AO = 4³ (2a)² = a² + ( 4³ ) ² ⇒ 4a² = a² + 48 a = 4 ⇒ Other diagonal = 2a = 8 Area of the rhombus = = 1² × 8 × 8³ 32³ Short trick : Let the other diagonal = a So, side = a In a rhombus, 4 = ⇒ 4 = a² d¹ 2 + d² 2 a² ( 8³ )² + a² = 64 , a = 8 a² Area of the rhombus = = 1² × 8"},
+{"id": "P1561", "q": "The sum of the radius of the base and the height of a closed solid cylinder is 12.5 cm. If the total surface area of the cylinder is 275 then its radius is: cm 2 ,", "o": ["3 cm", "3.5 cm", "5cm", "7 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of cylinder = r Height of cylinder = h ⇒ r + h = 12.5 Total area of cylinder = 275 cm 2² 𝜋 r ( r + h ) = 275 cm 2² 𝜋 r( 12.5) = 275 , cm 2 r = = 3.5 cm 7²"},
+{"id": "P1562", "q": "What is the perimeter of a right-angled triangle whose sides (maki- - ng 90°) are and ? 20³ cm 15³ cm", "o": ["60", "3", "55", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know that 15, 20 and 25 are pythagoras triplet so third side is 25³ So, total perimeter = 15 + 20 + 25 = 60³ 3³ 3"},
+{"id": "P1563", "q": "The base of a triangle is equal to the perimeter of a square whose diagonal is cm and its height is equal 7² to the side of a square whose area is 169 cm 2 . The area(in cm 2 ) of the triangle is :", "o": ["182", "175", "156", "130"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of the square = 7² Side of the square = 7 cm Perimeter = 4a = 28 = base of a triangle Area of another square = 169 Side of another square = height of the triangle = 13 Required area of triangle = = 182¹ 2 × 28 × 13 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1564", "q": "How many bricks each measuring will be 64 cm × 11 . 25 cm × 6 cm , needed to build a wall measuring ? 8 m × 3 m × 22 . 5 m", "o": ["200000", "250000", "67500", "125000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "No. of bricks = = 125000⁸ × 3 × 22 . 5 × 1000000⁶4 × 11 . 25 × 6"},
+{"id": "P1565", "q": "The square of the diagonal of a cube is 2175 . What is the total cm 2 surface area ( in ) of the cube? cm 2", "o": ["4305", "4272", "4530", "4350 SSC CPO 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If side of a cube is = a then its diagonal = a and total surface 3 area = 6a² ( a)² = 2175 then 3a² = 2175 , 3 a² = 725 and 6a² = 6 × 725 = 4350 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1566", "q": "The sides of a triangle are 24cm, 26cm and 10cm. At each of its vertices, circles of radius 4.2 cm are drawn. What is the area (in ) of the triangle, cm 2 excluding the portion covered by the sectors of the circle ?", "o": ["27.72", "120", "105.86", "92.28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since we know that (10,24,26) is a pythagorean triplet so we can easily find out the area of the triangle to be = height 1² × base × = × 24 × 10 = 120¹ 2 cm 2 So the area of the triangle will be equal to 120."},
+{"id": "P1567", "q": "A⁹ cm solid metallic cube and a solid metallic cuboid having dimensions 5 cm, 13cm, 31cm are melted and recast into a single cube. What is the total surface area(in ) of the new cube? c m²", "o": ["2744", "1362", "865", "1176"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cube = a³ = 9³ = 729 cm 3 Volume of cuboid = 5¹3³1 = 2015 × × Total volume = 2015 + 729 = 2744 cm 3 Side of resultant cube = 14 cm Surface area of resultant cube = 6a² = 6¹4² = 1176 cm 2 ×"},
+{"id": "P1568", "q": "A⁹cm solid metallic cube and a solid metallic cuboid having dimensions 5 cm, 13cm, 31cm are melted and recast into a single cube. How much (in Rs.) is the cost to polish the new cube at the rate of Rs.10 per cm 2", "o": ["13,620", "11,760", "8,650", "27,440"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cube = a³ = 9³ = 729 cm 3 Volume of cuboid = 5¹3³1 = 2015 × × Total volume = 2015 + 729 = 2744 cm 3 Side of a new cube = 14 cm Surface area of a new cube = 6a² = 6¹4² = 1176 cm 2 × Cost = 1176¹0 = 11,760 ×"},
+{"id": "P1569", "q": "A hexagon is . What 1944³ m² will be the cost (in Rs) of fencing it at the rate of Rs.11.50 per metre?", "o": ["2,256", "2,785", "3,200", "2,484"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a hexagon = 3³ 2 a² = = a = 36¹944³ 3³ 2 a² ⇒ Perimeter = 36⁶ = 216 m × Cost = 216¹1.50 = Rs. 2,484 ×"},
+{"id": "P1570", "q": "The base of a triangle is equal to the perimeter of a square whose diagonal is 6 cm , and its height is equal to the 2 side of a square whose area is 144 . cm 2 The area of the triangle (in ) m²", "o": ["144", "216", "288", "72"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of square = 6 cm 2 Side of square = 6 cm perimeter of square = 24 cm Base of triangle = 24 cm Height of triangle = = 12 (area of 144 square = side 2 ) Area of triangle = 12²4 =144¹ 2 × × cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1571", "q": "The areas of three adjacent faces of a cuboidal tank are and 3 m² , 12 m² . The capacity of the tank in litres 16 m² is :", "o": ["48000", "24000", "72000", "36000¹44"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let height = h ; Length = l Breadth = b b = 3 , bh = 12 , h = 16 l l bh = 24 ( lbℎ )² = 3 × 12 × 16 ⇒ l m³ As 1 m³ = 1000 l So total volume = 24000 l"},
+{"id": "P1572", "q": "The base of a right pyramid is a square of a side 10cm. If its height is 10 cm, then the area (in ) of its lateral cm 2 surface is:", "o": ["100¹00 ( 5 + 1 )", "50⁵ 100⁵"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of base = 40 cm Height(OE) = 10 cm In right angled triangle OEF OF = 5 = + EF = 5 ⇒ EF 2 OF 2 OE 2 ⇒ 5 Slant height(EF) = 5⁵ Lateral surface area = perimeter of base Slant height 1² × × = 40⁵ 100¹ 2 × × 5 ⇒ 5 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1573", "q": "The height of a cylinder is 30 cm and the diameter of its base is 10 cm. Two identical conical holes each of radius 5 cm and height of 12 cm are drilled out. what is the surface area (in ) of the remaining solid? cm 2", "o": ["430", "330", "120 π π π π"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of cylinder = 2 π rℎ = 2 π ×5 × 30 = 300 π Slant height of cone = 5² + 12² = 13 Surface area of cone = π rl = π × 5 × 13 = 65 π Surface area of 2 cone = 130 π Total surface area = 430 π"},
+{"id": "P1574", "q": "The base of a right prism is a regular hexagon of side 5 cm. If its height is cm, then its volume (in 12³ ) cm 3", "o": ["900", "1800", "1350", "675"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Regular hexagon consists of 6 equilateral triangles. Area of triangle = a = 3⁴ 2²5³ 4 Area of base = 6 Area of triangle × = 150³ 4 Volume of prism = area of base height × = = 1350¹50³ 4 × 12³ cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1575", "q": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 2.5 decimeter (dm), then its surface area increases by 110 . What d m² is the volume(in ) of the sphere dm 2", "o": ["3", "7", "11", "21"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "R = new radius R = r + 2.5 ⇒ Surface area of the sphere = 4 π r² 4 × π × ( R² − r² ) = 110 = ( R² − r² )³5⁴ (R + r)(R - r) = (R + r) = 3.5³5⁴ ⇒ R = 3 and r = 0.5 ⇒ Volume = 4³ π r³ = = 4³ × 22⁷ × 1² × 1² × 1² 11²1"},
+{"id": "P1576", "q": "A cylindrical roller made up of iron is 1.2m long. Its internal radius is 24 cm and thickness of the iron sheet used in making the roller is 15 cm. What is the weight (in kg ) of the roller, if 1 of the c m³ iron has 8 g mass ?", "o": ["892.8", "907.2 π π", "846.72", "845.75 π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "l = 1.2 m =120 cm r = 24 cm, R = 39 cm Volume = π( R² − r² ) ℎ = = 113400 π × 945 × 120 π cm 3 Mass = density volume × Mass = (113400 )/1000 π × 8 Mass = 907.2 kg π"},
+{"id": "P1577", "q": "From a solid cylindrical wooden block of height 18cm and radius 7.5cm, a conical cavity of same radius and same height is taken out. What is total surface area (in ) of the remaining solid? c m²", "o": ["326.25", "416.25 π π", "472.5", "270 π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "h = 18 ; r = 7.5 l = 19.5(by pythagoras theorem) Total surface area = lateral surface area of cylinder + lateral surface area of cone + area of circular side (above) Total surface area= 2 π r ℎ + π rl + π r² Total surface area = π r ( 2 ℎ + l + r ) Total surface area = π 7 . 5 ( 36 + 19 . 5 + 7 . 5 ) Total surface area = π 7 . 5 ( 63 ) Total surface area = 472 ."},
+{"id": "P1578", "q": "The base of a right prism is a square having side of 15 cm. If its height is 8 cm, then find the total surface area.", "o": ["920", "930 cm 2 cm 2", "900", "940 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of prism = 2 Area of base + Curved surface area × Area of base = = 225¹5² cm 2 Curved surface area = Perimeter of base height = 4¹5⁸ = 480 × × × cm 2 Total surface area of prism = 2²25 + 480 = 930 × cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1579", "q": "In the figure, L is the centre of the circle, and ML is the perpendicular to LN. If the area of the triangle MLN is 36, then the area of the circle is:", "o": ["70", "72", "66", "68 π π π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the triangle MLN = 36 = 6√2 ⇒ 1² × r² ⇒ r Area of circle = π = = 72 r² π ( 6√2 )² π"},
+{"id": "P1580", "q": "In the given figure, the ratio of the area of the largest square to that of the smallest square is:", "o": ["4 : 1", "3 : 1", "2 : 1² : 1"], "ol": ["a", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of smallest square = 2 unit Then, diameter of circle in which smallest square is inscribed will equal to diagonal of square = 2 unit and this 2 diameter is equal to the side of the middle square."},
+{"id": "P1581", "q": "Water flows into a tank 180 m × 140 m through a rectangular pipe of 1.2m at a rate of 15 km/h. In × 0 . 75 m what time will the water rise by 4 m ?", "o": ["6 hours 42 minutes", "7 hours 28 minutes", "5 hours 46 minutes", "8 hours 12 minutes"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the pipe take T hours to raise the water level by 4m. 180 m¹40 m × × 4 m = 1.2m × 0 . 75 m × 15000 m × T T = 7 hours = 7 hours 28 minutes 7¹5"},
+{"id": "P1582", "q": "The area of a rectangle is - a² b² and its length is a + b, what will be its breadth ?", "o": ["2ab", "a + b", "ab", "a - b"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rectangle = - a² b² (a + b) breadth = (a + b)(a - b) × breadth = (a - b)"},
+{"id": "P1583", "q": "The area of a square park is 16x² + 8x + 1. What is the length of the park?", "o": ["(4x - 1) units", "(4x + 1) units", "(4x + 1)² units", "4x units"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a square park = 16x² + 8x + 1 = ⇒ a² ( 4 x + 1 )² a = 4x + 1"},
+{"id": "P1584", "q": "If M is the mid point of the side BC of ABC, and the area of ABM is 18 ∆ ∆ , then the area of is: cm 2 ∆ ABC", "o": ["30", "34", "36", "32"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "AM is the median of ABC. ∆ Area of ABM = 18 cm 2 ∆ Therefore, area ( ABM) = area ( ACM) …. ∆ ∆ (Median divides the triangle into two equal areas)."},
+{"id": "P1585", "q": "The length of a rectangular plot is five times its breadth. If the area of the rectangular plot is 2000 then what is m² , the breadth of the rectangular plot ?", "o": ["40 m", "10 m", "20 m", "30 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In a rectangular plot, Length = 5 breadth × Therefore, L : B = 5 : 1 Area of rectangular plot = 2000 m² L B = 2000 × 5 B B = 2000 ⇒ B = 20 m × ×"},
+{"id": "P1586", "q": "In an isosceles right-angled triangle, the perimeter is 30 m. Find its area ( In Approximate.) m²", "o": ["38.63", "39.60", "37.86", "40"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For an isosceles right triangle, sides = a, a, a² Perimeter = a + a + a = 30² 2a + a = 30² a (2 + ) = 30, a = = 15(2 - )²³0² + 2² Area of triangle = a² = 225 (2 - )²¹ 2 × 1² × × 2 = 225 (4 + 2 - 4 )¹² × × 2 = 225 (6 - 4 ) = 225 (3 - 2 )¹² × × 2 × 2 = 225 (3 - 2 [1.414]) = 225 (3 - 2.828) × × = 225 (0.172)³8.7 m² × ≈ 181"},
