+{"id": "P1588", "q": "A circular disc of area 0.64 m² Π rolls down a length of 1.408 km. The number of revolutions it make is: (π = )²2⁷", "o": ["280", "360", "140", "180"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of disc = 0.64 m² Π Thus, radius of disc = 0.8 m Circumference = 2 = 1.6 m π r π Distance = 1.408 km = 1408 m Number of revolution = = 280¹408¹ ."},
+{"id": "P1589", "q": "The volumes of sphere A and B are in the ratio 125 : 64. If the sum of radii of A and B is 36 cm, then the surface area (in cm 2 ) of A is:", "o": ["512 π", "1600 π", "800 π", "1024 π SSC CPO 2019 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume ∝ (radius)³ = ( )³ = , = Volume A Volume B r A r B¹25⁶4 r A r B⁵ 4 r A + r B = 9x = 36 ⇒ x = 4 r A = 20 and r B = 16 Surface area of sphere A = 4 × Π × r A² = 4 = 1600 л × Π × 400 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1590", "q": "The height of a right circular cone is 35 cm and the area of its curved surface is four times the area of its base. What is the volume of the cone (in m³ and correct up to 3 decimal places)", "o": ["3.316", "3.384", "2.994", "2.625"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let r be the radius of the cone Height of the cone = 35 cm Curved surface area( is the slant height l of the cone) = 4(Area of the base) 𝛑r = 4 x 𝛑 , = 4r l r² l As per formula, = + l² ℎ 2 r² Putting the value of = 4r from equation l¹ in the above formula 16 = + ⇒ 16 - = ⇒ 15 r² ℎ 2 r² r² r² ℎ 2 r² Put h=35 in above equation 15 r r = 35³5 ⇒ = × × × r² 245³ Now, volu"},
+{"id": "P1591", "q": "A field is in the shape of a trapezium whose parallel sides are 200m and 400m long, whereas each of the other two sides is 260m long . what is the area (in of the field ? m² )", "o": ["48000", "52000", "72000", "60000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In , by pythagoras theorem ∆ ADE 260² − 100² = AE 2³60 × 160 = AE 2 AE = 6⁴ 100 × × ⇒ AE = 240 area of trapezium= ( 200+400)²40¹ 2 × × = 600¹20 = 72000 ×"},
+{"id": "P1592", "q": "In ABC, ∠A = 90°, AB = 16 cm ∆ and AC = 12 cm. D is the midpoint of AC and DE CB at E. What is the area (in ⊥ of CDE ? cm 2 ) ∆", "o": ["8.64", "7.68", "5.76", "6.25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "∆ CAB & ∆ CED are similar triangles ∠CAB = ∠CED = 90° ∠C = ∠C, ∠CBA = ∠CDE Now, = = Area of ∆ CED Area of ∆ CAB ( 6²0 )²³6⁴00 Here, 400 units corresponds to 96 cm 2 So 36 units corresponds to 36 × 96⁴00 = 8.64 ⇒ area cm 2 ∆ DEC = 8 ."},
+{"id": "P1593", "q": "When the radius of a sphere is increased by 5 cm, its surface area increases by 704 The diameter of the cm 2 . original sphere is _______.( take = ) Π 22⁷", "o": ["8.2", "5.2", "6.8", "6.2 SSC CGL 2018 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Initially area of sphere = 4 π r² Increased area of sphere = 4 π( r + 5 )² ATQ, 4 π( r + 5 )² − 4 π r² = 704⁴ π{( r + 5 )² − r² } = 704⁴ × 22⁷ × ( 2 r + 5 ) × 5 = 704²r + 5 = 8 ⇒ 2r = 6.2 × 7⁵ diameter = 6.2 cm"},
+{"id": "P1594", "q": "Three solid metallic spheres whose radii are 1cm, x cm and 8 cm, are melted and recast into a single solid sphere of diameter 18 cm. The surface area (in ) of the sphere with radius x cm 2 cm is :", "o": ["144", "72", "64", "100 π π π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the sphere = 4³ π r³ Here, = + + 4³ π( 9 )³⁴ 3 π( 1 )³⁴ 3 π( x )³⁴ 3 π( 8 )³ = ( + + )⁴³ π ( 9 )³⁴ 3 π 1³ x³ 8³ 729 = 1 + + 512 x = 6 x³ ⇒ Surface area of the sphere = 4 π r² = 4 ⇒144 × π × 6² π cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1595", "q": "The area of the base of a right circular cone is 400 and its height is 15 π cm. The curved surface area of the cone (in ) is : cm 2", "o": ["480", "500", "450", "560 π π π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the base of a cone = π r² 400 = r = 20 π π r² ⇒ Slant height (l) of the cone = ℎ 2 + r² = = 25¹5² + 20² curved surface area of the cone = = = 500 π rl π× 20 × 25 π cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1596", "q": "The base of a right pyramid is an equilateral triangle with side 8 cm, and the height of pyramid is 24 cm. The 3 volume (in ) of the pyramid is : cm 3", "o": ["1152", "480", "576", "384"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the pyramid = Base Area Height 1³ × × Area of an equilateral triangle = 3⁴ a² = = 16³ 4 × 8 × 8³ Volume of the pyramid = × 16²4 = 384¹ 3³ × 3 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1597", "q": "A field roller, in the shape of a cylinder, has a diameter of 1 m and length of 1 m. If the speed at which 1⁴ the roller rolls is 14 revolutions per minute, then the maximum area (in ) m² that it can roll in 1 hour is : (take π = )²2⁷", "o": ["3960", "3600", "3300", "3560"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area covered in one revolution = 2 π rℎ = 2 × × × = 22⁷ 1² 5⁴ 55¹4 Total revolution in one hour = 60¹4 × Area covered in one hour = 60¹4 = 3300 × × 55¹4 m²"},
+{"id": "P1598", "q": "The base of a right pyramid is an equilateral triangle with area 16 . If 3 cm 2 the area of one of its lateral faces is 30 , then its height (in cm) is: cm 2", "o": ["739¹2²09¹2", "611¹2⁶43¹2"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of an equilateral triangle = 3⁴ a² 16 = a = 8³ 3⁴ a² ⇒ Radius of the pyramid = inradius of the triangle = = = a² 3⁸ 2³ 4³ And area of its lateral face = 1² × base × slant ℎeigℎt = 30¹ 2 × 8 × slant ℎeigℎt = ⇒ slant ℎeigℎt¹5² Height of the pyramid = l² − r² = = ( 15² )² − ( 4³ )²⁶11¹2"},
+{"id": "P1599", "q": "A¹5m deep well with radius 2.8 m is dug and the earth taken out from it is spread evenly to form a platform of breadth 8m and height 1.5m. What will be the length of the platform ?", "o": ["28.4", "28.8", "30.2", "30.8 Q.724 . The internal diameter of a hollow hemispherical vessel is 24 cm. It is made of a steel sheet which is 0.5 cm thick. What is the total surface area (in ) of cm 2 the vessel ? SSC CGL Tier II (13/09/2019)", "612.75", "468.75 π π 147", "600.2", "600.5 π π SSC MTS 2019 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mud taken out from earth = π r² ℎ = = 369.60²2⁷ × 2 . 8 × 2 . 8 × 15 Let the length of of platform = l³69.60 = l × b × ℎ l = = 30.8 m³69 . 60⁸ × 1 ."},
+{"id": "P1600", "q": "There is a path of equal width of 3.5 m along with a building measuring 25 m in length and 15 m in breadth. Find the flooring cost of this path at the rate of Rs. 25.50 per sq . m.", "o": ["Rs. 8389.50", "Rs.4186.50", "Rs. 8146.50", "Rs. 9149.50 SSC CHSL 2018 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the Path = 2(width of path){length + breadth + 2(width of path)}= 2(3.5){25 + 15 + 2(3.5)} = 329 cm 2 Required cost = 329 × = Rs."},
+{"id": "P1601", "q": "What is the area of a rhombus (in ) whose side is 10 cm and the cm 2 smallest diagonal is 12 cm?", "o": ["120", "192", "96", "50 SSC CGL 2018 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that = ( )² + ( )² a² d¹ 2 d² 2 Where a = side of the rhombus and d¹ , d² are the diagonals of the rhombus."},
+{"id": "P1602", "q": "The area of a square is 16 ² + 40 + x x²5 square units. Find the perimeter of the square.", "o": ["3(10 + 8)", "3(8 + 10) x x", "2(10 + 8)", "2(8 + 10) x x"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of square = ( side )² = 16 ² + 40 + 25 = x x ( 4 x + 5 )² Side of square = (4 + 5) ⇒ x Perimeter of square = 4 × (4 + 5) ⇒ x = 2 (8 + 10) x"},
+{"id": "P1603", "q": "Two equal circles are drawn on a square in such a way that opposite side of the square forms the diameter of each circle. If the remaining area of the square is 42 cm 2 , what is the measurement (in cm) of the diameter of each circle?", "o": ["14", "2.5", "7", "3.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of remaining area = area of square - 2 × area of semicircle According to the question, 42 = - 2 × × × ( 2 r )²¹ 2 π ( r )²⁴2 = - × 4 r² 22⁷ ( r )²⁴2 = (4 - )⁴2 = ( ) r² 22⁷ ⇒ r² 6⁷ = 42 × = 49 = 7 r² 7⁶ ⇒ r So, diameter of each circle (2 ) = 14 cm r"},
+{"id": "P1604", "q": "A solid metal cylinder of 12 cm height and 7 cm radius is melted and recast into two cones in the proportion of 1 : 2 (volume), keeping the height 12 cm. What would be the percentage change in the flat surface area before and after [use = ] ? π 22⁷", "o": ["35%", "20%", "45%", "50%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cylinder = h π r² = × 7 × 7 × 12 = 1848 cm 3²2⁷ Let the two new recast cones volume be and 2 x x So, 3 = 1848 ⇒ x = 616 cm 3 and 2 = 1232 cm 3 ⇒ x x According to question, = ⇒ 616¹232¹ 3 π r¹ 2 ℎ 1³ π r² 2 ℎ = ⇒ 616¹232¹ 3 π r¹ 2 × 12¹ 3 π r² 2 × 12 = : = 1 : ⇒ r¹ 2 r² 2¹ 2 ⇒ r¹ r² 2 Now, : = 1 : 2 ⇒ π r¹ 2 π r² 2 Required percentage = × 100² − 1 "},
+{"id": "P1605", "q": "Three solid iron cubes of edges 8 cm, 10 cm and 12 cm are melted together to make a new cube. It is observed that 496 cm³ of the melted material is lost due to improper handling. The area (in cm²) of the whole surface of the newly formed cube is : Matriculation Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1331", "1176", "2197", "3375"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cubes = + + 8³ 1⁰ 3 = 512 + 1000 + 1728 = 3240¹ 2³ c m³ Remaining volume of cube = 3240 - 496 = 2744 c m³ = 2744 a = 14 cm a³ ⇒ Area of whole surface of the newly formed cube ( )⁶ a² = 6 × 14 × 14 = 1176 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1606", "q": "If the semi-perimeter and area of a rectangular field whose length and breadth are 'x' and 'y' is 12 cm and 28 cm², respectively, then find the value of x⁴ + x²y² + y⁴ . Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["6690", "6960", "6609", "6906"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Semiperimeter = = x + y = 12² ( x + y )² Area of rectangle = 28 xy = 28 Now, (x + y = + + (xy + xy) )² x² y² (x + y - xy = + + xy )² x² y² - 28 = + + xy 1² 2 x² y² 116 = + + xy x² y² Again, (x + y = + + (3xy - xy) )² x² y² (x + y - 3xy = + - xy )² x² y² - 28 × 3 = + - xy 1² 2 x² y² 60 = + - xy x² y² then, x⁴ + x²y² + y⁴ = ( + + xy)( + - x² y² x² y²"},
+{"id": "P1607", "q": "The sum of the radius of the base and the height of a cylinder is 42 m. If the total surface area of the cylinder is 6336 , find the curved surface area of the m² cylinder correct to two places of decimals (use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["2157.43", "2571.43 m² m²", "2715.43", "2517.43 m² m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of cylinder = (h + r)² π r⁶336 = 2 × 22⁷ × r × 42 = = 24 m r⁶336²2 × 12 Curved surface area of cylinder = h² π r = = 2715.43² × 22⁷ × 24 × 18 m²"},
+{"id": "P1608", "q": "A spherical ball of diameter 8 cm is cut into two equal parts. The curved area of one such part has to be painted with green colour, while the other part has to be painted with red colour. The bases of both the hemispheres are to be painted with blue colour. The cost of painting with blue is ₹2/cm², while the Search on TG: @apna_pdf cost of painting the curved area is ₹3/cm². What will be the cost (in₹) of painting the hemispheres? Take л = 3.14 Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["₹451.92", "₹492.92", "₹803.84", "₹401.92"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of hemisphere = 2 π r² Cost for green colour = 3 × (2 × 3.14 × 4 × 4) = 301.44 Rs. Cost for red colour = = 301.44 Rs. 3 × 2 × 3 . 14 × 4 × 4 ( ) Area of two bases = + = π r² π r² 2 π r² = = 100.48² × 3 . 14 × 4 × 4 ( ) The cost of painting with blue = = 200.96 Rs. 2 ×100 ."},
+{"id": "P1609", "q": "A sector of radius 10.5 cm with the central angle is folded to form a¹20 ◦ cone by joining the two bounding radii of the sector. What is the volume (in ) of cm 3 the cone so formed ?", "o": ["343² 6 π 343³ 6 π", "343³ 12 π 343² 12 π"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height of the cone = radius of the sector And θ 360 × perimeter of the circle = perimeter of the base of the cone Let the radius of cone = r = 120³60 × 2 × π × 10 . 5² × π × r r = 3.5 ⇒ Height of the cone = l² − r² = = 7 ( 10 . 5 )² − ( 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1610", "q": "A diagonal of a quadrilateral is 40 cm. The length of the perpendicular to the opposite ends is 7.5 cm and 8.6 cm. What is the area (in cm 2 ) of quadrilateral?", "o": ["434", "322", "368", "28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area = 20 × ( 7 . 5 + 8 . 6 ) = 322 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1611", "q": "A hemispherical bowl of internal radius 15 cm contains a liquid. The liquid is to be filled into cylindrical shaped bottles of diameter 5 cm and height 6 cm. The number of bottles required to empty the bowl is:", "o": ["40", "30", "60", "50"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given , internal radius of hemispherical bowl = 15cm Diameter and height of cylindrical shaped bottles = 5cm and 6cm Number of bottles required to empty the bowl Search on TG: @apna_pdf = Volume of ℎemispℎerical bowl volume of cylindrical sℎape bottles = = = 60² 3 π r³ π r² ℎ 2³ × 15 × 15 × 15⁵ 2 × 5² × 6"},
+{"id": "P1612", "q": "ABCDEF is a regular hexagon, and m ( ) = 12 cm. What is the area (in AD cm 2 ) of the given hexagon ?", "o": ["216", "54", "108", "162³ 3³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Each diagonal of hexagon = 2 × side( ) a So, = = 6 cm a¹2² Now, are of hexagon = 3³ 2 a² = = 54 cm 2³ 3² × ( 6 )²³"},
+{"id": "P1613", "q": "A hemispherical container of total surface area 7392 cm² is filled with oil. However, of the container is empty. 1⁴ This oil is to be transferred in small hemispherical bottles having radius of 6.3 cm. How many bottles will be required (rounded off to the nearest whole number)? (Take π = .)²2⁷", "o": ["351", "66", "75", "156"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of hemisphere = 3 π r² According to the question, 3 = 7392 π r² = 7392 × × = 784 r² 7²2¹ 3 Radius ( ) = = 28 r⁷84 of the hemispherical container is 1⁴ tℎ empty So, total volume of oil container = × = × × × cm 3³ 4² 3 π r³ 3⁴ 2³ 22⁷ ( 28 )³ Now, oil is to be transferred in small hemispherical bottles Then, volume per bottle = 2³ π r³ = × cm 3²"},
+{"id": "P1614", "q": "The side of a square exceeds the side of another square by 3 cm and the sum of the areas of the two squares is 225 cm 2 . Find the sum of the perimeter (in cm) of both squares.", "o": ["84", "74", "64", "94"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of one square = x cm Side of another square = x + 3 According to question = 225 ⇒ x² + ( x + 3 )² + + 9 + 6x = 225 ⇒ x² x² 2 + 6x - 216 = 0 + 3x - 108 = 0 ⇒ x² ⇒ x² + 12x - 9x - 108 = 0 ⇒ x² x (x + 12) - 9 (x + 12) = 0 ⇒ (x - 9) (x +12) = 0 ⇒ x = 9 , -12 ∴ Sides of two square are = 9 and 12 Hence sum of the perimeter of both the square are = 4 × 9 + 4 × 12 = 84 "},
+{"id": "P1615", "q": "The external curved surface area of a metallic hemispherical bowl is 308 cm 2 . If the density of metal is 8.7 gm per cm 3 , then the mass of the bowl is equal to: (Take = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["6254.2 gm", "6252.4 gm", "5262.4 gm", "5264.2 gm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CSA of a hemisphere = 2 π r² 308 = 2 × × 22⁷ r² = = 49 r = 7 cm r² 308 × 7² × 22 ⇒ Volume of the hemisphere = 2³ π r³ = × × 7 × 7 × 7 = 718.66 cm 3² 3²2⁷ Now, 1 cm 3 = 8.7 gm 718.66 cm 3 = 718.66 × 8.7 = 6252.342 gm 6252.4 gm ≈"},
+{"id": "P1616", "q": "A cylindrical vessel of height 14 cm has outer and inner radii 14 cm and 10 cm, respectively. It is to be filled by transferring water in it by using a small cylinder of height 7 cm and outer and inner radii 7 cm and 5 cm, respectively. What will be the unfilled height of the big vessel after transferring water 6 times by using the smaller cylinder? (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["2.2 cm", "3.5 cm", "2.9 cm", "3.8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Internal Volume of the large cylindrical vessel ( ) = V L π r¹ 2 ℎ 1 = × 10 × 10 × 14 = 1400 π π cm 3 Internal Volume of small cylindrical vessel ( ) = V S π r² 2 ℎ 2 = × 5 × 5 × 7 = 175 π π cm 3 Unfilled volume of big vessel after transferring 6 times = 1400 - 6¹75 π × π = 1400 - 1050 = 350 π π π cm 3 Now, Unfilled volume of big vessel = 350 π cm 3 = 350 = = 3.5 cm π r³ 2 ℎ "},
+{"id": "P1617", "q": "A cylindrical tube, which is open at both ends, is crafted from a metal. The internal diameter of the tube is 12 cm, and its length is 35 cm. The metal throughout has a thickness of 2 cm. Determine the total surface area (in cm 2 ) of the metal tube. (Take 𝜋 = )²2⁷", "o": ["3696", "3256", "3854", "3145"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Inner radius( ) = = 6 cm r¹2² Outer radius( ) = 6 + 2 = 8 cm R Length ( ) = 35 cm ℎ T.S.A. of cylindrical tube = C.S.A of inner part + C.S.A of outer part + area of rings Now, C.S.A of inner part + C.S.A of outer part :- = 2 = 2 × × 35 × (8 + 6) π ℎ ( R + r )²2⁷ = 3080 cm 2 For area of two ring :- 2 × = 2 × × [(8)² - (6)² ] π( R² − r² )²2⁷ = 2 × × = 176 cm 2²2⁷ [ 64"},
+{"id": "P1618", "q": "The perimeter of a rhombus is 160 cm and one of its diagonals has a length 50 cm. Find the area (in cm 2 ) of the rhombus.", "o": ["280", "300³9³9", "250", "175³9³9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of rhombus (4 ) = 160 a Side of rhombus( ) = 40 cm a Now, = ( )² + ( )² a² d¹ 2 d² 2 = ( )² + ( )² ( 40 )² d¹ 2⁵0² 1600 = ( )² + 625 ( )² = 975 d¹ 2 ⇒ d¹ 2 = = = 10 cm d¹ 975 × 4³900³9 Area of rhombus = × × 1² d¹ d² = × 10 × 50 = 250 cm 2¹ 2³9³9"},
+{"id": "P1619", "q": "The diameter of a hollow hemisphere is 30 cm. Water is filled in it up to its brim. When spherical lead shots each of radius 0.75 cm are dropped into the hemisphere, two-fifth of the water flows out. How many lead shots were dropped into the hemisphere ?", "o": ["1575", "2250", "1600", "1380"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of hemisphere = = ( × × 15 × 15 × 15)²³ π r³ 2³ π cm 3 Water displaced out = × × × 15 × 15 × 15 ) ( 2⁵ 2³ π cm 3 Volume of lead shot = 4³ π r³ = ( × 0.75 × 0.75 × 0.75 )⁴³ π cm 3 No of lead shots drop in the hemisphere = = 1600² 5 × 2³ × π × 15 × 15 × 15⁴ 3 π × 0 . 75 × 0 . 75 × 0 ."},
+{"id": "P1620", "q": "In a conical tent of diameter 13.2 m and vertical height 14 m, how many full bags of wheat can be emptied, if the space required for the wheat in each bag is 29.04 m³ ? [Use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["25", "28", "22", "21"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the cone = h¹ 3 π r² = × × × × 14¹ 3²2⁷ 13 . 2² 13 . 2² = 11 × 4.4 × 13.2 = 638.88 cm 3 According to question, Number of bags = ⇒ 638 . 88²9 ."},
+{"id": "P1621", "q": "If the radii of two right circular cylinders are in the ratio of 2 : 3 and their heights are in the ratio of 5 : 4, then find the ratio of their curved surface areas ?", "o": ["6 : 5", "5 : 6", "6 : 10", "10 : 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "curved surface area of cylinde r¹ curved surface area of cylinde r² = = = 2 π RH 2 π rℎ 2 × 5³ × 4⁵ 6 Required ratio = 5 : 6"},
+{"id": "P1622", "q": "From a circle with the radius of 15.75 cm, a sector with the arc length of 11 cm is cut off. Find the area (in cm 2 ) of this sector.", "o": ["86.525", "86.625 Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "86.875", "86.125"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector = × × 1² l r = × 11 × 15.75 = 86.625¹ 2 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1623", "q": "If a right circular cone of height 24 cm has a volume of 1232 cm 3 , then the total surface area of the cone is (use = ) : π 22⁷", "o": ["806 cm 2", "704 cm 2", "904 cm 2", "608 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cone = h¹ 3 π r² 1232 = × × × 24¹ 3²2⁷ r² 1232 = = 176⁷ r² ⇒ r² 1232 × 7¹76 = = 49 r = 7 cm r² ⇒ Slant height = = = 25 cm 7² + 2⁴ 2⁶25 TSA of cone = r(r + l) π = × 7(7 + 25) = 22 × 32 = 704²2⁷ c m²"},
+{"id": "P1624", "q": "A rectangular courtyard is 4m⁹5cm long and 16m⁶5cm broad. It is to be paved with the square tiles of the same size. Find the least number of such square tiles required to pave the rectangular courtyard.", "o": ["877", "944", "388", "407"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length = 495 cm Search on TG: @apna_pdf Width = 1665 cm Now, finding HCF of (495 and 1665) = 3 (remainder = 180)¹665⁴95 = 2 (remainder = 135)⁴95¹80 = 1 (remainder = 45)¹80¹35 = 3 (remainder = 0)¹35⁴5 HCF (495 , 1665) = 45 So, dimension of per required tile = 45 × 45 cm 2 Area of the courtyard = 495 × 1665 cm 2 Hence, required tiles = 495 × 1665⁴5 × 45 = 11 × 37 = 407"},
+{"id": "P1625", "q": "The height of a cylinder is 20 cm. The lateral surface area is 1760 cm 2 . Its volume is:", "o": ["12032 cm 3", "12302 cm 3", "12203 cm 3", "12320 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "lateral surface area of cylinder = 2 r h = 1760 π = 2 r²0 = 1760 ⇒ r = 14 × 22⁷ × × volume of cylinder = 14 × 14²0²2⁷ × × = 12320 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1626", "q": "A chord of the larger among two concentric circles is of length 20 cm and it is tangent to the smaller circle. What is the area (in cm 2 ) of the annular portion between the two circles ?", "o": ["100", "164", "122", "175 π π π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In the right angled OCA ∆ = + ⇒ = 100 R² ( 10 )² r² R² − r² Area of annular portion = (R² - r² ) π = 100 cm 2 π"},
+{"id": "P1627", "q": "Find the length of the longest stick that can be fitted in a cubical vessel of edge 70 cm.", "o": ["35 cm", "70 cm 3³", "10 cm", "70 cm 3²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of a cube = a³ = × 70 = 70 cm 3³"},
+{"id": "P1628", "q": "If the height and diameter of a cylinder are 12 cm and 28 cm, respectively, then find the ratio of the total surface area to the curved surface Search on TG: @apna_pdf area.", "o": ["13 : 5", "10 : 3", "13 : 6", "11 : 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Height and diameter of a cylinder are 12 cm and 28cm Total surface area of cylinder = 2 r(r + h) π = 2 × × 14 (14 + 12) = 88 × 26²2⁷ Curved Surface area of cylinder = 2 π rℎ = 2 × × 14 × 12 = 88 × 12²2⁷ The ratio of the total surface area to the curved surface area = 88 × 26 : 88 × 12 = 13 : 6"},
+{"id": "P1629", "q": "The perimeter of a rectangular garden is 48 m. If the length is 6 m more than the breadth, the area (in m² ) of the garden is:", "o": ["135", "96", "84", "112"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let breadth of the rectangular garden = x m Length of the rectangular garden = (x + 6) m Perimeter of rectangular garden [2(l + b)] = 48 m² (x + 6 + x ) = 48²x + 6 = 24 ⇒ ⇒ 2x = 18 x = 9m ⇒ ⇒ Length = 15 m and breadth = 9 m Area of rectangular garden = l × b = 15 × 9 = 135 m²"},
+{"id": "P1630", "q": "If three cubes of volume 512 cm 3 each are joined end to end, find the surface area of the resulting cuboid.", "o": ["896 cm 2", "986 cm 2", "895 cm 2", "869 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of each cube = 512 cm 3 ∴ Side of cube = = 8 cm 3⁵12 Now by joining three cube , length of the cuboid = 8 +8 + 8 = 24 cm Breadth = 8 cm and height = 8 cm ∴ Surface area = 2 ( lb + bℎ + ℎl ) = 2 (24 × 8 + 8 × 8 +8 × 24) = 2 (192 + 64 + 192 ) = 896 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1631", "q": "The base radius of a circular cylinder is 10.5 cm. If the area of its curved surface is 792 cm 2 , then what is the volume of the cylinder?", "o": ["4185 cm 3", "4518 cm 3", "4152 cm 3", "4158 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Base radius = 10.5cm Curved surface area of cylinder (2 π rℎ ) = 792 cm 2 h = = 12 cm 792 × 7 × 10² × 22 × 105 volume of the cylinder = π r² ℎ = × 10.5 × 10.5 × 12 = 4158 cm 3²2⁷"},
+{"id": "P1632", "q": "In a rectangular field, the sum of the length and the breadth is 9 cm and area is 18 cm². If the length is 'a' and breadth is 'b', then find the value of (a² - ab + b²).", "o": ["36", "24", "18", "27"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "given, (a + b) = 9 and ab = 18 We know that, (a - b) = ( a + b )² − 4 ab = = = = 3 ( 9 )² − 4 × 18⁸1 − 72⁹ then, (a + b) = 9 …..(i) (a - b) = 3 …."},
+{"id": "P1633", "q": "The total surface area of a closed cube is given as 1152 cm 2 . What is the length (in cm) of each side of the cube?", "o": ["9", "4", "8", "8² 13³ 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of cube = 6a² 1152 = 6a² a² = 192 a = 8 cm ⇒ ⇒ ⇒ 3"},
+{"id": "P1634", "q": "The volume of a right circular cylindrical box of radius 30cm is 600cm 3 . Find the height of the box.", "o": ["0.61cm", "0.31cm", "0.51cm", "0.21cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a right circular cylindrical box ( = 600cm 3 π R² ℎ ) × 30 × 30 × h = 600 ⇒ 22⁷ h = = = 0.21cm ⇒ 600 × 7²2 × 30 × 30⁷ 33"},
+{"id": "P1635", "q": "The ratio of the length, the breadth, and the height of a solid cuboid is given as 3 : 2 : 1, and the breadth of this cuboid is given as 12 cm. Find the volume (in cm 3 ) of the cuboid.", "o": ["1250", "1296", "1200", "1500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length : breadth : height = 3 : 2 : 1 Breadth (2 unit) = 12 cm Length (3 unit) = 18 cm Height (1 unit) = 6 cm Volume = 18 × 12 × 6 = 1296 c m³"},
+{"id": "P1636", "q": "From a point A, which is at a distance of 17 cm from the centre C of a circle with radius 8 cm, the pair of tangents AB and AD to the circle are drawn. The area of the quadrilateral ABCD is _______ cm 2 .", "o": ["192", "120", "60", "360"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ∆ ABC ∠ABC = … (radius tangent)⁹0 ° ⊥ hence, = = AB AC 2 − BC 2¹7² − 8² = = = 15 cm 289 − 64²25 Area of = × base × height ∆ ABC 1² = × AB × BC = × 15 × 8 = 60¹ 2¹ 2 cm 2 Area of quadrilateral ABCD = 2 × Area of = 2 × 60 = 120 ∆ ABC cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1637", "q": "The surface area of a sphere is 2464 cm 2 . Find its volume.", "o": ["13121 cm 3", "11498 cm 3¹ 3² 3", "11892 cm 3", "11621 cm 3² 3¹ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of sphere = 4 π r² 4 = 2464⁴ × × = 2464 π r² ⇒ 22⁷ r² = 2464 × × = 196 r² 7²2¹ 4 = = 14 cm r¹96 Now, volume of sphere = 4³ π r³ = × = 11498 cm 3⁴ 3²2⁷ × ( 14 )³² 3"},
+{"id": "P1638", "q": "The capacity of a cylinder tank is 8316 cm 3 . If the radius of its base is 21 cm, then find the depth of the tank.", "o": ["6 cm", "8 cm", "4 cm", "10 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Capacity of cylinder = 8316 cm 3 = 8316 × 21 × 21 × = 8316 π r² ℎ ⇒ 22⁷ ℎ = 8316 × = 6 cm ℎ 7²2 × 21 × 21"},
+{"id": "P1639", "q": "If the diameter of a hemisphere is 42 cm, then the volume of hemisphere (in cm 3 ) is : Take = π 22⁷", "o": ["19154", "19254", "19444", "19404"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the hemisphere = 2³ π r³ Volume of the hemisphere = × × 21 × 21 × 21² 3²2⁷ Volume of the hemisphere = 19404 cm³"},
+{"id": "P1640", "q": "The radius and height of a cylinder are in the ratio 6 : 7 and its volume is 792 cm 3 . Calculate its curved surface area in cm 2", "o": ["262", "490", "264", "226"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the cylinder = π r² ℎ = × = 792²2⁷ 6 x ( )² ( 7 x ) = = 1 so x = 1 x³ 792 × 7²2 × 36 × 7 So, the radius and height of the cylinder will be 6 and 7 Now, according to the question, CSA of the cylinder = 2 π rℎ = 2 × × 6 × 7 = 264 cm 2²2⁷"},
+{"id": "P1641", "q": "The curved surface area of a right circular cylinder of height 14 cm, is 88 cm 2 . Find the total surface area of the cylinder.", "o": ["cm 2", "cm 2³60⁷ 660⁷", "cm 2", "cm 2⁵60⁷ 460⁷"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CSA of the cylinder = 2 π rℎ 88 = 2 × × r × 14 r = 1 cm 22⁷ ⇒ Search on TG: @apna_pdf TSA of cylinder = 2 π r ( ℎ + r ) = 2 × × 1(14 + 1) = cm 2²2⁷ 660⁷"},
+{"id": "P1642", "q": "The area of a rectangular field is 3600 m² . If the field is 45 m long, what is its perimeter ?", "o": ["255 m", "260 m", "250 m", "265 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the rectangle = length × breadth 3600 = 45 × breadth Breadth = 80 m Perimeter of the rectangular field = 2(length + breadth) = 2(45 + 80) = 250 m"},
+{"id": "P1643", "q": "If the surface area of cuboid is 108 m² , then find the height of the cuboid, whose length is 6 m and breadth is 3 m.", "o": ["5.5 m", "5 m", "4.5m", "4 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cuboid = 2(lb + bh + hl)¹08 = 2(6 × 3 + 3h + 6h)⁵4 = 18 + 9h ⇒ h = = 4 m⁵4 − 18⁹"},
+{"id": "P1644", "q": "For a given circle of radius 4 cm, the angle of its sector is 45°. Find the area (in cm 2 ) of the sector. (Use π = 3.14.)", "o": ["7.28", "6.28", "6.18", "7.18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector = θ 360 π r² = = 45³60 × 3 . 14 × ( 4 )²¹ 8 × 3 . 14 × 16 = 6.28 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1645", "q": "If the area of a triangle whose base measures 6 cm is 18 cm 2 , then its height is:", "o": ["6 cm", "3.1 cm", "9 cm", "2.2 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of triangle = × base × height 1² 18 = × 6 × height Height = 6 cm 1² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1646", "q": "If the diameter of the base and curved surfaced area of a cylinder are 14cm and 352 cm 2 ,respectively, then the total surface area of the cylinder is equal to:", "o": ["660 cm 2", "654 cm 2", "760 cm 2", "754 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CSA of the cylinder = 2πrh 352 = 2 × × 7 × h h = 8 cm 22⁷ ⇒ TSA of the cylinder = 2πr(h + r) = 2 × × 7(8 + 7) = 44 × 15 = 660 cm 2²2⁷"},
+{"id": "P1647", "q": "From a circle, a sector with a central angle of 30° is cut off. If the length of the arc of this sector is 5.5 cm, then find the radius (in cm) of the circle. [Use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["12", "10", "11", "10.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the arc = × 2 θ 360 π r⁵.5 = × 2 × × r³0³60²2⁷ r = = 10.5 cm 42 × 5 . 5²2"},
+{"id": "P1648", "q": "The length, breadth and height of a cuboid are in ratio of 3 : 4 : 5. If the volume of the cuboid is 1620 m³ , find the total surface area of the cuboid.", "o": ["646 m²", "846 m²", "423 m²", "712 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : the ratio of cuboid dimensions = 3 : 4 : 5 Let length(l) = 3 , breadth(b) = 4 and x x height(h) = 5 x According to question, Volume of cube = l × b × h³ × 4 × 5 = 1620⁶0 = 1620 ⇒ x x x ⇒ x³ = 27 = 3 units ⇒ x³ ⇒ x Total surface area of cuboid = 2(lb + bh + hl) = 2(12 + 20 + 15 ) x² x² x² = 2 × 47 = 2 × 47 × 9 = 846 x² m²"},
+{"id": "P1649", "q": "If the length, breadth and total surface area of a cuboid are 30 cm, 20 cm and 2600 cm 2 , respectively, then find its height.", "o": ["50 cm", "30 cm", "14 cm", "15 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of cuboid = 2(lb + bh + hl)²600 = 2(30 × 20 + 20 × h + h × 30)²600 = 2(600 + 50h) ⇒ 2600 = 1200 + 100h ⇒ 100h = 1400 height (h) = 14 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1650", "q": "Two similar triangles have area 490 sq . cm. and 640 sq . cm. If the length of the one side of the first triangle is 21 cm, then what is the length of the corresponding side of the second triangle?", "o": ["16 cm", "14 cm", "24 cm", "21 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, = ⇒ Area of ∆ ABC Area of ∆ PQR AB 2 PQ 2 = = ⇒ 490⁶40²1² PQ 2 ⇒ 49⁶4²1² PQ 2 Taking square root both side, = PQ = 24 cm ⇒ 7⁸ 21 PQ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1651", "q": "The diameter of a roller is 35 cm and its length is 100 cm. It takes 200 complete revolutions to level a playground. Find the area of the playground in m²", "o": ["220", "2,20,00,000", "1,10,000", "110"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: radius = cm and length = 100 cm 35² Surface area of a roller = 2 × × × 100 = 11000 cm 2²2⁷ 35² 1 revolution of roller = surface area of a roller 200 revolution = 11000 × 200 = 2200000 cm 2 = 220 m² Hence, Area of the playground = 220 m²"},
+{"id": "P1652", "q": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 3.5 cm, its surface area increases by 550 cm 2 . What was the original radius of the sphere ? Search on TG: @apna_pdf (use = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["4 cm", "4.5 cm", "6 cm", "3.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of sphere = 4 π r² According to the question, 4 - 4 = 550 π( r + 3 . 5 )² π( r )²⁴ [ = 550 π ( r + 3 . 5 )² − r² ] [ = 550 × ( r + 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1653", "q": "The area of an isosceles right angled triangle is 16 m² . Its hypotenuse is _______.", "o": ["0.8 m", "8 m", "4 m", "8 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of isosceles right angle triangle = ( )² ℎypotenuse 2¹6 = ( )² Hypotenuse = 8 m ℎypotenuse 2 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1654", "q": "The length of a rectangular shaped park exceeds its breadth by 15 m. If the perimeter of the park is 110 m, find the length of the park (in m).", "o": ["35", "40", "25", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let breadth of park be m x Length = ( + 15) m x Perimeter of rectangular park = 2[( + 15) + ( )] = 4 + 30 x x x According to question, 4 + 30 = 110 = 20 x ⇒ x Length of rectangular park = + 15 = 35 m x"},
+{"id": "P1655", "q": "If the lateral surface area of a cube is 144 cm 2 , then find its volume.", "o": ["864 cm 3", "1728 cm 3", "117.58 cm 3", "216 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area of cube = 4a² 4a² = 144 a = 6 cm ⇒ Volume of cube (a³ ) = 6³ = 216 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1656", "q": "If the areas of three adjacent faces of a cuboid are 5 cm 2 , 15 cm 2 , 27 cm 2 , respectively, the surface area of the cuboid is:", "o": ["75 cm 2", "47 cm 2", "45 cm 2", "94 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of cuboid = 2(lb + bh + hl) = 2(5 + 15 + 27) = 94 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1657", "q": "A cuboidal water purifier can carry 10 litres of water. Its breadth is 1⁵ of its height and length is of the sum 1³ of the breadth and height. The height of the tank is:", "o": ["20 cm", "10 cm", "80 cm", "50 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, 1 litre = 1000 c m³ Then, 10 litres = 10000 c m³ Let the height be15 x Breadth of cuboidal water purifier = × 15 = 3¹ 5 x x Length of cuboidal water purifier = (3 + 15 ) = 6¹ 3 x x x Now, volume of cuboidal water purifier = 3 × 6 × 15 = 270¹0000 = 270 x x x x³ ⇒ x³ = = 1000²7 x³ ⇒ x¹0³ So, the height of cuboidal water purifier = 15 × = 50 cm 10³"},
+{"id": "P1658", "q": "The curved surface area of a right circular cone is 20 cm 2 . If its radius is 4 π cm, then find the volume of cone.", "o": ["21 cm 3", "20 cm 3 π π", "16 cm 3", "18 cm 3 π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of cone = π rl According to the question, = 20 π × 4 × l π Slant height ( ) = 5 cm l Height of cone(h) = l² − r² = = = 3 cm ( 5 )² − ( 4 )²⁹ Now, volume of cone = 1³ π r² ℎ × = 16 cm 3 ⇒ 1³ π × ( 4 )² × 3 π"},
+{"id": "P1659", "q": "The volume of the rectangular block is 12288 m³ . Its dimensions are in the ratio of 4 : 3 : 2. If the entire surface is polished at the rate 2 paise per m² ,then find the total cost of polishing :", "o": ["₹44.42", "₹11.14", "₹66.56", "₹33.28 SSC CPO 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length = 4 , Breadth = 3 , Height = 2 x x x Volume = 12288 = 12288 ⇒ l × b × ℎ = 12288⁴ x × 3 x × 2 x²4 = 12288 = 512 = 8 x³ ⇒ x³ ⇒ x Hence, Length = 4 = 4⁸ = 32 m x × Breadth = 3 = 3⁸ = 24 m x × Height = 2 = 2⁸ = 16 m x × Total surface area of box = 2( + + ) lb bℎ ℎl = 2( + + )⁴ x × 3 x³ x × 2 x² x × 4 x = 2( + + ) = 2 ( )¹2 x² 6 x² 8 x² 26 x² = 52 = 52⁶4 = 332"},
+{"id": "P1660", "q": "The base of a parallelogram is twice its height. If the area of the parallelogram is 338 cm 2 , then find its height (in cm).", "o": ["13", "11", "14", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of parallelogram = Base(b) × Height(h) According to the question, b = 2h³38 = 2h × h ⇒ 338 = 2 = 169 h = 13 cm ⇒ ℎ 2 ⇒ ℎ 2 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1661", "q": "What is the total surface area of a cone whose radius is and slant height r⁴ is 4 ? l", "o": ["8πr( + r )", "πr( + ) l l r¹6", "πr( + )", "4πr( + r) l r⁴ l Q.283 . How many metres of cloth will be required to make a conical tent, the radius of whose base is 21 metres and height is 28 metres. The width of the cloth is 5 metres. (Where π = )²2⁷ SSC CPO 27/06/2024 (1st Shift)", "470", "462", "456", "478"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of cone = R(L+ R) π = (4 + ) π r⁴ l r⁴ = × 4( + ) = πr( + ) π r⁴ l r¹6 l r¹6"},
+{"id": "P1662", "q": "The volume of a cube is four times the volume of a cuboid. If the sides of the cuboid are 32 cm, 8 cm and 4 cm, then find the ratio of the total surface area of the cube to that of the cuboid.", "o": ["23 : 13", "24 : 13", "21 : 13", "22 : 13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cube = 4 × volume of cuboid = 4 × 32 × 8 × 4 = 4096 a = 16 a³ ⇒ Now, TSA of cube TSA of cuboid = 6 × 16 × 16² ( 32 × 8 + 8 × 4 + 32 × 4 ) = = = 24 : 13⁶ × 16 × 16⁸32²4¹3"},
+{"id": "P1663", "q": "The length of the largest possible rod that can be placed in a cubical room is 42 m. The surface area (in m²) of 3 the largest possible sphere that fit within the cubical room is: [Use = ] π 22⁷", "o": ["3590", "4589", "2564", "5544 Q.287 .Find the area of a minor sector of a circle whose circumference is 88 cm and the length of its minor arc is 22 cm (use = ). π 22⁷ SSC CPO 27/06/2024 (2nd Shift)", "154 cm 2", "451 cm 2", "415 cm 2", "145 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the largest possible rod which can be placed in cubical room = a⁴2 = a a = 3 ⇒ 3³ ⇒ 42 m Required TSA of sphere = 4 × × = 5544 m² 22⁷ ( 42² )²"},
+{"id": "P1664", "q": "A drainage tile is a cylindrical shell 42 cm long. The inside and outside diameters are 8 cm and 14 cm, respectively. What is the volume (in cm 3 ) of clay required for the tile? ((Use = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["5241", "4356", "4881", "4125"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cylindrical shell = π( R² − r² ) ℎ = ( )⁴2²2⁷ × 7² − 4² × Search on TG: @apna_pdf = 22 (49 - 16)⁶ × × = 22³3⁶ = 4356 × × c m³"},
+{"id": "P1665", "q": "The distance between the parallel sides of a trapezium is 18 cm. If the area of the trapezium is 1188 cm 2 , then what is the sum of the lengths of the parallel sides?", "o": ["150 cm", "115 cm", "126 cm", "132 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of trapezium = sum of parallel sides height 1² × × ⇒ 1188 = sum of parallel sides 18¹ 2 × × sum of parallel sides = 132 cm"},
+{"id": "P1666", "q": "A school has two rectangular playgrounds, which are similar in shape. If the length and the breadth of the first playground are given as 224 m and 160 m, respectively, then which of the following options CANNOT be the dimensions of the second playground ?", "o": ["Length = 273 m; Breadth = 195 m", "Length = 168 m; Breadth = 120 m", "Length = 210 m; Breadth = 150 m", "Length = 343 m; Breadth = 255 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If both playgrounds are similar then their dimension must be in proportion. First playground = = = lengtℎ breadtℎ 224¹60⁷ 5 By checking option one by one we find that option (d) does not have the same ratio of length and breadth as the first playground."},
