+{"id": "P1674", "q": "If the cylinder height is 9 cm and the base area is 25 cm², then find the π total surface area. Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["240 cm 2", "140 cm 2", "440 cm 2", "340 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, Height of cylinder = 9 cm the base area = 25 cm² π = 25 cm² r = 5 cm ⇒ π r² π ⇒ Now, Total Surface Area = 2 rh + 2 π π r² TSA of cylinder = 2⁵ 9 + 2²5 × 22⁷ × × × 22⁷ × = 2⁵ (9 + 5) × 22⁷ × = 2⁵ 14 = 440 cm² × 22⁷ × ×"},
+{"id": "P1675", "q": "The height of one cone is 3 times the height of another cone, while its radius is half of the radius of the other cone. If their total volume is 100 unit³, then the difference in the volumes of the cones is _______ unit³. Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["12.5", "14.3", "13.4", "15.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let height of the first cone = 3h And height of the second cone = h Radius of first cone = r And radius of the second cone = 2r Total volume(V) = volume of first cone + volume of second cone V = 3h + 4 h ⇒ 1³ π r² 1³ π r² 100 = ( . 3h + 4 h) ⇒ 1³ π r² r² 100 = (7 h) h = ⇒ 1³ π r² ⇒ r² 300⁷ π Now, Difference between the volume of cones = (4 ."},
+{"id": "P1676", "q": "A cube is having surface area of 5400 square units. Its volume would increase approximately ________ if the side is increased by 5 units. Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["59%", "45%", "55%", "50%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of cube = 5400 square units 6 = 5400 = 900 a = 30 unit ⇒ a² ⇒ a² ⇒ Volume of cube = = 27000 Unit 3 a³ Now, New side = 30 + 5 = 35 unit New Volume of cube = 35³5³5 = 42875 Unit 3 × × Increment in volume = 42875 − 27000²7000 × 100 = 100 = 58.79 ≈ 59 % 15875²7000 ×"},
+{"id": "P1677", "q": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 2 cm, its surface area increases by 704 cm². What was the radius of the sphere before the increase? (Use π = )²2⁷ Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["14 cm", "11 cm", "12 cm", "13 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let radius = r cm Surface Area of sphere = 4 ⇒ π r² cm 2 New radius = r + 2 cm New surface area of sphere = 4 π( r + 2 )² cm 2 According to question, 4 - 4 = 704 π ( r + 2 )² π r² 4 ( + 4 + 4 r - ) = 704 ⇒ × 22⁷ r² r² 4 + 4r = 56⁴r = 52 r = 13 cm ⇒ ⇒ ⇒"},
