+{"id": "P1679", "q": "There is a large cone with a diameter of 14 m and height of 12 m. It is being filled with water at a rate of 2 m³ in every 20 seconds. How long will it take to fill the cone? Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["313 sec", "6160 sec", "616 sec", "12320 sec"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of cone = = 7 m¹4² Volume of cone = × × × 12 = 616¹ 3²2⁷ 7² m³ Required time taken to fill the cone = × 20 = 6160 sec 616²"},
+{"id": "P1680", "q": "The volume of a cuboid is twice the volume of a cube. If the dimensions of the cuboid are 12 cm, 16 cm and 18 cm, then the total surface area of the cube is: Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["625 cm 2", "864 cm 2", "484 cm 2", "764 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cuboid = 2 × Volume of a cube 12 × 16 × 18 = 2 × Volume of a cube 3,456 = 2 × Volume of a cube Volume of a cube = 1728 = 1728 a = 12 a³ ⇒ TSA of cube = 6 = 6 × = 864 cm 2 a² 1² 2"},
+{"id": "P1681", "q": "The height of a solid cylinder is 4 times its radius. Its curved surface area is ________ times its base area. Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["2", "6", "8", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ATQ, h = 4r CSA of cylinder Base area of cylinder = = = 2 π rℎ π r² 2 π r × 4 r π r² 8¹ So, the curved surface area is 8 times its base area."},
+{"id": "P1682", "q": "The lateral surface area of a cylinder is 3862.2 cm² and its height is 15 cm. Find its volume (take π = 3.14) correct to one decimal place. Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["79175.1 cm³", "88275.2 cm³", "78275.2 cm³", "89175.1 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Lateral surface area of cylinder = 2 rh π 3862.2 = 2 × 3.14 × r × 15³862.2 = 94.2r r = 41 cm ⇒ Volume of cylinder = h π r² = 3.14 × × 15 = 79,175.1⁴ 1² c m³"},
+{"id": "P1683", "q": "The length of cold storage of cuboidal shape is double its breadth and its height is half of its breadth. If its volume is 216 m³, then what are the dimensions of the cold storage? Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["12 m × 6m × 3m", "12 m × 9m × 5m", "14 m × 7m × 5m", "8m × 4m × 2m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "L = 2B and H = B¹ 2 Volume of cubical shaped cold storage = L × B × H²16 = 2B × B × B = B = 6 m ⇒ 1² B³ ⇒ Then, L = 2 × 6 = 12 m, H = × 6 = 3 m¹ 2 So, the dimensions are 12 m × 6 m × 3 m"},
