+{"id": "P1693", "q": "A sphere and a cube have equal surface areas. The ratio of the volume of the sphere to that of the cube is: Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": [":", ": 6 𝜋 𝜋 8", ":", ": 3 𝜋 2 𝜋"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Surface area of sphere = Surface area of cube 4 = 2 = ⇒ π r² 6 a² ⇒ π r² 3 a² Take square root both side, r = a …..(i) ⇒ 2 π 3 Volume of sphere = 4³ π r³ Volume of cube = a³ Required ratio = = [from eq ."},
+{"id": "P1694", "q": "The surface area of a sphere is 2464 cm². Calculate its volume. (Use π = )²2⁷ Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["11598.67 cm³", "11478.67 cm³", "11488.67 cm³", "11498.67 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of a sphere = 2464 cm² 4 = 2464⁴ × = 2464 ⇒ π r² ⇒ 22⁷ r² = 196 r = 14 cm ⇒ r² ⇒ Hence , Volume = 4³ π r³ = 14¹4¹4⁴ 3 × 22⁷ × × × = 11498.67 cm³"},
