+{"id": "P1709", "q": "In the given figure, the length of arc AB is equal to twice the length of radius r of the circle. Find the area of sector OAB in terms of the radius r. Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["3r", "2r", "πr²", "r²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector OAB = = = lengtℎ of arc × radius 2² r × r² r²"},
+{"id": "P1710", "q": "The difference between the areas Search on TG: @apna_pdf of two concentric circles is 264 . cm 2 What is the difference between the square of their radius ? (use ) π = 22⁷", "o": ["70", "140 cm 2 cm 2", "84", "64 cm 2 cm 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the radius of the inner and outer circle be r and R respectively. According to the question, Difference between the areas of two concentric circles = 264 cm 2 - = 264 = 264 π R² π r² ⇒ π( R² − r² ) = 264²2⁷ × ( R² − r² ) = 84 R² − r² cm 2 So, option (c) is the correct answer."},
+{"id": "P1711", "q": "The volumes of two cubes are in the ratio of 8 : 27. If the volume of the larger cube is 513 more than that of cm 3 the smaller cube, find the length of each side of the smaller cube. Higher Secondary 01/08/2022 ( Shift - 3 )", "o": ["27 cm", "7 cm", "6 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cube = a³ Where a = side of a cube = Side of smaller cube Side of larger cube 3 Volume of smaller cube volume of larger cube = = Side of smaller cube Side of larger cube 3⁸ 27² 3 Then , side of smaller cube = 2x and side of larger cube = 3x According to question, 27x³ - 8x³ = 513cm 3¹9x³ = 513 ⇒ x³ = 27 x = 3 ⇒ So, Side of smaller cube = 2 × 3 = 6cm"},
+{"id": "P1712", "q": "A person uses a rectangular metallic sheet of 45 m³0 m for × making an open box. From each corner of the sheet he cut offs a square. If the length of one side of each of the squares is 10 m, then what will be the volume of the box (in m³ ) ?", "o": ["5000", "4500", "7000", "2500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When the 4 square shaped cuts are made in rectangular sheet then Length = 25m, Breadth = 10m, Height = 10m Volume - = l × b × h = 25m × 10m × 10m = 2500 m³"},
+{"id": "P1713", "q": "A square of side is taken. A p rectangle is cut out from this square Search on TG: @apna_pdf such that the length of one side of the rectangle is equal to half of the length of one side of the square and the length of another side of the rectangle is equal to of the length of the first side of the 1³ rectangle. What is the area of the portion of the square that remained after the rectangle is cut out?", "o": ["7", "8", "p", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given length of side of square = p So, length of rectangle = p² Breadth of rectangle = p⁶ Now, required area = area of square - area of rectangle = - = p² p² 12¹1 p² 12"},
+{"id": "P1714", "q": "The base of a hemispherical bowl Search on TG: @apna_pdf has a circumference of 132 cm. Find the capacity of the bowl [Use π = ]²2⁷", "o": ["18240", "19404 cm 3 cm 3", "19708", "16540 cm 3 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumference of the base of hemispherical bowl = 132 cm 2 × × r = 132 × r = 132²2⁷ ⇒ 44⁷ r = = 21 cm 132 × 7⁴4 The capacity of the bowl = × × 21 × 21 × 21 = 19404² 3²2⁷ c m³"},
+{"id": "P1715", "q": "A hemispherical depression of diameter 4 cm is cut out from each face of a cubical block of sides 10 cm. Find the surface area of the remaining solid (in ) (Use π = ) cm 2²2⁷", "o": ["900", "112⁴ 7⁴ 7", "675", "713³ 7¹ 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of the hemisphere = 2 π r² Base area of the hemisphere = π r² Effective area increase on each face of the cube = 2 – = π r² π r² π r² Area of each face of the cube = = 100 + = 112 ( 10 )² + π r² 22⁷ × 2² 4⁷ c m² Total surface area of the cube = 6 × 112 = 675⁴ 7³ 7 c m²"},
+{"id": "P1716", "q": "The radius of a spherical balloon is inflated from 3.5 cm to 4.9 cm by pushing air into it. What is the percentage increase in the volume of the Search on TG: @apna_pdf original balloon ?", "o": ["74.4%", "174.4%", "73.6%", "173.6%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of old radius to new radius = 3.5 : 4.9 = 5 : 7. Old : New Radius 5 : 7 Volume : 5³ 7³ 125 : 343 Required percentage increase = × 100 = 174.4% 343 − 125¹25"},
+{"id": "P1717", "q": "The difference between the areas of two concentric circles is 88 . If the cm 2 radius of the inner circle is 6 cm then the area ( in ) of the larger circle is cm 2 closest to: (Use π = )²2⁷", "o": ["196", "201", "197", "198"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Difference between areas of two concentric circles = 88 cm 2 = 88 = 88 π R² − π r² ⇒ π( R² − r² ) = 88²2⁷ ( R² − 6² ) = 28 = 64 R² − 36 ⇒ R² Area of largest circle = π R² = 64 = 201.14²01²2⁷ × ≈ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1718", "q": "The area of a triangular field with sides 60 m, 175 m and 185 m is equal to that of a rectangular park whose sides are in the ratio of 21 : 10. The perimeter (in m) of the park is: Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["341", "403", "372", "310"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sides of the triangular field are triplets. Area of = Area of rectangular park ∆ 60¹75 = 21x¹0x¹ 2 × × × = 25 x = 5 x² ⇒ Perimeter of rectangular park = 2 [ 21x + 10x ] = 62x = 62 (5) = 310 m"},
+{"id": "P1719", "q": "A heap of wheat is in the form of a cone whose base diameter is 8.4 m and height is 1.75 m. The heap is to be covered by canvas. What is the area (in m² ) of the canvas required ? (π = )²2⁷", "o": ["60.06", "115.05", "63.6", "115.5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius = 4.2m, Height = 1.75m As radius and height is in the ratio of 12 : 5 So slant height = 13 unit Slant height = × 13 = 4.55 m l¹ . 75⁵ Curved surface area of the canvas = rl = 4.2 π 22⁷ × × 4 ."},
+{"id": "P1720", "q": "A chord in a circle with radius 10 cm subtends an angle of 90° at the center. What is the area of the minor segment ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["(25π - 50) sq . cm", "(100π - 50) sq . cm", "(50π - 100) sq . cm", "(25π - 100) sq . cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of sector = × × (10)² = 25⁹0° 360° π π Area of triangle = × (10)² × sin90 o = 50¹ 2 Area of minor segment = 25 - 50 π cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1721", "q": "A solid hemisphere is drilled with a cylindrical with radius hole through R⁴ its center. If the height of the removed cylinder equals the hemisphere's radius , find the ratio of the volume removed R² to the volume remaining. Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["5 : 1", "5 : 4", "3 : 4", "3 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Volume of cylinder = h π r² = ( )² × = × π R⁴ R² π R³ 32 Volume of remaining hemisphere = ( )³ - × = 2³ π R² π R³ 32⁸ π R³ − 3 π R³ 96 = 5 π R³ 96 So, Required ratio = × : π R³ 32⁵ π R³ 96 = 3 : 5"},
+{"id": "P1722", "q": "There is a slide in a park. One of its side walls, shaped like a triangle, is painted with a message: \"RESPECT NATURE, PRESERVE GREENERY.\" If the sides of the wall are 7 m, 8 m, and 9 m, what is the area painted in color ? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["12 m²", "15 m² 5⁵", "12 m²", "16 m² 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side of triangle = 7 m , 8 m , 9 m Semi-perimeter of triangle(s) = = 12 m⁷ + 8 + 9² Area of triangle = s ( s − a )( s − b )( s − c ) = = 12¹2 ×5×4×3⁵ m²"},
+{"id": "P1723", "q": "A field roller is in the shape of a cylinder whose diameter is 2.8 metres and length is 1.5 metres. If the roller rolls at a speed of 12 revolutions per minute, then find the maximum area (in m²) that it can roll in 1 hour (60 minutes). Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["9,504 m²", "8,640 m²", "9,000 m²", "10,250 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius (r) = 2 . 8² Maximum area rolled = CSA × Speed × time = 2 rh × 12 × 60 π = 2× × ×1.5 × 12 × 60 = 9,504 m² 22⁷ 2 ."},
+{"id": "P1724", "q": "A semi-circular window has a diameter of 2.8 meters. What is the total length of the frame required for this window? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["6.8 m", "7.2 m", "8.6 m", "9.0 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius = = 1.4 cm 2 . 8² Semicircle circumference = π r = × 1.4 = 4.4²2⁷ Total length = Semicircle circumference + diameter = 4.4 + 2.8 = 7.2 m"},
+{"id": "P1725", "q": "A cube is a special type of rectangular parallelepiped where: Which of the following correctly describes why a cube is considered a special type of rectangular parallelepiped? Matriculation Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["All edges (sides) are of equal length.", "The length is greater than the breadth, which equals the height.", "The length and breadth are equal, but greater than the height.", "The length, breadth, and height are all different."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All edges (sides) are of equal length Explanation: A rectangular parallelepiped has length, breadth, and height. If all three dimensions are equal, it forms a cube, making it a special case of a rectangular parallelepiped."},
+{"id": "P1726", "q": "If the semi-perimeter and area of a rectangular field whose length and breadth are 'x' and 'y' is 12 cm and 28 cm², respectively, then find the value of x⁴ + x²y² + y⁴ .", "o": ["6690", "6960", "6609", "6906"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Semiperimeter = = x + y = 12² ( x + y )² Area of rectangle = 28 xy = 28 Now, (x + y = + + (xy + xy) )² x² y² (x + y - xy = + + xy )² x² y² - 28 = + + xy 1² 2 x² y² 116 = + + xy x² y² Again, (x + y = + + (3xy - xy) )² x² y² (x + y - 3xy = + - xy )² x² y² - 28 × 3 = + - xy 1² 2 x² y² 60 = + - xy x² y² then, x⁴ + x²y² + y⁴ = ( + + xy)( + - x² y² x² y²"},
+{"id": "P1727", "q": "The weight of a circular disc varies directly as the product of the square of TG: @ikunal_x the radius and its thickness. Two identical/similar discs have their thickness in the ratio of 16 : 9. What is the ratio of their radii if the weight of the first is four times that of the second ?", "o": ["3 : 2", "2 : 3", "1 : 2", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, weight = radii 2 thickness × Ratio of weight = 4 : 1 Ratio of thickness = 16 : 9 Ratio of their radii = : 4¹6¹ 9 = : = 3 : 2² 4¹ 3"},
