+{"id": "P1729", "q": "A sector of radius 10.5 cm with the central angle is folded to form a¹20 ◦ TG: @ikunal_x cone by joining the two bounding radii of the sector. What is the volume (in ) of cm 3 the cone so formed ?", "o": ["343² 6 π 343³ 6 π", "343³ 12 π 343² 12 π"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height of the cone = radius of the sector And θ 360 × perimeter of the circle = perimeter of the base of the cone Let the radius of cone = r = 120³60 × 2 × π × 10 . 5² × π × r r = 3.5 ⇒ Height of the cone = l² − r² = = 7 ( 10 . 5 )² − ( 3 ."},
+{"id": "P1730", "q": "A solid cube of volume 13824 cm 3 is cut into 8 cubes of equal volumes. The ratio of the surface area of the original cube to the sum of the surface areas of three of the smaller cubes is : TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["2 : 3", "4 : 3", "8 : 3", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let side of bigger cube = R = 13824 R = = 24 R³ ⇒ 3¹3824 Let side of smaller cubes = r¹3824 = 8¹728 = 12 = r × r³ ⇒ r³ ⇒ Required ratio = (6 ) : (3⁶ ) × 24² × × 12² = 4 : 3"},
+{"id": "P1731", "q": "A circular park having a radius of 15 m. If a¹.5 m wide path is built around it, what is the approximate area of the path?", "o": ["148.5 m²", "158.5 m²", "138.5 m²", "118.5 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "r = 15 m New radius = 15 + 1.5 = 16.5 m Area of path = ( ) π R² − r² = × (272.25 - 225) = × 47.25²2⁷ 22⁷ = 148.5 m²"},
+{"id": "P1732", "q": "A triangular prism has base area of 25 cm 2 . If height is increased by 25 %,what is the new volume (original height was 16 cm) ?", "o": ["550 cm 3", "575 cm 3", "500 cm 3", "225 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume = area of base × height Initial height = 16 cm, new height = 16 × = 20 cm 5⁴ Volume = 25 × 20 = 500 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1733", "q": "A vertical cylindrical container is filled with oil. A solid hemispherical stone of radius 6 cm is immersed completely, and the oil level rises by 2.5 cm . What is the radius of the cylinder ?", "o": ["6.29 cm.", "7.59 cm", "8.79 cm", "11.41 cm TG: @ikunal_x"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q , Volume of hemispherical stone = Volume of cylinder = ⇒ 2³ π 6³ π R² × 2 . 5 = = = 57.6 ⇒ 2 × 6 × 6 × 6³ × 2 . 5 R² ⇒ R² 144² . 5 R = = 7.59 cm (approx) ⇒ 57 ."},
+{"id": "P1734", "q": "A sector of a circle has a central angle of 135 ∘ and a radius of 9 cm . Another sector of the same circle has a central angle of radians. What is the 3π 4 ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector ?", "o": ["4 : 3", "5 : 4", "1 : 1", "6 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "radians = × = 135° 3π 4¹80 π 3π 4 Angle of first sector is equal to angle of second sector and having same radius ∴ Ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector = 1 : 1"},
+{"id": "P1735", "q": "A circular pond is surrounded by a² m wide path. If the total area (pond + path) is 804.25 m² and the area of the pond alone is 615.75 m², what is the radius (approximately) of the pond ?", "o": ["10 m", "14 m", "12 m", "11 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the radius of the pond = r meters. Width of the path = 2 m Outer radius → = r + 2 meters then, Total area (pond + path) = 804.25 m² Area of pond = 615.75 m² So, (r + 2)² - r² = 804.25 - 615.75 π π [(r + 2)² - r² ] = 188.5 π (4r+ 4) = 188.5 π 4 (r + 1) = 188.5 π r + 1 = = = 14.9 ≈ 15¹88 . 5⁴ π 47 ."},
