+{"id": "P1751", "q": "A decorative column is made in the shape of a regular hexagonal prism. The side length of its base is 8 cm. The column is built from multiple sections, and their heights form an arithmetic progression: the first section is 8 cm tall, and each subsequent section is 3 cm taller than the previous one. If the column has 4 sections in total, what is the total volume of the column?", "o": ["4200 cm³ ( b)⁴800 cm³ 3³", "5500 cm³", "4600 cm³ 3³"], "ol": ["a", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total height = 8 + 11+ 14 + 17 = 50 cm Area of hexagon = × 3³ 2 a² TG: @ikunal_x = × 64 = 96³ 3² 3 cm 2 Volume of prism = 96 × 50³ = 4800³ cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1752", "q": "A cone is sliced into two sections by a plane that is parallel to its base, with the upper section representing 1/27 of the overall volume. What is the ratio of the heights of the smaller cone to the TG: @ikunal_x original cone ?", "o": ["1 : 4", "1 : 6", "5 : 1", "1 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= V small V original 1²7 For similar solids, the ratio of their volumes is equal to the cube of the ratio of their corresponding heights, radii, or slant heights."},
+{"id": "P1753", "q": "A sector of a circle has a central angle of 150° and a radius of 6 cm. Another sector of the same circle has a central angle of 180°. What is the ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector ?", "o": ["6 : 5", "3 : 4", "2 : 3", "5 : 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the first sector = π r² θ 360° = = π × 36 × 150° 360¹5 π Area of the second sector = = π × 36 × 180° 360¹8 π Ratio : = 5 : 6 → 15 π 18 π"},
+{"id": "P1754", "q": "A sector of a circle has a central angle of 45° and a radius of 9 cm. Another sector of the same circle has a central angle of radians. What is the π 4 ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector?", "o": ["1 : 1", "2 : 3", "3 : 5", "5 : 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "First Sector :- r = 9 cm Central Angle 45° = π 4 Second Sector :- r = 9 cm Central Angle = π 4 Since both sectors have the same radius and same angle Therefore the area will also be equal."},
+{"id": "P1755", "q": "If the curved surface area of a sphere is 154 cm², find its diameter.", "o": ["9 cm", "8 cm", "7 cm", "5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "4 = 154 cm² r = d(2r) = 7 π r² ⇒ 7² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1756", "q": "A cone has height h and radius r. The cone is melted and recast into a smaller cone whose height is and ℎ 4 radius is . What fraction of the original r² volume is unused ?", "o": ["17", "18", "15", "16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "volume of cone (V) = h¹ 3 π r² According to question, Volume of smaller cone = × × = h¹ 3 π r⁴ 2 ℎ 4¹ 48 π r² ⇒ V¹6 fraction of the original volume is unused = V - = V¹6¹5¹6 V"},
