+{"id": "P1758", "q": "A tank is in the shape of a rectangular parallelepiped of size 30m × 20m⁵ m. Its capacity in kilolitres is ×", "o": ["7,000 kilolitres", "3,000 kilolitres", "5,500 kilolitres", "3,500 kilolitres"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of tank = l × b × ℎ = 30 × 20 × 5 = 3000 m³ 1 = 1 kilolitres m³ Capacity of tank = 3000 kilolitres"},
+{"id": "P1759", "q": "A sector has a central angle of 60° and a radius of 18 cm. Another sector has a central angle of 2 π 3 radians. What is the ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector ?", "o": ["4 : 3", "1 : 2", "7 : 2", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= 120° 2 π 3 Area of sector = π r² θ 360° Area of first sector = = 54 π 18² 60° 360° π Area of second sector = π 18² 120° 360° = 108 π Ratio 54 : 108 = 1 : 2 → π π"},
+{"id": "P1760", "q": "In an urban project, triangular plots with side ratios 8 : 15 : 17 are allocated. If the perimeter is 120 m, find the area.", "o": ["380 m²", "320 m²", "400 m²", "540 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the side of the triangle be = 8x , 15x ,17x Parameter = 120 units 8x + 15x + 17x = 120 units x units = = 3 units 120⁴0²4, 45, 51 is a Pythagorean triplet."},
+{"id": "P1761", "q": "A prism with a square base of side length 6 cm is constructed in layers. Its height follows an arithmetic progression, increasing from 6 cm in the first layer to 24 cm in the fourth layer. What is the total volume of the prism ?", "o": ["1800 cm³", "1950 cm³", "1210 cm³", "2160 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Prism volume = base area × total height Base area = = 36 cm 6² First layer = 6 cm , fourth layer = 24 cm Hence the heights of the layers: 6 , 12 , 18 , 24 Total height = 6 + 12 + 18 + 24 = 60 cm Volume = 36 × 60 = 2160 cm³"},
+{"id": "P1762", "q": "A circle of radius of 14 cm. Two radii are drawn such that the length of the chord connecting their endpoints is 14 cm. What is the area of the minor segment formed ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["( - 49 ) sq . cm 98 π 3³", "( - 59 ) sq . cm 98 π 3³", "( - 49 ) sq . cm 78 π 3³", "( - 49 ) sq . cm 68 π 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "equilateral triangle then angle is 60° Area of sector = × × θ 360 ∘ π R² = × 14 × 14 × = cm 1⁶ π 98 π 3 Area of triangle = 1² R² sin θ = × 14 × 14 × = 49¹ 2³ 2³ Area of smaller segment = ( - 49 )⁹8 π 3³ cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1763", "q": "An L-shaped floor is made of two rectangles (7 m⁴ m and 7m⁶m). × × Tiles cost ₹500/m², but a¹0% discount is given if more than 60 m² is tiled. What is the total cost after discount?", "o": ["₹31,500", "₹39,160", "₹30,240", "₹31,540"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1st Area = 7 × 4 = 28m²nd Area = 7 × 6 = 42m Total area = 42m + 28m = 70m² Area is greater than 60m² , so , 10% discount is applicable Total cost = 70 × 500 = Rs.35000 After 10% discount = 35000 × 90¹00 = Rs."},
+{"id": "P1764", "q": "A triangular window has dimensions such that its area is 35% of a square window of area 300 m². If its base is 20 m, find its height.", "o": ["12.5 m", "18.6 m", "10.5 m", "24.5 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the triangular window = 300 × = 105³5¹00 m² Area of the triangle = × Base × Height 1² 105 = × 20 × Height 1² Height = 10.5 m"},
+{"id": "P1765", "q": "A company makes a gift box in the shape of a right pyramid with a square base.The base side of the box is 8 cm, and its height is 15 cm.Due to safety limits, the box can be filled only up to 80% of its total volume. If 1 cm³ of material costs ₹0.60, what will be the cost to fill one such box ?", "o": ["₹153.6", "₹163.6", "₹182.4", "₹192.3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "area of the square base = = = side 2⁸ 2⁶4 cm 2 volume of a pyramid = area of base × 1³ × height = × 15 = 320¹ 3⁶4 cm 3 Effective volume = 80% × 320 = 0.8 × 320 = 256 cm 3 total cost of material = 256 × 0.60 = ₹153.6"},
+{"id": "P1766", "q": "Consider a right trapezoidal field. Its two parallel sides are 40 meters and 60 meters long. One of its non-parallel sides, which acts as the height, measures 20 meters. What is the area of this field ?", "o": ["900 square meters", "1000 square meters", "1220 square meters", "1100 square meters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The formula for the area of a trapezoid is (A) = ( ) × h¹ 2 b¹ + b² = (40 + 60) × 20 = 50 × 20 = 1000 m² 1²"},
+{"id": "P1767", "q": "If the surface area of a sphere is equal to twice its volume, find the radius of the sphere.", "o": ["1 unit", "3 units", "2 units", "1.5 units"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Surface area of sphere = 2 × Volume of sphere 4 = 2⁴ = r ⇒ π r² × 4³ π r³ ⇒ 8³ r = 1.5 units ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1768", "q": "A triangular flag has base and height in the ratio 3 : 4. If the area is 216 cm², what are the base and height?", "o": ["16 cm and 12 cm", "18 cm and 24 cm", "20 cm and 25 cm", "18 cm and 20 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let base = 3x and height = 4x According to the formula, TG: @ikunal_x Area of a triangle = b × h¹ 2²16 = × 3x × 4x²16 = 6x² 1² ⇒ x² = = 36 x = 216⁶ ⇒ 6 Base (b) = 3x = 3 × 6 = 18 cm Height (h) = 4x = 4 × 6 = 24 cm"},
+{"id": "P1769", "q": "A triangular field with base 80m and height 60 m shares a side with a rectangle of length 80 m and breadth 50 m. Find the combined area and percentage of the triangle's area in the total.", "o": ["1, 450 m² and 24.5%", "2, 450 m² and 25.5%", "6,400 m² and 37.5%", "2, 500 m² and 25%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a triangle = × Base × height 1² = × 80 × 60 = 2400¹ 2 m² Area of rectangle=80 m ×50 m= 4000 m² Total area = 2400 + 4000 = 6400 m² So, Required % = × 100 = 37.5 % 2400⁶400"},
+{"id": "P1770", "q": "A spherical balloon is inflated, causing its radius to grow by 5%. By what percentage does its surface area TG: @ikunal_x increase?", "o": ["10.25%", "20%", "21.25%", "25%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The surface area of a sphere is = 4 π r² Where 4 is constant π Initial : Final 20 : 21²0 : 21 ………………………. 400 : 441 Diff = 41 × 100 = 10.25 % 41⁴00"},
+{"id": "P1771", "q": "A rectangular sheet has an area equal to a square plot. If the sheet measures 36 m in length and 25 m in breadth, and the square plot has an area equal to the sheet, find the perimeter of the square plot.", "o": ["110 m", "120 m", "140 m", "220 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The area of a rectangle = Length × Breadth = 36m × 25m = 900 m² Area of square plot = 900 m² The area of a square is the square of its side = 900 Side = 30 side 2 ⇒ The perimeter of a square is four times the length of its side 4 × 30 m = 120 m"},
+{"id": "P1772", "q": "A garden is in the shape of a regular hexagon, each side 30 m. If 5% of it is occupied by a circular fountain, find the remaining area.", "o": ["2,131.5 m²", "2,351.9 m²", "2,221.3 m²", "2,421.7 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of garden (hexagon) = = = 1350³ 3² ( l )²³ 3² ( 30 )²³ m² Remaining area of garden = 1350 × =1282.5 ≃ 2,221.3 m² 3⁹5¹00³"},
+{"id": "P1773", "q": "A triangular field has sides in the ratio 3 : 5 : 7 and a perimeter of 90 m. What is the area of the field ?", "o": ["196 m²", "234 m²", "186 m²", "182 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question Perimeter = 90 m³x + 5x + 7x = 90 ⇒ 15x = 90 x = 6 ⇒ ⇒ then, a = 3x = 18 , b = 5x = 30 , c = 7x = 42 The semi-perimeter (s) = 18 + 30 + 42² = = 45 m⁹0² using Heron's formula A = s ( s − a )( s − b )( s − c ) A = 45 ( 45 − 18 )( 45 − 30 )( 45 − 42 ) A = 45×27×15×3 = 5 × 9 × 9 × 3 × 5 × 3 × 3 = 9 × 5 × 3 = 135 × 1.732²34³ ≈ m²"},
+{"id": "P1774", "q": "The base of a prism is a rectangle whose length is twice its width. The perimeter of the base is 54 cm. The prism's height decreases in an arithmetic progression from 17 cm in the first layer to 11 cm in the fourth layer. What is the total volume of the prism ?", "o": ["9000 cm³", "9500 cm³", "9060 cm³", "9072 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : = 2b l According to question, 2(l + b) = 54²b + b = 27 ⇒ ⇒ b = 9 cm and l = 18 cm ⇒ Area of rectangle (base area) = 9 × 18 = 162 cm 2 Height are in AP = 17, = 11, n = 4 a¹ a⁴ Sum of height ( ) = = ( ) s⁴ s n n² a¹ + a⁴ = (17 + 11) = 2 × 28 = 56 cm s⁴ 4² So, Volume of prism = base area × Height = 162 × 56 = 9072 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1775", "q": "A large wooden box, open at the top, needs to be lined with fabric on its inner floor and inner four side walls. The inner dimensions of the box are 5 m length, 3.6 m wide, and 2.4 m high. If the fabric comes in square pieces of side 100 cm, and 30% extra fabric is needed for cuts and overlaps, how many approximate fabric pieces should be purchased ?", "o": ["77", "88", "62", "98"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of wooden box = 2h(l + b) + l × b = 2 × 2.4(5 + 3.6) + 5 × 3.6 = 59.28 m² 30% extra for fabric, = 59.28 × = 77.064¹30¹00 m² Area of Square = 100 × 100 = 10000 = 1 cm 2 m² So, the required fabric pieces = 77⁷7 ."},
+{"id": "P1776", "q": "A rectangular fish tank with a base of 80 cm 60 cm contains water × up to a height of 25 cm. If 4 identical spherical stones, each with a radius of 5 cm, are dropped into the tank and fully submerged, what is the rise in the water level?", "o": ["cm", "cm π 8⁵π 36", "cm", "cm π 5²π 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Base area = 80 × 60 = 4800 cm 2 radius = 5 cm No. of sphere = 4 Rise in water level = Total volume of spℎeres Base area of tank = = 4 × 4³ π r³ 4800⁴ × 4³ π × 125⁴800 = = cm 2000³ π 4800⁵ π 36"},
+{"id": "P1777", "q": "A square field has a diagonal of m. What is its area? 48", "o": ["46 m²", "24 m²", "40 m²", "12 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The area of square using diagonal A = d² 2 Where d = m⁴8 area = = = 24 ( 48 )²² 48² m²"},
+{"id": "P1778", "q": "A spherical tank is filled with water. The radius of the sphere is 12 meters. The tank is used to fill cylindrical containers, each with a radius of 2 meter and a height of 24 meters. How many containers can be filled ?", "o": ["24", "28", "54", "30"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of spherical tank = = = 2304⁴ 3 π R³ 4³ π 12 ( )³ π m³ Volume of one cylindrical container = × × 24 = 96 π 2² π m³ Number of containers that can be filled = = 24²304 π 96 π"},
+{"id": "P1779", "q": "A perfect cube with a side length of 4 cm has the largest possible sphere fitted inside it. What is the volume of the empty space within the cube ?", "o": ["64 - ( ) cm³", "12 - ( ) cm³ 32π 3⁶4π 3", "64 - ( ) cm³", "cm³ 56π 3²56π 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: Cube side (a) = 4 = Diameter of sphere Radius of sphere (r) = 2 ⇒ Volume of empty space = - a³ 4³ π r ( )³ = 64 - 4³ − 4³ π × 2³ ⇒ 32 π 3 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1780", "q": "A banner is shaped like a trapezium with bases 10 m and 6 m, and TG: @ikunal_x height 8 m. If printing costs ₹500/m², what is the total cost?", "o": ["₹32,000", "₹30,000", "₹28,000", "₹25,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of trapezium (sum of parallel sides) height 1² × × = (10 + 6)⁸ = 64 m² 1² × × Total cost = 64⁵00 = ₹32,000. ×"},
+{"id": "P1781", "q": "A warehouse floor is 16.5 meters long and 16 meters wide. If 2.5 meter × 2.2 meter rectangular tiles are used to completely cover the floor, how many tiles will be needed ?", "o": ["48", "68", "72", "80"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the floor = 16.5 × 16 = 264 m² area of one tile = 2.5 × 2.2 = 5.5 m² Number of tiles = = 48 tiles 264⁵ . 5"},
+{"id": "P1782", "q": "A large advertisement board is made on a¹0 m × 6 m rectangle. From this, a³ m × 2 m rectangular portion is cut out and removed for the advertisement display. If the cost of painting the remaining open area (the part left after cutting) is ₹250 per square meter, what will be the total cost of painting that open area ?", "o": ["₹13,240", "₹13,500", "₹13,960", "₹14,200"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of the large signboard = 10 m × 6 m = 60 m Area of the cutout = 3 m × 2 m = 6 m Area of the open part = 60 - 6 = 54 m² Total painting cost = Area × Rate = 54 × 250 = ₹13,500"},
+{"id": "P1783", "q": "A triangular storage prism has a base in the shape of a right triangle and its side lengths are in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. If the total perimeter of the base is 54 cm and the height of the prism is 8 cm, find the lateral surface area of the prism.", "o": ["360 cm²", "300 cm²", "480 cm²", "432 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LSA of prism = perimeter of base × height = 54 × 8 = 432 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1784", "q": "A bathroom floor measures 4.5 m in length and 3 m in width. One of its walls, which is to be tiled fully, measures 2 m in length and 2.5 m in height. If square tiles of side 25 cm are used, and an extra 12% of tiles are purchased to cover cuts and wastage, how many tiles are needed in total ?", "o": ["90", "70", "95", "80"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of wall = 2 × 2.5 = 5 m² Side of each tile = 25 cm = 0.25 m Area of one tile = 0.25 × 0.25 = 0.0625 m² Number of tiles = = 80 tiles 5⁰ ."},
+{"id": "P1785", "q": "A rectangular room measures 10 m long and 8 m wide. Its floor is to be covered with square tiles of side 50 cm. If 15% extra tiles are purchased for cutting and breakage, how many tiles are needed in total ?", "o": ["400", "350", "468", "368"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length = 8 m = 800 cm Breadth = 10 m = 1000 cm Area of rectangular room = 800 × 1000 = 800000 cm 2 Area of square tile = (50)² = 2500 cm 2 number of tile = = 320⁸00000²500 Extra tile = 320 × = 48¹5¹00 Total tile = 320 + 48 = 368"},
+{"id": "P1786", "q": "A rectangular lawn measures 60 m by 40 m. A⁵ m wide path is constructed all around the inside of the lawn. What percentage of the lawn's area is occupied by the path ?", "o": ["35%", "37.5%", "16.67%", "47.5%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of large rectangular lawn = 60 × 40 = 2400 m² Area of Path = 2W( + b - 2W) l = 2 × 5(60 + 40 - 10) = 900 m² percentage of the area of path = × 100 = 37.5% 900²400"},
+{"id": "P1787", "q": "An L-shaped floor is formed by adjoining a⁸m × 5m and a⁵m × 3m rectangle. Tiles cost ₹200/m². What is the total cost to tile the floor ?", "o": ["₹19,600", "₹21,700", "₹22,000", "₹11000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of first rectangle = 8 × 5 = 40 m² Area of second rectangle = 5 × 3 = 15 m² Total area of both rectangle = 40 + 15 = 55 m² Total cost to tile the floor = 55 × 200 = ₹11000"},
+{"id": "P1788", "q": "A building has 4 square pyramidal turrets, each of base 5 m and height 7 m. If each needs 1.5 times volume for structural fill, find total fill needed.", "o": ["350 m³", "260 m³", "280 m³", "180 m³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q, Volume of four pyramid = 4 × ( × base area × height) × 1.5¹ 3 = 4 × × 5 × 5 × 7 × 1.5 = 350 m³ 1³"},
+{"id": "P1789", "q": "If the height of a cylinder is equal to its diameter and radius is 6 cm, find its volume.", "o": ["432π cm³", "238π cm³", "500π cm³", "316 π cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius (r) = 6 cm Height (h) = diameter = 2r = 2 × 6 = 12 cm Volume of cylinder = πr²h = π × 6² × 12 = 432π cm³"},
+{"id": "P1790", "q": "A composite wall consists of a rectangle 20m by 8 m with a triangular window of base 15 m and height 8 m cut out. If the wall needs to be painted at ₹111 per m², find the painting cost after deducting the window area.", "o": ["12,528", "111,00", "120,00", "11,520"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rectangle wall = 160m² Remaining area = 160 - × 8 × 15¹ 2¹60 - 60 = 100 ⇒ Hence, total cost for painting = 100 × 111= 11100"},
+{"id": "P1791", "q": "A cuboid has a volume of 1400 cm³ and its length is twice its height. If the breadth is 7 cm, find its dimensions.", "o": ["18 cm × 7 cm × 9cm", "12 cm × 7 cm × 6 cm", "20 cm × 7 cm × 10 cm", "10 cm × 7 cm × 5cm."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cuboid = 1400 cm 3 L × B × H = 1400 ⇒ cm 3 Now by checking options one by one , option (c) is satisfied ."},
+{"id": "P1792", "q": "A rectangular parallelepiped has dimensions in arithmetic progression. If the sum of its dimensions is 42 cm and the volume is 1344 cm³, find its dimensions.", "o": ["8 cm, 14 cm, 20 cm", "6 cm, 14 cm, 22 cm", "10 cm, 12 cm, 20 cm", "4 cm, 14 cm, 24 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "On checking all options one by one, only option (d) satisfy, Dimensions = 4 cm , b = 14 cm and → l h = 24 cm Sum of the dimension(l + b + h) = 42 cm LHS = l + b + h = 4 + 14 + 24 = 42 cm = RHS Volume of cuboid (l × b × h) = 1344 cm 3 LHS = l × b × h = 4 × 14 × 24 = 1344 cm 3 = RHS"},
+{"id": "P1793", "q": "A triangular field with base 70 m and height 96 m shares a side with a rectangle of length 70 m and breadth 35 m. Find the combined area and percentage of the triangle's area in the total.", "o": ["4, 450 m² and 34.5%", "3, 450 m² and 25 %", "5810 m² and 57.83%", "5, 500 m² and 59 % TG: @ikunal_x"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a triangle = × Base × height 1² = × 70 × 96 = 3360¹ 2 m² Area of rectangle = 70 m × 35 m = 2450 m² Total area = 3360 + 2450 = 5810 m² So, Required % = × 100 = 57.83 % 3360⁵810"},
+{"id": "P1794", "q": "A hemisphere, cone, and cylinder have the same base radius and equal volumes. If the height of the cylinder is 3h, find the height of the cone.", "o": ["9h", "10h", "5h", "6h"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, π = π h = π × H² 3 r³ r² 1³ r² π h = π × H H = 9 h r² 3¹ 3 r² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1795", "q": "A rhombus has diagonals in the ratio 5 : 6. If its area is 135 cm², find the diagonals.", "o": ["18 cm and 24 cm", "12 cm and 16 cm", "15 cm and 18cm", "27 cm and 36 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "let diagonals of rhombus = 5 , 6 x x Area of rhombus = × × 1² d¹ d² × × = 135 ⇒ 1² 5 x⁶ x = 9 = 3 ⇒ x² ⇒ x Hence, diagonal are 15, 18"},
+{"id": "P1796", "q": "A solid cone is melted and recast into smaller cones of the same height but one-third of the radius . How many smaller cones can be made? Matriculation Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["3", "6", "9", "27"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number of smaller cones TG: @ikunal_x = = 9¹ 3 π R² H¹ 3 π( R³ )² H"},
+{"id": "P1797", "q": "A sphere and a cylinder have the same radius and height. The ratio of their volumes is: Matriculation Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1 : 2", "2 : 3", "4 : 3", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: h = r Required ratio = = 4³ π r³ π r² ℎ 4³"},
+{"id": "P1798", "q": "If the volume of a rectangular parallelepiped is 280 and its base cm 3 area is 20 What is its height? cm 2 Matriculation Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["6 cm", "14 cm", "10 cm", "12 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume = base area × height 280 = 20 × height height = 14 cm"},
+{"id": "P1799", "q": "The radius of the base of a cylinder is 7 cm and its height is 10 cm. What is its volume? (Take π = ). 22⁷ Matriculation Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1450 cm³", "1540 cm³", "1600 cm³", "1400 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cylinder = h π r² = × 7 × 7 × 10²2⁷ = 22 × 7 × 10 = 1540 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1800", "q": "If a cylinder and a cone have the same base radius and same height, then the volume of the cylinder is____of the volume of the cone. Matriculation Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Double", "Three times", "Equal", "Half"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let radius = r and height = h Volume of cone = h ⇒ 1³ π r² Volume of Cylinder = h ⇒ π r² According to formula: Volume of Cylinder = 3 × ( πr² h) ⇒ 1³ Volume of Cylinder = 3 × volume of ⇒ cone So, the volume of the cylinder is three times the volume of the cone"},
+{"id": "P1801", "q": "A box has dimensions 12 cm 6 × cm 4 cm. What is its volume? × Matriculation Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["144 cm³", "250 cm³", "288 cm³", "240 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of box = l × b × h = 12 × 6 × 4 = 288 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1802", "q": "What is the area of a triangle with base 14 cm and height 12 cm ? Matriculation Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["84 cm²", "42 cm²", "80 cm²", "96 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a triangle = × 14 × 12¹ 2 = 84 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1803", "q": "A conical party hat has a slant height of 8 cm and a radius of 5 cm. What is its curved surface area? (Use π = 3.14) Matriculation Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["115.4 cm²", "125.6 cm²", "136.2 cm²", "145.8 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved Surface Area of a cone = rl π = 3.14 × 8 × 5 = 125.6 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1804", "q": "A solid hemisphere with radius 6 cm is painted. Find its total surface area. Matriculation Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["339.12 cm²", "226.08 cm²", "452.16 cm²", "113.04 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of hemisphere = 3 r² π = 3 × 3.14 × (6)² = 339.12 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1805", "q": "The perimeter of a triangle is 30 cm. If two sides are 9 cm and 11 cm, what is the third side? Matriculation Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["8 cm", "10 cm", "12 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of triangle = Sum of all three sides 30 = 9 + 11 + Third side ⇒ Third side = 30 - 20 = 10 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1806", "q": "An ice cream cone is shaped like a cone having radius of 4 cm and a height of 10 cm. How much ice cream (in cm³) can it hold? Matriculation Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["167.61 cm³", "160 cm³", "165.5 cm³", "158 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cone = h¹ 3 π r² = × × 4 × 4 × 10¹ 3²2⁷ = × × 160¹ 3²2⁷ = = 167.61 cm 3³520²1"},
+{"id": "P1807", "q": "A tank in the shape of a hemisphere is filled with milk. The milk is then poured into a cylindrical container of the same radius but height equal to 4r. What fraction of the cylinder will be filled? Matriculation Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1", "3", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Volume of hemisphere = V = 2³ π r³ Volume of cylinder = (4r) = 4 π r² π r³ Required fraction filled = 2³ π r³ 4 π r³ = = = 2³ × 1⁴ 2¹2¹ 6"},
+{"id": "P1808", "q": "A rectangular parallelepiped has dimensions 6 cm × 5 cm × 4 cm. Find its total surface area. Matriculation Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["148 cm²", "150 cm²", "140 cm²", "135 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of rectangular parallelepiped = 2(lb + bh + hl) = 2(6 × 5 + 5 × 4 + 6 × 4) = 148 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1809", "q": "A conical tent has a radius of 6 m and a slant height of 14 m. Find its lateral surface area. Matriculation Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["72π m²", "84π m²", "90π m²", "56π m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area (LSA) of a cone = rl π = × 6 × 14 = 84 m² π π"},
+{"id": "P1810", "q": "A hemisphere is placed on top of a cylinder with the same base radius. If their combined height is 12 cm and radius is 4 cm, find the total surface area. Matriculation Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["785.97cm²", "351.68 cm²", "720 cm²", "785.97 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : radius r = 4 cm, total height = 12 cm height of the cylinder :h = 12 - 4 = 8 cm Total surface area (TSA) = Curved surface of hemisphere + Lateral surface of cylinder + Base of cylinder = 2 r² + 2 rh + r² = r(2r + 2h + r) π π π π = 3.14 × 4× ( 8 + 16 + 4) = 351.68 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1811", "q": "Find the surface area of a brick with dimensions 10 cm 4 cm 3 cm. × × TG: @ikunal_x Matriculation Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["160 cm²", "155 cm²", "164 cm²", "144 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of a brick = 2(10 × 4 + 4 × 3 + 10 × 3) = 164 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1812", "q": "A triangle has an area of 175 cm² and a base of 25 cm. What is its height? Matriculation Level 30/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["15 cm", "16 cm", "17 cm", "14 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question: Area of triangle = × base × height 1² 175 = × 25 × height 1² Height = 14 cm"},
+{"id": "P1813", "q": "An overhead water tank is made by placing a hemisphere over a cylinder. The cylinder has a height of 6 m, and the radius of both shapes is 3 m. What is the total volume of the tank in cubic meters? (Use π = 3.14) Matriculation Level 30/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["287.43 m³", "124.56 m³", "226.08 m³", "126.08 m³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of tank = volume of cylinder + volume of hemisphere = + = (h + r) π r² ℎ 2³ π r³ π r² 2³ = 3.14 × 9 (6 + 3) = 226.08 m³ × 2³ ×"},
+{"id": "P1814", "q": "A wooden block has dimensions 16 cm × 10 cm × 6 cm. What is its volume? Matriculation Level 30/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["865 cm³", "920 cm³", "960 cm³", "678 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of wooden block = 16 × 10 × 6 = 960 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1815", "q": "Find the volume of a right circular cone whose base radius is 21 cm and height is 36 cm. [ = ] π 22⁷ Matriculation Level 30/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["16632 cm 3", "17845 cm 3", "26252 cm 3", "16327 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cone = 21² 36¹ 3 × 22⁷ × × = 22³ 7³6 × × × = 16,632 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1816", "q": "From a cuboid of dimension 12 cm 6 cm 3 cm, small cubes of edge × × 3 cm are cut. How many small cubes are formed from the cuboid? Matriculation Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["8", "12", "24", "16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number of small cubes = = 8¹2 × 6 × 3³ × 3 ×3"},
+{"id": "P1817", "q": "The total surface area of a hemisphere is 1,539 m². If the radius of the hemisphere is halved, what will be the new curved surface area of the hemisphere? (Use π = )²2⁷ Matriculation Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["192.5 m²", "255.82 m²", "481.5 m²", "314 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of hemisphere (3πr²) = 1,539 m² 3πr² = 1,539 ⇒ r² = = = 163.22 ⇒ 1539 × 7³ ×22¹0773⁶6 r = m = 12.77 m ⇒ 163 . 22 If the radius is halved: = ≈ 6.38 m r² 12 ."},
+{"id": "P1818", "q": "If the volume of a cone is 84 π cm³ and the height is 7 cm. Find the radius of its base in nearest one decimal place. Matriculation Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["6 cm", "5 cm", "4 cm", "7 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cone = r² h = 84 cm³ 1³ π π ⇒ r² × 7 = 84¹ 3 π π r² = = 36 ⇒ r = 6 cm 84 × 3⁷"},
+{"id": "P1819", "q": "Find the total surface area of a cube, the length of whose diagonal is √75 cm. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["150 cm²", "180 cm²", "210 cm²", "250 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Diagonal of the cube = √75 a = a = = ⇒ 3⁷5 ⇒ 75³ 5 × 5 × 3³ = = 5⁵ 3³ Total surface area of the cube = 6 = 6 × 25 = 150 cm² a²"},
+{"id": "P1820", "q": "A bottle is made by attaching a hemisphere to a cylinder of the same radius. Radius = 3.5 cm, height of cylinder = 12 cm. Find the total surface area of the bottle. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["315.5 cm²", "341 cm²", "397 cm²", "309.5 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of the bottle = Surface area of the hemisphere + Surface area of the cylinder. = 2 + 2 π r² π rℎ = 2 × × 3.5 × 3.5 + 2 × × 3.5 × 12²2⁷ 22⁷ = 44 × 1.75 + 528 × 0.5 = 77 + 264 = 341cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1821", "q": "A cone has a slant height of 25 cm and a vertical height of 20 cm. What is the radius of the base ? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["15 cm", "12 cm", "18 cm", "9 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= l² ℎ 2 + r² = + 25² r² 20² = r² 625 − 400 r = = = 15 cm 625 − 400²25"},
+{"id": "P1822", "q": "A hollow hemisphere has an inner radius of 6 cm and an outer radius of 8 cm. Find its total surface area. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["678.36 cm²", "754.29 cm²", "804.02 cm²", "716.56 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of a hollow hemisphere = 3 + π R² π r² = 3 × × 64 + × 36²2⁷ 22⁷ = 603.42 + 113.14 = 716.56 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1823", "q": "A cone has a base radius of 9 cm and height of 12 cm. What is its slant height? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["15 cm", "14 cm", "13 cm", "16 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height = = radius 2 + ℎeigℎt² 9² + 12² = = 15 cm 81 + 144"},
+{"id": "P1824", "q": "Find the length of the longest pole that can be placed in a cubical room of edge 23 cm. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["16 cm", "23 cm 2²", "23 cm", "16 cm 3³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of pole = a = 23 cm 3³"},
+{"id": "P1825", "q": "A cuboid with dimensions (12 × 6 × 3) meters is melted and recast into a cube. Find the total surface area of the cube. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["216 m²", "324 m²", "486 m²", "600 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the cube = Volume of the cuboid = l × b × h a = = 6 m a³ ⇒ 3¹2 × 6 × 3 Total surface area of the cube = 6 a² = 6 × 36 = 216 m² TG: @ikunal_x"},
+{"id": "P1826", "q": "The ratio of the radius of Hemisphere A to Hemisphere B is 3 : 1. If the curved surface area of Hemisphere A is equal to the volume of Hemisphere B, find the radius of Hemisphere B. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["31 cm", "23 cm", "27 cm", "25 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius of hemisphere A ( r A ) = 3x and radius( ) of hemisphere B = x r B ATQ Curved surface area of hemisphere A = Volume of hemisphere B ⇒ 2 = π ( r A² )²³ π r B³ ⇒ 9 = ⇒ x = 9 × 3 = 27 cm x² 1³ x³"},
+{"id": "P1827", "q": "A wheel of a bicycle has a radius of 56 cm. How many revolutions will it make to cover a distance of 1.32 km? Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["276 revolutions", "352 revolutions", "375 revolutions", "415 revolutions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Circumference of the wheel = 2 × × 56 = 44 × 8 = 352²2⁷ Total number of revolutions = 132000³52 = 375 revolutions"},
+{"id": "P1828", "q": "The height and slant height of the cone are 20 cm and 29 cm respectively. Find the volume of the cone. Matriculation Level 01/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["8160 cm³", "9240 cm³", "8820 cm³", "9360 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= + l² ℎ 2 r² 841 = 400 + r² = 841 - 400 = 441 r² Volume of a cone = h¹ 3 π r² = × × 441 × 20¹ 3²2⁷ = 22 × 21 × 20= 9240 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1829", "q": "Find the volume of a cylinder whose radius is 7 cm and height is 14 cm. (π = )²2⁷ Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["2156 cm³", "2464 cm³", "2695 cm³", "3080 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a cylinder = h π r² = × 49 × 14 = 2156 cm³ 22⁷"},
+{"id": "P1830", "q": "Which of the following statements is true about Rectangle? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["all sides are equal", "All angles are right angles", "Diagonals are not equal", "opposite sides are unequal"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All angles are right angles"},
+{"id": "P1831", "q": "What is the area of a rhombus which has diagonals 12 cm and 6 cm ? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["35 cm²", "40 cm²", "36 cm²", "50 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a rhombus = × × 1² d¹ d² = × 12 × 6 = 36 cm² 1²"},
+{"id": "P1832", "q": "A triangle has sides of length 5 cm, 9 cm, and 13 cm. Find its perimeter. Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["27 cm", "28 cm", "32 cm", "25 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of the triangle = sum of all sides = 5 + 9 + 13 = 27 cm"},
+{"id": "P1833", "q": "If the height of a cylinder is tripled and the radius remains the same, what will be the change in volume? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Doubles", "Triples", "Halves", "Stays the same"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius = r , Height = h V= h π r² = (3h) = 3( h) V new π r² π r² = 3(V) V new"},
+{"id": "P1834", "q": "A cylindrical concrete pillar has radius 0.7 m and height 5 m. If the curved surface is to be plastered at the rate of ₹200 per square metre, what will be the total cost of plastering for 10 such pillars? (Take π = 22/7) Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["₹38,500", "₹42,000", "₹44,000", "₹46,200"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Cylinder’s curved surface area = 2 π rℎ = 2 × × 0.7 × 5 = 22²2⁷ Plastering cost for the pillar = 22 × 10 × 200 = 44,000"},
+{"id": "P1835", "q": "How will the volume of a cube change if its side is doubled ? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Twice", "Four times", "Six times", "Eight times"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume = a³ new side = 2a = (2a)³ = 8a³ ⇒ = 8(V) V new V new"},
+{"id": "P1836", "q": "A sphere and a hemisphere have the same radius. The ratio of their total surface areas is: Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["5 : 2", "9 : 1", "4 : 3", "7 : 8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area of a sphere = 4 π r² Total surface area of a hemisphere = 3 π r² Ratio = 4 : 3 = 4 : 3 π r² π r²"},
+{"id": "P1837", "q": "A square and a rectangle have the same perimeter. The length of the rectangle is three times its width. If the side of the square is 16 meters, then what is the difference between the area of the square and the area of the rectangle? Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1) TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["32 m²", "48 m²", "64 m²", "72 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the width = x and length = 3x According to the question: Perimeter of the square = Perimeter of the rectangle 4a = 2 (x + 3x)⁴ ×16 = 8x x = 8 m , length = 24 ⇒ Area of the square = 16 × 16 = 256 m² Area of the rectangle = 8 × 24 = 192 m² Difference = 256 - 192 = 64 m²"},
+{"id": "P1838", "q": "A regular hexagon has a side length of 8 cm. What is its perimeter? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["56 cm", "64 cm", "48 cm", "54 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter = 6 × 8 = 48cm"},
+{"id": "P1839", "q": "Which of the following statements is always true for any pyramid? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["All faces are similar", "The base is a polygon", "All lateral faces are circular", "All angles are right angles"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The base is a polygon"},
+{"id": "P1840", "q": "What is the slant height of a cone, base has a radius of 9 cm and a vertical height of 12 cm? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["14 cm", "15 cm", "16 cm", "18 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Slant height = r² + ℎ 2 = = 15 cm 9² + 12²"},
+{"id": "P1841", "q": "If the height of a cone is Triples while keeping the radius the same, how does the volume change? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["Doubles", "Triples", "Stays the same", "Becomes half"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Height = 3h, Radius = r V = h ⇒ = (3h)¹³ π r² V new 1³ π r² = 3( (h) V new 1³ π r² = 3(V) V new"},
+{"id": "P1842", "q": "The radius of a spherical ball increases from 3 cm to 9 cm. How many times does its surface area increase? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2", "3", "6", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Radius = 3 cm Surface area = 4 × 9 = 36 cm π π Radius = 9 cm Surface area = 4 × 81 = 324 cm π π The surface area increases 9 times."},
+{"id": "P1843", "q": "A company manufactures hollow spherical balls with internal radius of 10 cm. If the thickness of the rubber is 0.5 cm, what is the volume of rubber used in making one ball? (Use π = )²2⁷ Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["560.50 cm³", "660.52 cm³", "720.00 cm³", "840.25 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Internal radius (r) = 10 cm Thickness = 0.5 cm External radius (R) = 10 + 0.5 = 10.5 cm V = ( )⁴³ π ( 10 . 5 )³ − ( 10 )³ × × 157.625 = 4³ 22⁷ 13871²1 = 660.52 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1844", "q": "A bowl is in the shape of a hemisphere with radius 14 cm. What is its total surface area? (π = 3.14) Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1772 cm²", "1848 cm²", "1648 cm²", "1856 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total surface area = 3 π r² 3 × × 14 × 14 = 66 × 28 = 1848 cm² 22⁷"},
+{"id": "P1845", "q": "A circle and a square have the same perimeter. Which of these will have larger area? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["circle", "Square", "Both are equal", "Depends on dimensions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The area of a circle is always largest ."},
+{"id": "P1846", "q": "The area of a trapezium with bases 12 cm, 8 cm, and height 5 cm is: Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["45 cm²", "48 cm²", "50 cm²", "52 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a trapezium = (a + b) × h¹ 2 = (12 + 8) × 5 = 10 × 5 = 50 cm² 1²"},
+{"id": "P1847", "q": "Two rectangles have the same area. The first has sides 18cm and 22 cm. The second has one side 12 cm. What is the other side of the second rectangle? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["33 cm", "37 cm", "41 cm", "43 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the other side of the second rectangle be = x cm. 18 × 22 = 12 × x ⇒ x = 33 cm"},
+{"id": "P1848", "q": "A cylinder is cut horizontally into two equal parts. How will its volume change? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["doubles", "becomes half", "remains the same", "increase of 25%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Formula :- Volume of full cylinder (V) = r² h π Volume of each half- cylinder (V half ) = r² h¹ 2 π Thus, the volume of each part becomes half of the original volume."},
+{"id": "P1849", "q": "The parallel sides of a trapezium differ by 4 cm. Its height is 6 cm and the area is 60 cm². What are the lengths of the parallel sides ? Higher Secondary 24/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["6 cm and 10 cm", "7 cm and 11 cm", "8 cm and 12 cm", "5 cm and 9 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of trapezium = × (Sum of parallel 1² sides) × height 60 = × (a + b) × 6 ⇒ a + b = 20¹ 2 difference between parallel sides = 4 cm So, a = 12 cm and b = 8 cm."},
+{"id": "P1850", "q": "If the lateral surface area of a right circular cylinder is 264 cm² and radius is 3.5 cm, find the height. Higher Secondary 24/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["12 cm", "11 cm", "10 cm", "13 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CSA of cylinder (2 rh) = 264 cm² π 2 × × 3.5 × h = 264 h = 12 cm 22⁷ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1851", "q": "If the side of a square is reduced to half of its original length, the area of the square becomes: Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["One-half", "One-fourth", "Two times", "Four times"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Length of the side = a² Area of square = ( side lengtℎ )² = ( )² = a² a² 4 Hence, the area becomes one-fourth of the original."},
+{"id": "P1852", "q": "A room has a floor in the shape of a rectangle (25 m¹8 m), with a × triangular extension on one end. The triangle has a base of 15 m and height of 10 m. What is the total area of the floor? Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["252 m²", "525 m²", "550 m²", "335 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rectangle = 25 × 18 = 450 m² Area of triangle = × base × Height 1² = × 15 × 10 = 75¹ 2 m² Total Area = 450 + 75 = 525 m²"},
+{"id": "P1853", "q": "A solid sphere of radius 10 cm is melted and recast into smaller spheres of radius 2 cm. How many such small spheres will be formed ? Higher Secondary 25/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["100", "125", "500", "250"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a solid sphere of radius 10 cm = × × 10 × 10 × 10⁴ 3 π = × 1000⁴ 3 π Volume of a solid sphere of radius 2 cm = × × 2 × 2 × 2 = × 8⁴ 3 π 4³ π Number of small spheres = = 125⁴ 3 ×1000 π 4³ × 8 π"},
+{"id": "P1854", "q": "Determine the volumetric measure of a cuboidal solid with a length of 24 meters, a breadth of 14 meters, and a height of 10 meters. Higher Secondary 26/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["3360m³", "3350m³", "3260m³", "3920m³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "V = l × b × h = 24 × 14 × 10 = 3360 m³"},
+{"id": "P1855", "q": "A rectangular parallelepiped tank has dimensions 8 m × 6 m × 5 m. If it is filled with water and the cost of water is ₹50 per 1000 liters, what is the total cost to fill the tank? (1 m³ = 1000 liters) Higher Secondary 26/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["₹16750", "₹17000", "₹12000", "₹13000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of the tank = 8 × 6 × 5 = 240 m³ 1 m³ = 1000 ltr TG: @ikunal_x ∴ 240 = 240 × 1000 = 240000 ltr m³ Total cost to fill the tank = × 50²40000¹000 = 12000"},
+{"id": "P1856", "q": "A cuboidal block of metal is melted and recast into 12 identical cubes. If the original block had dimensions 24 cm × 18 cm × 6 cm, what is the edge of each cube ? Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["8 cm", "5 cm", "6 cm", "4 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cuboid: 24 × 18 × 6 = 2592 cm³ Volume of each of 12 cubes: 2592¹2 = 216 cm³ Edge of cube = cm = 6 cm 3²16"},
+{"id": "P1857", "q": "Five cubes, each with an of edge 4 cm are joined end to end. Find the total surface area of the resulting cuboid. Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["320 cm²", "384 cm²", "352 cm²", "480 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Edge of cube = 4cm 5 cubes joined: Length = 5 × 4 = 20 cm, Breadth = 4 cm, Height = 4 cm TSA of cuboid = 2(lb + bh + lh) = 2(20 × 4 + 4×4 + 20 × 4) = 2(176) = 352 cm²"},
+{"id": "P1858", "q": "One diagonal of a rhombus is double the length of the other. If the area of the rhombus is 100 cm 2 , what are the lengths of the diagonals ?", "o": ["10 cm and 20 cm", "5 cm and 10 cm", "8 cm and 16 cm", "20 cm and 40 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let diagonals be and x² x Area of the rhombus( × d¹ × d² )¹² = 100 cm² × × = 100 = 10 cm 1² x² x ⇒ x Diagonals: =10 cm and 2 =20 cm x x"},
+{"id": "P1859", "q": "Two right prisms have the same height, but their bases are triangles with areas in the ratio 2 : 5. What is the ratio of their volumes ? Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["4 : 25", "2 : 5", "8 : 125", "5 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of a prism = Area of base × Height. Since height is the same, the ratio of volumes = ratio of areas of bases. ∴ Ratio of volumes = 2 : 5"},
+{"id": "P1860", "q": "A right circular cylinder has height 10 cm and curved surface area 220 cm². What is its volume? (use π = )²2⁷ Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["385 cm³", "350 cm³", "420 cm³", "770 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Curved surface area of cylinder (2 rh) = 220 cm² π 2 × × r× 10 = 220 r = 3.5 cm 22⁷ ⇒ Now, Volume of cylinder = r² h π = × (3.5)² × 10= 385 cm³ 22⁷"},
+{"id": "P1861", "q": "A cuboidal tank has dimensions: Length = 30 cm, Breadth = 25 cm, and Height = 24 cm. If the length is increased by 25%, the breadth is decreased by 12.5%, and the height is increased by 50%, then by what percentage does the volume of the tank change ? TG: @ikunal_x Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["61.25% increase", "60% decrease", "64.06% increase", "78.25% decrease"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the volume of tank be 100 According to question, 100 × × × = 164.06 ⇒ 5⁴ 7⁸ 3² So, the increased volume = × 100 = 64.06% 164 ."},
+{"id": "P1862", "q": "How much iron sheet (in m²) will be needed to construct a rectangular tank measuring 8m × 10m × 11m, if a circular opening of radius 2.1 meters is to be left at the top of the tank ? Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["330.82 m²", "561.04 m²", "542.14 m²", "646.98 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA of rectangular tank = 2(lb + bh + hl) = 2(8 × 10 + 10 × 11 + 11 × 8) = 556 m² Area of circle = π r² = × 2.1 × 2.1 = 13.86 m² 22⁷ Required iron sheet = 556 - 13.86 = 542.14 m²"},
+{"id": "P1863", "q": "Which of the following is NOT a polynomial? Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["a + b", "y² + 3y + 2 b³ a³", ", , or", "bc + cd + ef + 9a² y y¹ 3 y − 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A polynomial cannot have negative exponents, fractional exponents and variables inside roots. Only option (c) satisfies, , , or ⇒ y y¹ 3 y − 3 These are not allowed in a polynomial."},
+{"id": "P1864", "q": "The total length around a regular 9-sided polygon is 72 cm. If the length of each side is increased by 1.5 cm, what will be the new perimeter ? Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["82.5 cm", "85.5 cm", "88.5 cm", "90.0 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Side of polygon = = 8 cm 72⁹ Increase per side = 1.5 cm New side = 8 + 1.5 = 9.5 cm New perimeter = 9⁹.5 = 85.5 cm. ×"},
+{"id": "P1865", "q": "A metallic sphere of radius 14 cm is melted to form a cone of height 56 cm. Find the radius of the cone. Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["14 cm", "21 cm", "17 cm", "11 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question Volume of sphere = Volume of cone = h ⇒ 4³ π r³ 1³ π R² = (56) ⇒ 4³ π( 14 )³¹ 3 π R² R = 14 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1866", "q": "What is the ratio of surface areas of two spheres whose radii are in the ratio 4 : 5 ? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["25 : 16", "9 : 4", "9 : 16", "16 : 25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of sphere(A) = 4 π r² = = = A¹ A² r¹ 2 r² 2 ⇒ A¹ A² 4² 5² 16²5"},
+{"id": "P1867", "q": "A cylindrical container with internal radius 9 cm and height 36 cm is completely filled with water. The water is then poured into identical conical vessels, each having a radius of 4.5 cm and height of 8 cm. How many such conical vessels can be completely filled with the water from the cylinder ? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["55", "54", "65", "72"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let , number of cone = n Volume of cylinder = n × volume of cone × 9² × 36 = n × × (4.5)² × 8 π 1³ π 36 = n × × 0.25 × 8 n = 54¹ 3 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1868", "q": "The length of the base and height of a triangle is 30 cm and 15 cm, respectively. If the area of the triangle is equal to the area of a rectangle whose length is 25 cm, then find the breadth of the same rectangle. Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["8 cm", "11 cm", "9 cm", "15 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of triangle = × base × height 1² = × 30 × 15 = 225 cm 2¹ 2 ATQ, 225 = Area of rectangle 225 = 25 × b b = 9 cm ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1869", "q": "A decorative candle consists of two parts: a cylindrical base and a conical top. The radius of both parts is 7 cm. The cylindrical part is 15 cm high, while the conical part rises to a height of 24 cm above it. Determine the estimated total surface area of the candle. (take π = )²2⁷ Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["1364cm²", "1540cm²", "1200 cm²", "1384 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given , r = 7 cm and height of cone = 24 cm Slaint height of cone = ⇒ 7² + 24² = 25 cm So, surface area of cone = × 7 × 25²2⁷ = 550 cm 2 Again, Surface area of cylinder = 2 × × 7 × 15 = 660 cm 2²2⁷ Base area of cylinder = × = 22 × 7 π 7² =154 cm 2 According to question, Total surface area of candle = 550 + 660 + 154 = 1364 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1870", "q": "If the perimeter of an equilateral triangle is 24 units, what is its area (in square units)? Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["144", "36", "144", "16² 2³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "let the side = a Perimeter of equilateral triangle (3a) = 24 a = 8 Area of triangle = 3⁴ a² = × = 16³ 4⁸ 2³"},
+{"id": "P1871", "q": "Each side of a square park is 89 meters. a⁴-meter-wide uniform path inside the park along its boundary is formed. Find the difference between the perimeter of the park and the path now. Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["35 meters", "32 meters", "30 meters", "34 meters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Difference between the perimeter of the park and the path = 4 × 89 - 4 × 81 = 4 × 8 = 32 meters"},
+{"id": "P1872", "q": "The sides of a triangle are in the ratio 15 : 17 : 27. If the perimeter of the triangle is 2655 cm, what is the length of the smallest side in metres ? Higher Secondary 29/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["675 m", "680 m", "695 m", "685 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let triangle sides are respectively, 15 , 17 , 27 x x x perimeter of triangle = 15 + 17 + 27 x x x = 59 x According to question, 59 = 2655 = 45 x ⇒ x Smallest side of triangle = 15 × 45 = 675 m"},
