+{"id": "P1874", "q": "A right prism has a rectangular base with dimensions 8 cm and 12 cm. The height of the prism is 20 cm. Find the total surface area of the prism. Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["800 cm²", "896 cm²", "992 cm²", "1024 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TSA = 2(lb + bh + hl) = 2(8 ×12 + 12 ×20 +20 ×8) = 2(496) = 992 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1875", "q": "A rectangular garden 30 m × 20 m has four full circular flowerbeds of radius 3.5 m placed within it. What is the area left for grass? Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["420 m²", "446 m²", "456 m²", "512 m²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rectangle = 30 × 20 = 600 m² Area of 4 circles = 4 × × (3.5)²²2⁷ = 154 m² Area left in the grass = 600 - 154 = 446 m²"},
+{"id": "P1876", "q": "The base of a right prism is a regular hexagon with a side length of 12 cm. The height of the prism is 16 cm. Find the volume of the prism. Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["5536 cm³", "5986 cm³", "5048 cm³", "5304 cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of prism = Base area × height = 6 × × 12 × 12 × 16 = 3456³ 4³ = 3456 × 1.732⁵986 cm 3 ≈"},
+{"id": "P1877", "q": "A composite shape has a rectangle (15 cm × 6 cm) with a semicircle on one short side. What is the total area of the shape ? Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["104.13 cm²", "158.12 cm²", "111.28 cm²", "106.12 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of shape = Area of rectangle + area of semicircle = 6 × 15 + = 90 + 14.13³ . 14 × 3 × 3² = 104.13 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1878", "q": "The base of a right prism is a regular hexagon with a side length of 6 cm. The height of the prism is 13 cm. Find the volume of the prism. Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1536.9 cm³", "1215.9cm³", "2048.9 cm³", "2304.9cm³"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of regular hexagon = 3 × 36 = 54³ 2³ Volume of Prism = 54 × 13³ = 1215.9 cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1879", "q": "A composite shape has a rectangle (20 cm × 8cm) with a semicircle on one short side. What is the total area of the shape ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["154.22 cm²", "158.34 cm²", "185.14 cm²", "156.42 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of rectangle = 20 × 8 = 160cm 2 Area of semicircle = (4)²¹ 2 π = × × 16 = 25.14cm 2¹ 2²2⁷ ⇒ 176⁷ Total area = 160 + 25.14 = 185.14cm 2 TG: @ikunal_x"},
+{"id": "P1880", "q": "The base of a right prism is a square of side 15 cm.If the height of the prism is 8 cm, find its volume in cubic centimetres. Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1710", "1800", "1720", "1690"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume = Area of base × height = (15)² × 8 = 1800cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1881", "q": "A sphere and a right circular cone have the same volume and radius. Find the ratio of their curved surface areas (sphere: Cone). Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["4 :", "3 : 17¹7", "4 :", "7 : 15⁵"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q, Volume of sphere = Volume of cone r³ = r² h⁴ 3 π 1³ π h = 4r Curved surface area of sphere = 4 r² π Curved surface area of cone = r π r² + 16 r² Curved surface area of cone = r² π 17 Reqd."},
+{"id": "P1882", "q": "A solid metallic sphere of radius 10 cm is melted and recast into 125 identical spheres. What is the ratio of the surface area of the original sphere to the total surface area of 6 smaller spheres so formed ? Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["49 : 108 cm", "25 : 6 cm", "109 : 84 cm", "25 : 96 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "V¹ = r¹ 3 = × (10)³⁴ 3 π 4³ π ATQ, 125 r² 3 = × (10)³⁴ 3 π 4³ π r² 3 = ( )³ r² = 2cm 10⁵ ⇒ Reqd.ratio 4 × 10² : 6 × 4 × 2² π π 25 : 6"},
+{"id": "P1883", "q": "A solid hemisphere is melted into a smaller hemisphere and a cone of equal radii. The radius of both the smaller hemisphere and the cone is r, and the height of the cone is also r . Find the radius R of the original hemisphere. Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["× r", "× r³ 1 . 2³ 1 . 5", "× r", "× r³ 2³ 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q , = + ⇒ 2³ π R³ 2³ π r³ 1³ π r² × r = + ⇒ 2³ π R³ 2³ π r³ 1³ π r³ = [ 2 + 1 ] ⇒ 2³ π R³ 1³ π r³ = 2 = 3 ⇒ 2³ π R³ π r³ ⇒ R³ r³ = 1.5 × r ⇒ R³ r³ ⇒ 3¹ ."},
+{"id": "P1884", "q": "The base of a right prism is a rectangle with sides 6 cm and 8 cm. The height of the prism is 14 cm. What is the volume? Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["672 cm 3", "456 cm 3", "628 cm 3", "700 cm 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of base = 6 × 8 = 48cm 2 Volume = Area of base × height = 48 × 14 = 672cm 3"},
+{"id": "P1885", "q": "Two semicircles of radius 14 cm are attached to opposite ends of a TG: @ikunal_x rectangle of 21 cm × 14 cm. What is the total area of the figure? Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["951.94 cm²", "769.5 cm²", "885.52 cm²", "909.44 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total area of 2 semicircle = (14)² = 3.14 ×196 = 615.44cm 2 π Area of rectangle = 21 × 14 = 294cm 2 Total area = 615.44 + 294 = 909.44cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1886", "q": "The base of a right prism is a right-angled triangle with legs 40 cm and 41 cm. The height of the prism is 16 cm. Find the lateral surface area of the prism. Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1440 cm²", "1660 cm²", "1672 cm²", "1684 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area of Prism = Perimeter of Base × height Pythagorean triplet = (9,40,41) Perimeter of base = 9 + 41 + 40 = 90 Lateral surface area of Prism = 90 × 16 = 1440 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1887", "q": "The total surface area of a solid in the shape of a hemisphere mounted on a cylinder both with equal radius and height of cylinder being twice its radius is equal to. Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["8πr²", "4πr²", "7πr²", "(2 rh + 2 r² ) π π"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the radius of the cylinder and sphere be r units ⇒ Height of the cylinder h = 2r units Curved Surface area of hemisphere = 2 r² π Curved Surface area of the cylinder = 2 π rh = 2 r × 2r = 4 r² π π Total surface area of hemisphere mounted on hemisphere is Curved Surface area of hemisphere + Curved surface area of cylinder + Base area of cylinder = 2 r² + 4 r² + r² = 7 r"},
+{"id": "P1888", "q": "A right prism has a regular pentagonal base of side length 8 cm and height 13 cm. Find the lateral surface area. Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["250 cm²", "580 cm²", "300 cm²", "520 cm²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Lateral surface area = Perimeter of base × height = (8 × 5) × 13 = 520 cm 2"},
+{"id": "P1889", "q": "A hemisphere has radius R. A sphere of maximum possible radius is inscribed in the hemisphere such that it touches the curved surface internally and rests on the hemisphere's base. Find the ratio of their volume. Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["4 : 1", "5 : 4", "6 : 5", "7 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Now , According to question : ( )³² 3 π R³ 4³ π R² 1 : 2 × 4 : 1¹ 8 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1890", "q": "An equilateral triangle and a regular hexagon share the same perimeter. What is the ratio of their areas? Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1 : 5", "2 : 3", "1 : 2", "2 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Side of equilateral triangle = A Side of regular hexagon = a According to question 3A = 6a ⇒ = = ⇒ A a⁶ 3² 1 Now , Area of equilateral triangle: area of regular hexagon × 2 × 2 : × 1 × 1 ⇒ 3⁴ 3³ 2 : 2 : 3 ⇒ 4³ 4³ 3² ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1891", "q": "Find the radius of a sphere whose volume is numerically equal to its curved surface area. Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["3 units", "4 units", "2 units", "1 units"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given , Radius of a sphere whose volume = curved surface area = 4 ⇒ 4³ π r³ π r² = 1 r = 3 unit ⇒ r³ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P1892", "q": "Two solid hemispheres of radii 2R and 3R are melted and recast into a sphere and a cone.The cone has the same radius as the new sphere, and its height is three times the sphere's radius.Find the radius of the newly formed sphere. Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["R", "R³ 8 × 3¹0 ×", "R", "R³ 12 × 3¹5 ×"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question , Volume of two solid hemisphere = Volume of sphere + Volume of cone Let the Cone radius = sphere radius = x + = + 2 .3 ⇒ 2³ π 8 R³ 2³ π 27 R³ 4³ π x³ 1³ π x x ( 8 + ) = ( ) ⇒ 2³ π R³ 27 R³ π x³ 7³ 70 = 7 ⇒ π R³ π x³ 10 = ⇒ R³ x³ = R ⇒ x³ 10 ×"},
+{"id": "P1893", "q": "A company produces plastic signs shaped like regular hexagons of side 10 cm. If plastic costs ₹4/cm 2 and design costs ₹250 per piece, what is the total cost per sign ? Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["₹1288", "₹2564", "₹2500", "₹4000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Area of a regular hexagon A = 3³ 2 a² Given , a = 10cm A = × 10² 3³ 2 A = 150 A = 259.5³ ⇒ cm 2 Plastic cost = 259.5 × 4 = 1038 After adding the design cost , Total cost per sign = 1038 + 250 = ₹1288"},
+{"id": "P1894", "q": "A running track is comprised of a rectangular shape with semicircles at each of its shorter ends. The combined area of the two semicircles is 80% of the area of the central rectangular section. What is the approximate ratio of the length of the rectangular section to its width?. (Use π = 3.14) Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1 : 3.14", "15.7 : 16", "1 : 2", "3.14 : 1 eduquity-based pattern (ebp) Questions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Now , according to question = (L × B) ⇒ π r² 80¹00 = × L × B ⇒ π B² 4⁴ 5³.14 × = × L × B ⇒ B² 4⁴ 5 = ⇒ 3 . 14 ×5¹6 L B ∴ 15.7 : 16 = L : B"},
+{"id": "P1895", "q": "A solid cone of base radius 7 cm and height 18 cm is melted and recast into a hollow metal hemisphere of internal and external radii 20 cm and R TG: @ikunal_x cm, respectively. What is the value of R (in cm)?", "o": ["3⁸144³ 8441", "3⁸448³ 8568"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Volume of cone = 1³ π r² ℎ = = 294 cm 3¹ 3 π × ( 7 )² × 18 π Volume of hollow sphere = = 2³ π( R³ − r³ )²³ π[ R³ − ( 20 )³ ] According to the question, = 294² 3 π[ R³ − ( 20 )³ ] π = 441 R³ − ( 20 )³ = 441+ 8000 = cm 3 R³ ⇒ R³ 8441"},
+{"id": "P1896", "q": "The diagonals of two squares are in the ratio of 5 : 6. What is the ratio of their areas ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["18 : 20", "25 : 36", "23 : 18", "2 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, : = 5 : 6 : = 5 : 6 ⇒ 2 a¹ 2 a² ⇒ a¹ a² Now, : = 25 : 36 ⇒ a¹ 2 a² 2"},
+{"id": "P1897", "q": "If the height and diameter of a cylinder are 12 cm and 28 cm, respectively, then find the ratio of the total surface area to the curved surface area.", "o": ["13 : 5", "10 : 3", "13 : 6", "11 : 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Height and diameter of a cylinder are 12 cm and 28cm Total surface area of cylinder = 2 r(r + h) π = 2 × × 14 (14 + 12) = 88 × 26²2⁷ Curved Surface area of cylinder = 2 π rℎ = 2 × × 14 × 12 = 88 × 12²2⁷ The ratio of the total surface area to the curved surface area = 88 × 26 : 88 × 12 = 13 : 6"},
+{"id": "P1898", "q": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 3.5 cm, its surface area increases by 550 cm 2 . What was the original radius of the sphere ? (use = ) π 22⁷", "o": ["4 cm", "4.5 cm", "6 cm", "3.5 cm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "क्षेत्रमिति 3D", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Surface area of sphere = 4 π r² According to the question, 4 - 4 = 550 π( r + 3 . 5 )² π( r )²⁴ [ = 550 π ( r + 3 . 5 )² − r² ] [ = 550 × ( r + 3 ."},
