+{"id": "P1911", "q": "A milkman mixes water in pure milk and offers the mixture for sale at the original cost price of milk. If he mixes 0.25 liters of water in every 6.50 liters of milk and sells the entire mixture at the price of pure milk, what is his profit percentage? Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["2.5%", "3.84%", "6.66%", "7.64%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Cost price of milk = ₹1 per litre Total cost price = ₹6.50 Now he mix 0.25 L water with 6.50 L , Total mixture = 6.50 + 0.25 = 6.75L Now total selling price = ₹6.75 Profit percentage = × 100⁶ . 75 − 6 . 50⁶ ."},
+{"id": "P1912", "q": "A⁴5-litre mixture of petrol and kerosene is in the ratio 5 : 4. Some of it is removed and replaced with pure petrol. The final ratio becomes 7 : 4. How much of the mixture was replaced ? Graduate Level 29/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["10.6 litres", "9.78 litres", "12.4 litres", "8.2 litres Q.4 A solution of phenyl and water is 28 litres, with phenyl and water in ratio 4 : 3. 21 litres phenyl-water solution which has phenyl to water ratio as 2 : 1 is added to the 28 litres phenyl-water solution. Again 51 litres phenyl-water solution that has phenyl to water ratio as 9 : 8 is", "57 : 43", "59 : 41", "41 : 59", "43 : 57"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TG: @ikunal_x A/Q, = ⇒ 25 − 5 x⁹ + x²0 − 4 x⁹ 7⁴ 4( ) = 7( ) ⇒ 25 + 4 x⁹ 20 − 4 x⁹ 100 + = 140 - ⇒ 16 x⁹ 28 x⁹ = 40 = 8.18 L ≃ 8.2L ⇒ 44 x⁹ ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1913", "q": "Two different quantities of the same solution having ingredients A and B are stored in two different containers. In the first container, there are 252 litre of A and 441 litre of B. In the second container, the total quantity of the solution was 1188 litre. How much of the solution in the second container was made up of ingredient B ?", "o": ["765 litre", "756 litre", "752 litre", "760 litre"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In container - 1 st Ratio of ingredients A and B = 252 : 441 = 12 : 21 In container - 2 nd Quantity of ingredient B = 1188²1³3 × = 756 litre"},
+{"id": "P1914", "q": "80 litres of a mixture of spirit and water in the ratio 7 : 9 is present in a container A. 20 litres of the mixture is transferred to another container B. Then the container A is filled with 20 litres of water. Then 32 litres of the mixture is again transferred to container B. The ratio of water to spirit of the mixture in container B is equal to:", "o": ["41 : 87", "87 : 41", "131 : 77", "77 : 131"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "when 20 litres of the mixture is transferred to another container B. then, Quantity of spirit in container B = 7¹6 After replacement with 20 liter water, Quantity of spirit in container A = × = 7¹6³ 4²1⁶4 Again 32 litres of this mixture is transferred to container B."},
+{"id": "P1915", "q": "A milk vendor has 2 vessels of milk and water. The first contains 80% milk and the rest is water. The second contains 50% milk. How much mixture (in L) should he mix from each of the vessels so as to get 9 litres of mixture such that the ratio of water to milk is 1 : 2 ? (Write your answer in the order of vessel 1 and vessel 2)", "o": ["6, 3", "4, 5", "3, 6", "5, 4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Ratio - milk : water 1st vessel - 4 : 1 = 5 ) × 2 × 3 = 6²nd vessel - 1 : 1 = 2 ) × 5 × 3 = 15³rd vessel - 2 : 1 = 3 ) × 2 × 5 = 10¹st vessel Milk = 2 × 3 × 4 = 24²nd vessel Milk = 5 × 3 × 1 = 15³rd vessel Milk = 2 × 5 × 2 = 20 Required quantity = 5 , 4"},
+{"id": "P1916", "q": "A blended tea in a barrel contains Assam, Darjeeling and Nilgiri Hills in the ratio 2 : 3 : 1. Another barrel contains Darjeeling, Nilgiri Hills and Kangra Valley in the ratio 5 : 4 : 3. If equal weights of both blended tea mix together to make a TG: @ikunal_x new brand, then the weight of Kangra Valley per kilogram in the new brand is:", "o": ["500 gm", "100 gm", "250 gm", "125 gm"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Assam : Darjeeling : Nilgiri hills → Tea 2 : 3 : 1 → or 4 : 6 : 2 = 12 unit Ratio Darjeeling : Nilgiri : kangra → Tea 5 : 4 : 3 = 12 unit → Ratio after blended tea are mixed :- A : D : N : K = 4 : (6 + 5) : (2 + 4) : 3 = 4 : 11 : 6 : 3 = 24 units Weight of kangra valley tea per kg = = 125 gm 3²4 × 1000"},
+{"id": "P1917", "q": "From a cask of milk containing 64 liters, 8 liters are drawn out and the cask is filled up with water. If the same process is repeated a second, then a third time, what will be the proportion of milk to water in the resulting mixture ?", "o": ["343 : 179", "333 : 169", "443 : 179", "343 : 169"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Left quantity of milk Total mixture = (1 - )³ = ( )³⁸ 64⁷ 8 = Left quantity of milk Total mixture 343⁵12 Required ratio = 343 : (512³43) − = 343 : 169"},
+{"id": "P1918", "q": "Two vessels of equal capacity, and both completely filled, contain mixtures of milk and water in the ratio 5 : 1 and 6 : 5, respectively. Both the mixtures are now mixed thoroughly. What is the ratio of milk to water in the new mixture so obtained ?", "o": ["105 : 67", "57 : 41", "91 : 41", "28 : 43"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question quantity of both the mixture is same So maintaining the ratio we multiply first mixture with 11 and second with 6 Milk : Water Milk : water ( 5 : 1 ) × 11⁵5 : 11 ( 6 : 5 ) × 6³6 : 30⁹1 : 41"},
+{"id": "P1919", "q": "Two bottles of same capacity are 35% and 33 % full of orange juice, 1³ respectively. They are filled up completely with apple juice and then the contents of both bottles are emptied into another vessel. The percentage of apple juice in the mixture is:", "o": ["34", "64", "60", "65¹ 6¹ 3² 3⁵ 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "35% = , 33 % = 7²0¹ 3¹ 3 Orange : Apple Bottle 1⁷ : 13 = 20) × 3 → Bottle 2¹ : 2 = 3) × 20 → Balancing the given ratio we have : Orange : Apple Bottle 1²1 : 39 → Bottle 2²0 : 40 → __________________ 41 : 79 Required percentage = × 100⁷9⁴1 + 79 = × 100 = 65 % 79¹20⁵ 6"},
+{"id": "P1920", "q": "A milkman uses three containers for selling milk, their capacities being 40L, 30L and 20L respectively. He fills respectively 87.5%, 80% and 90% of the containers with a mix of milk and water in the ratios, 3 : 2, 5 : 1 and 7 : 2 respectively. What is the ratio of total quantity of milk to that of water carried by him ?", "o": ["7 : 2", "31 : 12", "35 : 9", "5 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The quantity filled in container 1 = 87.5% of 40 = 35 litres The quantity filled in container 2 =80% of 30 = 24 litres The quantity filled in container 3 = 90% of 20 = 18 litres Total quantity of milk = 35 + 24 +18 × 3³ + 2 × 5⁵ + 1 × 7⁷ + 2 = 21 + 20 + 14= 55 litres Total quantity of water = (35 + 24 + 18) - 55 = 22 litres Required ratio = 55 : 22 = 5 : 2"},
+{"id": "P1921", "q": "A⁸0-liter mixture contains Milk and water in the ratio 5 : 3. How much water (in liters) must be added to this mixture to change the ratio of Milk to water to 2 : 3 ?", "o": ["40 litres", "45 litres", "35 litres", "30 litres"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "16 units = 80 ⇒ 9 units = × 9 = 45 litres ⇒ 80¹6"},
