+{"id": "P1937", "q": "An alloy contains gold and silver in the ratio 5 : 3. A second alloy contains gold and silver in the ratio 3 : 1. What quantity of the first alloy must be added to 40 kg of the second alloy to form a new alloy containing gold and silver in the ratio 4 : 2 ?", "o": ["20 kg", "60 kg", "80 kg", "40 kg"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Gold : Silver sum 5 : 3 → 8 × 3³ : 1 → 4 × 6⁴ : 2 → 6 × 4 After equalizing the ratio of the three alloys - Therefore, the required ratio = 2 : 1 According to the question, 1 unit → 40 kg 2 unit → = 80 kg 40 × 2¹ Another method :- Consider only gold in the mixtures - Therefore, the required ratio = 2 : 1 According to the question, 1 unit → 40 kg 2 unit → = 80 kg 40 × 2¹"},
+{"id": "P1938", "q": "A merchant wants to mix two types of tea priced at Rs. 400/kg and Rs. TG: @ikunal_x³40/kg. In what ratio should they be mixed to sell the mixture at Rs. 370/kg without profit or loss ?", "o": ["1 : 1", "2 : 1", "3 : 2", "1 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": ""},
+{"id": "P1939", "q": "A solution of 150 litres has a⁴0% salt concentration. How many litres of water must be added to reduce the concentration to 20%, and then how much pure salt must be added to bring the concentration back to 50% ?", "o": ["Add 150 L of water, then 180 L of salt", "Add 90 L of water, then 170 L of salt", "Add 170 L of water, then 30 L of salt", "Add 150 L of water, then 10 L of salt"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : Solution = 150 litres Case I :- Quantity of salt = 150 × 40¹00 = 60 L Quantity of water = 150 - 60 = 90 L According to question, = ⇒ 60⁹0 + x²0⁸0²40 = 90 + = 150 ⇒ x ⇒ x Case II :- = 60 + x⁹0 + 150¹ 1 = 240 - 60 = 180 L ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1940", "q": "A container has a⁸0-litre mixture of milk and water in the ratio 3 : 1. 12 litres is removed and replaced with water. Then 12 litres is removed again and replaced with milk. What is the final percentage of water ?", "o": ["21.25%", "30.81%", "25.25.%", "20.25%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Now, Required % = × 100 = 30.81% 24 . 65⁸0"},
