+{"id": "P1942", "q": "A¹00-litre container of pure milk undergoes a¹0-litre removal and 10-litre water replacement process, repeated 3 times. Approximately how much original milk remains?", "o": ["15 litres", "17 litres 78²55²9¹00", "8 litres", "72 litres 29¹00⁹ 10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Final Quantity = Initial Quantity × (1 - ) Amount Removed Total Volume n = 100 × (1- )³¹0¹00 = 100 × ( )³ = = 72⁹0¹00⁷29¹0⁹ 10"},
+{"id": "P1943", "q": "A container has 100 litres of a mixture of acid and water in the ratio 3 : 2. 10% of the mixture is taken out and replaced with water. This operation is repeated once more. What is the final percentage of acid in the mixture ?", "o": ["54.8%", "41.2%", "43.7%", "48.6%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "10% = 1¹0 Initial Volume of Acid = × 3 = 60 L¹00⁵ Final acid = 60 × × = 48.6 L⁹ 10⁹ 10 Required Percentage = × 100⁴8 ."},
+{"id": "P1944", "q": "A⁸0-litres mixture of acid and water contains acid and water in the ratio 4 : 1. 10 litres of this mixture is removed and replaced with another solution of acid and water in the ratio 1 : 4. What is the final ratio of acid to water in the resulting mixture ?", "o": ["29 : 11", "11 : 5", "11 : 29", "17 : 13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question: Final amount of acid = 64 - ( 64) + ( 10) = 64 - 8 + 2¹0⁸0 × 1⁵ × = 58 L Water = 16 - ( 16) + ( 10)¹0⁸0 × 4⁵ × = 16 - 2 + 8 = 22 L Final ratio = = = Acid Water 58²2²9¹1 = 29 : 11"},
+{"id": "P1945", "q": "A¹36 - litre container of pure milk undergoes a¹7-litre removal and 17-litre water replacement process, repeated 2 times. Approximately how much original milk remains?", "o": ["94 litres", "104 litres 1⁸ 2⁸", "94 litres", "104 litres 2⁸ 1⁸"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Final Quantity = Initial Quantity × (1 - ) Amount Removed Total Volume n = 136 × (1- )² =136 × ( )²¹7¹36⁷ 8 = 17 × = = 104 litres 49⁸ 833⁸ 1⁸"},
+{"id": "P1946", "q": "From a⁵4-liter container of pure spirit, 9 liters are removed and replaced by water. This operation is performed a total of three times. What is the final quantity of spirit remaining in the container ?", "o": ["31.34 liters", "36.45 liters", "31.25 liters", "42.88 liters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Remaining spirit = 54 × (1 - )³ = 54 × ( )³⁹ 54⁵ 6 = 54 × × × = 31.25 L⁵ 6⁵ 6⁵ 6"},
+{"id": "P1947", "q": "A cistern contains 100 liters of pure milk . 20 liters of milk are drawn out and replaced by water. Then, 20 liters of the mixture are drawn out and replaced by water again. What is the ratio of water to milk in the final mixture ?", "o": ["18 : 1", "9 : 16", "16 : 9", "1 : 18 SSC Selection Post (XIII)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Final quantity of milk = 100(1 - )²²0¹00 = 100 × = 64 L¹6²5 Quantity of water = 100 - 64 = 36L Ratio of Water to milk = 36L : 64L = 9 : 16"},
+{"id": "P1948", "q": "Malika bought two varieties of pulses, costing Rs. 75 per kg and Rs. 125 per kg each, and mixed them in some ratio. Then she sold the mixture at Rs. 121 per kg. Making a profit of 10 percent. What was the ratio of the mixture? Matriculation Level 30/07/2025(Shift - 1)", "o": ["3 : 7", "1 : 5", "7 : 3", "4 : 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given:- Selling Price of mixture = ₹121 per kg Cost Price of mixture = 100¹21¹10 × = ₹110 per kg Using Alligation Method:- Ratio = 15 : 35 = 3 : 7"},
+{"id": "P1949", "q": "Two varieties of rice are mixed. The first variety costs ₹60 per kg and the second variety costs ₹90 per kg. In what ratio should these be mixed so that by selling the mixture at ₹84 per kg, a profit of 20% is gained? Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1 : 2", "2 : 1", "3 : 2", "4 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CP = 84 × = Rs.70¹00¹20 So, Ratio = 2 : 1"},
+{"id": "P1950", "q": "A merchant mixes 80 kg of coffee at ₹100/kg with a dearer variety at ₹140/kg. He sells the blend at ₹138/kg and gains 15% profit. How many kg of the dearer variety did he add? Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["80 kg", "88 kg", "85 kg", "87 kg"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "CP of coffee = 138 × = ₹120 /kg 100¹15¹ units = 80 kg ⇒ So, the dearer variety of coffee added = 80 kg"},
+{"id": "P1951", "q": "A cistern contains 120 liters of pure milk . 30 liters of milk are drawn out and replaced by water. Then, 30 liters of the mixture are drawn out and replaced by water again. What is the ratio of water to milk in the final mixture ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["4 : 5", "5 : 4", "7 : 9", "9 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Final quantity of milk = 120(1 - )²³0¹20 = 120 × = 67.5 L⁹ 16 Quantity of water = 120 - 67.5 = 52.5 L Ratio of Water to milk = 52.5 L : 67.5 L = 7 : 9"},
+{"id": "P1952", "q": "A solution of 150 liters contains 30% acid. How much pure acid (in liters) must be added to make the solution 50% acid? Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["60 liters", "50 liters", "36 liters", "24 liters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Acid to be added = 60L"},
+{"id": "P1953", "q": "A shopkeeper mixes 45 kg of rice at ₹65/kg with another grade at ₹95/kg. He sells the mixture at ₹80/kg, making a profit of 14 %. How many kg of the 1⁷ dearer rice did he use? Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["45 kg", "9 kg", "25 kg", "5 kg"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "14 % = 1⁷ 1⁷ Cost price of the mixture = 80 × 7⁸ = ₹70/kg 5 unit = 45kg 1 unit = 9kg"},
+{"id": "P1954", "q": "A mixture contains juice and water in the ratio 4 : 3. If 21 litres of water are added to this mixture, the ratio of juice to water becomes 5 : 4. What was the initial quantity of the mixture (in litres)? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["165 litres", "176 litres", "147 litres", "190 litres"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1 unit = 21 liters Initial quantity of mixture = 7 × 21 = 147 litres"},
+{"id": "P1955", "q": "A⁶0-liter mixture contains acid and water in the ratio 7 : 3. How much water (in liters) must be added to this mixture to change the ratio of acid to water to 4 : 5? Graduate Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["25.5 litres", "34.5 litres", "45 litres", "20 litres TG: @ikunal_x eduquity-based pattern (ebp) Questions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Acid : Water ( 7 : 3)×4²8 : 12 ( 4 : 5)×7²8 : 35 Now according to question , (28 + 12 )unit 60 ⇒ → 1unit = = 1.5L ⇒ 60⁴0 (35 - 12) unit 23 × 1.5 = 34.5 liters ⇒ →"},
+{"id": "P1956", "q": "If two kinds of resins costing ₹160 per kg and ₹210 per kg are mixed in the ratio of 2 : 3, then find the cost (in ₹) of the mixture per kg.", "o": ["185", "190", "200", "180"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Cost of the mixture per kg = = = ₹190¹60 × 2 + 210 × 3² + 3⁹50⁵"},
+{"id": "P1957", "q": "A can contains a mixture of two liquids, grape juice and pineapple juice in the ratio 13 : 11. When 8 litres of the mixture is drawn off, and the can is filled with pineapple juice, the ratio becomes 13 : 14. How many litres of pineapple juice was initially contained in the can ?", "o": ["14 litres", "28 litres", "11 litres", "33 litres"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As per figure, 1 unit = ltr. 8³ Amount of pineapple juice in the remaining mixture before adding new pineapple juice = 11 unit = 11 × = ltr 8³ 88³ Now, pineapple juice in 8 ltr mixture = × 8 = ltr 11¹1 + 13¹1³ So, total pineapple juice initially in the can = + = = 33 ltr."},
+{"id": "P1958", "q": "The concentrations of three acids, A, B, and C, are specified as 20%, 30%, and 40%, respectively. They are blended in a ratio of 3 : 5 : a, yielding a solution with a concentration of 30%. What is the value of 'a' ?", "o": ["3", "1", "2", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: concentration in new solution = 30% Acid A : B : C → Ratio 3 : 5 : a → Concentration(%)²0 : 30 : 40 → Deviation -10 : 0 : + 10 → According to question = 30²0 × 3 + 30 × 5 + 40 × a³ + 5 + a = 30⁶0 + 150 + 40 a⁸ + a²10 + 40 = 240 + 30 a a¹0 = 30 = 3 a ⇒ a"},
+{"id": "P1959", "q": "2 varieties of tea powders worth ₹250/kg and ₹300/kg are mixed with a third variety of tea powder in the ratio 1 : 1 : 2. If the mixture is worth ₹350/kg, find the price of the third variety tea powder.", "o": ["₹450/kg", "₹400/kg", "₹425/kg", "₹500/kg"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the third variety of tea powder be x According to the question, 250 × 1 + 300 × 1 + 2 × = 350 × 4 x⁵50 + 2 = 1400 x² = 850 = ₹ 425 /kg x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1960", "q": "Half litre of a solution contains 15% of alcohol. To change the alcohol concentration to 50%, find the quantity of alcohol to be mixed.", "o": ["250 ml", "350 ml", "175 ml", "400 ml"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Alcohol : Water → Initial 3 : 17 total = 20 unit → → Final 1 : 1) × 17 = 17 : 17 → Part of the alcohol that was added = 17 - 3 = 14 units 20 unit = 500 ml 14 unit = 14 = 25¹4 = 350 ml 500²0 × ×"},
+{"id": "P1961", "q": "How much water should be added to 60 liters of milk at 1 liters a rupee 1² so as to have a mixture worth 1 liters a⁷ 8 rupee ?", "o": ["15 liters", "20 liters", "27 liters", "12 liters"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "मिश्रण", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let liter water be added x According to the question, = 60⁶0 + x³ 2¹5⁸ = × = 60⁶0 + x³ 2⁸ 15 ⇒ 60⁶0 + x⁴ 5³00 = 240 + 4⁴ = 60 = 15 x ⇒ x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P1962", "q": "The remainder of the term when divided 9 + 9² +............. + 9 ( 2 n + 1 ) by 6 is:", "o": ["1", "4", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given :- 9 + 9² + ... + 9 ( 2 n + 1 )⁶ = Rem 3 , = Rem 3 , 9⁶ 9² 6 ……. = Rem 3⁹ 2 n + 1⁶ So, = = Rem 3³ × ( 2 n + 1 )⁶⁶ n + 3⁶"},
+{"id": "P1963", "q": "The six-digit number 7x1yyx is a multiple of 33 for non-zero digits x and y. Which of the following could be a possible value of (x + y) ? Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["5", "4", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 33 : the given number must be divisible by 11 and 3 . Divisibility of 11 : the difference between the sum of odd place digit and the sum of even place digit is either 0 or 11. Divisibility of 3 : the sum of all digits of the given number must be divisible by 3."},
+{"id": "P1964", "q": "Which of the following statements is correct ? I.The Value of 100² - 99² + 98² - 97² + 96² - 95² + 94² - 93² + ...... + 22² - 21² is 4840. II. The value of ( ) ( ) ( K² + 1 K² K − 1 K K⁴ )( )( ) is K¹6 - + 1 K⁴ K + 1 K K⁴ − 1 K⁴ 1 K¹6", "o": ["Neither I nor II", "Both I and II", "Only II", "Only I"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "I. ( - ) + ( - ) + ( - )¹0⁰ 2⁹ 9² 9⁸ 2⁹ 7² 9⁶ 2⁹ 5² 13 + ( - ) .......... + - = 4840⁹ 4² 9³ 2² 2² 2¹ 2 = (100 + 99)(100 - 99) + (98 - 97)(98 + 97) + (96 - 95)(96 + 95) .........+ (22 - 21)(22 + 21) = (100 + 99 + 98 + 97 + 96 + 95 …..21) = × 80 × (21 + 100) = 40 × 121 = 4840¹ 2 So, LHS = RHS II."},
+{"id": "P1965", "q": "If the 9 - digit number 83P93678Q is divisible by 72, then what is the value of ? P² + Q² + 12", "o": ["6", "7", "8", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The given number is 83P93678Q is divisible by 72. Co - prime fact or of 72 is (8, 9). So the number must be divisible b y⁸ and 9 F or divisible by 8, last 3 digits must be divisible by 8 i.e."},
+{"id": "P1966", "q": "If the 7 - digit number x8942y4 is divisible by 56, what is the value of ( + x² y) for the largest value of y, where x and y are natural numbers?", "o": ["33", "44", "55", "70"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "56 = 7 × 8 For x8942y4 to be divisible by 56, it must be divisible b y both 7 and 8. F or 8, last 3 digits 2y4 is divisible by 8 y = 2 or 6,⇒ for maximum v alue we take y = 6. F or x8942y4 to be divisible by 7, the diff erence of the sum of alternate digits tak en 3 at a time ,must be divisible by 7. 894 – (264 + x) = 630 – x⇒ x = 7 (as x⁰)⇒ ≠ Ther efore, + y = + 6 = 55."},
+{"id": "P1967", "q": "Let p, q, r and s be positive natural numbers having three exact factors 3 including 1 and the number itself If q > p and both are two-digit numbers, and r > s and both are one-digit numbers, then the value of the expression is: p − q − 1 r − s", "o": ["- s - 1", "s - 1", "1 - s", "s + 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As prime numbers have 2 factors Only the squares of prime numbers will have three factors. ⇒ Let r = 9 and s = 4 And q = 49 and p = 25 = = = - 5 p − q − 1 r − s²5 − 49 − 1⁹ − 4 − 25⁵ Putting s = 4 in all options we find only option (a) satisfies this value."},
+{"id": "P1968", "q": "Let ab, a b, is a²-digit prime ≠ number such that ba is also a prime number. The sum of all such number is:", "o": ["374", "418", "407", "396"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "HINT : ab and ba both can be prime only and only when both are odd number Such numbers are 13, 31, 17, 71, 37, 73, 79, 97 Sum = 13 + 31 + 17 + 71 + 37 + 73 + 79 + 97 = 418"},
+{"id": "P1969", "q": "In finding the HCF of two numbers by division method, the last divisor is 17 and the quotients are 1, 11 and 2, respectively. What is the sum of the two numbers ?", "o": ["833", "867", "816", "901"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sequence of quotient from bottom to top: 17 × 2 + 0 = 34³4 × 11 + 17 = 391³91 × 1 + 34 = 425 So, the no’s are 391 and 425 Required sum = 391 + 425 = 816"},
+{"id": "P1970", "q": "One of the factors of ( ), 8² k + 5² k where k is an odd number, is :", "o": ["86", "88", "84", "89"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Short trick:- Put any odd value of k. For example k = 1 (8²k + 5²k ) (8²(1) + 5²(1) )= 89 ⇒ Clearly 89 will be the factor."},
+{"id": "P1971", "q": "If a¹1 digit number 5y5884805x6 is divisible by 72, where x = y, then the value of is : xy", "o": ["3", "7", "2⁷ 7"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since 5y5884805x6 is divisible by 72, it must be divisible by 9 and 8 (coprime factors of 72). So the sum of digits of this number must be divisible by 9 and last three digits by 8."},
+{"id": "P1972", "q": "What is the largest five digit number exactly divisible by 88 ?", "o": ["99992", "99986", "99984", "99968"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Largest 5 digits number = 99999 Now , = Rem.(31)⁹9999⁸8 So , required no. = 99999³1 = 99968 −"},
+{"id": "P1973", "q": "If a¹0-digit number 620x976y52 is divisible by 88, then the least value of (x² + y²) will be:", "o": ["8", "7", "11", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "620x976y52 is divisible by 88 (8 × 11) Divisibility of 8 = last three digit of the number must be divisible by 8 Divisibility of 11 = difference of sum of odd and even places of the number is 0 or multiple of 11 Now, in the given number y52 is must be divisible by 8 So, for least value, y = 1 Again , checking divisibility of 11 (6 + 0 + 9 + 6 + 5) (2 + x + 7 + y + 2) = 0 − or m"},
+{"id": "P1974", "q": "Find the sum of 3 + 3² + 3³ + ……. + 3⁸ .", "o": ["6561", "6560", "9840", "3280"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "3 + + +........+ 3² 3³ 3⁸ 3 + 9 + 27 +....... + 6561 ⇒ Common ratio (r) = = = 3 Second term First term 9³ = = = 9840 S n a ( r n − 1 ) ( r − 1 ) ⇒ S n³ ( 3⁸ − 1 ) ( 3 − 1 )"},
+{"id": "P1975", "q": "Find the value of a to make 6234a6 divisible by 9.", "o": ["8", "7", "10", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 9 :- sum of digit of the number be divisible by 9 Then, 6234a6 = 6 + 2 + 3 + 4 + a + 6 = 21 + a Hence , value of a = 6"},
+{"id": "P1976", "q": "What is the remainder when ( + x¹7¹) is divided by (x + 1) ?", "o": ["x", "x – 1", "0", "1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If a number is in the form of , where n is odd, then the number a n + b n is divisible by (a + b). x¹7 + 1¹7 x + 1 , it is completely divisible by (x + 1) Hence, remainder = 0"},
+{"id": "P1977", "q": "A⁹ - digit number 846523X7Y is divisible by 9, and Y - X = 6. Find the value of . 2 X + 4 Y", "o": ["4", "2", "6", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given number = 846523X7Y Divisibility of 9 : sum of all digits should be divisible by 9. Hence, Y + X = 10 …….(1) and Y - X = 6 ……..(2) By solving equation (1) and (2) we get, X = 2 and Y = 8 Now, 2 X + 4 Y = 4 + 32 = 36 = 6"},
+{"id": "P1978", "q": "A⁶ - digit number has digits as consecutive natural numbers. The number is always divisible by ____.", "o": ["4", "5", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "6 digit consecutive natural numbers = 123456, 234567, 345678…….. Clearly, we can see that the sum of its digits is always multiple of 3."},
