+{"id": "P1990", "q": "The number 974581297426 is divisible by : Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["6", "11", "4", "9⁶"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "974581297426 , (9 + 4 + 8 + 2 + 7 + 2) (7 + 5 + 1 + 9 + 4 − + 6) = 32³2 = 0 − Given no. is clearly divisible by 11."},
+{"id": "P1991", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 120 ? Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["170280", "140240", "156200", "170360"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 120 :- no. should be divisible by 3 , 8 and 5 Checking divisibility of 3 , from the given option , only , option (a) satisfies the condition."},
+{"id": "P1992", "q": "When 151314 is divided by 15, the remainder is: Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["11", "6", "9", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Rem. ( )¹51314¹5 = Rem.( )¹50000 + 1305 + 9¹5 Clearly , remainder = 9"},
+{"id": "P1993", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 12 ? Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["5409844", "4298123", "4512984", "3215678 SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 12 : The given number must be divisible by 4 and 3. Divisibility of 4 : The last 2 digits of the given number must be divisible by 4. Divisibility of 3 : The sum of all the digits of the given number must be divisible by 3. In 5409844 : (5 + 4 + 0 + 9 + 8 + 4 + 4) = 34 [ not divisible by 3 ] In 4298123 : last digit if odd. So, not divisible by 4."},
+{"id": "P1994", "q": "What is the value of the expression 1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 - 6 ..... to 100 terms ?", "o": ["- 50", "- 55", "- 49", "- 60"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 - 6 ..... to 100 terms (1 - 2 ) = -1, ( 3 - 4) = -1 and so on ⇒ Total terms = 50 Therefore, 1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 - 6 ....."},
+{"id": "P1995", "q": "What is the sum of the first 200 terms of the given series? 1 + 5 + 6 + 10 + 11 + 15 + 16 + 20 +.......", "o": ["49400", "49600", "50100", "48300"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Series = 1 + 5 + 6 + 10 + 11 + 15 + 16 + 20 + ....... = (1 + 6 + 11 + 16 + ....) + (5+10 + 15 +.. ) = [2 + (99) × 5] + [10 + (99) S²00¹00² 100² × 5] = [497] + 50[505] = 50 × 1002⁵0¹8 = 50100"},
+{"id": "P1996", "q": "What is the value of the expression 1 - 7 + 2 - 8 + 3 - 9 + 4 - 10 +.... to 100 terms?", "o": ["- 200", "- 360", "- 300", "- 240"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1⁷ + 2⁸ + 3⁹ + 4 − − − − 10 + .... to 100 (1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + .........50) (7 + 8 + 9 + − .......56) = ( ) ) S n⁵0² [ 1 + 50 ] − ( 50² [ 7 + 56 ] = 1275¹575 = 300 − −"},
+{"id": "P1997", "q": "If the sum of a number and its reciprocal is 4, find the sum of their squares,", "o": ["12", "16", "14", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number be x According to the question, x + = 4 then, sum of their squares 1 x = 16² = 14 ⇒ x² + 1 x² −"},
+{"id": "P1998", "q": "What is the value of - + 98² 97² - + - + ………… - 96² 95² 94² 93² 12² 11²", "o": ["4725", "4796", "4851", "4926"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "- + - + - 98² 97² 96² 95² 94² + ………… - 93² 12² 11² = (98 + 97) (98 - 97) + (96 + 95) (96 - 95) + (94 + 93) (94 - 93) + .............(12 + 11) (12 - 11) = 98 + 97 + 96 + 95 + 94 + 93……..12 + 11 Total term (n) = 88 Sum of given series = (first term + last n² term) = (98 + 11) = 44 × 109 = 4796⁸8²"},
+{"id": "P1999", "q": "If the sum of squares of two real numbers is 12 and the product of the numbers is 4, find the difference between the numbers.", "o": ["4", "8", "1", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the numbers be and y. x + = 12 , y = 4 ⇒ x² y² x = + 2 y = 12⁸ = 4 ⇒ ( x − y )² x² y² − x − = 2 ⇒ x − y"},
+{"id": "P2000", "q": "What is the value of - + - 4² 3² 6² 5² 7 + - + ...... - ? 8² 7² 92² 91²", "o": ["4272", "4280", "4278", "4275"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Formula :- = ( a + b)( a b) a² − b² − - + - + - + ...... - 4² 3² 6² 5² 8² 7² 92² 91² 19⁷ + 11 + 15 +.................183 Number of terms( ) = a + (n¹)d a n − 183 = 7 + (n¹)4 ⇒ n = 45 − S n = [2a + (n − 1) × d] n² = [2⁷ + (45 − 1) × 4]⁴5² × = [14 + 44 × 4] = 4275⁴5²"},
+{"id": "P2001", "q": "In a class of students, the first student has 2 toffees, second has 4 toffees, third has 6 toffees and so on. If the number of students in the class is 25, then the total number of toffees are divisible by___________.", "o": ["5 and 7", "5 and 13", "11 and 13", "7 and 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total number of toffee students have = 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 …… 25 terms Sum = { 2a + (n - 1)d} n² Sum = { 2 × 2 + (25 - 1) × 2} 25² = = 650 = 25 × 26 = 5 × 5 ×13 ×2²5² × 52⁶50 is clearly divisible by 5 and 13 ."},
+{"id": "P2002", "q": "The largest five-digit number which when divided by 7, 9 and 11, leaves the same remainder as 3 in each case, is:", "o": ["95840", "98685", "96720", "99795"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "L.C.M. (7, 9, 11) = 693 Now, largest five digit number is 99999 When we divide 99999 by 693 , the remainder will be 207. No."},
+{"id": "P2003", "q": "A number n when divided by 6, leaves a remainder 3. What will be the remainder when ( ) is divided n² + 5 n + 8 by 6 ?", "o": ["1", "3", "5", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concepts :- If a number ‘n’ when divided by ‘x’ leaves remainder ‘y’ Then ‘ ’ divided by the same no. then n² reminder will be ‘ ’ y² and ‘zn’ is divided by ‘x’ then the remainder will be zy. According to question , A number ‘n’ when divided by 6 leaves the remainder 3 . Now, Rem."},
+{"id": "P2004", "q": "If a number K = 42 × 25 × 54 × 135 is divisible by 3 a , then find the maximum value of a.", "o": ["6", "7", "4", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "K = 42 × 25 × 54 × 135 K = 3 × 14 × 5 × 5 × 3³ × 2 × 3³ × 5 = 3⁷ × 14 × 5 × 5 × 2 × 5 Hence, maximum value of a = 7"},
+{"id": "P2005", "q": "If the 9 - digit number 72x8431y4 is divisible by 36, what is the value of ( x y ) for the smallest possible value of − y x y, given that x and y are natural numbers?", "o": ["1", "5", "7", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "36 = 4 × 9 For 72x8431y4 to be divisible by 4, its last 2 digit y4 must be divisible by 4. For the smallest value of y, we have y = 2 Now, For 72x8431² 4 to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e. 7 + 2 + x + 8 + 4 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 31 + x must be divisible by 9, For this, the value of x must be 5 i.e. 31 + 5 = 36, which is divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2006", "q": "The number 150328 is divisible by 23. If the digits are rearranged in descending order and five times of 13 is subtracted from the new number thus formed, then the resultant number will be divisible by:", "o": ["3", "5", "11", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "After arranging the digits in descending order and subtracting 65 from the new no, we get : 853210⁸53210 - 65 = 853145, which → is divisible by 5 (∵last digit is 5)"},
+{"id": "P2007", "q": "A six-digit number 763254 is divisible by 18. If we subtract five times of 41 from the number, then the new number which is formed will be divisible by:", "o": ["2", "7", "5", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "763254 - 205 = 763049 So, the new number formed is divisible by 7."},
+{"id": "P2008", "q": "If lies between 6 and 7, where 3 N N is an integer then how many values N can take?", "o": ["126", "127", "128", "125"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "It is given that, 6 < < 7 ⇒ 6 < < 7³ N N¹ 3 < < ⇒ 216 < N < 343⁶ 3 ( N¹ 3 )³⁷ 3 So, the total possible values of N = (343 - 216) - 1 = 126"},
+{"id": "P2009", "q": "What is the sum of the first 20 terms of the following series ? 1² + 2³ + 3⁴ + 4⁵ …… × × × ×", "o": ["3160", "2940", "3240", "3080"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Clearly, we can observe that each term is followed by n(n+1). So, T n = n(n + 1) = + n n² S²0 = + n n = 1²0 ∑ n² n = 1²0 ∑ S²0 = ( ) + 20 × 21 × 41⁶ 20 × 21² S²0 = 2870 + 210 = 3080"},
+{"id": "P2010", "q": "What is the value of + + 7² 11³ 7⁶ + + + +…..+ + ? 11¹5⁷ 12¹1³5⁷ 156¹1⁵75", "o": ["3917", "355", "3816", "325"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given series is the combination of two series : I. + + + ..... 7² 7⁶ 7¹2⁷ 156 = 7( + + +… )¹¹ × 2¹ 2 × 3¹ 3 × 4¹ 12 × 13 = 7(1 - + - + - ….. - 1² 1² 1³ 1³ 1⁴ 1¹2 )⁷ (1 - ) = 7 × = 1¹3 ⇒ 1¹3¹2¹3⁸4¹3 II. + + ….. 11³ 11¹5¹1⁵75 = ( + …. )¹1² 2¹ × 3² 3 × 5² 23 × 25 = (1 - + - …."},
+{"id": "P2011", "q": "Which of the following is not a pair of co-prime numbers? Graduate Level 01/08/2022 ( Shift - 4 )", "o": ["22, 24", "1, 4", "3,7", "21, 22"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know, co-prime no’s are pairs of no’s that have only one common factor that is 1. From the given option, we get 22 and 24 have two common factors."},
+{"id": "P2012", "q": "The sum of three prime numbers is 90. If one of them exceeds another by 30, then one of the numbers is: Graduate Level 05/08/2022 ( Shift - 3)", "o": ["41", "67", "47", "59"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept : odd + odd = even, even + odd = odd Since, the sum of three prime no’s is even, it implies that one of the three no’s must be 2 i.e.the only even prime no."},
+{"id": "P2013", "q": "If 608xy0 is divisible by both 3 and 11, the nonzero digit in the hundred’s place and ten’s places, respectively, are: Higher Secondary 02/08/2022 ( Shift - 2 )", "o": ["5 and 6", "5 and 8", "8 and 5", "6 and 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 3 :- A number is divisible by 3 if the sum of the number is divisible by 3. Divisibility of 11 :- A number is divisible by 11 if the difference of sum of odd places values and even places values is equal to 0 or multiple of 11. Given no. = 608xy0 Sum of no."},
+{"id": "P2014", "q": "If the product 6352 × 7A1 is divisible by 12, then the value of A is: Higher Secondary 03/08/2022 ( Shift - 4 )", "o": ["6", "3", "5", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "12 = 4 × 3 = 6352 × 7 A¹ 4 × 3 As 6352 is divisible by 4 , so 7A1 should be divisible by 3. For 7A1 to be divisible by 3, the sum of its digits i.e. 7 + A + 1 = 8 + A, should be divisible by 3."},
+{"id": "P2015", "q": "If the 5-digit number 743pq, is divisible by 90, then = ? q p Higher Secondary 05/08/2022 ( Shift - 2 )", "o": ["0", "5", "10", "1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "90 = 10 × 9 For 743pq to be divisible by 10, its unit digit must be zero. so, q = 0 For 743p⁰ to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e.7 + 4 + 3 + p + 0 = 14 + p, should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2016", "q": "Find the unit digit in ( 14 )¹12 + ( 14 )¹13 Higher Secondary 05/08/2022 ( Shift - 2 )", "o": ["2", "8", "0", "4 SSC MTS 2021 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The unit digit of ( 14)¹12 + (14)¹13 = 14¹12 (1 + 14) = (14¹12 × 3) × 5 = 0 Unit digit is zero."},
+{"id": "P2017", "q": "What will be the smallest natural number to be filled in the blank for the number ’23_45678’ to be divisible by 22 ?", "o": ["7", "1", "9", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "22 = 11 × 2 For 23x45678 to be divisible by 11, difference of the sum of alternate digits. i.e (8 + 6 + 4 +3 ) - (7 + 5 + x + 2 ), should be divisible by 11."},
+{"id": "P2018", "q": "When f(x) = 15 x³ − 14 x² − is divided by (3x + 2), then the 4 x + 10 remainder is:", "o": ["− 1", "1", "− 2", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Using remainder theorem, g(x) = 3x + 2 = 0 x = - ⇒ 2³ Putting x = - in f(x)²³ f(x) = 15 x³ − 14 x² − 4 x + 10 f( - ) = 15 × - )³ - 14 × ( - )² - 4 × 2³ ( 2³ 2³ ( - ) + 10² 3 = - - + + 10 = - + 10⁴0⁹ 56⁹ 8³ 72⁹ = - 8 + 10 = 2"},
+{"id": "P2019", "q": "If the number 732XY is divisible by 70, then find the minimum value of . x + y²", "o": ["2", "1", "0", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "70 = 7 × 10 For 732XY to be divisible by 70. We have to check the divisibility of 10. So, for this unit digit i.e.y should be 0. Again, for 732X0 to be divisible by 7 . we have x = 2 or 9 but to get the minimum value we have to take x = 2."},
+{"id": "P2020", "q": "The sum of the first 78 natural numbers from 1 to 78 is divisible by", "o": ["79", "61", "29", "30"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of first 78 natural no. = = 39 × 79⁷8 ( 78 + 1 )² On checking the options we get the given no i.e. 39 × 79 is divisible by 79"},
+{"id": "P2021", "q": "If the nine-digit number 9m2365n48 is completely divisible by 88, what is the value of (m² n² ) , for the × smallest value of n, where m and n are natural numbers?", "o": ["36", "64", "32", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "88 = 11 × 8 For 9m2365n48 to be divisible by 8, last three digits that is, n48 must be divisible by 8, now if we take n = 2 (smallest possible value) then n48 = 248 which is divisible by 8. For 9m2365² 48 to be divisible by 11, the difference of the sum of its alternate digits i.e(8 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 9) - (4 + 5 + 3 + m) = 15 - m,should be divisible by 11."},
+{"id": "P2022", "q": "If each of the two numbers 5¹6 and 5²5 are divided by 6, the remainder are and , respectively. What is the R¹ R² value of ? R¹ + R² R²", "o": ["1", "6", "5", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "On dividing 5 by 6 we get R = 5 or -1. For ease of calculation we use R = -1. = = , = 1 R¹ 5¹6⁶ (− 1 )¹6⁶ R¹ Again, = = R² 5²5⁶ (− 1 )²5⁶ = = - 1 = 6 - 1 = 5 R² Now, = = ."},
+{"id": "P2023", "q": "Let p, q, r and s be positive natural numbers having three exact factors including 1 and the number itself If q > p and both are two-digit numbers, and r > s and both are one-digit numbers, then the value of the expression is: p − q − 1 r − s", "o": ["- s - 1", "s - 1", "1 - s", "s + 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As prime numbers have 2 factors Only the squares of prime numbers will have three factors. Let r = 9 and s = 4 And q = 49 and p = 25 = = = - 5 p − q − 1 r − s²5 − 49 − 1⁹ − 4 − 25⁵ Putting s = 4 in all options we find only option (a) satisfies this value."},
+{"id": "P2024", "q": "Let x be the least number which on being divided by 8, 12, 15, 24, 25 and 40 leaves a remainder of 7 in each case. What will be the remainder when x is 10 divided by 29 ?", "o": ["18", "27", "19", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM (8, 12, 15, 24, 25, 40) = 600 Required number = 600 + 7 = 607. When 607 is divided by 29 we get, 607 = 29 × 20 + 27 So, 27 is required remainder."},
+{"id": "P2025", "q": "The average of squares of five consecutive odd natural numbers is 233. What is the average of the largest number and the smallest number?", "o": ["11", "17", "13", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let five consecutive odd natural numbers are (x - 4), (x - 2), x, (x + 2), (x + 4) + + + ( x − 4 )² ( x − 2 )² x² ( x + 2 )² + = 233⁵ 5 + 40 = 1165 ( x + 4 )² × ⇒ x² 5 = 1125 ⇒ x = 15 , x² Largest number = 19 Smallest number = 11 Average = 15"},
+{"id": "P2026", "q": "If the 5-digit number 593ab is divisible by 3, 7 and 11, then what is the value of (a² - b² + ab) ?", "o": ["35", "31", "25", "29"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM of 3, 7, 11 = 231 When 59399 is divided by 231, Reminder = 32 Required number = 59399 - 32 =59367 Compare 59367 with 593ab 24 so , a = 6 , b = 7 , (a² - b² + ab) = 29"},
+{"id": "P2027", "q": "If a nine-digit number 489x6378y is divisible by 72, then the value of will be : 8 x + 6 y", "o": ["10", "4", "6", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "72 = 8 × 9 For divisibility of 8, last 3 digits should be divisible by 8 The possible value of y = 4 For divisibility of 9, the sum of digits should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2028", "q": "If the number 87m6203m is divisible by 6, then find the sum of all possible values of ‘m’.", "o": ["10", "20", "16", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "6 = 2 × 3 For divisibility of 6, number should be divisibility by 2 and 3 both For 2, last digit should be divisible by 2 Therefore, possible values of m = 0, 2, 4, 6, and 8 For 3, sum of digits of number should be divisible by 3 Put, m = 0 ⇒ 8 + 7 + 0 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 0 = 26 (not divisible by 3) Put, m = 2 ⇒ 8 + 7 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 2 = 30 (divisible by 3) Put, m = 4 ⇒ 8 +"},
+{"id": "P2029", "q": "When a positive integer n is divided by 12, the remainder is 5. What will be the remainder if is 8 n² + 7 divided by 12 ?", "o": ["2", "5", "3", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When a positive integer n is divided by 12 remainder is 5 N = 17 ⇒ 8n² + 7 = 2319 When 2319 is divided by 12, gives remainder 3"},
+{"id": "P2030", "q": "When positive numbers x, y and z are divided by 31, the reminders are 17, 24 and 27 respectively. When (4x - 2y + 3z) is divided by 31, the reminder will be : 11", "o": ["9", "8", "16", "19"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(4x - 2y + 3z) = 4 × 17 − 24 × 2 + 27 × 3 (4x - 2y + 3z) = 101 When 101 is divided by 31 we get reminder = 8"},
+{"id": "P2031", "q": "If the five digit number 235xy is divisible by 3, 7 and 11 then what is the value of (3x - 4y) ?", "o": ["8", "9", "5", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM of 3, 7, 11 is = 231 Let the number be 23599 When 23599 is divided by 231 we get remainder as 37 So the number is = 23599 - 37 = 23562 x = 6 and y = 2 (3x - 4y) = 18 - 8 = 10"},
+{"id": "P2032", "q": "Let a, b and c be the fractions such that . If c is divided by a, the a ≺ b ≺ c result is , which exceeds b by . If a + b⁵ 2⁷ 4 + c = 1 , then (c - a) will be equal to : 11¹2", "o": ["1", "3", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, a + b + c = 1 …(1) and = 11¹2 c a⁵ 2 Let c = 5 unit and a = 2 unit According to the question b = - = 5² 7⁴ 3⁴ Put this value in eq (1) a + c = - = 23¹2³ 4⁷ 6 (5 + 2) unit = 1 unit = 7⁶ ⇒ 1⁶ 5 unit = 2 unit = ⇒ 5⁶ ⇒ 1³ Required difference = - = 5⁶ 1³ 1²"},
+{"id": "P2033", "q": "Three fractions, x,y and z, are such that x y z. When the smallest ≻ ≻ of them is divided by the greatest, the result is , which exceeds y by 0.0625. 9¹6 If x + y + z = 1 , then the value of x + z¹3²4 is :", "o": ["1", "7⁸ 25²4⁷ 6"], "ol": ["b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, x + y + z = 1 …(1) and = 13²4 z x⁹ 16 Let z = 9 unit and x = 16 unit According to the question y = - 0.0625⁹ 16 = - = 9¹6⁶25¹0000¹ 2 Put this value in eq (1) x + z = - = ⇒ 37²4¹ 2²5²4"},
+{"id": "P2034", "q": "Let a,b and c be the fractions such that . If c is divided by a, a ≺ b ≺ c the result is , which exceeds b by . 9² 23⁶ If a + b + c = , then (2a + b - c) will be 19¹2 equal to :", "o": ["1", "2", "1", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, a + b + c = …(1) and = 19¹2 c a⁹ 2 Let c = 9 unit and a = 2 unit According to the question b = - = 9² 23⁶ 2³ Put this value in eq (1) a + c = - = 19¹2² 3¹1¹2 (9 + 2) unit = 1 unit = ⇒ 11¹2 ⇒ 1¹2⁹ unit = 2 unit = ⇒ 3⁴ ⇒ 1⁶ (2a + b - c) = 2( ) + - = 1⁶ 2³ 3⁴ 1⁴"},
+{"id": "P2035", "q": "If a¹0-digit number 897359y7x2 is divisible by 72, then what is the value of (3x - y) , for the possible greatest value of y ?", "o": ["3", "8", "7", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Since the number is divisible by 72 it must be divisible by 9 and 8. The number to be divisible by 8, the last three digits must be divisible by 8. When 7x2 is divided by 8, the possible value for x are = 1, 5, 9 The number to If x = 1, then y = 3 If x = 5, then y = 8be divisible by 9, the sum of numbers must be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2036", "q": "The five - digit number 45yz0 is divisible by 40. What is the maximum possible value of (y + z) ?", "o": ["15", "18", "16", "17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "45yz0 For divisibility of 40 number must be divisible by 8 and 5 Divisibility of 5:- A number is divisible by 5 if its last digit is 0 or 5 Divisibility of 8 :- if the last three digits of the number are either all zeros or are divisible by 8: Maximum possible value of y and z be 8 and 8 respectively, So, the value of (y + z) = 8 + 8 = 16"},
+{"id": "P2037", "q": "In an election, voters have the option to vote for one of three candidates. They also have the option to select 'None Of The Above' (NOTA) to reject all the candidates. All three candidates get 6 times the NOTA votes. The winner gets twice the votes of the second runner-up. The first runner-up gets 900 more votes than NOTA and defeats the second runner-up by 150 votes. Find the total number of votes cast.", "o": ["15177", "11577", "11025", "17715"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let winner = A , 1 st runner up = B, 2 nd runner up = C and nota = N According to question A = 2C, B = N + 900 and C = N + 900 - 150 Now, A + B + C = 6N²C + B + C = 6N³C + B = 6N³C + N + 900 = 6N³(N + 900 - 150) + N + 900 = 6N³N + 2250 + N + 900 = 6N³150 = 2N ⇒ N = 1575 Hence, B = N + 900 = 2475 C = N + 900 - 150 = 2325 ⇒ A = 2C = 4650 Total votes = A + B + C + N = 4650 +"},
+{"id": "P2038", "q": "Ram gives a six-digit number 468312 to Shyam to check the divisibility. Shyam tells Ram that the number is divisible by 57. Shyam asks Ram, “If we rearrange the digits of this number in descending order, then by which number will it be always divisible ?” Graduate Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2", "3", "19", "17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 3 : For any no to be divisible by 3, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 3. 57 = 19 × 3 Given that , 468312 is divisible by (19 ×3) On arranging it in descending order , digits remain the same ."},
+{"id": "P2039", "q": "A⁴-digit number '34PQ' divisible by 3,5 and 7. Find the value of P + Q . Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["11", "12", "10", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If the number is divisible by 5 means the last digit is either 0 or 5. Let Q = 0 Now we have to find the value of P . For divisibility by 3, the sum of the digits should be divisible by 3. P = 2, 5, 8 ⇒ But the numbers 3420, 3450 and 3480 are not divisible by 7. Now, take the value of Q = 5."},
+{"id": "P2040", "q": "A six-digit number is divisible by 33. If 21 is added to the number, then the new number which formed is also divisible by: Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["5", "4", "2", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let six digit number = 33 × x New number = 33 + 21 × x = 3{(11 ) + 7} × x We can say that new number is divisible by 3"},
+{"id": "P2041", "q": "When 200 is divided by a positive integer x, the remainder is 8. How many values of x are there? Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["7", "5", "8", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When 200 is divided by x, the remainder is 8. So, the number exactly divisible by x is 192. Factors of 192 = 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 192 The remainder is always less than the divisor , so x > 8 Desired values are 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, ⇒ 64, 96, 192."},
+{"id": "P2042", "q": "A length of a violin string varies inversely with respect to the frequency of its vibrations. The frequency of a¹4-inch-long violin string is 450 cycles per second. Find the frequency of a¹2-inch violin string.", "o": ["515 cycles per second", "525 cycles per second", "520 cycles per second", "510 cycles per second"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question , Length ∝ L = 1 Frequency ⇒ K F¹4 = K = 6300 ⇒ K⁴50 ⇒ Now , 12 = ⇒ 6300 F F = = 525 cycles per second ⇒ 6300¹2"},
+{"id": "P2043", "q": "b is the sum of two quantities, one of which varies inversely as the square of a² , and the other of which varies directly as a. Identify the relationship between a and b if b = 49 when a = 3 or 5.", "o": ["a = 3b", "a = 3b² − 7/a", "b = 8a + 225/a²", "b = 2a"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In this type question solving by the help of options, On checking all options one by one, only option (c) satisfies. b = 8a + ⇒ 225 a² LHS = b = 49 RHS = 8a + 225 a² = 8 × 5 + = 40 + 9 = 49²25²5 Hence, LSH = RHS"},
+{"id": "P2044", "q": "If P (P > 0) is the least possible number that must be subtracted from 7, 9, and 12 so that the resulting numbers are in continued proportion, then find the value of P² + 1.", "o": ["10", "12", "3", "8 SSC CGL 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If a, b and c are in continue proportion then it can be write as a : b : : b : c ⇒ b² = ac Let least possible number be P and subtracted from each other = (7 - P ) (12 - P ) P = 3 ⇒ ( 9 − P )² ⇒ ∴ P² + 1 = 9 + 1 = 10"},
+{"id": "P2045", "q": "Without doing the actual division, find the remainder when 28735429 is divided by 9.", "o": ["4", "2", "8", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 9:- sum of digits of number either be 0 or divisible by 9. Given number = 28735429² + 8 + 7 + 3 + 5 + 4 + 2 + 9 = 40 For making given number divisible by 9 we get remainder 4 i.e."},
+{"id": "P2046", "q": "In a division problem, the divisor is 4 times the quotient and 2 times the remainder. If the remainder is 32, then find the dividend.", "o": ["1056", "1650", "3240", "1065"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Remainder = 32 Divisor = 4 × quotient Divisor = 2 × remainder = 2 × 32 = 64 So, divisor = 64 , quotient = 16 dividend = divisor × quotient + ⇒ remainder dividend = 64 × 16 + 32 = 1056 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2047", "q": "In a garden, there are 6 daisy plants the first year. Each year, a gardener adds 3 new daisy plants. He has 26 jasmine plants the first year and loses 2 each year. When will the number of daisy plants equal to the number of jasmine plants after the first year?", "o": ["5 years", "4 years", "2 years", "6 years"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "After checking options one by one we get, After 4 years, Daisy plants = 6 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 = 18 And Jasmine plants = 26 - 2 - 2 - 2 -2 =18 Hence, after 4 years daisy plants and jasmine plants become equal."},
+{"id": "P2048", "q": "When f(m) = m⁵ + 5m⁴ - 3m + 7 is divided by (m - 2), then the remainder is _______.", "o": ["7", "5", "0", "113"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : f(m) = m⁵ + 5m⁴ - 3m + 7 According to the question, m - 2 = 0 m = 2 ⇒ Remainder = 2⁵ + 5 × 2⁴ - 3 × 2 + 7 = 32 + 80 - 6 + 7 = 113"},
+{"id": "P2049", "q": "A number r when divided by 8 leaves remainder 3. What will be the remainder when (r² + 6r + 7) is divided by 8?", "o": ["2", "3", "1", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number (r )⁸³ (rem) ÷ → Number ( ÷ 8 r² + 6 r + 7 ) = 2 (rem )³² + 6 ( 3 ) + 7⁸ 34⁸ →"},
+{"id": "P2050", "q": "If the 9-digit number 5x79856y6 is divisible by 36, then what is the negative value of for the largest ( 2 x + y ) possible value of y, given x and y are natural numbers?", "o": ["-7", "-2", "-4", "-5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number = 5⁷9856⁶ x y For divisibility of 36 a number must be divisible by 9 and 4. For divisibility of 4 :- last 2 digit must be divisible by 4. Hence , possible value of = 1, 3,5,7, 9 y We need largest possible value of = 9 y For divisibility of 9 :- sum of number must be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2051", "q": "What number should be subtracted from 3 - 4² - 8 + 11 to make the x x x number divisible by ( + 2)? x", "o": ["9", "5", "3", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When 3 - 4² - 8 + 11 ( + 2) , we get x x x ÷ x³ as remainder, so if 3 is subtracted from 3 - 4² - 8 + 11 than it is divisible by ( x x x x + 2)"},
+{"id": "P2052", "q": "Find the greatest value of ‘k’ in a⁶-digit number 6745k2 such that the number is divisible by 3.", "o": ["8", "6", "9", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 3 : Sum of the digit of the given number should be divisible by 3 Here , 6 + 7 + 4 + 5 + k + 2 = 24 + k If k = 9 , then 24 + 9 = 33 (which is divisible by 3 ) ∴ Greatest value of k = 9"},
+{"id": "P2053", "q": "Which composite number can divide the sum of the first 12 natural numbers?", "o": ["6", "12", "4", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Sum of first natural number = n n ( n + 1 )² Sum of first 12 natural number = = 6¹3¹2 ( 12 + 1 )² × Hence, 6 can divide the sum of first 12 natural numbers."},
+{"id": "P2054", "q": "A number whose fifth part increased by 5 is equal to its third part decreased by 7. Find half of the number.", "o": ["45", "150", "80", "60"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number is 15 (LCM of 5 and 3) x According to question of 15 + 5 = of 15 - 7¹ 5 x¹ 3 x³ + 5 = 5 - 7² = 12 = 6 x x ⇒ x ⇒ x Hence, number = 15 = 15⁶ = 90 x × Half of number = 45"},
+{"id": "P2055", "q": "The sum of the five consecutive even numbers is 2720. The sum of the third and fifth numbers is :", "o": ["1392", "1192", "1092", "1292"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let five consecutive number be - 4 , - 2, , + 2 , + 4 respectively x x x x x Their sum = 5 x According to the question, 5 = 2720 ⇒ = 544 x x Required sum = ( + + 4) x x = 2 × 544 + 4 = 1092"},
+{"id": "P2056", "q": "K being any odd number greater than 1, k³3 –k is always divisible by:", "o": ["5", "13", "24", "15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: k³3 –k = k(k³2 - k) = k(k¹6 - 1)(k¹6 + 1) = k(k⁸ - 1)(k⁸ + 1)(k¹6 + 1) = k(k⁴ - 1)(k⁴ + 1)(k⁸ + 1)(k¹6 + 1) = k(k² - 1)(k² + 1)(k⁴ + 1)(k⁸ + 1)(k¹6 + 1) = k(k - 1)(k+1)(k² +1)(k⁴ +1)(k⁸ +1)(k¹6 +1) Put the value of k = 3, 5 ,7….."},
+{"id": "P2057", "q": "A two - digit number is 12 more than five times the sum of its digits. The number formed by reversing the digits is 9 less than the original number. The number is:", "o": ["96", "78", "87", "69"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let number = 10 + y x According to the question, Number is 12 more than five times the sum of its digits 10 + y = 5( + y) + 12 x x⁵ - 4y = 12 -------(i) x Number formed by reversing the digits is 9 less than the original number 10y + = 10 + y - 9 x x - y = 1 -------(ii) x Equation [(i) - 5 × (ii)] we get; y = 7 Put y = 7 in equation (ii) we get; - 7 = 1 = 8 x ⇒ x Hence, number "},
+{"id": "P2058", "q": "Identify a single-digit number Search on TG: @apna_pdf other than 1, which may exactly divide the number 17³ + 18³ − 16³ − 15³", "o": ["3", "5", "7", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "17³ + 18³ − 16³ − 15³ 4913 + 5832 − 4096 − 3375 = 3274 Clearly, the number is divisible by 2."},
+{"id": "P2059", "q": "The number 611611611611 is: (A) divisible by both 6 and 11 (B) neither divisible by 6 nor by 11 (C) divisible by 6 only (D) divisible by 11 only", "o": ["(B)", "(D)", "(A)", "(C) SSC CPO 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "611611611611 As per question check divisibility by 6 and 11 For divisibility of 6 it must be divisible by 2 and 3⁶11611611611 is not divisible by 2 hence it is not divisible by 6 also now, for divisibility of 11, sum of alternate digits 1 + 6 + 1 + 1 + 6 + 1 = 16⁶ + 1 + 1 + 6 + 1 + 1 = 16 Difference of sum of alternate digits = 16 - 16 = 0 Hence it is divisible by 11 only."},
+{"id": "P2060", "q": "18 students of a class took part in a quiz. If the number of girls is 8 more than the number of boys, find the product of the number of boys and girls.", "o": ["56", "36", "63", "65 SSC Selection Post (Phase - XII)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Girls - Boys = 8 … (i) Girls + Boys = 18 … (ii) On solving eq . (i) and (ii), we get Girls = 13 and Boys = 5 Product of Girls and Boys = 13⁵ = 65 ×"},
+{"id": "P2061", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 11? Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["908781", "969331", "701611", "611571"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 11 : The difference of the sum of the alternate digits of any number is either 0 or multiple of 11. Now, after checking all the options, only option (b) gets satisfied."},
+{"id": "P2062", "q": "The number 10000 is exactly divisible by which of the following numbers ? Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["18", "17", "25", "14"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "From the given option, we have ; (a)18¹0000 is not divisible by 18 → (b)17 → 10000 is not divisible by 17 (c)25 → 10000 is divisible by 25 (d)14 → 10,000 is not divisible by 14 Clearly, we can see that only option (c) is correct."},
+{"id": "P2063", "q": "If the number 3727⁴ is x completely divisible by 8, then the smallest integer in place of will be x Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["6", "8", "2", "0"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisibility by 8, the last three digits should be divisible by 8. Here 7⁴ will be divisible by 8. x The value of will be 0, 4, 8."},
+{"id": "P2064", "q": "Which of the following is a condition of divisibility of a number by six? Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["Sum of digits is divisible by 6", "Last digit is 3 or 6", "Sum of digits is divisible by 3 and last digit is even", "Sum of digits is divisible by 3 and first digit is even"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Condition for the divisibility of 6 ; Sum of digits is divisible by 3 and last digit is even."},
+{"id": "P2065", "q": "The largest 4 - digit number that is exactly divisible by 88 is: Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["9848", "9988", "8888", "9768"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "88 = 11 × 8 From the given option, we have ; (a)⁹848 → 9848 is divisible by 8 but not divisible by 11 (b)⁹988→ 9988 is divisible by 11 but not divisible by 8 (c)⁸888 → 8888 is divisible by 8 and 11. (d)⁹768 → 9768 is also divisible by 8 and 11."},
+{"id": "P2066", "q": "Find the least value digit which is assigned to so that the number x is divisible by 9. 1972 x⁴71 Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["3", "5", "4", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For 1972⁴71 to be divisible x by 9, the sum of its digits i.e.1 + 9 + 7 + 2 + + 4 + 7 + 1 = 31 + , should be x x divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2067", "q": "If a number is divisible by both 11 and 13, then it must be : Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["divisible by (11 × 13)", "divisible by 42", "divisible by (11 + 13)", "divisible by (13 - 11)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If a number is divisible by both 11 and 13, then it must be divisible by (11 × 13)."},
+{"id": "P2068", "q": "If a⁹-digit number 937X728Y6 is divisible by 72, then one of the possible values of X + Y is : Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["12", "8", "9", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "72 = 9 × 8 For 937X728Y6 to be divisible by 8, its last 3 digits i.e.8Y6 should be divisible by 8. For this y can be 1 or 5. For 937X728Y6 to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e. 9 + 3 + 7 + X + 7 + 2 + 8 + Y + 6 = 42 + Y + X should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2069", "q": "A number when divided by a divisor leaves a remainder of 24. When twice the original number is divided by the same divisor, the remainder is 13. What is the value of the divisor ? Matriculation Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["35", "37", "25", "30"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the original number be x and divisor be d dq + 24 = x Multiplying both side by 2, 2dq + 48= 2x (2dq + 35)+ 13 = 2x So, d is either 35 or factor of 35 but greater than 24 d = 35 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2070", "q": "If (5)⁵5 is divisible by 4, then the remainder is : Matriculation Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["5", "1", "3", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Rem( ) = = 1⁵ 55⁴ 1⁵5⁴"},
+{"id": "P2071", "q": "How many numbers less than 1,000 are multiples of both 7 and 11 ? Matriculation Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["13", "11", "12", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "7 × 11 = 77 Numbers less than 1000 which are multiples of 77 = 77, 154, …………….924 since , the given series are in AP . so, we have ; 77 + (n - 1)77 = 924 ⇒ (n - 1)77 = 847 n - 1 = 11 ⇒ n = 12"},
+{"id": "P2072", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 4. (i)⁶7920598 (ii)⁶18703592 (iii)⁶18703594 (iv)⁶7920590 Matriculation Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["(i)", "(iii)", "(iv)", "(ii)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 4 : For any no. to be divisible by 4, its last 2 digits should be divisible by 4. Now, after going through all the options, we get only 618703592 is divisible by 4."},
+{"id": "P2073", "q": "In a division sum, the divisor is 13 times the quotient and 6 times the remainder. If the remainder is 39, then the dividend is: Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["4,800", "4,576", "4,251", "4,240"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Divisor = n , quotient = q, remainder = r (Dividend)N = n.q + r Given: n = 13.q , n = 6.r , r = 39 n = 39⁶ = 234 q = 18 ⇒ × ⇒ N = n q + r N = 234¹8 + 39 ⇒ × ⇒ × N = 4212 + 39 = 4251 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2074", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 36 ? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["1542", "96272", "55512", "8840 Search on TG: @apna_pdf"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisible by 36 the Search on TG: @apna_pdf number must be divisible by both 9 and 4. To check divisibility by 9 sum of all the numbers divisible by 9. and for divisibility by 4 the last two digits should be divisible by 4. By checking option one by one option (c) satisfies. i.e."},
+{"id": "P2075", "q": "The number 1254216 is divisible by which of the following numbers? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["8", "11", "5", "16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "By checking option one by one option (a) satisfies. Option (a)⁸ For divisibility by 8, last three digits should be divided by 8. And here 216 is divisible by 8."},
+{"id": "P2076", "q": "Find the sum of 3 + 3² + 3³ + .... +3⁸ . Higher Secondary 24/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["9840", "6561", "6560", "3280"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "3 + 3² + 3³ + .... +3⁸ 3 (1 + 3 + 3² + 3³ + .... +3⁷ ) ⇒ 3 ( 1 +3 + 9 + 27 + 81 + 243 + 729 + ⇒ 2187)³ (3280) = 9840 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2077", "q": "The number 2918245 is divisible by which of the following numbers? Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["3", "9", "11", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(a) For divisibility by 3² + 9 + 1 + 8 +2 + 4 + 5 = 31 (not divisible by 3) (b) Since the number is not divisible by 3, the number is not divisible by 9. (c) For divisibility by 11 Difference between the sum of the digits placed at odd places and even places is either divisible by 11 or 0."},
+{"id": "P2078", "q": "6²5 + 6²6 + 6²7 + 6²8 is divisible by : Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["254", "259", "256", "255"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "6²5 + 6²6 + 6²7 + 6²8 = 6²5 ( 1 + 6 + 6² + 6³ ) = 6²5 ( 1 +6 + 36 + 216) = 6²5 (259) Hence the given expression is divisible by 259."},
+{"id": "P2079", "q": "If a car covers 90 km using 4 litres of petrol, how much distance (in km) will it cover using 32 litres of petrol? Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["720", "710", "680", "650"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= 90⁴ Distance 32 Distance = 90⁸ = 720 km ⇒ ×"},
+{"id": "P2080", "q": "In a division sum, the divisor is 10 times the quotient and 5 times the remainder. If the remainder is 12, then what is the dividend? Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["368", "372", "386", "352 Q.164 .Which of the following numbers will completely divide 4¹2 + 4¹3 + 4¹4 + 4¹5 Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "17", "11", "3", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know Dividend (N) = divisor quotient + × remainder Given Divisor (n) = 10 × quotient (q) And Divisor (n) = 5 × remainder (R) R = 12 n = 60 and q = 6 ⇒ Now, N = 60⁶ + 12 = 372 ×"},
+{"id": "P2081", "q": "Without actual division, find the remainder when 379843 is divided by 3. Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["4", "1", "3", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisibility by 3, The sum of digits of the number should be divisible by 3. Here 3 + 7 + 9 + 8 + 4 + 3 = 34 And 34³ remainder is 1."},
+{"id": "P2082", "q": "If the six-digit number 15x1y2 is divisible by 44, then the minimum value of (x + y) is equal to: Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["5", "6", "8", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisibility by 4, the last two digits should be divisible by 4. Hence the possible value of y can be 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 For divisibility by 11, The difference between the sum of the digits at odd places and even places should be zero or divisible by 11."},
+{"id": "P2083", "q": "If a⁹-digit number 389x6378y is divisible by 72, then the value of 6x + 7y is: Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["64", "32", "16", "28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "72 = 9 × 8 For 389x6378y to be divisible by 8, its last 3 digit no i.e.78y should be divisible by 8. For this , y = 4 Now, For 389x6378⁴ to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e. 3 + 8 + 9 + x + 6 + 3 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 48 + x, should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2084", "q": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 9? Graduate Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["553986", "350846", "941201", "132490"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 9 : For any no to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 9. From the given options, we have ; (a)553986→5 + 5 + 3 + 9 + 8 + 6 = 36, which is divisible by 9. (b)350846→3 + 5 + 0 + 8 + 4 + 6 = 26, which is not divisible by 9. (c)941201→9 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 0 + 1 =17, which is not divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2085", "q": "The five-digit number 725yz is divisible by 15. What is the maximum possible value of the product of y and z ? Graduate Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["45", "30", "35", "40"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "15 = 5 × 3 For 725yz to be divisible by 5, unit digit i.e.z should be 0 or 5. For 725yz to be divisible by 3, the sum of digits i.e.7 + 2 + 5 + y + z = 14 + y + z should be divisible by 3. But for the maximum value of yz, we have to put z = 5 ."},
+{"id": "P2086", "q": "If the 6 digit number 7002 * 4 is completely divisible by 8, then the smallest integer in place of * will be: Graduate Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["0", "2", "4", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 8 ; For any number to be divisible by 8, its last 3 digits should be divisible by 8. For 7002⁴, 2⁴ should be divisible by 8 x x For this, must be 2."},
+{"id": "P2087", "q": "If 72 * 72 is divisible by 9, the missing * digit will be: Graduate Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["5 or 8", "0 or 9", "2 or 4", "3 or 6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 9, For any number to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 9. For 72⁷2 , 7 + 2 + + 7 + 2 = 18 + , x x x should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2088", "q": "The number 7918378 is divisible by: Graduate Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["13", "9", "11", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "After checking all the options one by one , only option(a) satisfied. So, 7918378 is divisible by 13."},
+{"id": "P2089", "q": "What least number must be subtracted from 2001 to get a number exactly divisible by 17 ? Graduate Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["12", "13", "11", "14"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Dividing 2001 by 17, we get 12 as remainder. So, On subtracting 12 from 2001 , we get 1989 which is exactly divisible by 17."},
+{"id": "P2090", "q": "If * is a digit such that 7235 * is divisible by 11, then the value of * is: Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["9", "6", "5", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 11 : For any no to be divisible by 11, the difference of the sum of its alternate digits should be divisible by 11. For 7235x to be divisible by 11, (7 + 3 + x) - (2 + 5) = 3 + x, should be divisible by 11."},
+{"id": "P2091", "q": "The average of 25 integers is zero. What is the maximum possible number of positive integers? Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["12", "20", "13", "24"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Average of 1 negative number = average of 24 positive numbers {Because here maximum (+ive) integers are asked whereas the average of 25 numbers is zero.} So the maximum positive integers will be 24"},
+{"id": "P2092", "q": "Find the largest number which should replace P in the 7- digit number 87893P4 to make the number divisible by 4. Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["8", "9", "2", "0"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 4, For any no to be divisible by 4, its last 2 digit should be divisible by 4 Then, For 87893P4, P4 should be divisible by 4 For this , P can be 2, 4, 6 or 8 But for the maximum value of P , it must be 8."},
+{"id": "P2093", "q": "Find the smallest non-zero value of k so that 7-digit number 48397k5 is divisible by 9 Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["2", "5", "4", "9 SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For 48397k5 to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e.4 + 8 + 3 + 9 + 7 + k + 5 = 36 + k, should be divisible by 9 For non zero value of k ⇒ k = 9"},
+{"id": "P2094", "q": "Which of the following is largest among (125) , (11) , (12) , (5) ? 1⁶ 1³ 1⁶ 1⁴ Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["(12)", "(11)", "(125)", "(5)¹⁶ 1³ 1⁶ 1⁴"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(125) , (11) , (12) , (5)¹⁶ 1³ 1⁶ 1⁴ (multiplying by 12 in the power) , , , ( 125 )² ( 11 )⁴ ( 12 )² ( 5 )³ , , , → ( 125 )² ( 121 )² ( 144 ) ( 125 ) Now we can see (125) is the largest 1⁶ value."},
+{"id": "P2095", "q": "The sum of three fractions A, B Search on TG: @apna_pdf and C, A > B > C , is . When C is 121⁶0 divided by B, the resulting fraction is , 9¹0 which exceeds A by . What is the 3²0 difference between B and C ?", "o": ["1", "15", "1", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = C B⁹ 10 ⇒ C⁹ 10 B According to the question, = + 9¹0 A³ 20 = – = = A⁹ 10³ 20¹5²0³ 4 Also, = A + B + C¹21⁶0 Putting the values of and as C A obtained in above equation, we get = 3⁴ + B + 9 B¹0¹21⁶0 = 15 + 20 B + 18 B²0¹21⁶0 = 45 + 60 B + 54 B¹21 = ⇒ = = 114 B⁷6 B⁷6¹14² 3 So, = = = C⁹ 10 B⁹ 10 × 2³ 3⁵ So, difference between B and C = – = 2³ 3⁵ 1¹"},
+{"id": "P2096", "q": "Find the value of x in given equation: = 7⁵ + x + 5 − x⁵ + x − 5 − x", "o": ["12", "5", "7", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given :- = 7⁵ + x + 5 − x⁵ + x − 5 − x By using componendo and Dividendo = 5 + x + 5 − x⁵ + x − 5 − x⁷ 1⁵ + x + 5 − x + 5 + x − 5 − x⁵ + x + 5 − x − 5 + x + 5 − x = = = 7 + 1⁷ − 1 ⇒ 5 + x⁵ − x⁸ 6⁴ 3 Square on both sides = 5 + x⁵ − x¹6⁹ 45 + 9x = 80 - 16x²5x = 35 x = = ⇒ 35²5⁷ 5"},
+{"id": "P2097", "q": "The difference between the two numbers is 1370. On dividing the larger by the smaller, the quotient is 7, and the remainder is 14. Find the smaller number. Graduate Level 28/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["240", "226", "285", "295"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A/Q, Let smaller number = and larger = (7 + x x¹4) (7 + 14) - = 1370 x x⁶ = 1356 = 226 x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2098", "q": "Converting the decimal number 187 to the binary number system we get: Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["10111011", "10111010", "11011101", "11011110"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(187)¹0 = (10111011)²"},
+{"id": "P2099", "q": "Which set of numbers includes all the other sets ? Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Integers", "Rational numbers", "Real numbers", "Natural numbers"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Real numbers"},
+{"id": "P2100", "q": "How many non-square natural numbers lie between 30² and 31² ? Matriculation Level 29/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["59", "60", "61", "62"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For any two consecutive natural numbers n and (n+1), there are 2n non-square numbers between their squares. n = 30 Next number= (n+1) =31 Total non-square numbers between 30² and = 2 × 30 = 60³1²"},
+{"id": "P2101", "q": "What will be the number of zeros at the end of the square of the following numbers ? (i)⁹0 (ii)⁶00 Choose the correct option: Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["1 zero in (i), 3 zeros in (ii)", "2 zeros in (i), 4 zeros in (ii)", "2 zeros in (i), 2 zeros in (ii)", "1 zero in both (i) and (ii)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(i)⁹0 = 90 × 90 = 8100 (ii)⁶00 = 600 × 600 = 360000 (i) has 2 zeros and (ii) has 4 zeros."},
+{"id": "P2102", "q": "If x = is a rational number and y = 5³ , an irrational number, then x + y is: 5 Matriculation Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["Rational", "Irrational", "Integer", "Whole Number"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "x + y = + = 5³ 5⁵ + 3⁵ 3 Their sum will also be an irrational number"},
+{"id": "P2103", "q": "If 3c2933k is divisible by both 5 and 11, where c and k are single digit natural numbers, then c + k = ______. TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["6", "8", "5", "7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility of 11: The difference of the sum of digits at odd position and sum of digits at even position in a number is 0 or divisible by 11. Now, (3 + 2 + 3 + k) - (c + 9 + 3) = 0 (8 + k) = (c + 12) ……(i) ⇒ Divisibility of 5 : If the last digit of the number should be 0 or 5 then that number will be divisible by 5."},
+{"id": "P2104", "q": "A⁴-digit number '34PQ' divisible by 3,5 and 7. Find the value of P + Q .", "o": ["11", "12", "10", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If the number is divisible by 5 means the last digit is either 0 or 5. Let Q = 0 Now we have to find the value of P. For divisibility by 3, the sum of the digits should be divisible by 3. P = 2, 5, 8 ⇒ But the numbers 3420, 3450 and 3480 are not divisible by 7. Now, take the value of Q = 5."},
+{"id": "P2105", "q": "Given that 2²0 + 1 is completely divisible by a whole number. Which of the following is completely divisible by the same number ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["2¹5 + 1", "5² 30 ×", "2⁹0 + 1", "2⁶0 + 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The whole number which divides 2²0 + 1 also divides the multiple of 2²0 + 1 ⇒ 2⁶0 + 1 = (2²0 + 1)(2⁴0 + 1 - 2²0 ) Using formula : a³ + b³ = (a + b)( a² + b² - ab)²⁶0 + 1 is the multiple of 2²0 +1 so,2⁶0 + 1 is completely divisible by that whole number."},
+{"id": "P2106", "q": "Let x = + and y = + . 3⁵ 8³ Which is greater ?", "o": ["x = y", "x > y", "x < y", "Cannot be determined"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given : - x = + = 1.732 + 2.236 = 3.968³ 5 y = + = 2.828 + 1.732 = 4.56⁸ 3 so , x < y"},
+{"id": "P2107", "q": "If ( ) - ( ) + 1⁴ − 15¹ 15 − 14 ( ) - ( ) + ( )¹¹4 − 13¹ 13 − 12¹ 12 − 11 - ( ) + ( ) = x¹ 11 − 10¹ 10 − 3 Then find the value of ( x + 1) = ?", "o": ["8", "7", "2", "0"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given:- ( ) - ( ) + ( )¹⁴ − 15¹ 15 − 14¹ 14 − 13 - ( ) + ( ) - 1¹3 − 12¹ 12 − 11 ( ) + ( )¹¹1 − 10¹ 10 − 3 Using Rationalization Method x = ( × ) - ( × 1⁴ − 15⁴ + 15⁴ + 15¹ 15 − 14 ) + ( × )¹5 + 14¹5 + 14¹ 14 − 13¹4 + 13¹4 + 13 - ( × ) + 1¹3 − 12¹3 + 12¹3 + 12 ( × ) - ( 1¹2 − 11¹2 + 11¹2 + 11¹ 11 − 10 × ) + ( × )¹1 + 10¹1 + 10¹ 10 − 3¹0 + 3¹0 + 3⁴"},
+{"id": "P2108", "q": "Solve system: y = 4x + 2 and y = − 2x + 8", "o": ["(1, 6)", "(2, 5)", "(3, 7)", "(0, 1)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "y = 4x + 2 ……… (i) y = − 2x + 8 …….. (ii) From eq . (i) and (ii), 4 x + 2 = − 2x + 8 ⇒ 6 = 6 = 1 ⇒ x ⇒ x Put the value in eq ."},
+{"id": "P2109", "q": "Which of the following is correct? (i) + > + 11³ 12² (ii) + < + 11³ 12² (iii) + = + 11³ 12²", "o": ["(i)", "(ii)", "(iii)", "(i), (ii) and (iii)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "( + )²¹1³ = 11 + 3 + 2 = 14 + 2¹1 × 3³3 ( + )² = 12 + 2 + 2¹2² 12 × 2 = 14 + 2²4 TG: @ikunal_x Hence, + > + 11³ 12²"},
+{"id": "P2110", "q": "Find the value of x in the given equation: = 5⁸ + x + 8 − x⁸ + x − 8 − x", "o": ["46", "13", "36", "13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given :- = 5⁸ + x + 8 − x⁸ + x − 8 − x Let ,a = and b = 8 + x⁸ − x ⇒ = 5 a + b a − b ⇒ a + b = 5a - 5b ⇒ - 4a = - 6b ⇒ = a b³ 2 Now, = 8 + x⁸ − x³ 2 Square on both sides = ⇒ 32 + 4x = 72 - 9x⁸ + x⁸ − x⁹ 4 -40 = -13x ⇒ x = 40¹3"},
