+{"id": "P2152", "q": "Given below are two statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Read and mark the correct options: Assertion (A): The sum of any two even natural numbers is always even. Reason (R): If a number can be written as 2k, then it is even, and the sum of two even numbers can be written as 2(k₁ + k₂), which is even. Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A", "Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A", "A is true, but R is false", "A is false, but R is true"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": ""},
+{"id": "P2153", "q": "Which of the following relationship between the sets of integers(z), rational numbers(x), and real numbers(y) holds good? Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["x ⊆ z ⊆ y", "y ⊆ x ⊆ z", "z ⊆ y ⊆ x", "z ⊆ x ⊆ y"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "All integers (z) are rational numbers (x), and all rational numbers are real numbers (y). Hence, z ⊆ x ⊆ y."},
+{"id": "P2154", "q": "If a pipe of length m is cut 392 into 14 equal parts, what is the length of each part, and is it rational or irrational? Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Each part is m irrational 4", "Each part is m irrational 2", "Each part is 7 m rational", "Each part is m irrational 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Length of each part = = 392¹4¹4² 14 = m² is an irrational number 2"},
+{"id": "P2155", "q": "If p is a natural number, then p(p + 1)(p + 2)(p + 3) + 1 is always: Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["A perfect cube", "Not a perfect square", "A perfect square", "An odd number"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Natural number (p) = 1, 2, 3, 4, …… p(p + 1)(p + 2)(p + 3) + 1 ⇒ On putting p = 1, 1 × 2 × 3 × 4 + 1 = 25 ⇒ 25 is a perfect square number On putting p = 2² × 3 × 4 × 5 + 1 = 121 ⇒ 121 is also a perfect square, It is clear that the given expression is a perfect square."},
+{"id": "P2156", "q": "The binary number 100010 in the decimal number system is equal to: Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["33", "34", "35", "36"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, = 1 × + 0 × + 0 × + 0 × ( 100010 )²² 5² 4² 3 + 1 × + 0 × 2² 2¹ 2⁰ = 32 + 2 = 34"},
+{"id": "P2157", "q": "Which of the following is not a like surd? Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["-2", "-3", "5", "15⁷ 37²5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Like surds must have the same irrational surd part (same radicand after simplification). -2 , -3 , and 5 all have irrational 15⁷ 37 square roots in their simplest form."},
+{"id": "P2158", "q": "The number of natural numbers between and is: 80⁸00 Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["10", "35", "25", "20"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = 4⁸0¹6 × 5 ( )⁵ = 4².236 = 8.944 × 0 = = 10 = 10² 80¹00 × 8 ( )⁸ × 2 = 10².828 = 28.28 × So the natural numbers are: 9,10,11,......27,28 Number of natural numbers = 28 - 9 + 1 = 20."},
+{"id": "P2159", "q": "The number of digits in the square root of a perfect square containing 4n digits is: Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["2n", "2n - 1", "2n + 1", "4n"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If a perfect square contains 4n digits, then: 4 = 2 (2 ) n × n [ Note : A perfect square with 2k digits has a square root with k digits.] Here, 2k = 4n k = 2n ⇒ TG: @ikunal_x So the number of digits in the square root is: 2n"},
+{"id": "P2160", "q": "When the binary value 10110101 is added to 11001010, the resulting sum in decimal form is: Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["330", "331", "332", "383"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Convert 10110101 to decimal: (1 × 2⁷) + (0 × 2⁶) + (1 × 2⁵) + (1 × 2⁴) + (0 × 2³) + (1 × 2²) + (0 × 2¹) + (1 × 2⁰) = 128 + 0 + 32 + 16 + 0 + 4 + 0 + 1 = 181 Convert 11001010 to decimal: (1 × 2⁷) + (1 × 2⁶) + (0 × 2⁵) + (0 × 2⁴) + (1 × 2³) + (0 × 2²) + (1 × 2¹) + (0 × 2⁰) = 128 + 64 + 0 + 0 + 8 + 0 + 2 + 0 = 202 Add the decimal numbers: 181 + 202 = 383 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2161", "q": "Consider the number . (− 49 ) Which of the following statements is true about the above number ? Higher Secondary 31/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["It represents a real number and is also an integer.", "It does not belong to the set of real numbers but belongs to the set of complex numbers.", "It is a real number though it is not an integer.", "It is neither a real number nor a complex number."], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question = . = 7 − 49⁴9 − 1 i It is not a real number because the square root of a negative number is imaginary, but it is a complex number."},
