+{"id": "P2167", "q": "The unit digit of is: 11²03 Graduate Level 25/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["5", "2", "0", "1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: 11²03 = 3 (Remainder) ⇒ 203⁴ then, = 1331¹1³ So, the unit digit = 1"},
+{"id": "P2168", "q": "What type of number is obtained when two irrational numbers are added ? Graduate Level 26/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["Always Rational", "Always Irrational", "Sometimes Rational, Sometimes Irrational", "Always Integer"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When two irrational numbers are added Case 1: + ) = 0 (rational)² (− 2 Case 2 : + = (irrational)²³ ∴ Number can be sometimes rational or sometimes irrational."},
+{"id": "P2169", "q": "What is the sum of all three-digit numbers divisible by 8 ? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["61376", "62707", "62006", "62407"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Smallest number divisible by 8 = 104 and largest 3 digit number divisible by 8 = 992 Number of terms = + 1 = 112⁹92 − 104⁸ Sum of numbers = S n = ( + ) n² a l S n = (104 + 992)¹12² = 56 × 1096 = 61376"},
+{"id": "P2170", "q": "Which is the most significant 4-digit number exactly divisible by 77 ? Graduate Level 02/08/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["9999", "9977", "9960", "9933 eduquity-based pattern (ebp) Questions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Largest four digit number = 9999 Now , 9999 = 129 × 77 + 66 If we subtract 66 then , resultant value is divisible by 77 ∴ 4-digit number exactly divisible by 77 = 129 × 77 = 9933"},
+{"id": "P2171", "q": "The number of heads on the farm, as determined by the farmer, was 60. When he counted, he discovered there were 150 legs. If all that was present TG: @ikunal_x were pigeons or horses, and every horse on the property had four legs while every pigeon had two, how many horses were there on the property ?", "o": ["14", "12", "15", "10"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "To solve this type of question, one is taken. Now, The total number of legs of all the horses on the farm = 4 × 60 = 240 Given:- number of pigeon legs = 2 and number of horse legs = 4 According to question, (4 - 2) = 2 unit = 240 - 150¹ unit = = 45⁹0² Hence, number of horses in the farm = 60 - 45 = 15"},
+{"id": "P2172", "q": "The length of a violin string varies inversely with respect to the frequency of its vibrations. The frequency of a¹4-inch-long violin string is 450 cycles per second. Find the frequency of a¹2-inch violin string.", "o": ["515 cycles per second", "525 cycles per second", "520 cycles per second", "510 cycles per second"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question , Length ∝ L = 1 Frequency ⇒ K F¹4 = K = 6300 ⇒ K⁴50 ⇒ Now , 12 = ⇒ 6300 F F = = 525 cycles per second ⇒ 6300¹2"},
+{"id": "P2173", "q": "If the 9-digit number 5x79856y6 is divisible by 36, then what is the negative value of for the ( 2 x + y ) largest possible value of y, given x and y are natural numbers?", "o": ["-7", "-2", "-4", "-5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Number = 5⁷9856⁶ x y For divisibility of 36 a number must be divisible by 9 and 4. For divisibility of 4 :- last 2 digit must be divisible by 4. Hence , possible value of = 1, 3,5,7, 9 y We need largest possible value of = 9 y For divisibility of 9 :- sum of number must be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2174", "q": "Each of Ravi and Kavita had some marbles. Kavita had 12 more marbles than Ravi had. If each of them had one TG: @ikunal_x more marble, then three times the number of marbles Kavita would then have had would have been equal to four times the number of marbles Ravi would then have had. How many marbles did Kavita actually have ?", "o": ["43", "47", "51", "48"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let number of marbles Ravi had = x Number of Marbles Kavita had = + 12 x According to question , 3 ( + 13 ) = 4 ( + 1 ) ⇒ x x³ + 39 = 4 + 4 = 35 ⇒ x x ⇒ x ∴ Number of Marbles Kavita had ( + 12 ) x = 35 + 12 = 47"},
+{"id": "P2175", "q": "Identify a single-digit number other than 1, which may exactly divide the number 17³ + 18³ − 16³ − 15³", "o": ["3", "5", "7", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "17³ + 18³ − 16³ − 15³ 4913 + 5832 − 4096 − 3375 = 3274 Clearly, the number is divisible by 2."},
+{"id": "P2176", "q": "The age of a tree depends on the number of rings in the trunk. The value of TG: @ikunal_x a such tree is proportional to its age. If a tree with 40 rings and 50 years of age has a value of ₹50,000, then a tree with 30 rings is ________ years of age and its value is ₹_______.", "o": ["37.5, 57500", "37.5, 37500", "57.5, 37500", "57.5, 57500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "age of a tree depends on the number of rings in the trunk 40 rings = 50years ⇒1 rings = 1.25 years Then, 30 rings = 30 × 1.25 = 37.5 years The value of tree is proportional to age of tree 50 years = Rs. 50000 ⇒ 1 years = Rs. 1000 Then, 37.5 years = 37.5 × 1000 = Rs. 37500 Hence, tree with 30 rings is 37.5 years of age and its value is Rs."},
+{"id": "P2177", "q": "If the number 3727⁴ is x completely divisible by 8, then the smallest integer in place of will be x", "o": ["6", "8", "2", "0"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisibility by 8, the last three digits should be divisible by 8. Here 7⁴ will be divisible by 8. x The value of will be 0, 4, 8."},
+{"id": "P2178", "q": "Find the least value digit which is assigned to so that the number x is divisible by 9. 1972 x⁴71", "o": ["3", "5", "4", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For 1972⁴71 to be divisible x by 9, the sum of its digits i.e.1 + 9 + 7 + 2 + + 4 + 7 + 1 = 31 + , should be x x divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2179", "q": "If a⁹-digit number 937X728Y6 is divisible by 72, then one of the possible values of X + Y is :", "o": ["12", "8", "9", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "72 = 9 × 8 For 937X728Y6 to be divisible by 8, its last 3 digits i.e.8Y6 should be divisible by 8. For this y can be 1 or 5. For 937X728Y6 to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e. 9 + 3 + 7 + X + 7 + 2 + 8 + Y + 6 = 42 + Y + X should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2180", "q": "Without actual division, find the remainder when 379843 is divided by 3.", "o": ["4", "1", "3", "2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "शेषफल", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For divisibility by 3, The sum of digits of the number should be divisible by 3. Here 3 + 7 + 9 + 8 + 4 + 3 = 34 And 34³ remainder is 1."},
+{"id": "P2181", "q": "If a⁹-digit number 389x6378y is divisible by 72, then the value of 6x + 7y is:", "o": ["64", "32", "16", "28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "72 = 9 × 8 For 389x6378y to be divisible by 8, its last 3 digit no i.e.78y should be divisible by 8. For this , y = 4 Now, For 389x6378⁴ to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits i.e. 3 + 8 + 9 + x + 6 + 3 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 48 + x, should be divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2182", "q": "Which of the following numbers is TG: @ikunal_x divisible by 9?", "o": ["553986", "350846", "941201", "132490"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Divisibility rule of 9 : For any no to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits should be divisible by 9. From the given options, we have ; (a)⁵53986→5 + 5 + 3 + 9 + 8 + 6 = 36, which is divisible by 9. (b)³50846→3 + 5 + 0 + 8 + 4 + 6 = 26, which is not divisible by 9. (c)⁹41201→9 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 0 + 1 =17, which is not divisible by 9."},
+{"id": "P2183", "q": "The five-digit number 725yz is divisible by 15. What is the maximum possible value of the product of y and z", "o": ["45", "30", "35", "40"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "संख्या पद्धति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "15 = 5 × 3 For 725yz to be divisible by 5, unit digit i.e.z should be 0 or 5. For 725yz to be divisible by 3, the sum of digits i.e.7 + 2 + 5 + y + z = 14 + y + z should be divisible by 3. But for the maximum value of yz, we have to put z = 5 ."},
+{"id": "P2184", "q": "Swati starts a business with ₹ 4,200 and after 5 months, Bani joins Swati as her partner. After a year, the pro fit is divided among Swati and Bani in the ratio 2 : 5. What is Bani's contribution?", "o": ["₹18,000", "₹17,050", "₹19,000", "₹16,500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Bani’s contribution is x⁴200¹2 : 7 = 2 : 5 × x × = = ₹18000 x⁴200 × 12 × 5⁷ × 2"},
+{"id": "P2185", "q": "Three partners P , Q and R invest ₹ 1,000, 1,200 and 1,500, respectively, in ₹ ₹ a business. What should be the share of Q if the total pro fit is 666? ₹", "o": ["216", "275", "252", "284 ₹ ₹ ₹ ₹"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Investment time is the same , So ratio of investment is equal to the ratio of pro fit . Their investment ratio :- P : Q : R = 10 : 12 : 15 Share of Q = = 18 × 12 = ₹216⁶66 × 12³7"},
+{"id": "P2186", "q": "Kapil initiated a business with an investment of ₹30,00,000 in April 2022. After six months, his friend Kunal joined him with an investment of ₹25,00,000. In February 2023, Kapil's Ex-Class fellow Saloni also invested an amount equal to the total investment made by the earlier two partners. In what ratio the pro fit earned after 3 years from the date on which Kapil initiated the business, will be distributed ?", "o": ["332 : 200 : 50", "108 : 75 : 143", "432 : 300 : 55", "432 : 400 : 55"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio = kapil : kunal : saloni Amount = 30 : 25 : 55 Time = 36 : 30 : 26 --------------------------------------------- Pro fit = 108 : 75 : 143"},
+{"id": "P2187", "q": "P invested Rs. 4000 for one year. Q joined him with an investment of Rs. 6000 after a few months. If at the end of one year the ratio of pro fits of P and Q is 4 : 3, then Q joined after how many months?", "o": ["4 months", "3 months", "8 months", "6 months"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio P : Q → Investment 4 : 6 Time 1 : x ------------------------------------------- Pro fit 4 : 3 → Let Q joined for x year As we know pro fit = investment × time Then, 4 × 1 : 6 × x = 4 : 3 = ⇒ 4⁶ x⁴ 3 x = = ⇒ 3⁶ 1² Here, Q joined for 6 months then, Q joined after (12 - 6) = 6 month"},
+{"id": "P2188", "q": "A, B and C started a business with initial investments of ₹ 20000, ₹25000 and ₹10000, respectively. After 5 months from start, A invested ₹ 4000 more. After 6 months from start, C invested ₹ 8000 more. After 4 months from start, B withdrew ₹ 8000. At the end of the year, they will receive a pro fit of ₹ ‘x’. In what ratio will they share the pro fits?", "o": ["71 : 57 : 42", "71 : 59 : 42", "59 : 68 : 42", "67 : 59 : 42"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total amount invested by A = 20000 × 5 + (20000 + 4000) × 7 = 100000 + 168000 = 268000 Total amount invested by B = 25000 × 4 + (25000 - 8000) × 8 = 100000 + 136000 = 236000 Total amount invested by C = 10000 × 6 + (10000 + 8000) × 6 = 60000 + 108000 = 168000 So, the ratio of their pro fit = 268 : 236 : 168 = 67 : 59 : 42"},
+{"id": "P2189", "q": "A, B and C started a business with their capitals in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. A increased his capital by 50% after 4 months, B increased his capital by 33¹ 3 % after 6 months and C withdrew 50% of 345 his capital after 8 months, from the start of the business. If the total pro fit at the end of a year was Rs. 86,800, then the difference between the shares of A and C in the pro fit was :", "o": ["Rs.12,600", "Rs.7,000", "Rs.9,800", "Rs.8,400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "50% = , 33 % = 1² 1³ 1³ Ratio A : B : C → Initial 2 × 4 : 3 × 6 : 5 × 8 → Final 3 × 8 : 4 × 6 : 2.5 × 4 → ------------------------------- Pro fit 32 : 42 : 50 → Total Pro fit (32 + 42 + 50) = 124 units 124 units = 86800 Rs. 1 unit = 700 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2190", "q": "A, B and C started a business by investing Rs 1,37,500 and Rs 1,62,500 and Rs 1,87,500 respectively. A is a working partner and gets 20% of the pro fit as working allowance and remaining is distributed in the proportion of their investment. If the total pro fit is Rs 2,19,375. What is the share of C?", "o": ["Rs 88,600", "Rs 64,500", "Rs 67,500", "Rs 62,700 Practice Questions SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B : C → Investment 137500 : 162500 : 187500 → 11 : 13 : 15 Therefore, C’s share :- 219375 = Rs. × 4⁵ × 15³9⁶7500"},
+{"id": "P2191", "q": "A and B enter into a partnership with ₹25,000 and ₹50,000, respectively, in a company for a year. After 7 months, C gets into a partnership with them with ₹30,000 and A withdraws his contribution after 9 months. What would be C's share in the pro fit, assuming a total pro fit of ₹3,900 at the end of the year?", "o": ["₹600", "₹800", "₹1,200", "₹1,000 SSC MTS 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of their money contribution A : B : C = 5 : 10 : 6 Ratio of their time A : B : C = 9 : 12 : 5 ∴ Ratio of their pro fit = 45 : 120 : 30 = 3 : 8 : 2 Hence, C’s share in pro fit = × 2 = 600³900¹3"},
+{"id": "P2192", "q": "Arvind, Bilal. Carmen invest ₹49,000 towards a business. Arvind invests ₹5,000 more than Bilal and Bilal invests ₹4,000 more than Carmen Out of a total pro fit of ₹98,000, how much does Bilal receive?", "o": ["₹34,400", "₹33,200", "₹30,500", "₹32,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let investment of Bilal be x According to the question, + ( + 5000) + ( 4000) = 49000 x x x − = 48000 , = 16000³ x x Then, investment of Bilal : Arvind : Carmen = 16000 : 21000 : 12000 = 16 : 21 : 12 Share of pro fit of Bilal = = ₹32,000⁹8000¹6 + 21 + 12 × 16"},
+{"id": "P2193", "q": "Mayur and Aham enter into a partnership by making investments in the ratio 2: 3. 10% of the total pro fit goes to charity. If Aham's share is ₹4,860, then what is the total pro fit (in ₹) earned?", "o": ["7,200", "9,000", "8,500", "11,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the total pro fit is ₹ x According to the question, = ₹4860 x × 9¹0 × 3⁵ = ₹9,000 ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2194", "q": "A , B and C started a business. A's capital is 7 times the capital of C and B's capital is 2 times the capital of A. If the pro fit is ₹7,920, then find the share of C (in ₹ ).", "o": ["350", "360", "365", "355 SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Concept :- pro fit is divided in the ratio of capital Ratio of pro fit of A , B , and C = 7 : 14 : 1 Share of C = 7920 = 360 × 1 ( 7 + 14 + 1 )"},
+{"id": "P2195", "q": "A is a working partner and B is a sleeping partner in a business. A invested ₹30,000 and B invested ₹50,000. A receives 20% of the pro fit for managing the business and the rest is divided in proportion to their capital. What does B get out of the pro fit of ₹10,000?", "o": ["₹5,500", "₹5,000", "₹4,500", "₹4,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A receive 20% of the pro fit for managing the business . Remaining pro fit excluding A’s managing pro fit = 10,000 × 80% = 8,000 B’s pro fit = 8,000 × = 5,000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2196", "q": "Anam and Bikash invest in a business in the ratio 3 : 2. If in a particular month, Anam gets ₹3,840 as pro fit, the total profit is:", "o": ["₹ 5,800", "₹6,300", "₹6,550", "₹6,400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "3 units = 3840 ₹ Total pro fit (5 units) = = 6400 ₹ 3840³ × 5"},
+{"id": "P2197", "q": "A, B and C started a business by investing ₹9,000, ₹18,000 and ₹ 21,000, respectively. If B's share in the pro fit earned by them is ₹759, then the total profit earned by them together is:", "o": ["₹2,808", "₹2,024", "₹2,504", "₹2,208 SSC CGL 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Their investment time is same , so the ratio of pro fit is equal to the ratio of investment. Ratio of investment :- A : B : C = 3 : 6 : 7 B’s share of pro fit (6 units) = ₹759 Total pro fit (16 units) = 759⁶ × 16 = 253 × 8 = ₹2024"},
+{"id": "P2198", "q": "A and B invested money in a business in the ratio of 7 : 5. If 15% of the total pro fit goes for charity, and A's share in the pro fit is Rs.5,950, then what is the total pro fit?", "o": ["Rs.12,500", "Rs.12,000", "Rs.10,500", "Rs.11,750 SSC Selection Post (Phase - XI)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the investment of A and B be 7 and 5 . x x If investment time is equal , then the ratio of pro fit is equal to the ratio of investment . According to the question, 7 = 5950 Rs. x¹2 = 5950 × = 10200 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2199", "q": "A starts a business with ₹45,000 and was joined afterwards by B with ₹30,000. When did B join if the pro fit at the end of the year was divided in the ratio 2 : 1 ? Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["After 6 months", "After 12 months", "After 3 months", "After 9 months SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B → Investment 3 : 2 → Time 12 : → x -------------------------------------- Pro fit 2 : 1 → 348 (time for which B invested ) x = = 9 month 12 × 3² × 2 Required time after which B invested = 12⁹ = 3 months −"},
+{"id": "P2200", "q": "A and B jointly start a business. The investment of A is equal to seven times the investment of B. Find the share of A (in ₹) in the annual pro fit of ₹2,75,000.", "o": ["2,40,625", "2,45,625", "2,42,365", "2,41,225 SSC MTS 2022 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If investment time is equal , then the ratio of pro fit is equal to the ratio of investment . Ratio A : B → Invest 7 : 1 → Pro fit 7 : 1 → Share of A = 275000 × = 240625 ₹ 7⁸"},
+{"id": "P2201", "q": "A and B enter into a partnership such that 5 times of A's investment is equal to 7 times of B's investment. If the total profit is Rs. 12000, then what is the share of A ?", "o": ["Rs.6300", "Rs.7000", "Rs.8000", "Rs.7500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, A × 5 = B × 7 ⇒ = A B⁷ 5 Share of the A = 12000 × = ₹ 7000⁷ 7 + 5"},
+{"id": "P2202", "q": "A and B started a business with Rs.15000 and Rs.30000 respectively. If A and B share pro fit in the ratio of 1: 5 respectively, then what is the ratio of the time period of investment for A and B respectively ?", "o": ["1 : 2", "2 : 5", "2 : 3", "2 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B → Investment 1 : 2 → Time : y → x ----------------------------------------- Pro fit 1 : 5 ⇒ = → 1 x² y¹ 5 Required Ratio of time period = : y = 2 : 5 x"},
+{"id": "P2203", "q": "Three partners P , Q and R invested a total of Rs. 52,000 in a business. At the end of the year, P got Rs. 1430, Q got Rs.1870 and R got Rs. 2420 as the share of pro fit. How much amount did Q invest in the business ?", "o": ["Rs. 17000", "Rs. 20400", "Rs. 15300", "Rs. 18700 SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know :- pro fit = time × investment If investment time is equal , then the ratio of pro fit is equal to the ratio of investment . According to the question, Total pro fit of P , Q and R = Rs."},
+{"id": "P2204", "q": "X, Y and Z invested Rs.4,000, Rs.6,000 and Rs.8,000 respectively in a business. They invested the money for 3,2 and 4 years respectively. If the total pro fit is Rs.56,000, then what is the share of Y in the pro fit?", "o": ["Rs.18,000", "Rs.12,000", "Rs.15,000", "Rs.9,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio X : Y : Z → Amount 2 : 3 : 4 → Time 3 : 2 : 4 → -------------------------------------- 6 : 6 : 16 profit → the share of Y = 56,000 × 6²8 = Rs 12000"},
+{"id": "P2205", "q": "Nikhil and Neha invested capital in the ratio 5 : 4. The time Neha invested her money for was one year more than that invested by Nikhil. The ratio of their 346 profits is in the ratio 6: 5. Find the time Neha invested the money for.", "o": ["26 years", "23 years", "24 years", "25 years SSC CGL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Nikhil : Neha → Investment : 4 → 5 Time : → x x + 1 ------------------------------ Pro fit 6 : 5 → Now , = 25 = 24 + 24⁵ x⁴ ( x + 1 )⁶⁵ ⇒ x x = 24 years ⇒ x So Neha invested for ( + 1) years x = 25 years"},
+{"id": "P2206", "q": "A, B and C did certain investments and the ratio of their time periods is 3 : 2 : 7 respectively. Ratio of the pro fits of A, B and C is 4 : 3 : 14 respectively. What is the ratio of the investments of A, B and C ?", "o": ["1 : 3 : 4", "7 : 9 : 11", "8 : 9 : 12", "2 : 3 : 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let , the investments of A, B and C be x, y, z respectively. Total Investment × Total time = Pro fit Ratio A : B : C → Pro fit : : = 4 : 3 : 14 → 3 x² y⁷ z : : = : : ⇒ x y z⁴ 3³ 2¹4⁷ = 8 : 9 : 12"},
+{"id": "P2207", "q": "Suresh, Dinesh and Ramesh became partners in a business by investing money in the ratio of 3 : 6 : 8. If their investments are increased by 5%, 15% and 20%, respectively, then what will be the ratio of their pro fits for one year ?", "o": ["7 : 46 : 64", "19 : 46 : 64", "21 : 46 : 64", "35 : 46 : 64"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Suresh : Dinesh : Ramesh → Investment 300 : 600 : 800 → Increased investment → 315 : 690 : 960 or 21 : 46 : 64"},
+{"id": "P2208", "q": "A starts a business with ₹75,000 and B joins the business 5 months later with an investment of ₹80,000. After 1 year, they earn a pro fit of ₹4,08,800. Find the share of A and B (in ₹).", "o": ["2,52,000 and 1,56,800", "2,50,000 and 1,58,800", "2,48,000 and 1,60,800", "2,49,500 and 1,59,300 SSC CGL 2021 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pro fit = Investment × Time 75000 x¹2 : 80000⁷ 45 : 28 × ⇒ 73 units = ₹ 4,08,800⁴5 units = ₹ 2,52,000²8 units = ₹ 1,56,800 Therefore Pro fit of A and B will be ₹ 2,52,000 and ₹ 1,56,800 respectively."},
+{"id": "P2209", "q": "A,B and C started a business with the investment of 100000 , 140000 , ₹ ₹ ₹ 200000 respectively. After 3 months, C left the business, 7 months after C left the business, B also left the business. B and C took their investment with them. At the end of the year, C received his share of pro fit as 1155. What is the total ₹ share of pro fits of A and B ?", "o": ["6150", "5005 ₹ ₹", "4995", "5555 ₹ ₹ SSC MTS 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of investment of A : B : C = 100000 : 140000 : 200000 = 5 : 7 : 10 According to the question, A works for 12 months, B works for 3 + 7 = 10 months, C works for 3 months. Pro fit sharing ratio among A : B : C = (5¹2) : (7¹0) : (10³) = 30 : 35 : 15 × × × Let total pro fit be y."},
+{"id": "P2210", "q": "The pro fit earned by a company is to be divided among three friends who invested their money in the company, in the proportion of 6 : 9 : 11. If the share of the person who invested the most is ₹2,310, then what is the sum of the money (in ₹) received by the other two friends?", "o": ["1,890", "3,150", "5,460", "1,260 SSC CGL 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of investment = 6 : 9 : 11. Let the shares of pro fit be 6x, 9x and 11x. According to the question, 11x = 2310 ⇒ x = 210."},
+{"id": "P2211", "q": "Keshav, Surjeet and Thomas started a business with investments in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4. The ratio of their period of investments is 5 : 6 : 9. Twenty percent of the pro fit was spent on rent and maintenance of the oﬃce. Remaining pro fit was distributed among themselves. If the difference in the share of pro fit of Keshav and Surjeet is Rs.7264 then how much is the total pro fit (in Rs.)?", "o": ["51060", "58112", "46490", "72640 SSC CPO 2020 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2021", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Investments 2 : 3 : 4 → Time period 5 : 6 : 9 → ------------------------------------------------------------ Pro fit 10 : 18 : 36 → According to question , Pro fit difference of Keshav and Surjeet → (18¹0)units = 8 units = 7264 Rs. − 1 unit = 908 Rs. Total Pro fit (10 + 18 + 36) = 64 units 64 units = 58112 Rs. Let , total pro fit = 100% Pro fit shared = 80% 80% 58112 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2212", "q": "A, B, C subscribe a sum of Rs.75,500 for a business. A subscribes Rs.3,500 more than B, and B subscribes Rs. 4,500 more than C. Out of a total pro fit of Rs.45,300 how much (in Rs.) does A receive ?", "o": ["12,600", "15,000", "17,400", "14,700 SSC CGL 2019 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2020", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total sum of A, B and C = 75,500 Rs. B = C + 4500 A = B + 3500 or C + 8000 According to the question (C + 8000) + (C + 4500) + C = 75,500³C + 12,500 = 75,500 C = 21,000 Rs. , A = 29,000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2213", "q": "X and Y enter into a partnership with capital in ratio 3 : 5. After 5 months X adds 50% of his capital , while Y withdraws 60% of his capital. What is share (in ₹ lakhs ) of X in the annual pro fit of ₹6.84 lakhs?", "o": ["3.72", "4.2", "3.6", "3.12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "X share in investment → 3⁵ + 4.5⁷ = 46.5 × × Y share in investment = 5⁵ + 2⁷ × × = 39 Total investment = 85.5 X share = Lakh 46 . 5⁸5 . 5 × 6 . 84 = 3 ."},
+{"id": "P2214", "q": "Ramesh started a business investing a sum of ₹40,000. Six months later, Kevin joined by investing ₹20,000. If they make a pro fit of ₹10,000 at the end of year, how much is the share of kevin?", "o": ["₹2,000", "₹4,000", "₹3,000", "₹2,500 SSC CPO 2019 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Ramesh : Kevin → Investment 4 : 2 → Time 12 : 6 → --------------------------------------- Pro fit (4 × 12) : (2 × 6) = 4 : 1 → Total Pro fit (5 units) = 10,000 Rs. Kevin share (1 unit)²000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2215", "q": "A, B and C are partners in a firm sharing pro fit in the ratio of 3:4:5. If they set aside 4% of the profits as emergency fund and shared the rest of the pro fit and B gets his share of pro fit as Rs. 1,81,400, the amount of pro fit set aside for emergency fund is:", "o": ["Rs. 27848", "Rs.18140", "Rs.22675", "Rs.24500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let total pro fit = P According to question , P × = 181400⁹6¹00 × 4³ + 4 + 5 P = 566875 Rs. amount of pro fit set aside for emergency fund 566875 = 22675 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2216", "q": "A, B, and C enter into partnership with capitals in the ratio : : . 2³ 3⁵ 5⁶ After 8 months, A increases his share of capital by 25%. If at the end of the year, the total pro fit earned is Rs 5,820, then the share of C in the pro fit is ?", "o": ["2250", "2350", "2050", "2450"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio : : = 20 : 18 : 25 ⇒ 2³ 3⁵ 5⁶ Profit A : B : C → (20 × 8) + (25 × 4) : (18 × 12) : (25 × 12)²60 : 216 : 300 Total Pro fit (260 + 216 + 300) units → 776 units = 5820 Rs. 1 unit = 7.5 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2217", "q": "A started a business with a capital of ₹1,12,000. After 2 months, B joined the business with a capital ₹ 80,000, and after another 2 months, C joined the business with a capital of ₹ 72,000. After 10 months from the start of the business, B withdrew ₹ 8,000 and C also withdrew ₹ 8,000. If B received ₹ 9,800 as his share in the pro fit at the end of a year, then the total pro fit was :", "o": ["₹ 30,800", "₹ 35,800", "₹ 32,400", "₹ 33,600"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Investment ratios of A, B and C → Total investment of A = 112000 × 12 Total investment of B = 80000 × 8 + 72000 × 2 Total investment of C = 72000 × 6 + 64000 × 2 Ratio of their Investment → 1344 : 784 : 560 = 84 : 49 : 35 Total Pro fit = 84 + 49 + 35 = 168 units 349 According to question , Share of B (49 units) = 9800 Rs. 1 unit = 200 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2218", "q": "A, B and C are partners in a business. A, whose capital has been used for 5 months, claims of the 1⁷ profit. B whose capital has been used for 7 months claims of the pro fit. C has 1⁵ invested Rs. 4600 for 9 months. How much capital did A contribute?", "o": ["1800", "1650", "1600", "1850 SSC CGL 2018 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pro fit ratios of A, B and C → A : B : C = : : = 5 : 7 : 23¹ 7¹ 5²3³5 Ratio of time 5 : 7 : 9 → Ratio of investments → : : = 9 : 9 : 23⁵ 5⁷ 7²3⁹ According to question , Investment of C (23 units) = 4600 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2219", "q": "A started a business with a capital of Rs. 54000 and admitted B and C after 4 months and 6 months respectively. At the end of the year, the pro fit was divided in the ratio 1 : 4 : 5. What is the difference between the capitals invested by B and C ?", "o": ["Rs. 1,08,000", "Rs. 1,62,000", "Rs. 2,16,000", "Rs. 3,24,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the amount invested by B and C be b and c respectively. According to the question = b = 54000⁶ 54000 × 12 b × 8¹ 4 ⇒ × Also, = c = 54000¹0⁵4000 × 12 c × 6¹ 5 ⇒ × Required difference = 54000¹0⁵4000⁶ = 2,16,000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2220", "q": "The ratio of investment by A to that by B is a business is 14:15 and the ratio of their respective pro fits at the end of a year is 2 : 5. If A invested the money for 3 months, then for how much time (in months) B invested his money?", "o": ["7", "6", "5", "9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pro fit is always proportional to Amount invested time period × Let amount invested by A = 14 unit, amount invested by B = 15 unit and the time period for which B invested the amount = t months = ⇒ 14 × 3¹5 × t² 5 t = = 7 months ⇒ 14 × 3 × 5¹5 × 2³50"},
+{"id": "P2221", "q": "A, B and C started a business with their capitals in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. A increased his capital by 50% after 4 months, B increased his capital by 33¹ 3 % after 6 months and C withdrew 50% of his capital after 8 months, from the start of the business. If the total profit at the end of a year was Rs. 86,800, then the difference between the shares of A and C in the profit was :", "o": ["Rs.12,600", "Rs.7,000", "Rs.9,800", "Rs.8,400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "50% = , 33 % = 1² 1³ 1³ Ratio A : B : C → Initial 2 × 4 : 3 × 6 : 5 × 8 → Final 3 × 8 : 4 × 6 : 2.5 × 4 → --------------------------------- Profit 32 : 42 : 50 → Total Profit (32 + 42 + 50) = 124 units 124 units = 86800 Rs. 1 unit = 700 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2222", "q": "A. B and C jointly started a business in which A invested ₹7,000 for 12 months, B invested ₹8,000 for 10 months and C invested ₹12,000 for 6 months. A was the working member for which he received 20% of the profits as his remuneration. The total profit earned at the end of one year was ₹14,750. What is C's share (in ₹) in the profit?", "o": ["4,000", "2,950", "3,600", "4,200 SSC CGL 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Share A : B : C → Investment 7000 : 8000 : 12000 → Time 12 : 10 : 6 → —------------------------------------------------------------ Ratio 84 : 80 : 72 → 21 : 20 : 18 A received 20% of the profits as his remuneration Remaining profit = 14,750 × = 11800⁴ 5⁵9 unit = ₹ 11800 C's share (18 unit) = × 18 = ₹3600¹1800⁵9"},
+{"id": "P2223", "q": "A, B and C invested money in a business such that 2 times A's share, 4 times B's share and 6 times C's share are all equal. If they earned ₹44,000, find the share of A.", "o": ["₹22,000", "₹12,000", "₹24,000", "₹20,000 SSC Selection Post (Phase - XII)"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "If 2 times A's share, 4 times B's share and 6 times C's share are all equal ∴ 2A = 4B = 6C Hence , A : B : C = 6 : 3 : 2 Now , A’s share = × 44000 = ₹24,000⁶ 11"},
+{"id": "P2224", "q": "Three partners decided to start a business. They decided to donate 10% of the profit to a charity organisation and then the remaining profit would be shared among first, second and third partner in the ratio 1 : 2 : 2. The total profit received was ₹1,80,000. Find the share of the first partner. Matriculation Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["₹32,400", "₹31,800", "₹33,200", "₹29,600 SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total profit distributed among partners in business = 1,80,000 × 90% = ₹1,62,000 Share of the 1st partner = ( ) × 1,62,000¹ 1 + 2 + 2 = = ₹32,400¹ , 62 , 000⁵"},
+{"id": "P2225", "q": "Three partners P , Q and R invested a total of Rs. 52,000 in a business. At the end of the year, P got Rs. 1430, Q got Rs.1870 and R got Rs. 2420 as the share of profit. How much amount did Q invest Search on TG: @apna_pdf in the business ?", "o": ["Rs. 17000", "Rs. 20400", "Rs. 15300", "Rs. 18700 SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "As we know :- profit = time × investment If investment time is equal , then the ratio of profit is equal to the ratio of investment . According to the question, Total profit of P , Q and R = Rs."},
+{"id": "P2226", "q": "Nikhil and Neha invested capital in the ratio 5 : 4. The time Neha invested her money for was one year more than that invested by Nikhil. The ratio of their profits is in the ratio 6: 5. Find the time Neha invested the money for.", "o": ["26 years", "23 years", "24 years", "25 years SSC CGL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Nikhil : Neha → Investment : 4 → 5 Time : → x x + 1 ------------------------------ Profit 6 : 5 → Now , = 25 = 24 + 24⁵ x⁴ ( x + 1 )⁶⁵ ⇒ x x = 24 years ⇒ x So Neha invested for ( + 1) years x = 25 years"},
+{"id": "P2227", "q": "P, Q, and R invest ₹20,000, ₹30,000, and ₹40,000, respectively. P invests for 8 months, Q for 12 months, and R for 10 months. The total profit is ₹46,000. What is P's share of the profit? Graduate Level 31/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["₹9,000", "₹10,000", "₹8,000", "₹12,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Profit = Investment × Time Ratio → P : Q : R Invest → 20000 : 30000 : 40000 Time → 4 : 6 : 5 …………………………………… Profit → 4 : 9 : 10 A/Q, 23 unit = 46000⁴ unit = × 4 = ₹ 8000⁴6000²3 So, The share of P in profit = Rs.8000"},
+{"id": "P2228", "q": "P and Q start a partnership. P invests ₹50,000. After 4 months, Q joins with ₹75,000. After 2 more months, P doubles his capital. If the business runs for 12 months, find the profit-sharing ratio of P to Q . Graduate Level 24/07/2025 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["2 : 3", "3 : 2", "5 : 4", "1 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio → P : Q Inv → (50,000×6 +1,00,000×6) : 75,000 × 8 Ratio of profit → 900 : 600 or 3 : 2"},
+{"id": "P2229", "q": "Sonu started a business by investing ₹40,000. After 4 months, Prem joined with ₹80,000. At the end of 8 months from the start, Alok joined with ₹1,20,000. If the total profit is ₹1,56,000 at the end of the year, find the share of Alok .", "o": ["₹47,500", "₹48,000", "₹47,200", "₹46,800"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Ratio Sonu : Prem : Alok → 40000 × 12 : 80000 × 8 : 120000 × 4 ________________________________________ 3 : 4 : 3 Now, 10 units = 156000³ units = × 3 = ₹ 46800¹56000¹0"},
+{"id": "P2230", "q": "P and Q start a business. P invests ₹40,000 for 9 months, Q invests ₹60,000 for 6 months. What is Q's share of a ₹45,000 profit ?", "o": ["₹26,500", "₹28,000", "₹36,000", "₹22,500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Ratio P : Q → 40000 × 9 : 60000 × 6 or 1 : 1 Now, 2 units = 45000¹ unit = = ₹ 22500⁴5000²"},
+{"id": "P2231", "q": "A and B invest ₹20,000 and ₹35,000 respectively in a business. What is A's share in a profit of ₹25,000?", "o": ["₹ 8090", "₹ 9091", "₹ 9250", "₹ 9000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Investment Profit (when ∝ time is constant ) Investment 4 : 7 → Profit 4 : 7 → 11 units = 25,000 A's share = 25,000 × ₹ 9091⁴ 11 ≈"},
+{"id": "P2232", "q": "P and Q contribute to a business investment in the ratio 3:5. They earn a profit of ₹66,000. P is a working partner and receives 10% of the profit extra. What is P's total share ?", "o": ["₹26,500", "₹28,875", "₹38,875", "₹36,875"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Investment Profit (when ∝ time is constant ) Investment 3 : 5 → Profit 3 : 5 → 10% of profit = 66000 × = 6600¹0¹00 Remaining profit = 66000 - 6600 = 59400 P's share = 6600 + 59400 × 3⁸ = 6600 + 22275 = 28 ,875"},
+{"id": "P2233", "q": "A and B invested ₹1,40,000 and ₹1,80,000 respectively. A remained for 10 months and B for 7 months. What is the total profit if B's share is ₹15,201 ?", "o": ["₹32,800", "₹32,091", "₹30,201", "₹31,091"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B → Investment 1,40,000 : 1,80 ,000 → 7 : 9 Time 10 : 7 → ----------------------------------- 70 : 63 = 10 : 9 A/Q, 9 unit = ₹15,201¹9 unit = ₹32,091 = 15 , 201 × 19⁹"},
+{"id": "P2234", "q": "Pankaj, Kuldeep, and Ankit invested ₹25,000, ₹35,000, and ₹40,000 respectively in a business. If the profit at the end of the year was ₹30,000, find Kuldeep's share.", "o": ["₹ 9500", "₹12,000", "₹11,000", "₹10,500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Pankaj : Kuldeep : Ankit = 25,000 : 35,000 : 40,000 = 5 : 7 : 8 So, Kuldeep’s share: × 30,000⁷ 5 + 7 + 8 = ₹10,500"},
+{"id": "P2235", "q": "X and Y started a business by investing ₹48,000 and ₹72,000 respectively. After 6 months, X withdrew half of his capital, while Y increased his capital by ₹24,000. At the end of the year, they earned a total profit of ₹55,000. What is Y's share in the profit?", "o": ["₹38,000", "₹27,000", "₹38,500", "₹33,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio:- X : Y⁴8,000 × 6 : 72,000 × 6 + + 24,000 × 6 : (72,000 + 24,000) × 6 ---------------------------------------------------------- 4,32,000 : 10,08,000 or 3 : 7 So, Y's share = × 55,000 = 38,500⁷ 10"},
+{"id": "P2236", "q": "Komal and Koyal started a business with ₹1,20,000 and ₹80,000 respectively. After 6 months, Koyal added ₹40,000 more. Komal withdrew ₹40,000 at the same time. What is the profit-sharing ratio at the end of 1 year?", "o": ["1 : 1", "5 : 6", "7 : 4", "1 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Komal’s investment = (1,20,000 × 6) + (80,000 × 6) = 12,00,000 Koyal's investment = (80,000 × 6) + (1,20,000 × 6) = 12,00,000 Ratio = 12,00,000 : 12,00,000 = 1 : 1"},
+{"id": "P2237", "q": "Ankit invested ₹20,000 and Shakti invested ₹30,000. The total profit was ₹80,000. Ankit receives 25% of the total profit as a management fee. The remaining profit is divided in proportion to the investments. What is Ankit's total share?", "o": ["₹41,000", "₹44,000", "₹46,000", "₹48,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ankit's Management Fee: 25% of ₹80,000 = ₹20,000 Remaining Distributable Profit: = ₹80,000 - ₹20,000 = ₹60,000 Investment Ratio = ₹20,000 : ₹30,000 = 2 : 3 Ankit's Share of Remaining Profit = ( ) ₹60,000 = ₹24,000² 5 × Ankit's Total Share = ₹20,000 + ₹24,000 (Profit Share) = ₹44,000"},
+{"id": "P2238", "q": "A, B, and C invested ₹30,000, ₹50,000, and ₹90,000 respectively in a business. If the total profit at the end of the year is ₹30,000, what is A's share of the profit?", "o": ["₹ 8823.53", "₹ 5294.12", "₹ 15882.35", "₹ 9000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B : C → Profit 30000 × 12 : 50000×12 : 90000×12 → ________________________________________ 3 : 5 : 9¹7 units 30000 = 3 units × 3 = ₹5294.12 ⇒ = 30000¹7"},
+{"id": "P2239", "q": "X and Y share a rented field. X utilizes 15 horses for 5 months, while Y uses 25 cows for 4 months and 40 sheep for 5 months. If 2 horses are equivalent to 5 cows, and 3 cows are equal to 9 sheep. What portion of the rent is X pay?", "o": ["8", "9", "10", "17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, 2H = 5C = ⇒ ⇒ H C⁵ 2 and 3C = 9S = 3 ⇒ ⇒ C S Ratio H : C : S → 5 : 2 : 2³ : 3 : 1 _____________________ 15 : 6 : 2 Rent by X = 15 × 15 × 5 = 1125 Rent by Y = (25 × 6 × 4) + (40 × 2 × 5) = 600 + 400 = 1000 X’s portion = = 1125¹125 + 1000⁹ 17"},
+{"id": "P2240", "q": "A and B start a business. A invests 2 times more than B. After 6 months, A withdraws half of his capital, and B triples his capital. If the total profit after one year is ₹65,000, find the share of A.", "o": ["₹30,000", "₹32413.78", "₹38,000", "₹34,411.77"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: A : B = 3 : 1 According to question, Ratio A : B → Profit 3 × 6+(3 -1.5) × 6 : 1 × 6 + 3 × 6 → (18 + 9) : (6 + 18)²7 : 24 or 9 : 8¹7 units = 65000⁹ units × 9 = ₹ 34411.77 = 65000¹7"},
+{"id": "P2241", "q": "Ravi, Aman, and Karan started a business together. They invested ₹40,000, ₹60,000, and ₹80,000 respectively for one year. If the total profit at the end of the year is ₹55,000, what will be Aman's share in the profit ?", "o": ["₹18,333.33", "₹19,333.67", "₹23,333.76", "₹28,333.33"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Ravi : Aman : Karan → Investment 40000 : 60000 : 80000 → Time 12 : 12 : 12 → ___________________________ 2 : 3 : 4 A/Q , (2 + 3 + 4) unit ₹55,000 = 3 unit × 3 = ₹ 18,333.33 = 55000⁹"},
+{"id": "P2242", "q": "A and B invest ₹50,000 and ₹1,00,000 respectively, in a business. After one year, the profit is distributed, including simple interest at 10% per annum on the capital. Total profit, including interest, is ₹30,000. What is A's share ?", "o": ["₹9,000", "₹10,000", "₹11,000", "₹12,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total interest on investment of A and B = 50000 × + 100000 × 10¹00¹0¹00 = 5000 + 10000 = ₹15000 Total profit = ₹30,000 - ₹15000 = ₹15000 Investment Ratio 50,000 :1,00,000 = 1:2 → A’s share = × 1 = 5000¹5000³ A’s share with interest = 5000 + 5000 = ₹10000"},
+{"id": "P2243", "q": "Sohan started a business with ₹80,000. After 5 months, Rohan joined with ₹1,60,000. After another 4 months, Sohan withdrew ₹40,000. What is the ratio of their profits at the end of the year?", "o": ["2 : 5", "5 : 6", "1 : 5", "3 : 4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Ratio Sohan : Rohan → Profit 80000× 9 + 40000 × 3 : 160000 ×7 → __________________________________________ 3 : 4 So, required ratio = 3 : 4"},
+{"id": "P2244", "q": "X, Y, and Z started a business with capitals in the ratio 3:5:8 After 4 months, Z withdrew 50% of his capital. After another 4 months, Y withdrew half of his capital. The business continued for a total of 18 months. If total profit is ₹9,44,955, find the ratio of profit shares of X : Y : Z.", "o": ["33 : 33 : 53", "54 : 65 : 88", "81 :72 : 62", "15: 63 : 17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, Ratio X : Y : Z → Profit 3 × 18 : (5 × 8 + 2.5 × 10) : (8 × 4 → + 8 × × 14)¹² 54 : 65 : 88 ________________________________________ X : Y : Z = 54 : 65 : 88"},
+{"id": "P2245", "q": "Rohit invests ₹50,000 for 12 months, Ramesh invests ₹1,00,000 for 6 months. What is Rohit's share of ₹20,000 profit ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["₹10,000", "₹12,000", "₹15,000", "₹18,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "profit = investment × time Rohit : Ramesh 12 × 50000⁶ × 100000¹ : 1 Profit share of Rohit = × 20000¹ 2 = ₹10000"},
+{"id": "P2246", "q": "A and B start a business with capitals in the ratio 5 : 3. After 6 months, A withdraws ₹10,000 and B doubles his investment. If the initial investment of A was ₹50,000, and the total profit after 1 year is ₹90,000, find the profit share of A.", "o": ["₹42,000", "₹50,000", "₹60,000", "₹45,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "profit = investment × time A : B⁵0,000× 6 +6 ×40000 : 30000 × 6 + 60000 × 6⁵40,000 : 540,000 TG: @ikunal_x¹ : 1 the profit share of A = × 90,000¹ 2 = ₹45,000"},
+{"id": "P2247", "q": "Ashish started a business with a sum of ₹ 60,000. Sachin joined him 8 months later with a sum of ₹ 35,000. At what respective ratio will the two share the profit after two years?", "o": ["5 : 7", "14 : 7", "16 : 7", "18 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio → Ashish : Sachin Investment → 60000 : 35000 Time → 24 : 16 We know that Profit = Investment × Time Profit = 12 × 3 : 7 × 2 = 18 : 7"},
+{"id": "P2248", "q": "Amit invested ₹90,000 in a business. After 3 months, Sumit joined the partnership with ₹60,000. After another 3 months, Amit withdrew ₹30,000. Find the ratio of their profits at the end of the year.", "o": ["3 : 2", "4 : 3", "5 : 3", "2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Profit = investment × time Amit : Sumit (90,000 ×6) + (60,000 × 6) : 60000 × 9⁹00000 : 540000⁵ : 3"},
+{"id": "P2249", "q": "Ram invests ₹60,000 while Shyam invests ₹90,000, with Ram's investment lasting for 10 months and Shyam's for 8 months. The total profit amounts to ₹40,000. What is the Ram's share ?", "o": ["₹30,181.82", "₹32,181.82", "₹41,181.81", "₹18,181.82"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Profit = investment × time Ram : Shyam 60000 × 10 : 90000 × 8⁶0 : 72⁵ : 6 Share of Ram = = ₹18,181.82⁵ × 40000¹1"},
+{"id": "P2250", "q": "P and Q invested in a business in the ratio 4 : 5. The profit ratio was 8 : 9. If Q invested his money for 9 months, for how many months did P invest?", "o": ["12 months", "10 months", "16 months", "14 months"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio P : Q → Investment 4 : 5 → Profit 8 : 9 → Let P invest for x years A/Q , = 4 × x⁵ × 9⁸ 9⁴ = 40 = 10 months ⇒ x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2251", "q": "P, Q, and R invested 12,000, ₹16,000, and ₹20,000 respectively. P's investment was for 12 months, Q's for 8 months, and R's for 4 months. The total profit is ₹55,000. What is Q's share of the profit ?", "o": ["₹20,000", "₹30,000", "₹25,000", "₹32,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio P : Q : R Invest 12000 : 16000 : 20000 Or 3 : 4 : 5 Time 12 : 8 : 4 ----------------------------------------- 36 : 32 : 20 or 9 : 8 : 5 Q's share = × 55000 = ₹20,000⁸ 22"},
+{"id": "P2252", "q": "Sumit starts a business with ₹80,000. Three months later, Sachin joined with ₹100,000. Six months after starting, Sumit increased his investment by ₹40,000. Sachin leaves the business three months before the end of the year. What is their profit-sharing ratio ?", "o": ["7 : 4", "2 : 1", "1 : 4", "1 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total amount invested by Sumit = 80,000⁶ + 1,20,000⁶ × × = 4,80,000 + 7,20,000 = 12,00,000 Total amount invested by Sachin = 1,00,000⁶ = 6,00,000 × Therefore, their profit ratio = 12 : 6 = 2 : 1"},
+{"id": "P2253", "q": "A and B invest ₹60,000 and ₹80,000 respectively. A remains in business for 8 months, B for 9 months. If the total profit is ₹40,000, what is A's share ?", "o": ["₹16,000", "₹18,000", "₹20,000", "₹24,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio → A : B Investment → 60000 : 80000 Time → 8 : 9 Profit = 60000 × 8 : 80000 × 9 = 48 : 72 = 2 : 3 A/Q, 5 unit 40000 = 2 unit × 2 = ₹ 16000 = 40000⁵"},
