+{"id": "P2263", "q": "P and Q start a business with Rs. 2,40,000 and Rs. 3,60,000 respectively. After 4 months, P adds Rs. 60,000 more, and Q withdraws Rs.60,000. At the end of 1 year, they make a profit of Rs. 2,40,000. What is Q's share of profit?", "o": ["Rs.1,28,000", "Rs.1,25,000", "Rs. 2,00,000", "Rs. 2,90,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "we know Profit = Invst. × Time P = 2,40,000 × 4 + 3,00,000 × 8 = 33,60,000 Q = 3,60,000 × 4 + 3,00000 × 8 = 38,40,000 By ratio P : Q⁷ : 8 = 15 Unit 15 Unit 2,40,000¹ Unit 16,000 = ⇒ = Profit of Q = 8 × 16,000 = ₹1,28,000"},
