+{"id": "P2265", "q": "'A' and 'B' entered a joint venture. 'A' brought Rs. 3,00,000 and 'B' Rs. 4,00,000. 'A' also contributed skilled labor equivalent to Rs. 1,00,000. At the end of the year, they earned Rs. 2,40,000 in profit. If they agreed to divide the profit in proportion to their effective contributions, what was A's share ? TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["Rs. 1,10,000", "Rs. 1,20,000", "Rs. 1,24,500", "Rs. 1,50,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A’s effective capital = 3,00,000 + 1,00,000 = ₹4,00,000 B’s capital = ₹4,00,000 Ratio A : B = 1 : 1, therefore Profit ⇒ share ratio = 1 : 1 A’s share = 2,40,000 = ₹1,20,000 × 1²"},
+{"id": "P2266", "q": "P, Q, and R started a textile business. Their initial capital investments were ₹1,200,000, ₹800,000, and ₹1,000,000, respectively. After four months, P added ₹200,000, and R withdrew ₹100,000. Q kept his investment unchanged. The partnership lasted for 12 months (one year). What was the ratio of their effective capital contributions to profits ?", "o": ["10 : 4 : 15", "16 : 15 : 7", "10 : 7 : 5", "10 : 6 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "साझेदारी", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "We know that Profit = Investment × Time Investment Of P = 1200000 × 4 + 1400000 × 8 = 1,60,00,000 Investment Of Q = 800000 × 12 = 9600000 Investment Of R = 1000000 × 4 + 900000 × 8 = 1,12,00,000 then, Investment ratio (P : Q : R) = 160 : 96 : 112 = 10 : 6 : 7"},
