+{"id": "P2305", "q": "The ratio of cheese to sauce for a single pizza is 1 cup to cup. If Rama 1² used 15 cups of sauce to make a number of pizzas, then how many cups of cheese did she use on those pizzas ? Graduate Level 27/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["20 cups", "10 cups", "40 cups", "30 cups"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Cheese : sauce = 2 : 1 → According to the question , Sauce used to make pizza (1 unit) = 15 cups Cheese to be used (2 unit) = 30 cups"},
+{"id": "P2306", "q": "Out of the total income, a family saves 15% and the rest of the amount is spent on three types of expenditure - health, education and food in the ratio of 1 : 2 : 2. The income is Rs.300 less than thrice the expenditure incurred on education. What is the difference between the savings and the expenditure incurred on health? Graduate Level 27/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["Rs.300", "Rs.350", "Rs.2,250", "Rs.500"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let total Income = 100 units Then , Savings = 15 units Expenditure on health , education and food be 17 units , 34 units and 34 units respectively. According to the question , 3 × (34 units)¹00 units = 300 Rs. − 2 units = 300 Rs. Required difference = (17 units 15 units) = 2 units = 300 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2307", "q": "Let M denote the mean proportional between 16 and 9 and let N denote the third proportional of 9 and 15. Find the value of 5M + 3N. Graduate Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["300", "125", "135", "225"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "M = = 12¹6 × 9³35 N = = 25¹5² 9⁵M + 3N = 5 × 12 + 3 × 25 = 60 +75 = 135"},
+{"id": "P2308", "q": "A company is manufacturing three different products - Glass, Plate and Bowl. The number of Plates is double the number of Glasses. The number of Glasses manufactured is twice the number of Bowls. What is the difference between the number of Plates and the number of Bowls if the total units manufactured by the company is 2380? Graduate Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1360", "680", "1120", "1020"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of manufacturing → Plate : Glasses = 2 : 1 and Glasses : Bowl = 2 : 1 Plate : Glasses : Bowl = 4 : 2 : 1 According to the question , Total manufacturing (7 units) = 2380 Required difference (3 units) = = 1020 units 2380⁷ × 3"},
+{"id": "P2309", "q": "Two numbers are in the ratio of 7 : 6. If the difference between their squares is 637, then the numbers are Higher Secondary 30/06/2023 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["49 and 42", "49 and 12", "43 and 36", "14 and 12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the numbers be 7 and 6 x x According to question, = 637⁷ x ( )² − 6 x ( )² = 49³6 = 637 x² − x² = = 49 = 7 x² ⇒ x Therefore, the numbers are 49 and 42."},
