+{"id": "P2312", "q": "In an examination, the ratio of practical to theory marks is 3 : 7. If 80% of the marks are scored in the practical and 60% of marks are scored in the theory, what is the ratio of marks scored in the theory and the practical ? Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["6 : 7", "5 : 7", "7 : 4", "3 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the marks of practical and theory be 300 and 700. According to question, Required ratio = (700 × ) : (300 × )⁶0¹00⁸0¹00 = 420 : 240 = 7 : 4"},
+{"id": "P2313", "q": "If a : b : c = 4 : 7 : 9 and b : c : d = 28 : 36 : 21, then a : b : c : d is: Matriculation Level 28/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["12 : 21 : 27 : 17", "16 : 28 : 36 : 21", "8 : 14 : 18 : 21", "4 : 7 : 9 : 11"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "a : b : c = 4 : 7 : 9 ) × 4 a : b : c = 16 : 28 : 36 ⇒ and b : c : d = 28 : 36 : 21 or a : b : c : d = 16 : 28 : 36 : 21"},
+{"id": "P2314", "q": "The ratio of the number of boys to that of girls in a village is 5 : 3. If 40% of the boys and 60% of the girls appeared in an examination, then the ratio of the number of boys and girls who appeared in the examination to the number who did not appear in the same examination, is :- Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["17 ∶ 21", "19 ∶ 21", "17 ∶ 27", "19 ∶ 23 SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number of boys and girls in the village be 500 and 300. According to question, Total number of boys and girls who appeared in the examination → (500 × ) + (300 × ) = 380⁴0¹00⁶0¹00 Total number of boys and girls who did not appear in the examination 800³80 = 420 → − Required ratio = 380 : 420 = 19 : 21"},
+{"id": "P2315", "q": "If 750 is divided into two parts such that the ratio of one to the other is in the ratio 8 : 7, then find the smallest number.", "o": ["135", "120", "350", "90"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Smallest number = 750 × = 350⁷ 8 + 7"},
+{"id": "P2316", "q": "If the third proportion of 3 and is x²7 and the third proportion of 2 and y is 8, then find x : y", "o": ["7 : 9", "4 : 5", "3 : 7", "9 : 4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "3rd proportion of a, b = b² a So the value of ⇒ 27 = ⇒ = 9 x x² 3 x and the value of ⇒ 8 = ⇒ y = 4 y y² 2 = 9 , y = 4 x Required ratio = 9 : 4"},
+{"id": "P2317", "q": "If = = , then what is the J⁴ K⁵ L³ value of (L + J)² : (J + K)² : (K + L)² ?", "o": ["25 : 16 : 9", "64 : 25 : 81", "49 : 81 : 62", "49 : 81 : 64"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = J⁴ K⁵ L³ J = 4, K = 5, L = 3 According to the question, (L + J)² : (J + K)² : (K + L)² (3 + 4)² : (4 + 5)² : (5 + 3)² 49 : 81 : 64"},
+{"id": "P2318", "q": "These positive numbers are in the proportion of 2 : 3 : 5. If the sum of their squares is 342, then find the largest number.", "o": ["35", "55", "15", "25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let numbers be , and 2 x³ x⁵ x According to the question, + + = 342 ( 2 x )² ( 3 x )² ( 5 x )²³8 = 342 = 9 = 3 x² ⇒ x² ⇒ x Largest number ( ) = 15⁵ x"},
+{"id": "P2319", "q": "In three positive numbers, the ratio of first and second is 3 : 4 and the ratio of second and third is 3 : 5. The 323 product of first and third is 4500. What is the sum of the three numbers?", "o": ["282", "235", "198", "205"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1st no. : 2nd no. : 3rd no. 3 : 4 : 4³ : 3 : 5 ------------------------- 9 : 12 : 20 According to the question, (9 × 20 ) unit = ₹4500 x x = = = 5 x² 450¹8 ⇒ x²25⁹ Sum of three numbers = (41 ) = 41 × 5 x = 205"},
+{"id": "P2320", "q": "If 20% of a number is th of 1⁶ another number, what is the ratio of first number to the second number?", "o": ["4 : 7", "5 : 6", "5 : 3", "4 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, = x × 1⁵ y × 1⁶ Ratio of the numbers = 5 : 6 ⇒ x : y"},
+{"id": "P2321", "q": "If A : B : C = 2 : 3 : 4 , then what will be the value of : : ? A B B C C A", "o": ["9 : 5 : 36", "8 : 7 : 25", "8 : 9 : 24", "12 : 10 : 13"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A : B : C = 2 : 3 : 4 : : = : : A B B C C A² 3³ 4⁴ 2 = 8 : 9 : 24"},
+{"id": "P2322", "q": "The ratio of income of Jitendra, and Narendra is 4 : 7 and the ratio of their expenditure is 6 : 5 respectively. If Jitendra saves Rs.400 out of Rs.2,800 income, then find the savings of Narendra.", "o": ["Rs. 2,900", "Rs. 2,000", "Rs. 3,900", "Rs, 4,900"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the income of Jitendra and Narendra = 4x and 7x And expenditure of Jitendra and Narendra = 6y and 5y According to the question, 4x = 2800 x = 700 → Savings of Jitendra 4x - 6y = 400 ⇒ y = 400 ⇒ Savings of Narendra 7x - 5y ⇒ = 4900 - 2000 = 2900 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2323", "q": "The ratio of the incomes of two employees is 7 : 4, and the ratio of their expenditures is 3 : 1. If each of them manages to save ₹4,800 per month, find the sum of their monthly incomes (in ₹) .", "o": ["21120", "20120", "21150", "18150"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B → Income 7 : 4 ) × 2 → Expenditure 3 : 1 ) × 3 → ----------------------------------- Savings of A = 7 × 2 ( ) − 3 × 3 ( ){ } = 5 units ⇒ 5 units = 4800 ₹ Total Income of A and B = = 22 units ( 7 + 4 ) × 2²2 units = 21120 ₹ → 4800⁵ × 22"},
+{"id": "P2324", "q": "Find the mean proportion between (6 + ) and (3 - ). 8²", "o": ["2", "12¹4", "(6 - )", "- 7⁸ 15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mean proportional between a and b is . ab Mean proportional of and 6 + 8 ( ) = 3 − 2 ( )⁶ + 8 ( )³ − 2 ( ) = 18 − 6² + 3⁸ − 16 ( ) = 18 − 6² + 6² − 4 ( ) ⇒ 14"},
+{"id": "P2325", "q": "A varies directly as the positive square root of B, and inversely as the cube of C. If A = 15, when B = 27 and C=2, then find B when A = 9 and C = 2.", "o": ["281", "42", "243", "25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A ∝ B ∝ 1 C³ A = 15 = k × B c³ ⇒ k × 27² 3 k = ……...e.q .(1)¹20³ 3 Again , A = 9 = k × B c³ ⇒ 120× B³ 3 × 2³ = B = B⁹ 3 ×8⁴0 ⇒ 243²5"},
+{"id": "P2326", "q": "The mean proportional of a and b is c. What is the mean proportional of and ? a² c b² c", "o": ["c", "3c", "c³ c²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mean proportional of a and b is ‘c’ = = ab ab ⇒ c² Now, Mean proportional of and a² c b² c = = = abc = a² c × b² c a² c² b² c³"},
+{"id": "P2327", "q": "The third proportional of ‘ ’ and a is: b⁴ 4 a", "o": ["b", "8", "16", "a"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Third proportional of a and = = = b⁴ 4 a ( b⁴ 4 a )² a b⁸ 16 a² × a b⁸ 16 a³"},
+{"id": "P2328", "q": "The salaries of A, B and C are in ratio of: , , . The salary of A and B³ 2⁶ 5⁴ 3 together is Rs.40,500. By what percentage is the salary of A more than that of C ?", "o": ["12%", "13%", "11.5%", "12.5%"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM of (2, 5, 3) = 30 Then, the ratio of the salary of A, B and C = : : 3² × 30⁶ 5 × 30⁴ 3 × 30 = 45 : 36 : 40 Required percentage = × 100⁴5 − 40⁴0 = × 100 = 12.5% 5⁴0"},
+{"id": "P2329", "q": "If the mean proportional between 5 and 125 is x and the mean proportional between and is y, find the value of 4⁴ 6² 2x : y. Graduate Level 04/08/2022 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["25 : 48", "25 : 128", "25 : 64", "25 : 96"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "x = = = 25¹25 × 5⁶25 y = = × 6 = 96⁴ 4 × 6² 4² So, 2x : y = 25 × 2 : 96 = 50 : 96 = 25 : 48"},
+{"id": "P2330", "q": "The mean proportional between 75 and x is five times the mean proportional between 15 and 26. The value of x is: Higher Secondary 05/08/2022 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["100", "120", "110", "130 SSC MTS 2021 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question ⇒ = 5 × 75 x¹5 × 26 ⇒ 5 = 5 × 3 x¹5×26 ⇒ = ⇒ = 5 × 26= 130³ x³ × 5×26 x"},
+{"id": "P2331", "q": "What number must be subtracted from each of the numbers 55, 23, 43 and 325¹9, so that the new values are in proportion?", "o": ["9", "11", "7", "5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The difference between (55 and 43) = 12 The difference between (23 and 19) = 4 Ratio of their difference → 12⁴ Difference = (12 - 4) = 8 units Again , the difference between 55 and 23 = 32 Making previous difference equal to 32, = 12 × 4⁴ × 4⁴8¹6 Now , compare with initial fraction we get, 55²3 → 48¹6 Clearly, we can see that (55 - 48) = 7 must be subtracted from each of "},
+{"id": "P2332", "q": "The ratio between the volumes of Sphere 1 and Sphere 2 is 27 : 64. Find the ratio of the surface areas of Sphere 1 and Sphere 2 .", "o": ["9 : 16", "16 : 9", "3 : 4", "1 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= volume of spℎere 1 volume of spℎere 2⁴ 3 π r¹ 3⁴ 3 π r² 3 = So, = ⇒ 27⁶4 r¹ 3 r² 3 r¹ r² 3⁴ Surface area of sphere 1 = 4 π r¹ 2 = 4 × = 36 π 3² π Surface area of sphere 2 = 4 π r² 2 = 4 × = 64 π 4² π So, the required ratio = 36 : 64 = 9 : 16 π π"},
+{"id": "P2333", "q": "A number when subtracted from 3 times the second number, gives a result equal to of the first number. 3⁴ What is the ratio of the first number to the second number ?", "o": ["11 : 6", "12 : 7", "9 : 5", "10 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "let the first number = a And second number = b According to the question , 3b - a = 3b = + a³ a⁴ ⇒ 3 a⁴ 3b = = ⇒ 7 a⁴ ⇒ a b¹2⁷ therefore ratio a : b = 12 : 7 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2334", "q": "If a : b = b : c, then what is the value of : ? a⁶ b⁶", "o": [":", ": ac", ":", ": a³ b³ b³ a³ c³ a² b²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "ac = a b = b c ⇒ b² Now, : = : a⁶ b⁶ a⁶ ( b² )³ = : ⇒ a⁶ : b⁶ a⁶ ( ac )³ = : ⇒ a⁶ : b⁶ a⁶ a³ c³ : ⇒ a⁶ : b⁶ = a³ c³"},
+{"id": "P2335", "q": "There are a total of 60 students in a class and the ratio of the number of boys to that of the girls is 4 : 1, respectively. If 22 of the boys from this class are vegetarians, then find the number of non-vegetarian boys from the same class.", "o": ["26", "18", "38", "28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total students = 60 B : G⁴ : 1⁴ + 1 = 5⁶0 (given) ⇒ → So number of boys = 4 × 4 = 48 → 60⁵ Number of non-vegetarian = 48 - 22 = 26"},
+{"id": "P2336", "q": "On a tree, there are some parrots and some pigeons in the ratio of 7:9 , respectively. After an hour, 8 parrots fly away, and 6 pigeons and 10 sparrows come and sit on the tree. The ratio of the parrots and the pigeons on the tree now is 1 : 4. What is the ratio of the parrots and the sparrows that are now on the tree?", "o": ["1 : 1", "1 : 2", "3 : 5", "4 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the parrots be 7 and pigeon be 9 x x . According to the question, = 28 - 32 = 9 + 6⁷ x − 8⁹ x + 6¹ 4 ⇒ x x¹9 = 38 = 2 ⇒ x ⇒ x Initial Numbers of parrots = 7 × 2 =14 Remaining parrots = 14 - 8 = 6 Therefore ratio of parrots and sparrows 6 : 10 = 3 : 5 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2337", "q": "A sum of ₹3400 is divided among P and Q in such a way that of P's³ 4 share is equal to of Q's share. What is 2³ the positive difference between the shares of P and Q?", "o": ["₹500", "₹400", "₹200", "₹300"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "× P = of Q³ 4² 3 = P + Q = 8 + 9 = 17 unit ⇒ P Q⁸ 9 ⇒ 339 positive difference = Q - P = 9 - 8 = 1 unit ⇒ 17 unit = 3400¹ unit = Rs 200 ⇒ ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2338", "q": "Rs 21000 is to be distributed between Raj and Karan such that Raj gets Rs 9000 less than Karan. What is the ratio of the amount received by Raj to 326 that received by Karan?", "o": ["2 : 5", "3 : 5", "5 : 3", "5 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Karan gets = x Raj gets = x - 9000 As per question, x + x - 9000 = 21000 x = 15,000 ⇒ ⇒ Rato of Raj : Karan = 6000 : 15000 = 2 : 5"},
+{"id": "P2339", "q": "If 60% of a number is equal to three-fourth of another number, what is the ratio of the first number to the second number?", "o": ["3 : 7", "2 : 5", "7 : 3", "5 : 4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number be and . x y According to question, 60% × = × x³ 4 y × = × ⇒ = 3⁵ x³ 4 y x y⁵ 4 So, the required ratio = 5 :4"},
+{"id": "P2340", "q": "If y varies directly with x, and y = 61 when x = 42, find y when x = 54 (consider integral value).", "o": ["86", "78", "82", "72"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question , y = kx k = → y x When , x = 42 then y = 61 = y¹ x¹ y² x² = 78.42⁷8 y² → 61 × 54⁴2 ≈"},
+{"id": "P2341", "q": "The ratio of the monthly incomes of A and B is 11 : 13 and the ratio of their expenditure is 9 : 11. If both of them manage to save ₹ 4,000 per month, then find the difference in their incomes (in ₹).", "o": ["2,500", "3,200", "4,000", "3,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B → Income 11 : 13 → Expenses 9 : 11 → ---------------------------------------- Savings 2 : 2 → According to question , Saving (2 units) = 4000 Rs. Difference b/w their income (13¹1) units − 2 units = 4000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2342", "q": "If a, b and c are positive numbers such that ( ) : ( ) : ( ) = a² + b² b² + c² c² + a² 34 : 61 : 45, then b - a : c - b : c - a = ____.", "o": ["1 : 2 : 3", "3 : 1 : 2", "2 : 1 : 3", "3 : 2 : 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, ( ) : ( ) : ( ) a² + b² b² + c² c² + a² = 34 : 61 : 45 , Adding all we get, 2( ) = 140 a² + b² + c² ( ) = 70. a² + b² + c² = ( ) - ( ) c² a² + b² + c² a² + b² = 70 - 34 = 36."},
+{"id": "P2343", "q": "The income of A is of B's² 3 income and the expenditure of A is of 3⁴ B's expenditure. If of the income of B¹ 3 is equal to the expenditure of A, then the ratio of the savings of A to those of B is:", "o": ["3 : 4", "3 : 5", "5 : 3", "4 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A : B Income 2x : 3x Expenditure 3y : 4y ______________ Savings (2x - 3y) : (3x - 4y) According to the question, = 3y, ⇒ x : y = 3 : 1¹ 3 × 3 x Savings ratio = (2x - 3y) : (3x - 4y) ⇒ (2 × 3 - 3 × 1) : (3 × 3 - 4 × 1) = 3 : 5 Short Trick :- Ratio A : B → Income 2 : 3 ) × 3 → Expenses 3 : 4 ) × 1 → ------------------------------------------ Savings of A = (2 × 3) (3 × 1) = 3 − "},
+{"id": "P2344", "q": "One cup has juice and water in the ratio 5 : 2, while another cup of the same capacity has them in the ratio 7 : 4, respectively. If the contents of both the cups (when full) are poured in a vessel, then what will be the final ratio of water to juice in the vessel?", "o": ["25:52", "52:25", "25:26", "26:25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Juice : water = total → Cup 1⁵ : 2 = 7 ) × 11 → Cup 2⁷ : 4 = 11 ) × 7 → -------------------------------------------- Cup 3 Juice : Water ⇒ (5 × 11) + (7 × 7) : (2 × 11) + (4 × 7)¹04 : 50 = 52 : 25 Ratio water : juice = 25 : 52 →"},
+{"id": "P2345", "q": "In a library, the ratio of the number of mathematics books to that of physics books , is the same as the ratio of the number of physics books to that of chemistry books. If there are 144 mathematics books and 100 chemistry 327 books, then the ratio of the total number of mathematics and physics books to the total number of chemistry and physics books is :-", "o": ["3 : 2", "6 : 5", "5 : 4", "4 : 3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let number of Mathematics books = M, number of Physics books = P and number of Chemistry books = C According to question, = = = 144¹00 = 14400 M P P C ⇒ P² MC × So, = 120 P So, required ratio (M + P) : (C + P) → = (144 + 120) : (100 + 120) = 264 : 220 = 6 : 5"},
+{"id": "P2346", "q": "70 males and 100 females are working in a firm. During one mass recruitment drive, an equal number of males and females are recruited and their ratio becomes 3 : 4. The total number of people working in the firm after recruitment is:", "o": ["240", "200", "210", "220"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let males and females x x are added in the recruitment drive. According to the question, = 70 + x¹00 + x³ 4²80 + 4 = 300 + 3 ⇒ = 20 x x x Total males now = 70 + 20 = 90, Total females now = 100 + 20 = 120 Total working population = 90 + 120 = 210"},
+{"id": "P2347", "q": "Between two consecutive years, my income is in the ratio 2 : 5 and expenses are in the ratio 4 : 7. If my income in the second year is ₹75,000 and my expenses in the first year are ₹20,000, then my total savings in the two years together are:", "o": ["₹55,000", "₹60,000", "₹50,000", "₹40,000"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio 1st year : 2nd year → Income 2x : 5x → Expenses 4y : 7y → According to question, 5x = 75000 x = 15000 ⇒ 4y = 20000 y = 5000 ⇒ Savings of both years combined = (2x - 4y) + (5x - 7y) = (2 × 15000 - 4 × 5000) + (5 × 15000 - 7 × 5000) = 10000 + 40000 = 50000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2348", "q": "When is subtracted from each of x²1, 22, 60 and 64, the numbers obtained in this order are in proportion. What is mean proportional between ( + 4) and x ( )? x² − 1", "o": ["8", "5", "6", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= 21 − x²2 − x⁶0 − x⁶4 − x (21 – ) (64 – ) = (22 – ) (60 – ) x x x x¹344+ –21 –64 = 1320+ –60 – 22 x² x x x² x x¹344 – 85 = 1320 – 82 x x²4 = 3 ⇒ = 8 x x So, Mean proportional = ( x + 4 ) ( x² − 1 ) = ( 8 + 4 ) ( 8² − 1 ) = = = 6 ( 12 ) ( 3 )³6"},
+{"id": "P2349", "q": "If (a + b) : (b + c) : (c + a) = 7 : 4 : 5, and a + b + c = 16, then ( : is equal a² + b² + c² ) ( ab + bc + ca ) to :", "o": ["24 :17", "26 : 19", "27 : 20", "23 : 15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let (a + b) = 7x , (b + c) = 4x, (c + a)=5x So, according to question 7x + 4x + 5x = 2(a + b + c)⁷x + 4x + 5x = 2(16)¹6x = 32 x = 2 ⇒ So, a + b = 7x = 14 , b + c = 4x = 8 and c + a = 5x = 10 So, a = 8 , b = 6 , c = 2 Now, ( a² + b² + c² ) : ( ab + bc + ca ) ( : 8⁶ + 6² + 8² 8² + 6² + 2² ) × × × = ( 64 + 36 + 4 ) : ( 48 + 12 + 16 ) = ( = 26 : 19¹04 ) : ( 76 )"},
+{"id": "P2350", "q": "Renuka got 1 times as many 1² marks in Mathematics as in English. Her total marks in Mathematics, English and Science are 190. If the ratio of the marks in Mathematics and Science is 2 : 3, find her Science marks.", "o": ["92", "90", "85", "88"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio Maths : English : Science → 3 : 2 )² × 2 : 3)³ × -------------------------------------- 6 : 4 : 9 Total marks (6 + 4 + 9) units = 190 Marks in Science (9 units) = 90"},
+{"id": "P2351", "q": "A certain sum is divided among A, B, C and D such that B's share is of A's¹ 3 share, C's share is 40% of B's share, and D's Share is 50% of C's share. If the difference between the shares of B and D is ₹1,600, then the sum is:", "o": ["₹9,600", "₹9,400", "₹9,000", "₹9,200"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio A : B : C : D → 3 : 1⁵ : 2² : 1³41 ------------------------------------ Final 30 : 10 : 4 : 2 → Difference between B and D = (10 - 2)units 8 units = ₹1600¹ unit = 200 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2352", "q": "A sum of ₹3,900 is divided among P , Q and R such that R receives two-fifths of P’s share and Q receives three times of R’s share. What is Q’s share (in ₹)?", "o": ["1,500", "600", "1,800", "1,200"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the share of P be 5 units, Now share of R = × 5 = 2 units. 2⁵ Share of Q = 3 × 2 = 6 units. So, ratio of share of P : Q : R = 5 : 6 : 2. Share of Q = × 3900 = 1,800."},
+{"id": "P2353", "q": "x and y are two numbers having opposite signs such that, : = 49 : 64. x² y² What is the value of (5x - 6y) : (6x - 7y)?", "o": ["44 : 65", "13 : 14", "94 : 117", "83 : 98"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given, : = 49 : 64 x² y² As x and y have opposite signs, let x be positive and y is negative. x = + 7 and y = - 8 Putting these values in (5x - 6y) : (6x - 7y) we get 5 × 7 - 6 × (-8) : 6 × 7 - 7 × (-8)³5 + 48 : 42 + 56 ⇒ 83 : 98"},
+{"id": "P2354", "q": "In an examination, the ratio of the number of candidates who passed to those who failed was 5 : 2. If the number of failed candidates had been 14 more, 328 then the ratio of the number of passed candidates to those who failed would have been 4 : 3. The number of candidates who appeared in the examination was:", "o": ["126", "98", "70", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total number of students appeared = 7 unit = 98"},
+{"id": "P2355", "q": "The ratio of two numbers is 4 : 5. If one is subtracted from the first number, and two is added to the second number, then the ratio becomes 3 : 4. What will be the ratio when eight and four are, respectively, added to the first and the second number?", "o": ["2 : 3", "8 : 9", "6 : 7", "1: 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the numbers be 4x and 5x respectively. According to question, = 4 x − 1⁵ x + 2³ 4 ⇒ 16 x − 4 = 15 x + 6 ⇒ x = 10 . So the numbers are 40 and 50 respectively."},
+{"id": "P2356", "q": "If 9685 is divided into three parts in such a way that one-fourth of the first part, one-third of the second part and one-sixth of the third part are equal, then what is the first part?", "o": ["4470", "2253", "2980", "2235"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the three parts be a, b and c . a : b : c = 4 : 3 : 6 a⁴ = b³ = c⁶ → First part (a) = 4⁴ + 3 + 6 × 9685 = 2980"},
+{"id": "P2357", "q": "In a proportion, the product of the first and fourth terms is 70 and that of the second and third items is 3.5y. The value of y is.", "o": ["17", "20", "15", "22"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "When a , b , c and d are in proportion , then ad = bc According to question , ad = 70 and bc = 3.5y⁷0 = 3.5y ⇒ y = 20"},
+{"id": "P2358", "q": "A person divided a certain sum between his three sons in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. Had he divided the sum in the ratio 1³ , 1⁴ , , the son, who got the least share earlier, 1⁵ would have got ₹1,188 more. The sum (in ₹) was :", "o": ["6,840", "6,768", "7,008", "5,640"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Initial Ratio 3 : 4 : 5 = 12 units ) × 47 → Final Ratio 20 : 15 : 12 = 47 units ) × 12 → Equating the total units , we get Initial Ratio 141 : 188 : 235 = 564 units → Final Ratio 240 : 180 : 144 = 564 units → Least share difference = 240¹41 = 99 − 99 units = 1188 Rs. , 1 unit = 12 Rs. Total sum (564 units)⁵64 × 12 = 6768 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2359", "q": "If a : b : c = , then 1⁴ : 1³ : 1² = ? a b : b c : c a", "o": ["12 : 9 : 8", "8 : 9 : 24", "9 : 8 : 24", "9 : 12 : 8 SSC CHSL 2019 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2020", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "LCM of 4, 3, 2 is 12 Multiply the ratio by 12 a : b : c = 3 : 4 : 6 = a b : b c : c a³ 4 : 4⁶ : 6³ LCM of 4 , 6 and 3 is 12 ."},
+{"id": "P2360", "q": "The sum of three numbers is 79. If the ratio of the first number to the second number is 4 : 7 and that of the second number to the third number is 4 : 5, then the second number is:", "o": ["15", "28", "35", "12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio a : b : c → 4 : 7 : 7³43⁴ : 4 : 5 ------------------------------------------ 16 : 28 : 35 Sum of three numbers (16 + 28 + 35) units 79 Units → 79 → Second number (28 units) = 28"},
+{"id": "P2361", "q": "If 2145 : :: 3003 : 42, then the x value of so that : 2508 :: : 11704, is y x y", "o": ["212", "156", "140", "96"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "2145 : :: 3003 : 42 x = ⇒ = 30²145 x³003⁴2 x Now , : 2508 : : y : 11704 x = ⇒ y = 140³0²508 y¹1704"},
+{"id": "P2362", "q": "The perimeter of a rectangular field is 32 meters and its sides are in the ratio 5 : 3, Then the sides of the field are:", "o": ["10 m and 6 m", "9 m and 7 m", "12 m and 10 m", "5 m and 3 m"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2020", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Perimeter of rectangle = 2 (l + b)³2 m = 2 (5 + 3 ) = 2m x x ⇒ x Length (5 ) = 10m , Breadth (3 ) = 6m x x"},
+{"id": "P2363", "q": "If (a + b) : (b + c) : (c + a) = 7 : 6 : 5 and a + b + c = 27, then what will be the value of : : ? 1 a¹ b¹ c", "o": ["3 : 6 : 4", "3 : 2 : 4", "4 : 3 : 6", "3 : 4 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "d", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let (a + b) = 7 units (b + c) = 6 units , (c + a) = 5 units Adding all three , we get (a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = (7 + 6 + 5) units (a + b + c) = 9 units According to the question , 9 units = 27¹ unit = 3 ⇒ a = (a + b + c) (b + c) ⇒ − = 9⁶ = 3 units − 3 unit = 3 × (3) = 9 Similarly , b = 12 and c = 6 : : = : : = 4 : 3 : 6 ⇒ 1 a¹ b¹ c¹ 9¹ 12¹ 6"},
+{"id": "P2364", "q": "If x is subtracted from each of 23, 39, 32 and 56, the numbers so obtained 330 in this order are in proportion. What is the mean proportional between (x + 4) and (3x + 1) ?", "o": ["15", "10", "12", "14"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "To find the value of :- x Method :1 = x ad − bc ( a + d ) − ( b + c ) = 5 x ⇒ 23 × 56 − 39 × 32 ( 23 + 56 ) − ( 39 + 32 ) Method :2 = --- (i)²3 − x³9 − x³2 − x⁵6 − x By hit and trial, we can find that = 5 x satisfies the eq . (i) Mean proportion of (x + 4) and (3x + 1) i.e."},
+{"id": "P2365", "q": "The mean proportional of 8a² and , where a is a positive number, is ____. 18 a⁴", "o": ["12a", "12a²", "12 a² 12 a"], "ol": ["b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mean proportion = = = 8 a² × 18 a⁴ 144 a² 12 a"},
+{"id": "P2366", "q": "Find the fourth proportion of the following numbers: rd of 27, th of 1³ 4⁵ 30, th of 35. 3⁷ Higher Secondary 24/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["35", "40", "45", "38"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "For the fourth proportion = = 1³ × 27⁴ 5 × 30³ 7 × 35 x ⇒ 9²4¹5 x = 40 ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2367", "q": "The prices of two articles are in the ratio 4 : 5. If the price of the first article is increased by x% and that of the other is decreased by 30% , then the new prices of A and B will be in the ratio 10 : 7. The value of x is :", "o": ["24.5", "22.5", "25", "20 Practice Questions SSC CHSL 2024 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2019", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the price of the articles be 400 and 500. According to the question , = 400 × 100 + x¹00⁵00 × 100 − 30¹00¹0⁷ = ⇒ 4 ( 100 + x )⁵ × 70¹0⁷ 400 + 4 = 500 = 25 % ⇒ x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2368", "q": "141 is divided into two parts in such a way that the one-eighth part of the first and one-ninth part of the second are in the ratio 5 : 6. Find the first part.", "o": ["36", "72", "48", "60"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the first part and second part be and respectively, x y According to question, = ⇒ 141 × x⁸ 141 × y⁹ 5⁶ = = ⇒ 9 x⁸ y⁵ 6 ⇒ x y²0²7 Now, 47 units = 141²0 units = × 20 = 60 ⇒ 141⁴7"},
+{"id": "P2369", "q": "The ratio of the incomes of Rama and Ganga is 4 : 3 and the ratio of their expenditures is 3 : 2. If each person saves ₹2,700, then find their expenditures, respectively.", "o": ["₹8,100 and ₹5,000", "₹8,000 and ₹5,000", "₹8,100 and ₹5,400", "₹8,000 and ₹5,400"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio - Rama : Ganga Income - 4 : 3 x x Expendi. - 3 : 2 y y -------------------------------------- Savings - 4 - 3 : 3 - 2 x y x y According to the question, 4 - 3 = 3 - 2 x y x y = x y savings of Rama (4 - 3 ) x y = 4 - 3 = = ₹2700 x x x So, expenditure of Rama = 3 = ₹8100 x And expenditure of Ganga = 2 = ₹5400 x"},
+{"id": "P2370", "q": "If 49 : x :: x : 81 and 64 : y :: y : 169, where x and y are both natural numbers, then find the value of 2x + 3y.", "o": ["312", "126", "348", "438"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In 49 : :: : 81 x x = = 63 x² 49 × 81 ⇒ x In 64 : :: : 169 y y = = 104 y² 64 × 169 ⇒ y Now 2 + 3 = 2⁶3 + 3¹04 x y × × = 126 + 312 = 438"},
+{"id": "P2371", "q": "The quantity of milk ordered on the first, second, third and fourth day of a four day ceremony is in the proportion of 30 litres, 24 litres, 35 litres and ‘x’ litres, respectively. Find the quantity of milk (in litres) ordered on the fourth day.", "o": ["30", "32", "28", "26 SSC CGL 2024 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required proportion = 30 : 24 :: 35 : x³0 = 24³5 × x × = = 28 litres x²4 × 35³0"},
+{"id": "P2372", "q": "At present, A is thrice as old as B. C is 5 years elder than B. The sum of the ages of A, B, C is 75 years. The ratio of the age of B five years ago to the age of A three years from now is:", "o": ["2 : 3", "1 : 4", "4 : 7", "1 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, {A = 3B , C = B + 5 } -------- (i) A + B + C = 75-------- (ii) By putting the value of A and C from eq .(i) to (ii) we get; 3B + B + (B + 5) = 75⁵B = 70 B = 14 A = 3B = 42 ⇒ ⇒ Hence, (B - 5) : (A + 3) = 9 : 45 = 1 : 5"},
+{"id": "P2373", "q": "If varies inversely as and = 2 x y x when = 6, then the value of when = y y x³ is:", "o": ["2", "3", "4", "6"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, ∝ x¹ y = k × {where k is constant} x¹ y Given that = 2 and = 6 we get; x y² = k × k = 12¹ 6 ⇒ Now, for = 3 x³ = 12 × = 4¹ y ⇒ y"},
+{"id": "P2374", "q": "What is the value of D, if A : C = B : D in the given table? Search on TG: @apna_pdf A B C D²5⁴0³0 ?", "o": ["56", "48", "45", "42"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, = = D = = 48 A C B D ⇒ 25³0⁴0 D ⇒ 30×40²5"},
+{"id": "P2375", "q": "A money bag contains one rupee, 5 rupee and 10 rupee coins in the ratio of 3 : 5 : 7 respectively. If the total amount in the bag is ₹980, then find the number of coins of ₹10.", "o": ["69", "70", "71", "68"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Denomination → ₹1 : ₹5 : ₹10 No of coins → 3 : 5 : 7 x x x Total amount in the bag = 3 + 5 × 5 + 10 × 7 x x x = 3 + 25 + 70 = 98 x x x x Now, 98 = 980 = 10 x ⇒ x No of coins of ₹10 = 7 × 10 = 70"},
+{"id": "P2376", "q": "There are y yellow marbles and b blue marbles in a box. 18% of the yellow marbles were added to 24% of the blue marbles, and the total was 30. Three times the number of yellow marbles exceeds two times the number of blue marbles by 200. What is the ratio of y² to b² ?", "o": ["6 ∶ 5", "4 : 1", "2 ∶ 1", "5 ∶ 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, × + b × = 30 y¹8¹00²4¹00³ + 4b = 500 ……..(i) ⇒ y And , 3 = 2b + 200 y³ - 2b = 200 ……..(ii) ⇒ y Subtract equation (i) from equation (ii), we get 6b = 300 b = 50 ⇒ Put the value of b in equation (i)³y + 200 = 500³y = 300 y = 100 ⇒ ⇒ Required ratio : = 100 × 100 : 50 × 50 = 4 : 1 y² b²"},
+{"id": "P2377", "q": "The mean proportional of 4a² and x is , where a is a positive number, then 1⁵ a the value of x is ______", "o": ["1", "100", "a", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mean proportion = pq = ⇒ 1⁵ a⁴ a² × x Taking square both side, = = ⇒ 1²5 a² 4 a² × x ⇒ x¹ 100 a⁴"},
+{"id": "P2378", "q": "The age of the older of two boys is thrice that of the younger. 9 years ago it was five times that of the younger. Find the present age of each.", "o": ["15 years, 45 years", "18 years, 54 years", "17 years, 51 years", "12 years, 36 years"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the age of younger boy be year x Then, age of older boy = 3 x Now, according to the question, ( - 9) = 5 ( - 9)³ x x³ - 9 = 5 - 45² = 36 = 18 x x ⇒ x ⇒ x So, the present age of each is 18 yr and 54 yr."},
+{"id": "P2379", "q": "M varies inversely as (N² + 3). If M = 3 when N = 3, then what will be the value of M when N² = 69 ?", "o": ["1", "1⁴ 69¹ 2"], "ol": ["a", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Accordion to the question, M ∝ 1 ( N² + 3 ) M = k × -------(i)¹ ( N² + 3 ) {where k is constant} Puting M = 3 and N = 3 in equation (i)³ = k × k = 36¹ ( 3² + 3 ) ⇒ Now, value of M when given that N² = 69 M = 36 × ⇒ M = = 1 ( 69 + 3 )³6⁷2¹ 2"},
