+{"id": "P2386", "q": "In a school, the total number of Search on TG: @apna_pdf boys is 20% more than the total number of girls. What is the ratio of the number of boys to that of girls in the school ?", "o": ["6 : 5", "5 : 6", "5 : 3", "4 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "20% = 1⁵ Girls = 5 unit, Boys = 6 unit required ratio of Boy to Girls = 6 : 5"},
+{"id": "P2387", "q": "In an educational institution, the ratio of the numbers of students in middle school and in high school, respectively, in a given year was given as 4 : 3. If there were 324 students in middle school in that year in that institution, what was the number of students in high school in the same year in that institution? Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["243", "240", "249", "246"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "No of students in high school = × 3 = 243³24⁴"},
+{"id": "P2388", "q": "If class A has 11 boys and 18 girls, class B has 13 boys and 17 girls, and class C has 20 boys and 9 girls, which class has the biggest ratio(s) of boys to girls? Matriculation Level 20/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["Class A", "Both class A and class B", "Class C", "Class B"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of boys and girls in class A = 11 : 18 = 0.61 Ratio of boys and girls in class B = 13 : 17 = 0.76 Search on TG: @apna_pdf Ratio of boys and girls in class C = 20 : 9 = 2.22 class C has the biggest ratio of boys to ⇒ girls."},
+{"id": "P2389", "q": "A recipe is made using cheese and butter in the ratio 4: 3. If Arohi uses 8 bowls of cheese, how many bowls of butter should she use? Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["4", "6", "8", "3"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio cheese : butter → 4 : 3⁴ units = 8 ⇒ 3 units = × 3 = 6 ⇒ 8⁴ So, she used 6 bowls of butter."},
+{"id": "P2390", "q": "The ratio of the salaries of S to F is 2 : 3 and the ratio of their savings is 3 : 4. What is the ratio of their expenditures if their total savings are equal to the salary of S? Matriculation Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["8 : 15", "7 : 15", "8 : 13", "7 : 12"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "S : F Salaries 2 : 3 → Savings 3 : 4 → Since, total savings are equal to the salary of S. Total savings = 3 + 4 =7. Now, S : F Salaries 2 : 3 → ( 7) × Savings 3 : 4 → ( 2) × Hence, S : F Salaries 14 : 21 → Savings 6 : 8 → ____________________________________ Expenditure 8 : 13 →"},
+{"id": "P2391", "q": "S varies directly as (R + 7), and S = 42 when R = 17. What is the value of S when R = 29 ? Matriculation Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["51", "63", "58", "66"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "S (R + 7) ∝ S = k(R + 7) Putting, S = 42 and R = 17, 42 = k(17+7) ⇒ 42 = 24k ⇒ k = = 42²4⁷ 4 Now, putting R = 29 in the above expression, we have ; S = k(R + 7) ⇒ S = (29 + 7)⁷⁴ ⇒ S = × 36 = 63⁷ 4"},
+{"id": "P2392", "q": "The price of a television set and a washing machine are in the ratio of 8 : 7. If the cost of the television set is ₹4,800 more than the cost of the washing machine, then find the price of the washing machine. Matriculation Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 1)", "o": ["₹33,000", "₹33,500", "₹33,600", "₹33,700"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "8 - 7 = 1 unit = ₹4800⁷ unit = 4800 × 7 = ₹33,600 So, the price of the washing machine = ₹33,600"},
+{"id": "P2393", "q": "Pooja, Chameli and Anju have a total of ₹450 in their purses. Pooja has ₹50 more than Chameli. Anju has two times what Pooja has. How much do Pooja, Chameli and Anju, respectively, have in their purses ? Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["₹150, ₹75 and ₹225", "₹100, ₹50 and ₹300", "₹125, ₹75 and ₹250", "₹125, ₹50 and ₹275"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let Rupees with Pooja = x + 50 Rs. Rupees with Chameli = x Rs. Rupees with Anju = 2(x + 50) Rs. Total Rupees = x + 50 + x + 2x + 100 = 450 Rs. 4x + 150 = 450⁴x = 300 x = 75 ⇒ ⇒ ⇒ Hence, Pooja’s Rupees = 75 +50 = 125 Rs. Chameli’s Rupees = 75 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2394", "q": "Two numbers are in the ratio 4 : 5. If 3 is added to the smaller and 7 is subtracted from the larger number, they are in the ratio 1 : 1. Find the numbers. Higher Secondary 20/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["60, 75", "40, 50", "55, 44", "20, 25"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let first number = 4 x Second number = 5 x According to question, = 4 + 3 = 5 - 7 = 10⁴ x + 3⁵ x − 7¹ 1 ⇒ x x ⇒ x Hence, First number = 40 And second number = 50"},
+{"id": "P2395", "q": "What is the mean proportional of 45x⁴ and 5y² ? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["5x² y", "25x⁴ y", "15x² y", "45x² y²"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Mean proportional = = 15 y⁴5 x⁴ × 5 y² x²"},
+{"id": "P2396", "q": "The ages of A and B are in the ratio 4 : 7, respectively. After 8 years, the ratio of their ages will be 2 : 3. What is the sum of the ages of A and B (in years)? Higher Secondary 21/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["44", "36", "38", "42"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, = 12 + 24 = 14 + 16 ⇒ 4 x + 8⁷ x + 8² 3 ⇒ x x² = 8 = 4 ⇒ x ⇒ x Present age of A and B will be 16 yrs and 28 yrs respectively, Now, sum of the age of A and B = 16 + 28 = 44 years Alternate method :- 2 units = 8¹ unit = 4 ⇒ ⇒ 11 units = 44 years ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2397", "q": "Which number should be added to 3, 11, 4 and 14 to make them in proportion? Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["3", "2", "4", "1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: = 3 + x¹1 + x⁴ + x¹4 + x By putting option one by one, we get = 1 x As = = 3 + 1¹1 + 1⁴ + 1¹4 + 1 ⇒ 5¹5¹ 3"},
+{"id": "P2398", "q": "Two numbers are in the ratio 4 : 5. If 17 is subtracted from each, the new numbers are in the ratio 11 : 14. If 20 is added to each of the original numbers, then the ratio becomes: Higher Secondary 25/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["224 : 275", "275 : 241", "241 : 275", "224 : 241"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let first number = 4 x²nd number = 5 x Given = 4 x − 17⁵ x − 17¹1¹4⁵6 - 238 = 55 - 187 = 51 ⇒ x x ⇒ x original ratio = = ⇒ 51 × 4⁵1 × 5²04²55 Hence, Required ratio = 204 + 20²55 + 20 = or 224 : 275²24²75"},
+{"id": "P2399", "q": "A bag contains a total of 180 coins in the denominations of ₹5 and ₹1. Find the number of ₹5 coins in the bag, if the total value of the coins is ₹500. Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["60", "120", "80", "100"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let all coins are of denomination ₹5 Total value = 180⁵ = 900 ₹ ⇒ × Let all coins are of denomination ₹1 Total value = 180¹ =180 ⇒ × By allegation 4 : 5 ⇒ 9 unit 180¹ unit 20 ⇒ → ⇒ → Hence, the number of ₹5 coins in the bag = 4²0 = 80."},
+{"id": "P2400", "q": "Find the third proportional of 9, 7, ?, 14. Higher Secondary 26/06/2024 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["21", "16", "24", "18"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the third proportional = x = 9¹4 = 7 = 18⁹ 7 x¹4 ⇒ × x ⇒ x"},
+{"id": "P2401", "q": "Find the ratio between the fourth proportional of 42, 56, 63 and the fourth proportional of 189, 273, and 153. Graduate Level 21/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["33 : 221", "217 : 42", "33 : 84", "84 : 221 Q.135 . Rishi and Sarita have ₹4,760. If of Rishi's amount is equal to of 9¹6³ 4 Sarita's amount, how much does Sarita have? Graduate Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "₹3,570", "₹1,190", "₹2,720", "₹2,040"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Fourth proportional of 42, 56, 63 = = 84⁶3 × 56⁴2 Fourth proportional of 189, 273, 153 = = 221¹53 × 273¹89 Required ratio = 84 : 221"},
+{"id": "P2402", "q": "A sum of money was divided between Cyrus, Rohan and Mishti. The ratio of the sums received by Cyrus and Rohan was 3 : 2, while the ratio of the sums received by Rohan and Mishti was 7 : 12. If the sum received by Cyrus was ₹1,800 less than the sum received by Mishti, how many rupees did Rohan receive as his share? Graduate Level 24/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["₹9,240", "₹7,560", "₹8,400", "₹6,300"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Cyrus Rohan Mishti 3 : 2 : 2⁷ : 7 : 12 _______________________ 21 : 14 : 24 According to the question, 24 - 21 = 3 unit = ₹1800 Then, 14 unit = × 14 = ₹8400¹800³"},
+{"id": "P2403", "q": "The third proportional to (5² - 3² ) and (5 - 3) is: Graduate Level 25/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["1", "3", "1", "8"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "(5² -3² ) = 16, 5 - 3 =2 Third proportional to 16 and 2 = = 2 × 2¹6¹ 4"},
+{"id": "P2404", "q": "Four distinct positive numbers, ‘a’, ‘b’, ‘c’ and ‘d’, in the order given, are in proportion. ‘b’ is 35 more than ‘a’ and ‘d’ is 60 more than ‘c’. The product of ‘a’ and ‘c’ is 5376. What is the sum of ‘a’, ‘b’, ‘c’ and ‘d’? Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 3)", "o": ["398", "400", "399", "397"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, b = 35 + a --------------- (i) d = 60 + c --------------- (ii) Since a,b,c,d are in proportion. Then we have ; = a b c d ad = bc a(60 + c) = (35 + a)c [from eqn(i)&(ii)]⁶0a + ac = 35c + ac ⇒ 60a = 35c = = a c³5⁶0⁷ 12 Let a and c be 7 and 12 x x Then, 7 × 12 = 5376 x x⁸4 = 5376 ⇒ = = 64 = 8 x² x² 5376⁸4 ⇒ x Then, a = 7 × 8 = 56, b = 35 + 56 = 91, c"},
+{"id": "P2405", "q": "A bag contains rupee, 50-paise and 25-paise coins in the ratio 3 : 4 : 6. If the total amount is ₹143, the number of 50-paise coins is: Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["132", "66", "90", "88"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Types of coins ₹1⁵0P²5P No of coins 3 : 4 : 6 Total amount = 3 × 1 + 4 × + 6 × 1² 1⁴ = 3 + 2 + 1.5 = 6.5⁶.5 unit = ₹143⁴ unit = × 4 = 88¹43⁶ ."},
+{"id": "P2406", "q": "The sum of the four numbers A, B, C and D is 875. If the ratio of A to B is 1 : 2, the ratio of B to C is 3 : 1 and the ratio of C to D is 2 : 3, find the value of C. Graduate Level 26/06/2024 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["120", "130", "125", "135 Search on TG: @apna_pdf SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, we have given ratio; A B C D¹ : 2 : 2 : 2³ : 3 : 1 : 1² : 2 : 2 : 3 ______________________ 6 : 12 : 4 : 6 = 3 : 6 : 2 : 3 Search on TG: @apna_pdf Value of C = × 875² 3 + 6 + 2 + 3 = = 125¹750¹4"},
+{"id": "P2407", "q": "Profit of ₹29,120 is divided among A, B and C so that A's share is 2 times B's and B's share is 1 times 1² 1⁵ C. Find B's share.", "o": ["₹6,940", "₹7,820", "₹6,720", "₹7,140"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, Ratio - A : B : C Profit - 15 : 6 : 5 x x x B’s share = 29120 × 6 x¹5 x + 6 x + 5 x = ₹ 6720"},
+{"id": "P2408", "q": "If A : B : C = 3 : 4 : 5, then : is: A² + B² C² − B²", "o": ["3 : 2", "4 : 5", "5 : 3", "3 : 5 SSC CHSL 2023 Tier - 1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": ": A² + B² C² − B² = : ⇒ : = 5 : 3⁹ + 16²5 − 16²5⁹"},
+{"id": "P2409", "q": "What is the fourth proportional of 3 , 5 and 3 ? 5⁸ 10 Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["10", "40", "30", "20⁵ 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Fourth proportional = 3¹0 × 5⁸ 3⁵ = = 5 × 4 = 20² × 5⁸"},
+{"id": "P2410", "q": "The ratio of the number of boys to that of girls in a village is 5 : 3. If 40% of the boys and 60% of the girls appeared in an examination, then the ratio of the number of boys and girls who appeared Search on TG: @apna_pdf in the examination to the number who did not appear in the same examination, is :- Matriculation Level 30/06/2023 (Shift - 4)", "o": ["17 ∶ 21", "19 ∶ 21", "17 ∶ 27", "19 ∶ 23 SSC CHSL 2022 Tier - 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2024", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number of boys and girls in the village be 500 and 300. According to question, Total number of boys and girls who appeared in the examination (500 × ) + (300 × ) = 380 → 40¹00⁶0¹00 Total number of boys and girls who did not appear in the examination 800³80 = 420 → − Required ratio = 380 : 420 = 19 : 21"},
+{"id": "P2411", "q": "In three positive numbers, the ratio of first and second is 3 : 4 and the ratio of second and third is 3 : 5. The product of first and third is 4500. What is the sum of the three numbers?", "o": ["282", "235", "198", "205"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2023", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "1st no. : 2nd no. : 3rd no. 3 : 4 : 4³ : 3 : 5 ------------------------- 9 : 12 : 20 According to the question, (9 × 20 ) unit = ₹4500 x x = = = 5 x² 450¹8 ⇒ x²25⁹ Sum of three numbers = (41 ) = 41 × 5 x = 205"},
+{"id": "P2412", "q": "In a bag there are Rs 5 and Rs 10 coins such that the product of their numbers is 135 and the total amount in the bag is Rs 165, what is the amount Search on TG: @apna_pdf from all Rs 10 coins?", "o": ["90", "85", "80", "95"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the 5 coin be x and 10 coins be y ₹ ₹ xy = 135 and 5x + 10y=165 So, ( )⁵¹35 y + 10 y = 165² y² − 33 y + 135 = 0 y = 9 or 7.5 (number of coins cannot be Search on TG: @apna_pdf in decimal) So, amount=10 × 9 = 90 ₹"},
+{"id": "P2413", "q": "Let x, y, z be fractions such that x<y<z. If z is divided by x, the result is , 5² which exceeds y by . If x + y + z = 1⁷ 4¹1¹2 then the ratio of (z – x) : (y – x) is: Search on TG: @apna_pdf", "o": ["6 : 5", "9 : 5", "5 : 6", "5 : 9"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2022", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "कठिन", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= ⇒ = z x⁵ 2 z⁵ x² According to the question , = y + ⇒ y = – = 5² 7⁴ 5² 7⁴ 3⁴ Also, + y + z = 1 x¹1¹2 Putting the values of z and y as obtained in above equation, we get = x + 3⁴ + 5 x² 23¹2 = ⇒ = 4 x + 3 + 10 x⁴ 23¹2¹4 x + 3²3³ = 23 – 9 ⇒ = 42 x x¹ 3 = = , So, z⁵ × 1³ 2⁵ 6 ( z – x ) : ( y – x ) = ( ) ( )⁵⁶ – 1³ : 3⁴ – 1³ = : = 6 : 5³ 6⁵ 12"},
+{"id": "P2414", "q": "If (a + b) : (b + c) : (c + a) = 7 : 4 : 5, and a + b + c = 16, then ( a² + b² + c² ) : is equal to : ( ab + bc + ca )", "o": ["24 :17", "26 : 19", "27 : 20", "23 : 15"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let (a + b) = 7x , (b + c) = 4x, (c + a)=5x So, according to question 7x + 4x + 5x = 2(a + b + c)⁷x + 4x + 5x = 2(16)¹6x = 32 x = 2 ⇒ So, a + b = 7x = 14 , b + c = 4x = 8 and c + a = 5x = 10 So, a = 8 , b = 6 , c = 2 Now, ( a² + b² + c² ) : ( ab + bc + ca ) ( : 8⁶ + 6² + 8² 8² + 6² + 2² ) × × × = ( 64 + 36 + 4 ) : ( 48 + 12 + 16 ) = ( = 26 : 19¹04 ) : ( 76 )"},
+{"id": "P2415", "q": "The ratio of the number of students in Science to that in Humanities, in Grade 12 of 360 students, is 2 : 3. When some new students are admitted, the number of Science Search on TG: @apna_pdf students increases by 18 and the ratio of the Science students to Humanities students changes to 3 : 5. What is the number of new Humanities students admitted?", "o": ["54", "45", "63", "72"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC MTS", "y": "2021", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "आसान", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Students in Science = 2 x Students in Humanities = 3 x² + 3 = 360, 5 = 360, ⇒ = 72 x x x x Let students added in Humanities be y."},
+{"id": "P2416", "q": "A bag contains ₹5, ₹2, and ₹1 coins in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. If the total amount of money in the bag is ₹252, find the number of coins of each kind.", "o": ["16 coins of ₹5, 24 coins of ₹2, and 40 coins of ₹1", "20 coins of ₹5, 30 coins of ₹2, and 50 coins of ₹1", "24 coins of ₹5, 36 coins of ₹2, and 60 coins of ₹1", "18 coins of ₹5, 27 coins of ₹2, and 45 coins of ₹1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let ₹5 coins = 2x, ₹2 coins = 3x, and ₹1 coins = 5x. According to the question, Total amount = (5 × 2x) + (2 × 3x) + (1 × 5x) ⇒ 252 = 10x + 6x + 5x ⇒ x = = 12²52²1 Now, the number of coins of each type is ₹5 coins = 2x = 2 × 12 = 24 ₹2 coins = 3x = 3 × 12 = 36 ₹1 coins = 5x = 5 × 12 = 60"},
+{"id": "P2417", "q": "If 9A = 10B and 12B =13C, find the ratio A : C Higher Secondary 29/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["15 : 16", "39 : 40", "27 : 28", "65 : 54"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "TG: @ikunal_x From:- 9A = 10B = ⇒ A B¹0⁹ From:- 12B = 13C = ⇒ B C¹3¹2 Ratio:- A : B : C¹0⁹ 13¹2 —---------------------------------- A : B: C¹0 × 13 : 9 ×13 : 9 ×12 → Now, A : C = 10 × 13 : 9 ×12 = 65 : 54"},
+{"id": "P2418", "q": "The savings of two persons are in the ratio 8 : 7 . If the first person increases his savings by 20% and the second person increases his savings by 15% , find the new ratio of their savings. Higher Secondary 28/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["32 : 28", "46 : 40.25", "9.6 : 8.05", "184 : 161"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Required ratio: 8 × : 7 × 120¹00¹15¹00 = 9.6 : 8.05"},
+{"id": "P2419", "q": "A scholarship amount of ₹1500 is to be distributed between A and B in the ratio 7:5. An amount of ₹250 is deducted for administrative charges; the remaining amount is increased by 20% as a bonus before the final distribution. How much amount will student A receive? Higher Secondary 24/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["₹875", "₹900", "₹833.33", "₹800"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Fund after charges: ₹1500 − ₹250 = ₹1250²0% bonus: ₹1250 × = ₹1500¹20¹00 A’s share = × 1500 = ₹875⁷ 12"},
+{"id": "P2420", "q": "In a zoo, there are horse and pigeons. If heads are counted, there are 200 heads and if legs are counted there are 580 legs. How many pigeons are there? Matriculation Level 29/07/2025(Shift - 1)", "o": ["90", "110", "100", "120"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let the number of horses = H and pigeons = P According to question, + = 200 —--(i) H P² + 4 = 580 P H + 2 = 290 -(ii) P H Equation (ii) - Equation (i) = 290 - 200 = 90 H Number of pigeons = 200 - 90 = 110"},
+{"id": "P2421", "q": "A recipe needs 4 cups of sugar to make 16 cookies. How many cups of sugar are needed to make 24 cookies in the same proportions? Matriculation Level 24/07/2025(Shift - 1)", "o": ["5 cups", "8 cups", "6 cups", "7 cups"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "16 cookies = 4 cups sugar 24 cookies = × 24 = 6 cups 4¹6"},
+{"id": "P2422", "q": "The incomes of P, Q and R are in the ratio of 9 : 15 : 10 and their savings TG: @ikunal_x are in the ratio is 10 : 15 : 12. If R spends 60% of his income, what is the ratio of the expenditures of P, Q and R?", "o": ["18 : 17 : 30", "17 : 30 : 18", "17 : 18 : 30", "18 : 30 : 17"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let income of P, Q, and R is 9 , 15 and 10 x x x and savings of P, Q, and R is 10 ,15 ,12 y y y According to the question, 10¹2 = 10 x − y x × 60¹00¹0¹2 = 6 ⇒ = x − y x x y³ 1 Ratio of expenditure of P, Q, and R = (9 - 10 ) : (15 - 15 ) : (10¹2 ) x y x y x − y = (27 - 10) : (45 -15) : (30¹2) − = 17 : 30 : 18"},
+{"id": "P2423", "q": "The ratio of the income of A to that of B is 5 : 7. A and B save Rs. 4000 and Rs. 5000 respectively. If the expenditure of A is equal to 66 % of the expenditure 2³ of B, then the total income of A and B is : TG: @ikunal_x", "o": ["Rs. 25,200", "Rs. 24,000", "Rs. 26,400", "Rs. 28,800"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Fractional Value 66 % = → 2³ 2³ Ratio A : B → Income 5 : 7 → Expenditure 2 : 3 → -------------------------------------- Savings 4000 : 5000 → Now, (5³) (7²)units × − × = (3⁴000) (2⁵000) × − × ⇒ 1 unit = 2000 Rs. Total income of A and B (5 + 7) units → 12 units = 12²000 = 24000 Rs."},
+{"id": "P2424", "q": "If 50% of A = 0.4 of B = of C , 1⁸ find A : B : C", "o": ["4 : 5 : 16", "16 : 10 : 4", "6 : 3 : 10", "10 : 4 : 16"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A = B = C¹ 2⁴ 10¹ 8 A = B = C¹ 2 × 4⁴ 10 × 4¹ 8 × 4 = = A : B : C = 4 : 5 : 16 A⁸ B¹0 C³2 ⇒"},
+{"id": "P2425", "q": "If M : N = 3 : 4, N : O = 5 : 6, and O : P = 8 : 10, then find N : P.", "o": ["5 : 7", "2 : 3", "4 : 5", "3 : 2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio M : N : O : P → 3 : 4 : 4 : 4⁵ : 5 : 6 : 6⁸ : 8 : 8 : 10 _____________________________ 120 : 160 : 192 : 240 So, the ratio of N and P = 160 : 240 or 2 : 3"},
+{"id": "P2426", "q": "If P : Q = 7 : 5, Q : R = 2 : 3, and R : S = 4 : 5, find the ratio P : S.", "o": ["28 : 25", "56 : 75", "30 : 25", "70 : 56"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "P : Q : R : S⁵6 : 40 : 60 : 75 Reqd. ratio = 56 : 75"},
+{"id": "P2427", "q": "If x : y = 2 : 5, then find (3x + 2y) : (7x − 2y).", "o": ["3 : 2", "4 : 1", "7 : 4", "9 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given: x : y = 2 : 5 (3x + 2y) : (7x − 2y). (3 × 2 + 2 × 5) : (7 × 2 − 2× 5)¹6 : 4 = 4 : 1"},
+{"id": "P2428", "q": "A ₹48,000 annual bonus is distributed among Sales, Marketing, and Operations in a⁵ : 4 : 3 ratio. Marketing uses ₹3,000 for team building and ₹1,500 for an intern, then allocates the rest to two top performers in a³ : 2 ratio. How much does the top performer with the smaller share receive ?", "o": ["₹5,833.33", "₹5,250", "₹4,600", "₹4,200"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "The marketing team's share of the total profit = × 4 = ₹16000⁴8000¹2 After use remaining amount = 16000 - 4500 = ₹11500 The share of the top performer with a smaller portion = × 2 = ₹4600¹1500⁵"},
+{"id": "P2429", "q": "If A : B = 4 : 7, B : C = 3 : 5, and C : D = 8 : 9, find A : B : C : D.", "o": ["96 : 168 : 280 : 315", "168 : 96 : 280 : 315", "96 : 168 : 315 : 280", "96 : 280 : 168 : 315"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "A : B : C : D⁴ : 7 : 7 : 7³ : 3 : 5 : 5⁸ : 8 : 8 : 9 --------------------------------------------- 96 : 168 : 280 : 315"},
+{"id": "P2430", "q": "A box contains ₹10, ₹5, and ₹2 coins in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3. If the total amount of money in the box is ₹416 , find the number of coins of each kind.", "o": ["20 coins of ₹10, 40 of ₹5, and 60 of ₹2", "16 coins of ₹10, 32 of ₹5, and 48 of ₹2", "10 coins of ₹10, 20of ₹5, and 30 of ₹2", "16 coins of ₹10, 32 of ₹5, and 46 of ₹2"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let number of ₹10, ₹5, and ₹2 coins are , 2 , 3 respectively x x x A/Q , 10 × + 5 × 2 + 2 × 3 = 416 x x x¹0 + 10 + 6 = 416 ⇒ x x x²6 = 416 = 16 ⇒ x ⇒ x Number of coins are 16 , 32 , 48 →"},
+{"id": "P2431", "q": "If a : b = 5 : 3, find (3a + 4b) : (3a - 4b).", "o": ["9 : 1", "1 : 9", "7 : 1", "1 : 7"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC CGL", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "= = or 9 : 1 ( 3 a + 4 b ) ( 3 a − 4 b )³ × 5 + 4 × 3³ × 5 − 4 × 3²7³"},
