+{"id": "P2457", "q": "The ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls in a class is 10 : 13. If there are 115 students in the class, how many boys are there? Higher Secondary 30/07/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["50", "75", "85", "60"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "a", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Given :- Boys : Girls = 10 : 13 According to question, (10 + 13) = 23 units = 115 ⇒ 10 units = × 10 = 50 ⇒ 115²3"},
+{"id": "P2458", "q": "The ratio of the ages of two friends is 5 : 6. After 15 years, the ratio becomes 8 : 9. What are their present ages? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["20 and 30", "52 and 58", "25 and 30", "24 and 28"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Let , present age = 5 , 6 x x = 45 + 135 = 48 + 120⁵ x + 15⁶ x + 15⁸ 9 ⇒ x x³ = 15 = 5 x ⇒ x Present age = 25, 30"},
+{"id": "P2459", "q": "Three people P, Q, and R, have incomes that are in the ratio 13 : 14 : 15. If their total earnings are Rs. 2,31,000, how much money does Q earn? Higher Secondary 02/08/2025 (Shift - 2)", "o": ["Rs. 91,000", "Rs. 93,500", "Rs. 1,04,500", "Rs. 77,000 eduquity-based pattern (ebp) Questions"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Total income of P, Q, R = 13 + 14 + 15 = 42 Income of Q = × 14 = ₹ 77000²31000⁴2"},
+{"id": "P2460", "q": "At present, A is thrice as old as B. C is 5 years elder than B. The sum of the TG: @ikunal_x ages of A, B, C is 75 years. The ratio of the age of B five years ago to the age of A three years from now is:", "o": ["2 : 3", "1 : 4", "4 : 7", "1 : 5"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "d", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to the question, {A = 3B , C = B + 5 } -------- (i) A + B + C = 75-------- (ii) By putting the value of A and C from eq .(i) to (ii) we get; 3B + B + (B + 5) = 75⁵B = 70 B = 14 A = 3B = 42 ⇒ ⇒ Hence, (B - 5) : (A + 3) = 9 : 45 = 1 : 5"},
+{"id": "P2461", "q": "What is the value of D, if A : C = B : D in the given table? A B C D²5⁴0³0 ?", "o": ["56", "48", "45", "42"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "According to question, = = D = = 48 A C B D ⇒ 25³0⁴0 D ⇒ 30×40²5"},
+{"id": "P2462", "q": "If class A has 11 boys and 18 TG: @ikunal_x girls, class B has 13 boys and 17 girls, and class C has 20 boys and 9 girls, which class has the biggest ratio(s) of boys to girls?", "o": ["Class A", "Both class A and class B", "Class C", "Class B"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Ratio of boys and girls in class A = 11 : 18 = 0.61 Ratio of boys and girls in class B = 13 : 17 = 0.76 Ratio of boys and girls in class C = 20 : 9 = 2.22 class C has the biggest ratio of boys to ⇒ girls."},
+{"id": "P2463", "q": "The price of a television set and a washing machine are in the ratio of 8 : 7. If the cost of the television set is ₹4,800 more than the cost of the washing machine, then find the price of the washing machine.", "o": ["₹33,000", "₹33,500", "₹33,600", "₹33,700"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "c", "e": "SSC", "y": "2025", "t": "अनुपात", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "8 - 7 = 1 unit = ₹4800⁷ unit = 4800 × 7 = ₹33,600 So, the price of the washing machine = ₹33,600"},
