+{"id": "P3056", "q": "Using 2cosA cosB = cos(A + B) + cos(A – B), find the value of cos75° cos 15°.", "o": ["1", "2", "1", "4"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CHSL", "y": "2022", "t": "त्रिकोणमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "Formula used:- 2cosA cosB = cos(A + B) + cos(A – B) Putting A = 75°, B = 15°. We have , 2 × cos 75°cos 15° = cos(75° + 15°) + cos(75° - 15°)² × cos 75°cos15° = cos 90° + cos 60° cos75 °cos15° = ( 0 + )¹² 1² = × = 1² 1² 1⁴"},
