+{"id": "P3291", "q": "If A, B and C are the interior angles of ABC, then what is the value of ∆ {tan + cosec } {tan - cosec A² B + C² A² } ? B + C²", "o": ["2", "-1", "-2", "1"], "ol": ["a", "b", "c", "d"], "a": "b", "e": "SSC CPO", "y": "2024", "t": "त्रिकोणमिति", "d": "मध्यम", "p": "general", "lang": "en", "sol": "In ABC ∆ ∠A + ∠B + ∠C = 180 ° + = ∠ A² ∠ B + ∠ C² 90 ° Now, {tan + cosec }{tan - A² B + C² A² cosec } B + C² {tan + cosec(90° - )} {tan - A² A² A² cosec(90° - )} A² (tan + sec )(tan - sec ) A² A² A² A² tan 2 - sec 2 = -1 A² A²"},
